window.AKK_TRANSMIGRATED_INTO_A_SISTER_FORTUNE_ON_THE_FARM_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_TRANSMIGRATED_INTO_A_SISTER_FORTUNE_ON_THE_FARM_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":201,"title":"Chapter 201: Before the Results Are Announced","paragraphs":["After leaving his teacher's house, Song Gaoli went straight to the Song residence to find Song Qiming. Placing his recreated exam paper on the table, he did nothing but sigh, his face full of worry.","\"The teacher said my chances of passing are slim and it will all depend on luck. What about you? What did the Dean say?\"","Although he had never expected to pass the provincial exam and become a successful candidate this time, since he had taken it, he couldn't help but harbor a bit of hope. If a blind cat happened to catch a dead mouse and he passed, wouldn't that be a stroke of immense luck? Besides, his luck had always been good, scraping by the passing mark every time.","Song Qiming withdrew his gaze from the recreated exam paper. \"The Dean said I performed well. Passing the exam won't be a problem, so the next step is to prepare for the spring metropolitan exam next year.\"","Song Gaoli slid forward, his body slumping weakly into the chair. In a deflated tone, he said, \"Even if I'm lucky enough to make the list, I definitely have no hope for the spring exam. I'll just have to wait another three years.\"","The capital was so far away. If he couldn't go with Qiming, he would have to make the journey all alone in three years!","Song Qiming reached out and patted his shoulder. \"If you pass this time, you must definitely go to the spring exam in February. Just treat it as getting used to it in advance, so you won't be at a loss next time.\"","Song Gaoli lay face down on the table, his arms dangling by his sides as he wailed, \"Are you really not going back to the village after the results are posted? There's nothing to do in the capital if you go this early!\"","If he didn't pass, he would definitely have to stay at the academy and continue studying. If he was lucky enough to pass, he still had to return to the village to reunite with his family and properly celebrate.","After all, there was nearly half a year before next year's spring exam. He could stay a few more months; there was plenty of time to head to the capital later.","Song Qiming shook his head. He didn't mention the matter of the potatoes, only saying, \"My teacher is waiting for me in the capital. The spring exam gathers the finest elites, all rare talents from various provinces. I want to go and prepare early.\"","Song Gaoli buried his head between his arms in great frustration. He decided to wait until the results were out; if he didn't pass, overthinking it would be pointless anyway.","After everyone else had left, He Feixuan turned back and returned to the Mu residence. \"Dean, you said I have a chance to aim for the top five, but what about the first place? Do I have a chance at that?\"","He didn't believe for a second that Song Qiming had underperformed. In this provincial exam, Qiming was the only one who could possibly surpass him. Since the Dean had already reviewed both of their recreated papers, he surely knew who had done better.","He Feixuan was very confident in himself. In his eyes, no one in the entire Longbei Province could surpass him. The only rising star was Song Qiming, and the first place was bound to be one of them.","Mu Hongyue hadn't expected He Feixuan to specifically turn back to ask him this. Just as he had commented earlier, He Feixuan's performance in all three sessions of the exam was incredibly outstanding. But forcing a comparison between him and Song Qiming made it genuinely difficult to choose on the spot.","After pondering for a moment, Mu Hongyue replied in a gentle tone, \"The scores of the top five are often neck and neck. Who takes first place depends entirely on the chief examiner's thoughts and preferences. It doesn't mean the runners-up are any worse than the winner. The exam is already over, and you should look forward. The spring metropolitan exam is the truly difficult challenge.\"","He Feixuan cupped his hands in thanks. \"Thank you for your guidance, Dean. I will keep it in mind.\"","Mu Hongyue said nothing more, yet it seemed as if he had said everything.","He must have seen a paper better than his own. Otherwise, the Dean would have smilingly told him he had a chance at first place, rather than telling him not to mind the rankings.","While waiting for the results to be posted, Song Jinzhao began organizing the properties under her name.","The braised food shop, the vegetable shop that Song Jinzhao had bought and converted into an agricultural market after the season passed, the barbecue restaurant that had been open for four months, as well as the medical clinic, the farm estate outside the city, and the leased farmland—all needed designated managers. These had to be long-term arrangements.","The trip to the capital this time would not be short. Once these managers were confirmed, it was highly likely they would remain in Anyang forever. She had to think it over carefully.","Inside a highly sealed space within the examination hall, the inner-curtain grading officials had been staying up by candlelight for six whole days to mark the papers.","Out of more than five thousand exam papers, they had to select three hundred people. A passing paper required the joint review of at least four examiners before it could be placed in the approved pile to be presented to the chief examiner. Even those that were rejected had to be jointly reviewed by two officials before being completely eliminated.","Under the immense workload, they couldn't eat or sleep well. The dozens of officials all had bloodshot eyes.","After final deliberations, dozens of shortlisted papers were placed on the chief examiner's desk.","An inner-curtain official, rubbing his sleepy eyes, bowed his head and said, \"My Lord, we are somewhat unsure about these. We ask that you review them and decide whether to pass them or not.\"","The chief examiner tilted his chin up and rolled his stiff neck; one could almost hear the bones cracking.","When he read the final paper, he let out a soft exclamation of surprise, his expression turning much more serious.","It wasn't until he finished the entire paper that he smiled faintly and shook his head. The two inner-curtain officials standing before the desk noticed this and exchanged a silent glance. Would he pass it or not?","In terms of overall performance across the three exam sessions, this student was indeed still a bit short of passing. However, his insights on classics, history, and current affairs were incredibly unique and unconventional, completely different from the others. He seemed to be a pragmatist.","Yet, the poem he wrote made them unsure of his true nature. Was he simply a smooth operator, or did he hold genuine admiration? It was truly hard to say.","The main issue was that his writing was too direct. Once one person wrote the word to pass, the others had no choice but to give face. Otherwise, if the chief examiner found out, it would be easy to offend people. In the end, they had to present it up and let the man in charge make the decision himself.","The day before the results were posted, all the luggage had been loaded onto the carriages. One hundred and fifty catties of potatoes, placed in wooden crates lined with straw, were heavier than the combined luggage of Song Jinzhao and the other three.","In order to reach the capital before the Emperor's birthday, Song Jinzhao opted to travel light. Two people rode in the carriage with Song Anhao, while everyone else rode horses.","On the day the results were posted, the entrance to the examination hall was a sea of people. Anyone even slightly plump wouldn't be able to squeeze their way in.","Besides the students who took the provincial exam and their families, many commoners came to join the excitement. Some were even clamoring to snatch a son-in-law right there and then, having brought their daughters along, eager to grab a newly minted successful candidate to take home for marriage immediately."]},{"number":202,"title":"Chapter 202: Release of Results","paragraphs":["Half past the hour of Chen, the vermilion doors of the examination hall opened wide. The crowd instantly surged forward like a tide. The people standing at the very front strained their voices and shouted, \"Here they come! The results are being posted!\"","The crowd rubbed shoulders and bumped heels, squeezing together into a tight mass. Everyone was packed like sardines, and shouts rose and fell in succession.","Ten yamen runners wielding curved blades rushed out from the examination hall, struggling to hold the crowd back at a distance of five steps from the bottom of the stairs.","A moment later, a gray-haired Confucian scholar dressed in green robes slowly walked out of the examination hall, holding a yellow silk roster. His heavy footsteps beat against the hearts of the thousands of students, making them feel increasingly anxious.","All eyes were fixed unblinkingly on the scholar's hands. Even before the list was fully posted, the crowd began to push forward.","Song Qiming and Song Gaoli stood together. When the first name in the first row on the far right was revealed, both of them froze on the spot.","After briefly recovering his senses, Song Gaoli excitedly threw his arm around Song Qiming's shoulders and patted him incessantly. \"First place! Qiming, you are the Jieyuan!\"","Oh my god, his good brother was the Jieyuan. He wasn't dreaming, was he?","Song Qiming nodded in a daze, his eyes and ears going blank. In an instant, the bustling noise around him vanished without a trace, leaving only the sound of his heart pounding wildly in his chest.","Standing nearby, Lanxi immediately turned around and struggled to squeeze his way out, his whole body aching from being crushed in the crowd.","Four or five people away in the front row, He Feixuan stared at his name on the list, taking a deep breath and swallowing hard. Sure enough, he was the Yayuan; Song Qiming was ranked above him.","Hearing Song Gaoli's excited voice, Wang Xu turned his head to look, a flash of jealousy in his eyes. He had been in the Upper House for less than a year and had already surpassed everyone. He was still so young, yet he was the closing disciple of a third-rank imperial official. All the good things and halos had fallen onto one person's head; how could one not be envious and jealous?","The two, having snapped back to reality, began searching the yellow roster for Song Gaoli's name, scanning row by row and column by column from right to left, terrified of missing it.","The further back they looked, the more Song Gaoli's heart sank.","Under the eaves opposite the examination hall, Song Shixue stood on her tiptoes, looking for Song Qiming. \"Why hasn't brother come out yet? I'd better go in and take a look.\"","She had barely taken two steps forward when a disheveled Lanxi came running toward her.","Seeing him, Song Shixue stopped and immediately asked, \"How did it go?\"","Lanxi panted and replied, \"First place! The eldest young master is the Jieyuan.\" In just that short moment, he had almost been squeezed to suffocation.","Song Shixue's eyes widened in pleasant surprise. Looking utterly disbelieving, she turned to Song Jinzhao. \"Sister! Brother is the Jieyuan!\"","The corners of Song Jinzhao's lips curled up, and she gave a soft nod of acknowledgment.","A thirteen-year-old Juren was an absolute boy genius. In modern times, he would be a provincial top scorer, with Tsinghua and Peking University fighting over him.","With his results, becoming a Jinshi was practically set in stone. She didn't need to worry at all anymore.","On the other side, Song Qiming and Song Gaoli, still squeezed in the crowd, simultaneously widened their eyes and blinked furiously to see more clearly.","The two exchanged a glance, countless emotions flashing through their eyes. Song Gaoli seemed unable to digest this massive good news. His grin stretched from ear to ear as he suddenly jumped up and laughed heartily at the sky, \"I passed! I passed! I passed!!! Ahhhhh~~\"","His shrill screams hurt the eardrums of the crowd. One by one, they turned their heads to stare at the jumping and bouncing Song Gaoli. Had he gone mad?","Song Qiming watched his joyful appearance, his eyes curving into a smile. Last place in the prefectural exam, last place in the college exam, and now last place in the provincial exam. His level of excitement was even stronger than if he had placed first three times. He was simply the chosen one.","Song Gaoli's mood could not calm down for a long time. While everyone around watched him go crazy, someone suddenly grabbed the clothes on Song Qiming's shoulder. \"Has the Jieyuan Master been betrothed? My daughter is sixteen, right in the prime of her blooming beauty. Her dowry includes a thousand mu of fertile land, ten shops, and a three-courtyard mansion in the bustling market.\"","Bright, glittering eyeballs sat within the middle-aged man's wrinkled eye sockets. His posture, like a hungry wolf pouncing on a sheep, gave Song Qiming a fright.","The surrounding onlookers immediately began to clamor, their expressions filled with extreme envy.","This was Master Guo of the grain estate in the south of the city. He had no sons, only one daughter. Not only was she as beautiful as a celestial maiden, but her reputation for talent was also widely known. Marrying her was equivalent to obtaining the entire Guo family fortune.","Seeing that everyone's eyes were focused on him, Song Qiming quickly pulled Master Guo's hand away. \"I am still young and have no plans to take a wife for the time being.\"","Master Guo refused to let go, arguing, \"We can arrange the engagement first and marry in a couple of years.\"","Song Gaoli, whose excitement had been interrupted and cooled down, stepped between the two to separate them. \"Good sir, my brother is only thirteen, and your precious daughter is sixteen. In a couple of years, she'll be eighteen. It really is a bit inappropriate.\"","Master Guo's chest pressed against Song Gaoli's. \"What's inappropriate about it? A wife three years older brings a gold brick. The thirteen-year-old Jieyuan Master is absolutely perfect.\"","On the left, another wealthy master dressed in silk rushed out. \"Jieyuan Master, my daughter is twelve this year. Marrying in a couple of years would be absolutely perfect.\"","Song Qiming waved his hands repeatedly. \"Thank you all for your flattering attention, but I am still young and have no plans for engagement or marriage at the moment.\"","He forcefully pushed the crowd aside and squeezed his way out.","Song Gaoli was just about to follow closely behind when he was stopped. \"And what about this Juren Master? I see you are of the perfect age. Are you married?\"","Song Gaoli's face stiffened for a moment. He raised his hands and said, \"My family elders are not present, so I cannot make decisions regarding marriage. You two noble masters should look elsewhere.\"","The two quickly squeezed out of the crowd, running as if a bandit were chasing right behind them."]},{"number":203,"title":"Chapter 203: Song Gaoli Wants to Go to the Capital Together","paragraphs":["Seeing them come out, Song Shixue happily waved her arms. \"Brother, we are over here.\"","As they approached, the two did not look much better than Lan Xi; even their hair crowns were askew.","\"Congratulations, Brother, on placing first in the provincial exam! Did Brother Gaoli pass? What was his rank?\"","Song Gaoli grinned triumphantly and held up his pinky finger. \"Dead last, but I barely made it! Hahaha!\"","Song Jinzhao could not help but laugh. He really was a child of destiny; he always placed last, yet his luck was the best. Perhaps his future would be limitless.","\"Tomorrow, after attending the Luming Banquet, we will set off for the capital. First, we need to go back and get the gifts to visit each of our teachers' homes to show our gratitude.\"","Even though they were not hosting a formal appreciation banquet, the gifts could not be omitted, lest it cause hard feelings.","Song Jinzhao had prepared the items long ago and kept them at home, just waiting for the results to be posted to avoid being rushed for time.","Song Gaoli exclaimed in surprise, \"Leaving right after the Luming Banquet? So soon?\"","Song Qiming nodded. \"We head out early the morning after next. We are already prepared.\"","Song Gaoli's excitement slowly cooled as his thoughts fell into a state of anxious indecision.","Now that he had passed, should he go to the capital with Song Qiming and the others?","If he went with them, he would have to leave the day after tomorrow. If he did not, he would have to travel to the capital alone before the end of the year. The journey was long and treacherous, and the thought of it made him feel a bit panicked.","Seeing them about to board the carriage and leave, Song Gaoli gritted his teeth, stomped his foot, and made up his mind. \"Qiming, can I go to the capital with you?\"","He could go to the capital first to see the world, rent a house, and study behind closed doors for a few months. If he performed exceptionally well, he might even pass the metropolitan exam.","The spring examination was only held once every three years. Since he had decided to take it, he could not let the opportunity go to waste.","Song Qiming glanced at Song Jinzhao and then nodded in agreement. \"Of course you can. If you are not going back to the village, remember to write a letter home. This afternoon, Ah Jie will have someone deliver letters back to Songjia Village; you can bring your letter over to be sent together.\"","Song Gaoli nodded vigorously. \"I will write it as soon as I get back. Thank you, Sister Jinzhao.\"","Upon returning to the Song Mansion, the servants loaded all the gifts onto the carriage. Song Qiming took Lan Xi to the Mu Mansion first to express his gratitude. Any teacher who had taught him at the Anyang Academy could not be left out. Running from the east side of the city to the west, he drank more than a dozen cups of hot tea alone.","When Song Gaoli came over in the afternoon to deliver his letter, Song Jinzhao was also writing a letter to Old Man Song. Besides the letter, there was a chest of items to be taken back.","In this provincial examination, a total of three hundred people had passed, but only the top twenty were invited to attend the Luming Banquet.","The next day, just as Song Qiming reached the entrance of the examination hall, he ran into Mu Hongyue walking over. Impressively, right beside him was Song Gaoli, who had ranked dead last.","Song Gaoli's eyes lit up when he saw Song Qiming. Upon approaching, he naturally walked over to his side. \"Thank goodness you are here, otherwise I would really be a bit panicked.\"","Song Qiming lowered his voice and asked curiously, \"Why are you here?\"","Hu Fengye, who ranked twenty-third, had not been invited. Song Gaoli, at three hundredth place, should not be appearing here.","Mu Hongyue glanced at the two of them. To see the first place and the last place getting along so well was something he had never encountered before.","\"What are you doing just standing here? Hurry up and go inside. Most of the people should have arrived by now.\"","Song Gaoli answered as they walked, his brows furrowed in slight frustration.","\"I do not know what happened either. I was just packing my things when the academy head suddenly called me to attend the Luming Banquet. If I had known earlier, I could have gone to buy a new set of clothes. The outfit I am wearing was bought last year, and the color is already fading.\"","Everyone around them was wearing brand-new silk scholar robes, looking bright and glamorous, perfectly displaying the elegance of literati. He was the only one in a plain cotton robe, which made him feel quite embarrassed and ashamed, instinctively wanting to hide away from people."]},{"number":204,"title":"Chapter 204: The Deer-feasting Banquet","paragraphs":["Song Qiming looked Song Gaoli's clothes up and down. He couldn't see any fading; Song Gaoli took great care of what he wore, without even a single wrinkle.","\"It's fine, wearing cyan makes you look elegant. Just remember that you are a provincial graduate now, and that is enough.\"","Compared to their origins and family backgrounds, being able to pass the provincial examination and become a provincial graduate was already bringing honor to their ancestors and making them dragons among men. There was nothing to feel inferior about.","Back in Xining City, a provincial graduate would be treated with great respect by anyone who met him.","Song Gaoli didn't have much money right now. If he chose not to continue taking the exams and instead went back to open a private school as a teacher, he would become as wealthy as Provincial Graduate Wang in just a few years. There was absolutely no need to fret over a set of silk clothes.","Coming to Chongde Hall once again, compared to the apprehension he felt when attending the Hairpin Banquet, Song Qiming was now able to remain as calm as still water in the exact same place.","Half of the top twenty were acquaintances. Seven were classmates from Anyang Academy, and the other three Song Qiming had met at the Xiyuan Literary Gathering; they were all top scholars from other academies.","The remaining half had very unfamiliar faces. They were likely not from Anyang Prefecture and had rushed over from other prefectural cities specifically to participate in the provincial examination.","\"Is that this year's Jieyuan? Why does he look so young?\" The speaker wore a hair crown tied with a cyan silk ribbon that fluttered in the wind. Dressed in a cyan shirt, he looked very refined, giving off the feeling of a youthful literati.","The sixteenth-place scholar standing nearby lowered his voice and replied, \"A thirteen-year-old Jieyuan is naturally young. I heard he was also the Anshou of the Anyang Prefecture college examination last year.\"","The man in cyan widened his eyes in shock. \"He only passed the county examination to become a Xiucai a year ago?\"","The sixteenth-place scholar nodded. \"I heard Song Qiming comes from a peasant family. When he was young, his family was so poor that he could only eat until he was half full. He only started studying at the age of eleven, and in less than three years, he has already become a provincial graduate. He is truly a heaven-sent genius with a boundless future!\"","Wang Xu, who was passing by, caught a earful of this. He paused his steps slightly and glanced at the two of them.","What heaven-sent genius? If it weren't for Lord Ye giving him special daily guidance, Song Qiming would never have been able to win first place as the Jieyuan.","It was a pity for He Feixuan. He had been first every time for the past three years, but right at the very end, someone took advantage of a loophole. It was just too unlucky.","Dozens of tables were arranged in a U-shape on three sides, divided equally between students and examiners. Sitting in the very center was Duan Yanhua, the chief examiner of this Longbei Province provincial examination.","\"Student Song Qiming pays his respects to the esteemed teachers.\"","\"Student Song Gaoli pays his respects to the esteemed teachers.\"","All the examiners present held official positions in the imperial court, but here they were uniformly addressed as mister or teacher, even the chief examiner Duan Yanhua.","The Luming Banquet was not just a feast; it was more of a starting point for building social networks and political factions.","Although all the examiners came from the imperial court, almost all of them originated from Longbei. The official careers of the twenty newly minted provincial graduates present would largely depend on their promotion and care.","Although with Ye Liangyu around, Song Qiming did not lack patronage, no one would ever complain about having too many connections. It was hard to guarantee they wouldn't come in handy one day.","The moment he stood up, Song Qiming astutely noticed that the chief examiner Duan Yanhua's attention lingered on Song Gaoli for a long time.","Thinking of the poem Song Gaoli had written during the provincial examination, and the fact that the academy headmaster had called him to attend the Luming Banquet, could it be related to Duan Yanhua?","If he disliked Song Gaoli and called him over just to teach him a lesson, there would have been no need to let him barely pass the provincial examination; failing him outright would have sufficed.","As it stood now, the only possibility was that Song Gaoli's poem had pleased him. Duan Yanhua was very satisfied with him and looked upon him favorably. This was a great opportunity.","After exchanging a few pleasantries, they were about to take their seats. Their assigned seats were quite far apart. Before separating, Song Qiming pulled Song Gaoli close and whispered in his ear.","\"After you sit down, look at Duan Yanhua a few more times. Remember, you revere him greatly. Your eyes must show excitement, joy, and adoration, but do not overdo it, or it will backfire.\"","Their eyes met. Song Gaoli's pupils darkened slightly, and he gave a quiet, inconspicuous hum of agreement.","After sitting down, he glanced at Duan Yanhua several times, and finally, their eyes met.","At the first moment of eye contact, Song Gaoli instantly lowered his gaze to avoid it. Then, pretending to have mustered up his courage, he raised his head to meet the examiner's eyes again. His gaze was three parts joyful, three parts excited, and four parts adoring, as if it were about to melt into water.","Duan Yanhua smiled faintly, shifted his gaze away, and continued speaking with the others.","Song Gaoli slowly exhaled. Did this mean he succeeded?"]},{"number":205,"title":"Chapter 205: Song Gaoli Becomes a Disciple of Duan Yanhua","paragraphs":["As the welcoming melody of the Deer Call poem echoed through the hall, the triennial Luming Banquet officially commenced. The twenty newly minted provincial graduates present were the most promising candidates to pass the metropolitan exam. This banquet served as a signal of their entry into officialdom. Especially for those from ordinary backgrounds, it could very well alter the course of their entire lives.","Amidst the clinking of glasses, everyone gathered in joyous celebration. The examiners congratulated the new graduates on their success, encouraging them to continue their diligent studies to ace the upcoming spring exams and serve the country in the future.","Adorned with golden silk flowers on their hair crowns, Song Qiming and the other nineteen graduates bowed in gratitude to the twenty examiners. Standing in the corner, Song Gaoli looked at the golden flowers on everyone's crowns, feeling a sense of emptiness in his heart.","He was leaps and bounds behind these people. The spring metropolitan exam selected only one in ten thousand—could he really pass it?","Catching Duan Yanhua's gaze from the corner of his eye, Song Gaoli quickly masked his disappointment, puffed out his chest, and nodded respectfully in greeting.","Following the flower-pinning and bowing ceremonies, musicians and dancers slowly made their way to the center of the tables. After five performances, the grand finale of the Luming Banquet began.","The examiners presented the prompts, and the twenty graduates began to compose impromptu poetry to showcase their talents. All eyes zeroed in on Song Qiming, attempting to outshine the thirteen-year-old Jieyuan, the top scorer. It was as if surpassing him would prove their brilliance was greater than the very best.","The scholars from Anyang Prefecture had already witnessed Song Qiming's abilities at previous literary gatherings, but the ten scholars from outer prefectures knew little about this young top scorer. Seeing his young age, they were quite unconvinced. After answering their prompts, each of them threw a few provocative remarks his way.","Holding his wine cup, Duan Yanhua let his gaze fall on Song Gaoli, who looked even more anxious than Song Qiming himself. A knowing smile graced Duan Yanhua's lips.","Barely half an hour later, whether it was poetry or couplets, no one had managed to outdo Song Qiming. Instead, they only cemented his title as the top scorer, proving it was entirely well-deserved.","During the intermission, Duan Yanhua stood up and walked out of the Chongde Hall. Mu Hongyue was just about to shoot a look at Song Gaoli to follow him, only to find that before he could even open his mouth, the kid had already trailed after him.","He couldn't help but lower his head and chuckle; the boy was sharper than he had imagined.","When he first received the news, Mu Hongyue couldn't fathom why Duan Yanhua would take an interest in Song Gaoli. He was the last-place passer; logically, an examiner wouldn't even remember his name, let alone specifically request him to be brought to the Luming Banquet. It was simply bizarre.","It was only upon asking on their way here that he learned the kid had played a clever trick in his examination poetry, utterly flattering the chief examiner. That was likely when the seed of opportunity was planted.","Duan Yanhua was a compiler in the Hanlin Academy, working under Fei Yanzhang. If Song Gaoli could secure this connection, it would mean standing alongside Song Qiming when he eventually entered the imperial court. This was by no means a bad thing for him.","Song Gaoli only hurried back as the Luming Banquet was nearing its end. No matter how well he tried to suppress the joy hidden between his brows, Song Qiming, who knew him well, saw right through it.","His gaze drifted over the faces of Song Gaoli and Duan Yanhua, and a happy smile tugged at the corners of his lips.","On the way home after the banquet, Song Gaoli couldn't wait to climb into Song Qiming's carriage. His brows were raised in sheer delight. Guess what Teacher Duan said?","Song Qiming raised an eyebrow in thought. Teacher Duan—that sounded quite intimate. He took you in as a student?","Song Gaoli's eyes widened. How did you know?","Song Qiming parted his lips in a smile, his eyes holding a trace of surprise alongside his happiness. He really took you as a student? What exactly did he say?","Song Gaoli leaned back against the carriage wall, looking upwards as he recalled. The smile on his face was like a blooming sunflower, radiant yet slightly goofy.","He said that although I am not a top-tier genius, he felt a strong sense of destiny with me. Teacher Duan was also the very last to pass his metropolitan exam back in the day, and I passed both the college and provincial exams in last place. He said our master-disciple relationship is the will of heaven, a red thread tied by God himself.","The more Song Qiming listened, the more mystical it sounded. Why did it feel like someone was being swindled?","Song Gaoli held up a finger. Oh, right! He knows we are setting off for the capital tomorrow and wants to travel with us.","Song Qiming blinked. Did you tell him we will be rushing the journey and it might not be very comfortable?","Song Gaoli nodded vigorously. I did, but Teacher said he is in a hurry to return to the capital and needs to rush too, so it is perfectly on the way.","Spending day and night together on the road makes it easier to build a bond. I can use this opportunity to perform well and leave a deeper impression as a good student.","Song Qiming swallowed hesitantly. He couldn't shake the feeling that this was all going a bit too smoothly. Could there be something off about this Duan Yanhua?"]},{"number":206,"title":"Chapter 206: Departing for the Capital","paragraphs":["After returning, Song Qiming told Song Jinzhao about the matter. How much do you know about Duan Yanhua?","Song Qiming sat down and explained in detail, Just his past achievements, essays, and poems. Originally, it was just to let Gaoli gain a clever advantage. I didn't expect it to turn out like this.","Song Jinzhao stopped her fingers, which had been repeatedly tapping on the table. Can the person who placed last in the metropolitan examination enter the Imperial Academy?","Song Qiming froze for a moment, then shook his head and replied, He shouldn't be able to. With that result, he could only go to a remote area to be a county magistrate.","Yet Duan Yanhua had entered the Imperial Academy, which was a bit strange.","Song Jinzhao continued asking, How old is he this year?","Song Qiming: Fifty-six.","Raising the corner of her eye, she asked, When did he pass the examination to become a tribute student?","Song Qiming recalled the information he had gathered earlier. At thirty-seven.","Song Jinzhao said, That means he has stayed in the position of a compiler at the Imperial Academy for nineteen years without a promotion. This implies that the person who patronized him and stuffed him into the Imperial Academy made no further moves afterward. And he himself lacked the ability to climb higher.","Song Qiming moved his lips, nodding in contemplation. His past achievements are indeed not very outstanding. They can be considered quite average.","When he suggested that Song Gaoli praise Duan Yanhua, he had put in a lot of effort. It was like picking meat scraps from chicken bones, trying his best to exaggerate the merits.","Early the next morning, before the sun had even risen, Song Gaoli arrived at Song Jinzhao's house at the agreed time, carrying two large bundles on his back.","Chunxing and Fushun stood at the door with disappointed faces. Eldest Miss, please rest assured. In half a year, we will definitely be able to train our successors.","Seeing that their employer was about to achieve great success, they also wanted to follow her to the capital. However, the business in Anyang Prefecture could not be left without supervision, so they could only wait until the newcomers were completely familiar with the work before leaving.","If the Eldest Young Master could pass the imperial examination and become a presented scholar, he would definitely return next March, and they could all leave together then.","Song Jinzhao gave a slight nod. She looked up at the Song Manor's plaque, her eyes deep and distant.","Having been here for just over a year, she was leaving again. What would the road ahead be like? Would it bring fortune or disaster? In this feudal era where imperial power was supreme, even as a woman, she was determined to forge her own path.","She swung herself onto her horse. Her skirt fluttered between heaven and earth, elegant and unrestrained, exuding an aura no less impressive than that of a man.","Four people rode on horseback, flanking the carriage in the middle. Song Gaoli, sitting inside the carriage, looked at Song Jinzhao leading the way. He lifted the window curtains to look left and right. Even three-year-old Song Anhao was being held by Song Shixue on horseback. Inside the carriage, besides himself, there was only Lanxi driving, and Xuetuan sleeping in its cage.","Whenever he lifted the curtain, he would meet the slightly adorable and dazed eyes of the tiger. If they stared at each other for too long, the adorable look would turn fierce, and the low roars rumbling from its throat terrified him into quickly dropping the curtain.","When it was little, it was as cute as a kitten, but growing up, it really became quite fierce.","Even a king of the forest with a defective brain was still the king of the forest. When enraged, it would definitely eat people.","When they reached the city gates, a carriage had already been waiting for a long time.","Master, they are here, the carriage driver turned his head and said into the cabin.","Duan Yanhua emerged from the carriage. His gaze fell upon the woman riding the tall, majestic horse, and a smile appeared on his face. He figured this must be Lady Linghui.","As they approached, Duan Yanhua cupped his hands and bowed. Greetings, Lady Linghui.","Song Jinzhao dismounted and gave a slight nod in response. Lord Duan, there is no need for such formality.","Song Qiming bowed to Duan Yanhua in greeting. This student pays his respects to Lord Duan. Standing behind him, Song Shixue silently curtsied.","The slightly stagnant atmosphere was broken by Song Gaoli calling out, Teacher! He jumped down from the carriage and ran over to Duan Yanhua, his smile so enthusiastic that several of his front teeth were showing.","Duan Yanhua's gaze swept over Xuetuan. Why did they bring a tiger along? Weren't they afraid?","Song Jinzhao spoke up, It is getting late. We should set off quickly so we don't end up sleeping in the wilderness.","If they left now and did not delay on the road, they could make it to the next city to rest before dark.","As they departed, Song Gaoli had already boarded Duan Yanhua's carriage. Their group was not large. Besides the driver, there were only two guards on horseback, who looked like they knew some martial arts."]},{"number":207,"title":"Chapter 207: Constantly on the Journey, the Letter Arrives at Songjia Village","paragraphs":["After leaving the city and reaching a deserted stretch of the road, Song Shixue let Xuetuan out of its cage.","\"Sister, the leash.\" She handed the rope to Song Jinzhao to hold. Only her older sister had the strength to subdue Xuetuan, ensuring that no one else would be in danger.","Sitting in the carriage, Duan Yanhua's eyes darted around for a long time before he turned to Song Gaoli and asked aloud, \"Where did they get this white tiger?\"","Song Gaoli glanced at Xuetuan's wagging tail. \"Sister Jinzhao found it when she took Qiming and the others hunting in the mountains. They've raised it since it was born, so it's very obedient.\"","Duan Yanhua continued to press, \"Do all three of the Song siblings know martial arts?\"","Song Gaoli nodded, praising them highly. \"Yes, Qiming and Shixue's martial arts were both taught by Sister Jinzhao. Her kung fu is incredibly impressive; there's no one she can't defeat.\"","After saying this, a thought crossed his mind. The journey from Anyang Prefecture to the capital would take nearly two months. Perhaps he could ask Qiming to teach him how to ride a horse, so he could ride his own once he bought one in the future.","Duan Yanhua had originally intended to chat more with the Song siblings on the road, but they traveled at a breakneck pace without resting in between. The bumps made his old bones crack and rattle, leaving him with a sore back and a numb body by the end of the day.","By the time they rushed into the city before dark, he was so exhausted he could barely keep his eyes open. He hastily ate a meal and fell straight to sleep. The next day, they got up early again to set off, and spent the night in a ruined temple. After enduring this for three days, Duan Yanhua felt as though he had suddenly aged several years. Half his soul seemed to have left his body, leaving him in a constant daze.","\"Lady, the capital is far away, but there is no need to rush like this. If we take our time, we can reach it in three months and even enjoy the sights along the way.\"","Song Jinzhao's hand, which was picking up food with her chopsticks, paused slightly. Three months? It would be too late by then.","Song Qiming calmly took over the conversation. \"To be honest with you, Lord Duan, Mr. Ye hopes I can reach the capital as soon as possible so he can keep me by his side and tutor me. That way, I can achieve a good rank in next year's spring examinations.\"","Duan Yanhua's beard twitched, a bitter feeling rising in his throat. As a top provincial scorer, passing the metropolitan exam to become a Jinshi was already a sure thing. He was only thirteen; was it really necessary to work this hard?","\"It's a good thing that Lord Ye has high hopes for you, but it's just too exhausting.\"","Song Qiming smiled and shook his head. \"Compared to working in the fields under the wind and sun, studying really isn't hard work at all. Whenever I pick up a book, I actually find it quite enjoyable.\"","Duan Yanhua let out a few awkward chuckles, lowering his head as he recalled his own youth spent studying.","In the dead of winter, his hands had been covered in chilblains. Enjoyable? Only the moment he passed the exam was enjoyable; everything else was pure misery.","Song Gaoli had attended to Duan Yanhua for several days. During the latter few days, the older man did nothing but sleep. Unable to sit still, Gaoli went to find Song Qiming to ask him to teach him how to ride a horse.","Every time Duan Yanhua opened his eyes and heard the laughter outside, he would shake his head and lament that he was getting old.","Burying his head in the bedding, he wondered how these youths could have so much energy. Weren't they tired?","The clip-clop of horse hooves echoed across the fields, growing ever more distinct as they entered the village.","Song Mancang, who had been counting the days, sat at his doorway whenever he had free time these past few days. He didn't know the results of the provincial exams yet. Even if they failed, they should at least send a letter to let him know.","Hearing the sound of hooves, he instantly stood up, craning his neck to look ahead until he saw a man from the escort agency riding over.","\"Old man, where is Song Gaoli's house?\" the messenger asked, pulling tight on the reins to stop.","Song Mancang's eyes lit up. He broke into a wide grin and said, \"I'm Song Gaoli's grandfather. Did my grandson send a letter back?\"","Hearing this, the rider swiftly pulled a letter from his breast pocket and handed it to Song Mancang. \"Here you go, just brought back from Anyang Prefecture. Old man, let me ask you, where is Song Youshui's house?\"","Song Mancang, who was about to open the letter, paused and pointed toward the inside of the village. \"See that? That blue-brick and tile house furthest inside is the one.\"","It seemed that Song Jinzhao's and Gaoli's letters were delivered together. He wondered how Song Qiming had done on the exam.","At this thought, Song Mancang impatiently tore open the letter to find out the results. Even though the chances were slim, you never knew.","The escort leader hadn't ridden far when an earth-shattering scream suddenly erupted behind him. He hurriedly pulled the reins to steady his startled horse.","Looking back, he saw the old man who had just received the letter jumping up and down in place, roaring at the sky as if he had gone mad.","What was going on?","Hearing the shouts, Song Dazhuang's family all ran out of the house. They saw Song Mancang screaming incessantly at the door, his face flushed bright red.","\"Father, what's wrong with you?\" Could he have caught mad cow disease?","Master Zhao's plowing ox had suffered a bout of pinkeye these past few days. Could he have been bitten?","Song Mancang rushed over holding the letter, waving it at them, his face wrinkled with a massive smile. \"Gaoli passed the exam and became a Juren! Gaoli is a Juren!\"","Repeating it twice still didn't feel like enough, so he simply unfolded the letter and pointed at the words, letting Song Dazhuang see for himself.","\"A Juren! This is a Juren! Gaoli is truly promising; he passed on his very first try.\"","Faced with Song Mancang's frantic ecstasy, Song Dazhuang and the others still hadn't quite processed the news.","Song Gaoli's mother eagerly slapped Song Dazhuang's arm. \"Husband, read it to me quickly, read it!\""]},{"number":208,"title":"Chapter 208: Your son Qiming has achieved the top score in the provincial examination.","paragraphs":["When the head of the escort agency delivered the letter to Song Jinzhao's house, Old Man Song was in the courtyard chopping wood.","Fearing that the house would easily fall into disrepair if left unoccupied for too long, Old Man Song and Old Lady Song had simply moved in back in June, rather than having to thoroughly clean the whole place top to bottom every few days.","Carrying a chest, the escort leader stood at the door and called out, \"Is Song Youshui home?\"","Old Man Song looked up and stood. \"That's me. What's the matter?\"","The escort leader set the chest down on the stone table. \"These are the things your granddaughter asked me to bring back from Anyang Prefecture, along with this letter.\"","Old Man Song opened the chest and took a look, finding several sets of new clothes inside—both thin and thick—as well as several pairs of new shoes.","Hearing the voices, Old Lady Song walked out of the kitchen. Seeing the items in the chest, her eyes filled with smiles.","\"Last year's clothes are still perfectly fine. Why did this girl buy so much again?\"","Old Man Song couldn't read. He opened the letter but couldn't understand it. Over the past few days, the village chief had repeatedly mentioned the provincial exams. Could it be that Qiming had passed and become a Juren?","Seeing his brows furrowed so tightly they could crush a fly, Old Lady Song spoke up, \"Don't tear the letter. We'll know what it says when Yongnian and the others get back.\"","Old Man Song folded the letter, clutched it in his hand, and walked out. \"I can't wait. I'm going to find the village chief right now.\"","Second Song and his wife, their trouser legs covered in mud, bumped into him head-on, their faces carrying a trace of urgency.","\"Father, I saw the people from the escort agency coming over. Did Jinzhao send things back?\"","The couple had just returned from the fields and happened to run into the escort leader leaving on horseback. Few families in the village had connections with escort agency caravans. They stopped him to ask, and sure enough, it was related to Song Jinzhao.","Seeing the large wooden chest sitting on the stone table, Second Aunt Song leaned her head over to take a look.","My goodness, it was full of new clothes and new shoes. The sleeves even had embroidery, though the colors looked quite old-fashioned.","Pleasantly surprised, she looked up and asked Old Lady Song, \"Mother, did Jinzhao send someone to bring all these back?\"","Seeing that their attention was entirely on the chest, Old Man Song sighed and closed the lid. \"These are all things Jinzhao sent for me and your mother.\"","With a signaling glance, Old Lady Song moved the chest into the room and then locked all the doors.","Seeing them locking the doors, Second Song thought the two elders were guarding against him and said in dissatisfaction, \"Why lock the doors? Now there won't be any airflow.\"","Old Man Song pinched the letter and explained, \"Yongnian and Yaozu aren't home. Your mother and I are going to the village chief's house to have your Uncle Mancang see what's written in the letter.\"","Second Song: \"You can wait for Yaozu to come back to read it.\"","Old Lady Song shot him a glance. \"It's only noon. Your father can't wait.\"","The couple exchanged a look. They also wanted to know what was written in the letter, so they followed along.","Passing by the old house, they picked up another person. Elder Aunt Song had to look after the children and couldn't come out, so Oldest Song tagged along to the village chief's house.","When the five of them reached the door, they found quite a few people standing in the courtyard. Aside from Song Mancang's family, the neighbors from both sides were surprisingly all there.","\"What's going on? Why is everyone so happy?\" Old Man Song asked in confusion.","Song Mancang, his hair disheveled, rushed up and threw his arms around Old Man Song. \"Brother, my Gaoli also passed the exam and became a Juren! Our village suddenly has two Juren masters. Smoke is rising from our ancestral graves; it must be a blessing from the ancestors!\"","Old Man Song, having been sprayed with spit, pushed Song Mancang away. His eyes carried a trace of uncertainty. \"My Qiming passed and became a Juren?\"","Song Mancang froze. \"You didn't know? My Gaoli said he's going to the capital with Jinzhao and the others. Your Qiming definitely passed too.\"","The gazes of the other two families in the courtyard instantly focused on Old Man Song and his group.","More than one Juren master? Song Qiming passed as well?","Old Man Song blankly held up the letter. \"I didn't know yet. Village Chief, help me read what's written in this letter.\"","Song Mancang didn't hesitate at all. He quickly took the letter and began to read.","\"Grandfather, Qiming performed exceptionally well in the provincial exam and successfully achieved the title of Jieyuan. The spring exams are approaching, so we will set off for the capital in a few days. I'm afraid we won't be able to return home until the spring exams end next year. Inside the chest are gifts bought for you and Grandmother, and as for the rent for this year's autumn harvest, there is no need to...\"","It took quite a while to read the letter, as Song Jinzhao had mentioned several things at once. Everyone in the courtyard heard it loud and clear. Song Mancang's hands started trembling from the very first sentence, and his voice sounded a bit breathless.","After finishing the letter, he stood motionless for a long time, until Old Man Song gave him a nudge.","\"Village Chief, what is a Jieyuan?\"","Song Mancang turned his stiff neck. He reached out, gripped Old Man Song's shoulders, and replied, \"Jieyuan is the first place in the provincial exams. Brother, your Qiming is incredible.\"","To think it was first place! Gaoli had said he passed in last place, so he never expected Song Qiming to be first. With this result, he would definitely be able to pass the spring exams next year and become a Jinshi.","Old Man Song's lineage was truly going to strike it rich and rise to prominence. Their Song Village was about to produce a government official."]},{"number":209,"title":"Chapter 209: Longing and Regret: The Second Wife","paragraphs":["It felt as if a bolt of lightning had struck right above the heads of Oldest Song and Second Song and his wife. A blinding light exploded before their eyes, making it impossible to open them.","A Juren! He really passed the provincial exam to become a Juren! And so quickly, taking first place no less—they couldn't even dare to imagine it.","Was it really that easy to pass the provincial exam? Their own son hadn't even managed to pass the entry-level exams, yet their nephew was already a Juren!","Old Man Song's legs gave out, causing him to stumble back two steps. His right hand hurriedly grabbed Old Lady Song's arm to steady himself, his clouded eyes bursting with a dazzling light.","He took a couple of deep breaths to calm himself, raised his head, and asked, his voice panting slightly, \"He went to the capital?\"","The village chief nodded. \"Yes, my Gaoli went along with him. They said they needed to leave enough time to prepare for the spring imperial examination and would return after it's over. By now, they've probably been on the road for six or seven days.\"","Old Man Song clutched the letter tightly as he returned home. He slumped heavily into a chair, still not entirely recovered from the shock.","Second Song crossed his arms and complained, \"Such a huge matter and Qiming didn't even come back for a visit. It wouldn't have been too late to wait another two months before heading to the capital.\"","Second Aunt Song pursed her lips, feeling exceptionally dissatisfied in her heart.","He had already passed the provincial exam, yet he only sent back such a meager amount of things. Aside from the two elders, the rest of them, his aunts and uncles, got absolutely nothing. He clearly had no respect for them at all. It was simply too much.","Old Man Song looked up, glaring sharply at Second Song. \"What if he freezes and ruins his health traveling to the capital in the dead of winter? The spring exam is in February. It's better to go early to avoid falling ill from the change in climate, and it gives him more time to study.\"","Sitting to the side, Old Lady Song nodded in agreement. \"That's right, a round trip would take more than half a month. The exam is much more important.\"","\"Old man, we should tell Third Song such wonderful news. I'll go get the paper money.\"","Old Man Song clenched his fists, nodding as he stood up. \"Yes, we must tell Third Song. We'll go right now.\"","Watching his parents busy themselves, Oldest Song prepared to head home to call Elder Aunt Song to go with them.","On the way back, thinking of Song Yongnian who was still studying at the private school, he felt an empty void in his heart. It felt as though there was a vast distance between them, something he could never quite reach or grasp, leaving him feeling unsettled.","In front of the graves at the foot of the mountain, looking out at the mounds scattered in the distance, only the tombstone of Third Song and his wife was made of high-quality bluestone. Even the area right in front of the tombstone was paved with stone bricks, covering a large space.","Old Man Song squatted in front of the tombstone, pouring wine into a cup. \"Third Song, Qiming has become a Juren. When he becomes a high-ranking official in the future, you'll be the father of a nobleman. Our Song family finally has a worthy successor.\"","The flames in the clay basin burned higher and higher. The yellow firelight danced in the wind, as if someone had truly come to visit.","Lying in bed that night, Second Aunt Song couldn't fall asleep no matter what.","She opened her eyes, rolled over, and said to Second Song, \"Jinzhao said in her letter that the silver from selling this year's village rent doesn't need to be sent to Anyang Prefecture anymore. She told your parents to keep it for themselves. What do you think about that?\"","After Old Man Song forcefully took back the land rented by the second branch last year, the fourteen acres belonging to the third branch were now rented out, half to the eldest branch and half to Tudan's family. It was almost time to harvest the rice. Based on this year's yield, there would be at least seven or eight taels of silver.","Second Song opened his eyes and turned his head away. \"What can we do? Even if we wanted it, Father wouldn't give it to us. He's getting more and more impatient with me. Even if he gave it to Big Brother, he wouldn't give it to me.\"","Second Aunt Song kicked Second Song in the calf. \"Why are you so useless? What do your parents need so much money for at their age? Jinzhao buys everything for them anyway. That money should be spent on the younger generation. Think of a way! If the eldest branch asks for it first, you won't even have a place to cry.\"","\"I'm even worried that Father won't collect Big Brother's rent this year. Half of it saved up is worth several taels of silver.\"","Second Song sat up instantly. The moonlight shone on his face, his expression somewhat dark and heavy.","\"You're right. Before, when the silver from the sold grain had to be given to Jinzhao, Big Brother had no choice but to pay. Now that it's all being left for Father and Mother, if he doesn't want to give it to them, they definitely won't force him. We're losing out big time.\"","Second Aunt Song sat up too. \"And I'm worried it won't just be this year. Maybe Jinzhao won't even want the rent for those fourteen acres in the future. She's a Township Princess now, her business in the city is so big, and Qiming just became a Juren. She definitely doesn't care about this little bit of money anymore.\"","Thinking of this, Second Aunt Song began to sigh again. \"The third branch has struck it rich. Who knows how wonderful their lives will be from now on. Meanwhile, we elders still have to work in the fields. Just a little bit leaking through their fingers would be enough for us to enjoy a life of ease.\"","\"If we had known, we should have taken those children in to raise right after the third brother and his wife died. Then things wouldn't have turned out like this.\"","Second Song lay back down on his pillow. \"Agreeing to adopt her to bring good luck wasn't my idea alone. Who knew Jinzhao would be so capable? Not only can she make money, but she also supported Qiming through his studies. It's too late to dwell on the past now!\"","Even though Song Qiming and Song Gaoli hadn't returned, Old Man Song and Song Mancang still hosted a banquet at home while the news was hot. They were determined to let all their relatives and friends know that their grandsons were now esteemed Juren.","They even opened the village ancestral hall. As the elders, Song Mancang and Old Man Song entered the inner hall to offer sacrifices to the ancestors on behalf of Song Gaoli and Song Qiming.","For nearly half a month, the entire Song Family Village gossiped about Song Qiming and Song Gaoli passing the provincial exam, constantly discussing whether they would be able to pass the metropolitan exam and become high-ranking officials."]},{"number":210,"title":"Chapter 210: Arriving in the Capital","paragraphs":["The road to the capital was rugged and long. Even Song Anhao, who was always energetic and curious about everything, began to feel bored.","In the swaying carriage, Duan Yanhua lay half-squinting on the bedding spread across the floorboards, his head so dizzy and heavy that he hardly knew which way was up.","Every day, they traveled as soon as they opened their eyes and slept as soon as they closed them. Although he hadn't done anything, he felt extremely tired, especially in his head, which felt terribly swollen.","Song Gaoli lifted the carriage curtain and leaned half his body inside. Teacher, Yuncheng is just ahead. Sister Jinzhao said we will go into the city this afternoon to buy some things, and we will spend the night there.","Duan Yanhua opened his crusty eyes, lifted the window curtain, and took a look outside. The sun was high; they could enter the city for lunch.","Good, good, good. We will spend the night in Yuncheng. After traveling for more than half a month, they could finally rest for a day.","After entering the city, they quickly found an inn to eat and book rooms. After resting for a while, Song Jinzhao took Song Qiming and the others out to the streets to shop in the afternoon.","Having lain in the carriage for the better part of a month, Duan Yanhua did not want to stay at the inn. He offered to go with Song Jinzhao and the others. As a result, he was not interested in any of the places they visited. After walking for less than half an hour, he took his servants to a teahouse to listen to storytelling instead.","Song Gaoli muttered beside Song Qiming, I feel like my teacher is a bit idle, very different from Lord Ye.","Shouldn't an official always stand straight and hold a book, just like Mr. Ye? Even when his legs were crippled and he couldn't stand, his upper body was perfectly straight.","He never let a book leave his hands, and his entire demeanor clearly marked him as a great scholar—someone to be admired from afar but not treated lightly.","As for his own teacher, what he saw most over the past half month was him lying down, just like the second granduncle in the village. After a while, it was truly hard to watch.","Song Qiming laughed. You can just say he's a bit lazy. Lord Duan is over fifty years old; it's normal for his energy to fall behind during long journeys.","He hadn't been promoted in twenty years. Even the person in last place should have moved up a bit by now. It was easy to imagine that he probably wasn't very diligent.","Song Gaoli sighed. His excitement over successfully acknowledging a master was no longer as strong as it had been at the beginning. He originally thought he would be carefully guided by his teacher just like Song Qiming, but now it seemed the difference was unusually large.","On a densely wooded mountain path, Duan Yanhua tightly gripped the carriage curtain, his eyes peering through the gap to observe the situation outside.","White blades went in and red blades came out. Blood sprayed onto the ground, an eerie shade of red.","The Lingyun spear in Song Jinzhao's hands instantly pierced through the chests of two people, skewering them like lamb kebabs. With a flick of her wrist, the two corpses smashed onto the ground, both dying with their eyes wide open. Their dilated pupils gave Duan Yanhua a fright.","He knew the three Song siblings knew martial arts, but seeing them kill people with his own eyes was another matter entirely. It was like chopping tofu, except this was human flesh.","Song Gaoli put away his unused crossbow and walked over to Duan Yanhua's carriage. Before the bandits could even rush over, they had been swiftly dealt with by Sister Jinzhao and the others. Not only him, but even Duan Yanhua's two guards had been of no use.","Teacher, the bandits have been dealt with. You weren't frightened, were you?","Duan Yanhua coughed twice. I have seen plenty of such things. How could I be frightened? Since it's resolved, let's hurry up and continue our journey. Who knew if there were still accomplices? They absolutely must not be caught up to.","More than a month later...","Looking at the towering city walls, the two characters for the Capital on the city gate seemed to be inlaid with silver edges, exuding a regal dominance and solemnity.","Duan Yanhua climbed out of the carriage clutching his neck, took a deep breath, and sighed with emotion, We have finally arrived.","For the next three years, he absolutely did not want to be the chief examiner again. The long trek was simply too grueling; his bones were about to fall apart.","He turned his head to look at Song Jinzhao. If Lady Linghui does not mind, you may stay at my humble residence during your time in the capital.","Song Qiming cupped his hands and said, Thank you for your kindness, Lord Duan. I already wrote a letter to my teacher before setting off. He has likely already found a place for us to stay, so we will not impose on you.","Duan Yanhua nodded. If that is the case, we shall gather another day. Gaoli, you have no place to stay in the capital, so come back to the manor with me.","It will also be convenient to supervise your studies every day.","Song Gaoli looked hesitant. Although they had spent nearly two months together on the road, he felt his relationship with Duan Yanhua was still a bit distant. Moving into the other party's home so rashly seemed somewhat inappropriate.","Seeing that he didn't respond, Duan Yanhua urged, Living in the manor, I can guide you every day. You also have several senior martial brothers there, so you can learn from one another.","Since things had reached this point, refusing again would only alienate them further.","Song Gaoli nodded and agreed, Thank you, Teacher. Then I shall impose on you."]},{"number":211,"title":"Chapter 211: Staying at the Ye Residence","paragraphs":["At a tea stall in the city, a man dressed in a dark red short tunic kept his eyes fixed on the city gate. Whenever he saw a familiar-looking young man, he would unroll a portrait to check, and upon realizing it was not the right person, he would sit back down to continue drinking his tea. He had been waiting for days; why had they not arrived yet?","Passing through the city gate, a cacophony of bustling noise rushed forth. At a glance, the streets were packed with people, its prosperity far surpassing all the cities they had passed through along the way.","The man at the tea stall suddenly stood up, unrolling the portrait in his hands to compare carefully.","This was it. An exact match.","He rushed over to Song Qiming's horse and stopped, bowing deeply and raising his voice to greet him, \"Are you Young Master Song Qiming?\"","Song Qiming stopped and asked, \"And you are?\"","The man's eyes lit up, and he replied with a flattering smile, \"I am a servant from the Ye Residence. I was ordered to wait here for Young Master Song and the Lady. I have been looking forward to your arrival for days, and finally, you are here.\"","Duan Yanhua, sitting in the carriage, saw the Ye Residence's servant receiving them at the city gate after waiting for days. It seemed Song Qiming was truly highly regarded by Ye Liangyu.","Under the man's guidance, Song Jinzhao and her family were led to the entrance of the Ye Residence.","The unadorned main gate exuded a sense of rustic simplicity. The plaque engraved with the words 'Ye Residence' featured simple pine needle patterns. Except for its size, it was almost identical to the Ye estate in Anyang Prefecture.","The man quickly rushed to the door and told the porter, \"Hurry and tell the butler that Young Master Song and his party have arrived.\"","Just as Song Anhao's feet touched the ground, Yunhe ran out from the estate. His eyes practically sparkled when he saw Song Qiming.","He gestured for them to walk inside. \"Lady Linghui, Young Master Song, please come in. The master has long prepared the guest rooms and has just been waiting for your arrival.\"","The group was welcomed into the Ye Residence. The servants responsible for moving the luggage stared at the white tiger in the cage, not knowing where to start.","With a mouthful of sharp fangs, it was truly terrifying when it opened its mouth, making them afraid to touch it.","Lanxi reached out to block them. \"We will handle this ourselves. You just move the rest.\"","Qingshuang and Lanxi each lifted a corner and carried the tiger cage inside.","Yunhe explained as they walked, \"The master is still at the Hanlin Academy and has not returned yet. I have already had the kitchens prepare lunch. The Lady and Young Master Song can take a short rest.\"","Ever since receiving the letter, Ye Liangyu had instructed the servants to make preparations. The guest rooms and all necessary items had been ready for half a month, with someone assigned to clean them every day.","After bringing them to their rooms, Yunhe beckoned to two older female servants. \"These are servants of the estate. If the Lady needs anything, please feel free to instruct them. I will not disturb your rest any longer.\"","\"Thank you,\" Song Jinzhao nodded slightly. Since entering the estate, she had not seen a single woman, let alone a young maid. These two older women must have been specially assigned to serve her.","After stepping out of the room, Yunhe immediately ordered a servant to go to the Hanlin Academy to notify Ye Liangyu. \"Tell the master that Young Master Song and the Lady have arrived.\"","By the time they woke up from a nap after lunch, Ye Liangyu had already rushed back from the Hanlin Academy.","In the study, he pressed his hands on Song Qiming's shoulders, praising him endlessly. \"I did not expect you to place first in the provincial examinations. It seems you did not slack off on your studies after I left Anyang Prefecture.\"","Song Qiming curled his lips into a smile and bowed with folded hands. \"Teacher arranged everything for me before leaving; how could I dare to slack off?\"","Ye Liangyu nodded incessantly. \"I already know your sister's purpose for coming. The Emperor's birthday is in three days. When the time comes, I will definitely help you achieve your wish.\"","The more noble Song Jinzhao's status was, the greater the help she could provide to Song Qiming. They absolutely could not miss such a great opportunity as the birthday banquet.","After leaving the study, the two went to see the potatoes. Holding them in his hands, they felt cool to the touch with their yellow skin. It was hard to imagine that this thing could yield a thousand catties per mu.","When he received the letter, Ye Liangyu could not believe it. At the thought of such a miraculous crop appearing, he wished he could immediately enter the palace to tell the Emperor.","But seeing Song Jinzhao's instructions at the end of the letter, he calmed down and began to think about how to maximize the benefits of this matter.","At such a grand occasion as the birthday banquet, which would also be Song Jinzhao's first time having an audience with the Emperor, there was a lot of room to maneuver. How far the results could go depended heavily on the process, which had to be planned properly.","Before they arrived in the capital, Ye Liangyu had already formulated several plans in his mind, just waiting for Song Jinzhao to arrive so they could discuss and finalize them.","The next day, the Ye Residence's kitchen was bustling with activity. Song Gaoli, sporting dark circles under his eyes from a poor night's sleep, came knocking on the door.","Inside the pavilion, Song Gaoli sprawled on the table with a miserable expression, his hands trembling violently.","\"It was not until I entered his residence yesterday that I found out Duan Yanhua has many disciples. There are six poor students like me living in his estate. They all became his disciples before me and are considered highly valued. There are several more who do not live in the estate; I cannot even count them all on my fingers.\"","\"I thought I was special, but it turns out he is just casting a wide net, hoping to catch whichever one makes it.\"","Song Qiming furrowed his brows tightly. Initially, they had only inquired about Duan Yanhua's literary talent and official career, but they had not considered this aspect.","Taking in so many students, could he even guide them all? And with them all living in the estate, the daily food expenses alone would be a considerable sum."]},{"number":212,"title":"Chapter 212: The Birthday Banquet Begins","paragraphs":["\"With so many students living in his house, can he afford to support them?\" The annual salary of a Hanlin Academy compiler didn't seem very high.","Song Gaoli puffed out his cheeks for a long while before finally exhaling and swallowing his frustration.","He said aggrievedly, \"He doesn't have money, but his wife is quite wealthy—so wealthy that even I'm a bit envious.\"","After Song Qiming asked for details, he found out that Duan Yanhua was able to enter the Hanlin Academy back then because he had a rich father-in-law.","Because the father-in-law had no sons and worried that his estate would be divided up by the clan after his death, he simply donated two hundred thousand taels of silver to the imperial court right before he died. For the sake of the money, the Emperor bestowed the position of Hanlin Academy compiler upon Duan Yanhua. Unexpectedly, Duan hadn't climbed any higher in over a decade, making the two hundred thousand taels essentially a wasted donation.","If his father-in-law knew about this in the underworld, he would surely crawl out from the depths of hell to scold him to death.","Duan Yanhua's wife brought a substantial dowry when she married him. Although it had been mostly depleted over the years, a starved camel is still bigger than a horse; it was more than enough to support a few extra mouths.","After hearing Song Gaoli's explanation, Song Qiming didn't know what to say.","\"How talented are the students Duan Yanhua is keeping in his estate? Is there any hope of them passing the metropolitan examination to become Jinshi?\"","Song Gaoli shook his head. \"I chatted with them for a couple of hours yesterday. They can't compare to you, but they are much better than me. I'm not sure if they can pass.\"","Song Qiming asked, \"What do you plan to do now?\"","He had already formally acknowledged him as his teacher; it was too late to back out now.","Song Gaoli took a deep breath, cheering himself up. \"What else can I do? This is how it has to be. With my qualifications, I didn't have much of a choice anyway. Having a teacher is better than not having one at all.\"","That evening, in the rear courtyard of the Prince of Ying's estate, Xiao Rongyan went to Li Qinyun's courtyard.","\"Song Jinzhao and her brother have arrived in the capital and are staying at Ye Liangyu's estate. Didn't you say you got along wonderfully with her in Anyang Prefecture? Then invite the siblings over for a chat another day.\"","Li Qinyun raised her elegant eyebrows in surprise, not expecting them to arrive so soon. She asked, \"Did Song Qiming pass the provincial examination?\"","Xiao Rongyan nodded with a displeased expression. \"He took first place in the Longbei Province provincial examination. Ye Liangyu really taught a good student. It's almost a certainty that this boy will pass the metropolitan examination next spring.\"","Li Qinyun's crimson lips tightened slightly. \"In that case, I will invite Song Jinzhao and her brother over tomorrow.\"","Xiao Rongyan shook his head. \"The day after tomorrow is my royal father's birthday banquet. Let's wait until after the banquet to invite them. I want to see this thirteen-year-old top scholar with my own eyes.\"","It was golden autumn. On the day of the Dongzhao Emperor's fiftieth birthday, red silk was hung high all over the capital in celebration. As the sky slightly darkened in the evening, the lights inside the Hall of Supreme Harmony shone as dazzlingly as bright pearls. Officials of the fifth rank and above wore their court attire and brought their families into the palace to celebrate.","Following a long, ringing call from the Directorate of Ceremonial, the crowd was guided by the master of ceremonies to their seats according to their ranks, standing in place to wait quietly.","Accompanied by solemn ceremonial music, Emperor Xiao Chengjing appeared at the entrance of the Hall of Supreme Harmony.","The moment he appeared, everyone knelt down in succession to perform the grand ceremony of three kneelings and nine kowtows, shouting loudly, \"Long live the Emperor, long live, long long live.\"","The voices echoed throughout the Hall of Supreme Harmony and lingered in the imperial palace for a long time.","In a carriage outside the palace walls, Song Qiming pricked up his ears and said uncertainly, \"Sister, I think I hear people shouting 'long live'.\"","The crowd's loud shouts were already very faint and muffled by the time they reached outside the palace walls. If it weren't for the surrounding silence, they wouldn't have been heard at all.","Song Jinzhao, who had sharp hearing, nodded slightly. \"It's 'Long live the Emperor, long live, long long live.' The birthday banquet has begun.\"","Song Qiming took a deep breath, feeling a bit apprehensive.","Even though he knew he wouldn't be summoned by the Emperor, he was still a little nervous at the thought of his sister seeing His Majesty.","Song Jinzhao looked calm. Her gaze toward the palace gates was distant and peaceful, as if she could see right through everything to the grand occasion inside the Hall of Supreme Harmony.","Sitting on the resplendent Nine Dragon Throne, Xiao Chengjing looked down at his subjects with immense satisfaction. He had sat on this dragon throne for twenty years. Now over fifty, he was still in the prime of his life. There would be another ten, twenty, thirty years, or even longer. An emperor shared the same lifespan as the heavens; what did it matter if he lived to be a hundred?","\"Rise, my beloved subjects. Today is a birthday banquet for you to celebrate with Us. There is no need to be overly formal. Please, take your seats.\"","After a piece of music was played, the eunuch from the Directorate of Ceremonial shouted the words \"Present the gifts\" in his sharp voice, dragging out the final syllable for a very long time.","The most crucial part of this birthday banquet had finally begun."]},{"number":213,"title":"Chapter 213: Tribute","paragraphs":["Sitting at the very front on opposite sides, Prince Qi and Prince Ying exchanged a glance. The smiles on their faces were laced with fierce sparks, as if they had already clashed several times in the depths of each other's eyes.","Ye Liangyu and Fei Yanzhang exchanged a silent look, their unspoken words perfectly aligning. They went over the gift-presenting procedure, which they had already discussed numerous times, one more time in their minds.","\"The presentation of gifts begins! All princes and princesses shall offer their congratulations to the Emperor—\"","Prince Qi was the first to rise and walk to the center of the hall. Everyone's eyes focused on Xiao Rongche, curious to see what kind of birthday gift he would present to the Emperor.","Xiao Rongche clapped his hands, and eight attendants carried a scroll measuring dozens of feet long into the hall from outside.","As the scroll was slowly unrolled, Xiao Rongche bowed and cupped his hands toward the Emperor. \"Your son respectfully presents the Panoramic Map of the Imperial Territories. This map was drawn to scale by thirty renowned masters who traveled across every inch of our Dongzhao Kingdom. Every mountain and river is depicted from actual scenery. With this map, your son wishes Imperial Father an eternal reign over these lands, and everlasting peace for the state.\"","Even before the scroll was completely unfurled, its majesty was already apparent. Once fully opened, it took up nearly a third of the Hall of Supreme Harmony.","Emperor Xiao Chengjing's gaze fell upon the scroll in a daze. This was the world in his hands; he was the monarch of this land.","\"Good, good, good!\" Saying the word \"good\" three times in a row was enough to represent Xiao Chengjing's delight with this birthday gift.","Seeing this, Prince Qi cast a smug glance at Prince Ying. Well? How could your longevity mountain jade carving possibly compare to this?","Prince Ying smiled faintly, appearing exceedingly calm and composed.","Just as the Emperor opened his mouth, wanting to continue offering a few more words of praise, Prince Ying lifted the hem of his robe and slowly walked until he was standing just three feet away from Prince Qi.","\"I never expected that I would share such a telepathic connection with my royal brother. Imperial Father, your son has scoured ancient texts and personally painted a map to present to you. I invite Imperial Father and all the ministers to take a look.\"","The Hall of Supreme Harmony, which had just been filled with the mingling of wine cups, instantly fell into a dead silence. It was as if everyone had their throats gripped tight, unable to utter a single sound.","Rather than calling it a coincidence, it was more like a provocation.","Presenting the exact same birthday gift—whoever had the uglier one would be the one humiliated.","If Prince Qi Xiao Rongche's Panoramic Map of the Imperial Territories required a third of the Hall of Supreme Harmony to be laid out, then Prince Ying Xiao Rongyan's Complete Map of the Earth could cover more than half of the hall. It took the combined strength of over a dozen people to keep it from falling over.","Looking at the thousands of densely packed cities on the scroll, the boundary line in the middle was incredibly distinct. The map not only clearly recorded the magnificent mountains and rivers of the Dongzhao Kingdom, but even every city, every pool, and every single route of the Shuobei Kingdom was so clear that it seemed one could just reach out and strike directly at the enemy's heart, unifying the world.","Xiao Rongche's hands, hanging by his sides, clenched tightly into fists. His jaw was clamped so hard it felt as though his jawbone might shatter.","Xiao Rongyan had definitely planted spies around him. To find out what birthday gift he was going to give and deliberately pull this stunt to overshadow him was simply going too far.","Prince Ying took a large step forward, fell to both knees, cupped his hands, and declared loudly, \"Under the whole heaven, every spot is the sovereign's ground; to the borders of the land, every individual is the sovereign's minister. With this map, your son wishes Imperial Father virtues that match heaven and earth, a mighty prestige that reaches the four seas, and the heavenly mandate to unify the world into one.\"","What emperor in this world had never harbored the grand ambition of unifying the realm? When Xiao Chengjing first ascended the throne, he too had thought of sweeping across Shuobei, but reality had dealt him a harsh slap in the face.","An empty national treasury, turbulent internal rebellions, and the extremely formidable combat power of Shuobei—all these complications made him unable to even ensure his own subjects were fed and clothed, let alone unify the world.","Having been on the throne for decades, seeing this Complete Map of the Earth now, and hearing Prince Ying painting such a grand illusion in his ears, that passionate ambition of Xiao Chengjing's youth seemed to be ignited once more from the bottom of his heart.","With a wave of Xiao Rongyan's small hand behind his back, the Prince Ying faction stepped forward one after another to offer their flattery: \"Your Majesty's virtues match heaven and earth, and your mighty prestige reaches the four seas. Long live the Emperor, long live, long, long live!\"","Anyway, the people of the Shuobei Kingdom were not present. As long as just saying it could coax the Emperor into a good mood, no one would take it seriously as long as troops were not actually deployed.","Emperor Xiao Chengjing walked down the white jade steps step by step. The thudding sound struck everyone's hearts, as if they were going to leap out of their chests.","He reached out and gently brushed over the mountains and cities on the map. His slightly trembling fingertips revealed the excitement in Xiao Chengjing's heart.","If only he could truly unify the world during his reign, leaving a legacy for countless generations, he would be the greatest emperor of all time!"]},{"number":214,"title":"Chapter 214: The Emperor's Stratagem","paragraphs":["Thinking of the current situation in the Dongzhao Kingdom, Xiao Chengjing calmed down and let out a heavy sigh.","He did not raise his eyes to look at Prince Ying, but instead swept his gaze lightly over the civil and military officials. His tone carried a bitter smile and a touch of self-mockery.","\"This item from Prince Ying truly wins my heart, but I wonder who can help me fulfill this wish.\"","The great hall was dead silent. Not a single civil official dared to speak. The military officials exchanged glances, many of them letting their eyes fall upon Chu Liuyun, the Duke of Qing. If they were to attack the Shuobei Kingdom, he would definitely be the first to bear the brunt.","Sitting below Prince Ying, Princess Yongjia looked at Chu Liuyun with worried eyes. Even though she knew that fighting on the battlefield was the destiny of most generals, she still could not help but worry.","Chu Liuyun secretly shook his head at her. The Emperor was merely talking; it was absolutely impossible for him to take the initiative to deploy troops.","Ultimately, the current Dongzhao Kingdom lacked the capital and confidence to forcefully endure a war with an unknown outcome. Xiao Chengjing could not afford the price of defeat. He feared his throne would become unstable and that he would be condemned by the people of the world.","When no one spoke up for a long time and the atmosphere grew stiff, Prince Qi suddenly stood forward.","He said loudly, \"Since Second Brother was able to personally draw the Complete Map of the World, he must already have a thorough understanding of the Shuobei Kingdom. When war breaks out between our two nations in the future, if you lead the troops into battle, you will surely conquer Shuobei and fulfill Imperial Father's grand vision of unifying the world. As your elder brother, I will be the first to congratulate you, Second Brother, and to congratulate Imperial Father.\"","Silence. Numbness.","Having Prince Ying lead troops into battle meant that if he accidentally died on the battlefield, the throne would naturally fall to Prince Qi. This was no congratulation; it was sheer sarcasm.","But the Emperor did not think this way. His desire to unify the world had been ignited. Looking at the Complete Map of the World, he only felt that Xiao Rongche made sense.","Nearly two years had passed since the new monarch of the Shuobei Kingdom ascended the throne, and there was no telling when war might break out again. Sending his younger son to the battlefield to fight might be a good idea; it could boost military morale and hone his abilities.","\"Rongche makes sense.\"","Prince Ying's body stiffened, and he looked at the Emperor in disbelief. However, the Emperor completely ignored him and directly looked at Chu Liuyun, saying, \"Duke of Qing, the troops under your command have the strictest discipline. I am entrusting Prince Ying to you. You must help me cultivate a commander capable of sweeping away thousands of enemy troops.\"","Chu Liuyun, who had not said a single word from beginning to end, did not expect Xiao Chengjing to suddenly call upon him.","Training a prince to be a supreme commander meant he could neither scold him nor use physical force. And he was supposed to make him capable of sweeping away thousands of enemy troops? What if the prince died? This was absolutely a troublesome burden.","Just as he was about to step forward and refuse, the semi-retired Duke Zhenguo preemptively knelt down. \"To reply to Your Majesty, my son is still young and cannot even sweep away enemy forces amidst thousands of troops himself. How could he possibly cultivate His Highness Prince Ying into a masterful commander? I beseech Your Majesty to retract this order.\"","With a white-haired, highly decorated veteran general kneeling before him, even the Emperor had to give him some face. However...","\"Duke Zhenguo is too modest. Liuyun may still be young, but you are still here. I am entrusting Prince Ying to you father and son. After a year, no matter how he turns out from your teachings, I will accept it. If he cannot become a commander, treating it as physical training is fine too.\"","Since words had reached this point, even if Duke Zhenguo and Chu Liuyun were extremely reluctant, they could only bow their heads and accept. This coming year was probably going to be difficult.","Sitting in his seat, Ye Liangyu looked at the Emperor with a profoundly meaningful expression. A year's time—what was the Emperor planning to do?","Prince Qi swayed back to his seat, his mind half-lost in a daze.","Having Duke Zhenguo and his son instruct Prince Ying could easily lead to trouble. If they switched allegiances, Prince Ying would gain the backing of the military.","If he had known his Imperial Father would do this, he shouldn't have spoken out of turn just now. Damaging the enemy by a thousand while losing eight hundred oneself was truly not worth it.","Prince Ying picked up his wine cup and took a small sip. Today's events were too sudden; he needed a little time to process them.","The ministers kept their heads down, drinking and eating, while their minds had already spun through eight hundred different schemes. In contrast, the female relatives sitting in the grand hall were completely baffled.","How did a perfectly fine gift presentation suddenly involve court politics? It truly made them feel awkward, not knowing whether to sit or stand.","Sitting on the dragon throne, Xiao Chengjing took in the expressions of everyone below the dais, a faint, almost imperceptible smile curving the corners of his lips.","For a year, Prince Ying staying in the military camp would inevitably distract him, which would perfectly facilitate the Emperor's dealing with Prince Ying's faction in the court.","As for Prince Qi, he would be sent out next year to inspect the river floods in Jiangnan and wouldn't be able to return for a year or half. Once the spring examinations were over, it would be time for some fresh blood in the imperial court.","Thinking about how he only had two sons, and how giving them too much power made them eager to turn him into a figurehead, yet abandoning them would leave no one to inherit the great lineage, Xiao Chengjing wanted to sigh.","Could they not just behave themselves and wait to compete for the throne when he was in his seventies or eighties? Starting to form factions for selfish interests now truly showed a lack of respect for him as their Imperial Father. He had to suppress them and teach them a proper lesson."]},{"number":215,"title":"Chapter 215: A Special Bowl of Longevity Noodles","paragraphs":["Seeing the atmosphere ease, Princess Yongjia calmed her mind, knowing it was now her turn.","She turned around to take a brocade box from her maid's hands, walked to the white jade steps, and knelt down. Raising the box above her head with both hands, she said, \"This is the Boundless Longevity embroidery that I stitched myself. I wish Imperial Father fortune as vast as the Eastern Sea and a life as long as the Southern Mountains.\"","Facing his only daughter, Xiao Chengjing's attitude was incredibly tolerant and doting.","The embroidery was unrolled by the palace maids. It depicted lifelike immortal cranes and auspicious beasts, evergreen spiritual trees and immortal herbs. Natural landscapes and ethereal auspicious clouds intertwined, while a golden dragon coiled upon a pine tree, displaying the full majesty of the dragon. At a glance, it did not look like embroidery at all, but rather a living scene.","Unlike the strictness he showed toward his sons, Xiao Chengjing's face was now full of affection. The crinkles at the corners of his eyes seemed like melting snow in the spring.","\"This piece is ingeniously conceived. The flora and fauna blend seamlessly into one entity; it is truly flawless. Look at your eyes, they are red from staying up late. This must have cost you a lot of time and energy. You must not do this next time. Even if you simply embroidered a few characters for longevity, I would still be delighted.\"","Princess Yongjia raised her chin with a hint of playfulness, her eyes full of deep adoration for the Emperor. \"The birthday gift for Imperial Father naturally has to be the best. I am clumsy and only have this bit of craftsmanship to show. As long as Imperial Father likes it, that is all that matters.\"","Xiao Chengjing nodded repeatedly, grinning from ear to ear. \"Imperial Father likes it very much.\"","Sitting cross-legged on their cushions, Prince Qi and Prince Ying exchanged glances, inevitably feeling a trace of unfairness in their hearts.","They had put in so much thought, yet they did not receive such praise from their father. It was just a piece of embroidery. Ultimately, their father did not favor them enough and was biased toward Princess Yongjia.","After the princes and princesses presented their gifts, it was the turn of the imperial clan and the ministers.","Shoushan stone carvings, longevity vases, ancient books and paintings, corals, and bright pearls—the variety was so vast that the registry in the hands of the Directorate of Ceremonial was almost running out of space.","When it was time for the Censorate to present their gifts, the first to rise was the head of the Censorate, Ye Liangyu.","He rose gracefully, cupped his hands, and bowed to the Son of Heaven, speaking with a righteous and earnest tone, \"Someone has prepared a special birthday gift and entrusted me to present it to Your Majesty. I invite Your Majesty to have a taste.\"","Everyone looked at Ye Liangyu in astonishment. Who prepared the gift? How special was it?","To have a taste? Was it a local specialty presented by some regional official, or a rare famous tea?","\"Oh? Who sent it?\" Xiao Chengjing asked curiously.","Ye Liangyu smiled faintly and replied calmly, \"Please allow me to keep it a secret for now. It will certainly not disappoint Your Majesty.\"","Xiao Chengjing's curiosity was thoroughly piqued. He rested his arm on the dragon head of his throne and said in a deep voice, \"In that case, bring it up and let me have a look.\"","Sitting on his cushion, Prince Ying cast a dark, profound gaze at Ye Liangyu. Could it be Song Jinzhao?","Yunhe slowly walked in from outside the hall, carrying a tray.","Worried about dropping the item in his hands, he took every step with extreme steadiness.","In the middle of the tray sat a black clay pot, accompanied by a soup spoon and chopsticks.","Prime Minister Gu Qishan and the others raised their eyebrows in surprise. Served in a clay pot, could it be a dish?","An attendant immediately walked down the steps to take the tray. Before his hands even touched the clay pot, he could feel the scorching heat radiating from its walls, as if it had just been cooked.","After the item was taken away, Yunhe let out a deep breath and slowly retreated. He had waited for the right time to cook it fresh over a charcoal fire. If Lady Linghui had not prepared the ingredients and soup base in advance, he would have been terrified of ruining everything by cooking it wrong and ruining the flavor.","The attendant lifted the lid of the pot, and a blast of hot steam carrying a savory aroma wafted out. As the mist dispersed, noodle-like potato vermicelli came into view, glowing white. It was actually a bowl of longevity noodles.","Xiao Chengjing raised an eyebrow in surprise and looked at Ye Liangyu. \"Beloved subject Ye, why are these noodles so thick?\"","Ye Liangyu raised a hand to gesture. \"Your Majesty, please have a taste first.\"","The attendant tested it for poison before handing the chopsticks to Xiao Chengjing.","With his first bite, his immediate impression was that it was delicious. The light broth was incredibly savory, better than what the imperial kitchens made.","The soft and tender texture of the noodles was like tofu, yet with an added hint of chewiness. They looked like noodles, but the texture was unlike any noodles.","\"Beloved subject Ye, how are these noodles made? I have never eaten noodles like these before.\"","Ye Liangyu said, \"Would Your Majesty care to guess what these noodles are made of?\"","Xiao Chengjing glanced at the snow-white potato vermicelli in the clay pot. \"They are not made of wheat flour?\"","Ye Liangyu smiled and knelt. \"To answer Your Majesty, they are not made of wheat flour, but of potato flour. This is the birthday gift that Lady Linghui brought all the way from Anyang Prefecture to the capital, entrusting me to present to Your Majesty—a type of food crop that no one present here has ever eaten before.\""]},{"number":216,"title":"Chapter 216: The Birth of the Potato: Summoning Song Jinzhao","paragraphs":["The hall fell silent for a moment, making the sound of someone gulping exceptionally distinct.","The Minister of Revenue glared sideways behind him, and the Vice Minister of Revenue sitting right behind him immediately held his breath, not daring to move.","He was craving a bite. Judging by the Emperor's expression, His Majesty seemed quite pleased with that bowl of potato noodles. He wondered how it tasted.","Xiao Chengjing picked up a potato noodle to examine it carefully. Potato noodles? He had never heard of it.","\"Song Jinzhao has come to the capital?\"","Ye Liangyu nodded, \"She just arrived a few days ago, traveling through the night just to present a birthday gift to Your Majesty.\"","Xiao Chengjing really wanted to meet this extraordinary woman with high martial arts skills who invented the waterwheel and winter vegetable greenhouses, but...","Prince Qi picked up his wine cup and chuckled, saying in a mocking tone, \"Lady Linghui truly lives up to her peasant origins. For Imperial Father's fiftieth birthday, traveling overnight to deliver food as a birthday gift is truly unconventional.\"","The ministers of Prince Qi's faction shook their heads and echoed, \"Our Dongzhao Kingdom spans thousands of miles, with vast lands and abundant resources. There are many unseen foods; this potato noodle is nothing rare.\"","Princess Yongjia subconsciously looked at Chu Liuyun. Seeing that he was sitting on his cushion with no reaction, her suspended heart relaxed a little.","Facing the ministers' ridicule, Ye Liangyu calmly looked at the Emperor sitting upright on the dragon throne. \"To reply to Your Majesty, what if this humble minister tells you that these potatoes can yield a thousand catties per mu?\"","The noisy hall became terrifyingly quiet at this moment. All sounds died away, and even the music of strings and bamboo stopped.","Prince Qi hastily put down the wine cup in his hand. The porcelain bumped against the table with a clatter, and the Hall of Preserving Harmony instantly erupted into an uproar.","\"How is that possible!\"","\"A thousand catties per mu, is there really such a divine object?\"","\"What on earth do potatoes look like? I want to see them right now.\"","...","Whether it was rice or wheat, the best paddy fields could only reach a yield of two hundred catties per mu. Medium paddy fields only yielded one hundred and twenty catties, and dry land couldn't even reach one hundred.","A yield of a thousand catties per mu was something they didn't even dare to imagine.","If it were true, it would be equivalent to the arable land of Dongzhao Kingdom instantly multiplying five or six times. The common people of the world would no longer have to worry about running out of food and starving to death.","The surrounding noisy sounds gave people a headache, like a swarm of flies buzzing around their ears, but Ye Liangyu found these sounds incredibly pleasant at this moment.","The Emperor staggered up from the resplendent dragon throne. \"Beloved Subject Ye, is this true? Can these potatoes really yield a thousand catties per mu?\"","Ye Liangyu answered sonorously, \"To reply to Your Majesty, Lady Linghui has already test-planted a crop. With ten catties of potato seeds on two and a half fen of land, a total of two hundred and seventy catties of potatoes were harvested.\"","Everyone now had an abacus in their heads, and the beads were clicking loudly.","If two and a half fen of land could yield two hundred and seventy catties, then one mu would be one thousand and eighty catties. How could it be so high-yielding? It was truly a divine crop.","Xiao Chengjing had also figured it out. He paced back and forth in excitement. Suddenly thinking of something, he quickly turned around to look at Ye Liangyu.","\"Where is Lady Linghui? Have her bring the potatoes to see me immediately.\"","Looking again at the potato noodles in the clay pot, Xiao Chengjing's eyes were shining.","Ye Liangyu cupped his hands and said, \"To reply to Your Majesty, Lady Linghui is currently waiting outside the palace walls to be summoned.\"","Xiao Chengjing waved his large hand and shouted impatiently, \"Hurry and let her in. Have the Imperial Guards drive a carriage to invite her, the faster the better.\"","The sound of horse hooves at night was exceptionally clear. Qingshuang lifted the carriage curtain and whispered, \"Eldest Miss, someone has come out.\"","Song Jinzhao turned her head slightly. Through the gap in the door curtain, she could see the armored Imperial Guards sitting on the carriage frame, the bright lanterns reflecting off the adjacent city wall.","The carriage stopped in front of Qingshuang. Meeting Song Jinzhao's calm pupils, the Imperial Guard jumped off the carriage frame and asked, \"May I ask if you are Lady Linghui?\"","Even though he had never seen Song Jinzhao before, with just one glance, the man could confirm that the young girl before him was Lady Linghui.","His first impression of this woman was that she was completely unfathomable, especially those eyes. They were clearly beautiful, but they always felt a bit dangerous.","Song Jinzhao emerged from the carriage cabin, nodded, and replied, \"I am.\"","The Imperial Guard cupped his hands and said, \"The Emperor invites you. Please bring the potatoes, My Lady, and follow me into the palace.\"","\"Here, Sister. I will wait for you outside.\" Song Qiming took a deep breath and hurriedly handed the box containing the potatoes to Song Jinzhao.","Inside were three catties of potatoes, all carefully selected from the one hundred and fifty catties they had brought this time.","Both their shape and skin were impeccable. Additionally, there was one catty of potato starch.","The carriage passed through the palace gates and continued forward. Song Jinzhao lifted the window curtain and looked around at the palace buildings shrouded in darkness.","The imperial palace was vast and majestic, but at night, it revealed a hint of danger, empty and seemingly endless at a glance.","This was the place with the most concentrated power in the world, a place countless people yearned for.","But when they actually walked inside, under the majesty of the Son of Heaven, there was more apprehension than awe.","Song Jinzhao lowered the carriage curtain and looked down at the wooden box in her hands. Personally bringing some positive changes to this world felt wonderful, making one unable to resist wanting to change even more."]},{"number":217,"title":"Chapter 217: Presenting the Sea Chart to the Emperor","paragraphs":["Seeing the imperial guards leading a young woman slowly up the steps, the eunuch, with his hands clasped before his stomach, called out loudly as she approached, \"Lady Linghui is granted an audience!\"","The lake-blue brocade official dress worn by Song Jinzhao did not make her look older; instead, it exuded a composure that seemed beyond her seventeen years. Her perfect oval face carried a hint of heroic spirit, and her straight back looked as though not even the weight of a ten-thousand-pound boulder could bend it.","Prince Ying's displeased gaze was firmly fixed on Song Jinzhao. Back in Anyang Prefecture, his side consort had made things practically crystal clear, yet he never expected this girl to be so unappreciative of his favors.","Such a high-yielding crop like the potato should have been presented to him first. Then, he could have offered it to his imperial father to claim a monumental merit. Not only would it have made his father value him more, but it would also have won him the love and support of the common people. But now, he hadn't gotten a single piece of the pie. It was truly detestable.","Xiao Chengjing stared at Song Jinzhao as she walked toward him step by step, a look of admiration involuntarily welling up in his eyes.","She was truly young, only in her teens. Recalling the things she had accomplished, it was almost unbelievable.","It was a pity she was a woman. If she were a man, her benefit to the imperial court might have been even greater.","Song Jinzhao calmly placed the wooden box aside, then lifted the hem of her skirt and knelt. \"Your subject, Song Jinzhao, pays her respects to Your Majesty. Long live the Emperor.\"","At only fifty years old, this emperor looked a bit aged.","Xiao Chengjing immediately raised his hand to let Song Jinzhao rise, asking impatiently, \"Lady Linghui, is the potato inside the box? Quickly, bring it for Us to see.\"","\"Yes,\" Song Jinzhao nodded slightly. She opened the lid and offered the box with both hands.","The eunuch hurried up and down the steps with quick, short strides. In the blink of an eye, the potato was placed on Xiao Chengjing's dragon desk.","With its oval shape and pale yellow skin covered in small grayish-brown spots, it looked quite ordinary. Yet, in Xiao Chengjing's eyes at this moment, it was the most beautiful thing in the world, capable of bringing him boundless joy.","His heart had not stopped racing since he heard Ye Liangyu say it could yield a thousand catties per mu.","\"Can this potato truly yield a thousand catties per mu?\"","Song Jinzhao replied, \"To answer Your Majesty, not only does this crop have a high yield, but it is also not as delicate as other crops. It can be planted in barren land, is extremely drought-resistant, and prefers a cool climate.\"","\"Its growth cycle takes only three to four months. It can be planted twice a year, and in warmer climates, even three times. This greatly increases the frequency of land use, achieving an annual yield of three thousand catties.\"","Every word Song Jinzhao spoke struck a chord in everyone's hearts. Not only was the yield high, but it was also resistant to drought and cold, and it wasn't picky about the soil. If every household planted it, why would they ever worry about the common people not having enough food to eat?","Xiao Chengjing's hand, gripping the potato tightly, trembled uncontrollably. No matter how he tried to steady it, he couldn't stop.","His gaze fell upon Song Jinzhao. Suddenly, he felt as if this young woman's figure had grown much taller. But upon looking closely, she was still as slender and delicate as before.","How on earth did she do it? Could this truly be an auspicious blessing bestowed upon the Dongzhao Kingdom by the heavens?","\"Lady Linghui, where did you obtain this potato?\"","Song Jinzhao recounted the events that took place at the docks in detail, then pulled out the parchment map from her sleeve and presented it.","As early as the day after she received the parchment map, Song Jinzhao had already copied the nautical chart on it. Although some parts were unclear, she still managed to draw nearly seventy percent of it.","The ocean was vast and boundless, fraught with the dangers of giant waves and tsunamis. Relying solely on herself and a single nautical chart to find a new continent would be fraught with difficulties.","But if it were the imperial court, much like Zheng He's voyages to the Western Seas in history, they might just succeed.","Xiao Chengjing stared at the blurry nautical chart on the parchment, finding it hard to imagine that beyond the endless sea, there were people he knew nothing about.","His gaze fell upon the Complete Map of the Myriad Countries. The blank spaces at the edges began to seem somewhat mysterious. Aside from Dongzhao and Beishuo, there were other countries, and he knew absolutely nothing about them.","\"Lady Linghui, how many more of these potatoes do you have?\"","Song Jinzhao answered, \"To answer Your Majesty, your subject harvested a total of two hundred and seventy catties of potatoes in August, and brought one hundred and fifty catties to the capital this time.\"","Xiao Chengjing's eyes darted around as he calculated. Ten catties of potatoes could yield two hundred and seventy catties. One hundred and fifty catties would yield four thousand catties. Continuing to plant them would result in one hundred and ten thousand catties. Assuming they were planted twice a year, the growth rate would be rapid, and it wouldn't take many years to reach a massive scale.","Seeing the emperor's expression growing increasingly excited, Ye Liangyu signaled Fei Yanzhang with his eyes. The timing was just about right. According to their plan, as soon as the emperor offered to reward Song Jinzhao, the Hanlin Academy and the Censorate would strike together, determined to snatch a substantial piece of the merit."]},{"number":218,"title":"Chapter 218: Promoted Four Ranks in a Row, the County Lady of Linghui","paragraphs":["Chu Liuyun's meaningful gaze darted back and forth between Ye Liangyu and Song Jinzhao. Between the leg injury and Song Qiming, Ye Liangyu was essentially tied to the same boat as Song Jinzhao. It was hard to imagine that a peasant girl from two years ago could reach where she was today. The title of Lady was probably just the first step.","Xiao Chengjing sat down on the dragon throne, a smile playing at the corners of his lips, his voice clear and resonant.","\"Lady Linghui, Song Jinzhao, step forward to receive the decree. Bearing the mandate of heaven, I value the sustenance of the common people. The high yield of potatoes has saved thousands of people from the plight of hunger and poverty. Your merit will be recorded in history and benefit generations to come. To commend this achievement and to set an example for women across the world, I hereby grant you the title of County Princess Linghui, and bestow upon you a thousand taels of gold, a thousand mu of fertile land, and a mansion. I hope you will continue to keep the nation in your heart and serve the imperial court in the future.\"","Ye Liangyu, who had just slightly lifted his bottom, instantly hovered in mid-air. Everyone in the Hall of Supreme Harmony widened their eyes and looked at Xiao Chengjing.","Not a County Lady, not a Commandery Lady, but a County Princess?","To be elevated from a Township Lady to a County Princess was an instant four-level jump. Was the Emperor joking?","Fei Yanzhang squinted hard at Ye Liangyu, signaling him to sit down quickly, as there was no need for them to worry anymore.","They originally thought the Emperor would grant Song Jinzhao the title of County Lady, so they had planned to fight for the position of Commandery Lady. Now she was directly conferred the title of a third-rank County Princess. The imperial grace was immense, far exceeding the reward Song Jinzhao should have received. To ask for more would be crossing the line.","Ye Liangyu slowly sat back down, his heart pounding so hard it felt like it might leap out of his chest.","Everyone was so shocked that they could hardly recover. As the person involved, Song Jinzhao merely lifted her eyes slightly before kneeling down to bow and accept the decree.","\"This subject's daughter receives the decree. Thank you, Your Majesty, for your profound grace. Long live, long live, may Your Majesty live for ten thousand years.\"","The crowd snapped back to reality. Seeing that the matter was settled and the Emperor was greatly pleased, they knew they absolutely could not ruin the mood and offend the Emperor at this moment. Thus, they all knelt down to congratulate him in unison, \"Long live, long live, may Your Majesty live for ten thousand years.\"","It was not only the civil and military officials who were startled, but also the family members they had brought along.","A commoner woman being granted the title of County Princess—this was a reward usually reserved for the daughters of Commandery Princes. One could only imagine how high the newly appointed County Princess Linghui stood in the Emperor's heart.","They had to take her seriously. If they ever encountered her in the future, they absolutely must not offend her.","Just as Song Jinzhao stood up, Xiao Chengjing said, \"I will immediately order someone to go to Anyang Prefecture to fetch the remaining one hundred and twenty catties of potatoes.\"","\"To reply to Your Majesty, this subject's daughter has already had those one hundred and twenty catties planted at the farmstead and built vegetable greenhouses. It is estimated that they can only be harvested in early December.\"","Xiao Chengjing was even more delighted upon hearing this. That meant that after the harvest in December, there would be over three thousand more catties of potatoes.","\"Very well. Then wait until after the harvest and send them all to the capital.\"","With her head lowered, the corners of Song Jinzhao's mouth twitched. Asking for so much meant he had no intention of letting her keep much for herself.","Never mind, her goal had been achieved anyway. She would keep a few catties to plant for her own family's consumption, and hand the rest over to the imperial court so they could expand the planting scale as soon as possible and benefit all the people.","\"Yes. After the harvest, this subject's daughter will have them sent over.\"","Xiao Chengjing nodded in satisfaction. \"Someone, grant County Princess Linghui a seat.\"","A table was quickly set up just below Princess Yongjia. The palace maids swiftly served fruit platters and dishes, and then waited quietly to the side, ready to serve at any moment.","The presentation of gifts continued, but the people present no longer had any interest in watching.","Countless gazes frequently landed on Song Jinzhao. Among them were dissatisfaction, wariness, envy, and admiration. They pricked her like needles, but even though it felt like having thorns in her back, Song Jinzhao did not feel the slightest bit of panic.","She sat on the soft cushion, as steady as a mountain, and calmly picked up her chopsticks, as if everything that had just happened had nothing to do with her. It was like passing clouds, not a big deal at all.","She had to admit that the imperial chefs in the palace really had some skill. The dishes were much more delicious than those in the restaurants outside.","After the gift presentation came the song and dance performances. The officials began to raise their wine cups to toast each other and whispered among themselves under the tables.","Faced with Song Jinzhao, the newly appointed County Princess, no one dared to take the initiative to strike up a conversation before the two princes spoke. Even the female family members did not dare to cast an extra glance at her. Only Ye Liangyu raised his wine cup toward Song Jinzhao.","Ou Shinian, the Minister of Works, thought of everything that had happened before. Perhaps he might need her help with something in the future, so it was best to stay on good terms.","He kept staring at Song Jinzhao until she noticed him, at which point he immediately smiled and raised his wine cup to gesture to her.","Song Jinzhao did not know Ou Shinian, but she nodded at him and took a small sip from her cup. Given his seating position, he should be one of the Ministers of the Six Ministries.","Sitting in his original seat, Prince Ying had almost crushed his back molars from gritting his teeth. If such a great merit had fallen on him, his position as the Crown Prince would definitely be secured. Now it was all ruined by Song Jinzhao. It was just the title of a County Princess, what use was it? She was still just a woman.","\"Will County Princess Linghui be residing in the capital permanently from now on?\"","A soft voice came from her left. Song Jinzhao turned her head and saw a young girl wearing a magnificent gold phoenix hairpin inlaid with a pearl the size of a pigeon egg. Her sunset-colored cloud silk brocade was embroidered with gold thread peonies, and her whole body exuded a noble temperament distinct from the other female family members.","Sitting alone at a table right next to the princes, she must be the Emperor's only daughter, Princess Yongjia.","Recalling what Li Qinyun had told her, Song Jinzhao lowered her eyes and smiled faintly without losing her manners. \"To reply to Her Highness the Princess, this subject's daughter will temporarily stay in the capital for a period of time.\"","Princess Yongjia gave a slight nod and did not ask any further questions.","When Prince Qi saw Xiao Yongjia talking to Song Jinzhao, he thought that enemies were meeting face-to-face and that she was going to cause trouble for her. In the end, it went quiet after just two sentences. He was instantly furious, thinking to himself that Xiao Yongjia was too cowardly and completely useless.","On the dragon throne, the Emperor had eaten the entire pot of potato noodles and grew more and more satisfied the more he looked at the potatoes in the box.","A divine object appearing on the day of his birthday banquet—he truly was the Son of Heaven. Even the heavens were sending him a birthday gift.","If Song Jinzhao had heard Xiao Chengjing's inner thoughts, she would definitely have rolled her eyes hard at him. If it really was a birthday gift from the heavens, wouldn't she have to be a deity?","Seeing that a pile of crab shells had accumulated on Song Jinzhao's table, the Emperor said in a deep voice, \"Anyang Prefecture is not near the sea. Presumably, County Princess Linghui has never eaten sea crabs before.\"","\"Since you like them, someone, bring my plate over to the County Princess as well.\"","Song Jinzhao paused her hand holding the crab claw and stood up to thank him for his grace. \"This subject's daughter likes them very much. Thank you, Your Majesty, for the reward.\"","The eunuch waiting to the side immediately bowed and brought the plate full of sea crabs over to Song Jinzhao's table.","Riding fast horses all the way from Mingzhou, a single sea crab cost ten taels of silver. Such fresh ones could only be found in the imperial palace.","Envious gazes fell upon Song Jinzhao. Indeed, the imperial favor was profound. The Emperor valued her very much.","Seeing that Song Jinzhao liked his reward, the Emperor was also pleased. A person who was useful to him and posed no threat was completely worry-free to use.","\"I heard that your younger brother passed the civil service examination at the county level at the young age of twelve. I wonder how he performed in the provincial examination this year?\"","Song Jinzhao replied, \"Blessed by heavenly grace and ancestral virtue, my younger brother luckily achieved the top rank in the provincial examination this time. He has also come to the capital to prepare for the metropolitan examination next year, hoping to live up to Your Majesty's profound grace of education.\""]},{"number":219,"title":"Chapter 219: Stealing the Spotlight, the Astonished Song Qiming","paragraphs":["The Emperor's pupils contracted, his gaze suddenly locking onto Song Jinzhao's face. The Dongzhao Kingdom had never seen a thirteen-year-old provincial top scorer. To call him young was an understatement; he was not even an adult yet.","The uninformed officials and their female relatives stared blankly, their mouths hanging open. What kind of monstrously talented family was this? Each one was more formidable than the last.","Recovering his composure, the Emperor looked toward Ye Liangyu and praised him, saying, Beloved subject Ye, I never expected that during your time away from the court, you would cultivate such a young talent for me. Since you are so gifted at teaching, you truly ought to take on a few more students.","Suddenly called upon, Ye Liangyu hastily stood up, his voice carrying a trace of solemnity. At that time, this humble minister believed he would never be able to serve the imperial court again in this lifetime, which is why I took on a student.","His ability to place first in the provincial exams is not entirely due to my efforts. Qiming is extraordinarily intelligent. Perhaps because he was born into poverty, he cherishes the opportunity to study all the more. Furthermore, having begun his education late, he studies bitterly late into the night every single day, never relaxing all year round. To have accepted such a self-disciplined student is an exceptional honor for this humble minister.","Hearing Ye Liangyu's unreserved praise, Xiao Chengjing looked at Song Jinzhao with immense gratification. With an elder sister setting such a fine example, the younger brother surely cannot be far behind. I greatly look forward to his results in next year's metropolitan examination.","Song Jinzhao smiled calmly. To be favored by Your Majesty is my younger brother's great blessing. He will surely study day and night to repay the imperial grace.","As Ye Liangyu and Song Jinzhao echoed each other seamlessly, and with the Emperor showing such strong support, the factions of Prince Qi and Prince Ying sitting below looked as though they had bitten into bitter melons—unable to spit them out, yet unable to swallow them down.","The birthday banquet did not conclude until the hour of the pig. Following the Emperor's departure, the attendees gradually began to disperse.","Ye Liangyu walked beside Song Jinzhao and whispered, The one who toasted you at the banquet was the Minister of Works, Ou Shinian. He was previously reprimanded twice by the Emperor for incompetence regarding the waterwheels and vegetable greenhouses. However, the man is quite open-minded and deeply appreciates talent. He was likely showing his goodwill toward you.","Song Jinzhao gave a calm nod. She had not detected any hostility from the man earlier, either.","As they walked toward the palace gates, everyone who caught sight of Song Jinzhao was secretly whispering to their companions.","Song Jinzhao's appearance at the birthday banquet today had been entirely unexpected for them, but the impact of this surprise was sensational—so significant that it could change the future of the commoners in the Dongzhao Kingdom.","Between the maritime maps and the potatoes, tomorrow's morning court session was bound to be exceptionally lively.","Song Qiming, who had been waiting outside the palace gates the entire time, saw people trickling out. With eyes full of nervous anticipation, he stared intently at the gates, searching for Song Jinzhao's figure.","He wondered how the birthday banquet had gone and whether his elder sister had achieved her goals.","The moment Song Jinzhao and Ye Liangyu appeared at the palace gates, Song Qiming threw open the carriage curtain with a swish, leapt down, and rushed over to Song Jinzhao.","His tense gaze swept up and down her frame. Seeing that she was safe and sound, and that both of them wore smiles on their faces, the heavy anxiety in Song Qiming's heart finally lifted by eighty percent.","His eyes sparkled brightly, and his voice carried a trace of hopeful anticipation. How did it go, Sister? What did the Emperor bestow upon you?","Ye Liangyu clapped his right hand heavily onto Song Qiming's shoulder, teasing him with a smile. You need to be more steady. You should really learn from your sister in this regard. Facing the Emperor for the very first time, she was even calmer than I was, acting as if it were nothing at all.","Song Jinzhao offered a faint smile. In front of so many people, and with such vital treasures in my hands, even if I had acted somewhat inappropriately, the Emperor would not have made things difficult for a mere woman. Showing too much weakness would have only made people think I was unworthy of my standing.","Ye Liangyu withdrew his gaze in admiration. Gripping Song Qiming's shoulder, he said with utmost seriousness, The Emperor has already conferred the title of County Princess Linghui upon your sister, and he even mentioned you at the birthday banquet. If you fail to place in the Second Class in next year's spring metropolitan examinations, you will become a laughingstock.","Ye Liangyu had full confidence in Song Qiming's ability to pass the examinations and become a presented scholar.","But merely passing was not enough; his ranking had to be high. The starting point for a newly minted scholar was crucial. If he wanted to reach the pinnacle of officialdom in the future, his very first step had to be entering the Hanlin Academy.","To enter the academy, placing in the Second Class was the absolute minimum requirement. As long as Qiming could achieve that, Ye Liangyu could pull the strings to get him in.","The words Second Class had barely registered in Song Qiming's mind before they were instantly blown away by the title County Princess. His eyes widened larger than a bull's, and his slightly parted lips and throat trembled so much that he could not even speak.","The Emperor conferred the title of County Princess upon his sister?","His expression suddenly relaxed. He was just about to jump up in wild ecstasy when he noticed numerous officials in their official robes stealthily glancing their way. His arms stiffened, and he forcefully suppressed his excitement, though he simply could not lower the wide grin on his face.","This was a County Princess, a proper third-rank title! Buying those potatoes had been entirely worth it; they had struck gold.","Sister, hurry up and tell me what happened at the birthday banquet. I am dying to know right now.","Seeing him grinning so widely that his eyes had narrowed into slits, Song Jinzhao gave a helpless but doting smile. Let us get in the carriage and return to the estate first.","Song Qiming nodded vigorously. Overjoyed, he carefully supported Song Jinzhao's arm, allowing her to board the carriage first.","Following behind them, Ye Liangyu shook his head with a sigh. It was only in front of Song Jinzhao that Qiming acted like a child who had not yet fully grown up, showing such deep reliance on his elder sister.","After returning to his princely estate, Xiao Rongyan stormed fiercely into Li Qinyun's room to interrogate her.","Did you not say that you and Song Jinzhao had a delightful conversation, that she was already leaning toward me, and that she promised to persuade Ye Liangyu to pledge his allegiance to me? Why did she not tell you about presenting the potatoes today, causing me to miss out on an absolutely massive achievement?","Awakened by the noise, Li Qinyun was still lying in bed. Before she could even open her eyes, she was met with a barrage of furious accusations. She looked at Xiao Rongyan with utter confusion, having no idea what had happened.","What potatoes? This concubine knows nothing of this...","Xiao Rongyan was so furious that his face turned bright red. He forcefully swung his fist, terrifying Li Qinyun so much that she instinctively squeezed her eyes shut. Her shoulders trembled as she braced herself for his blow, but after a long moment of feeling no pain, she opened her eyes to find that his fist had slammed into the bedding.","Send an invitation to Song Jinzhao tomorrow. I want to see her personally. Watching Xiao Rongyan fling his sleeves and storm out, followed by the heavy slam of the door against its frame, Li Qinyun collapsed onto the bed as if all the strength had been drained from her body.","What on earth was going on?","Was today not the Emperor's birthday banquet? How did Song Jinzhao get involved, and what was all this about potatoes?","The maidservant guarding outside the room had lost all color in her face. Only after Xiao Rongyan had left did she hurriedly rush inside.","She knelt by the edge of the bed, her face full of worry. My lady, are you alright?","Li Qinyun shook her head, completely flustered. I am fine.","She blinked, steadying her nerves as she looked at her personal maidservant, and ordered, Tomorrow morning, you must leave the estate immediately and find out exactly what happened at the Emperor's birthday banquet today. Especially anything concerning Song Jinzhao.","The maidservant nodded frantically, her head bobbing faster than a chick pecking at rice. This servant understands. I will go the moment the sun rises."]},{"number":220,"title":"Chapter 220: The Emperor of Decisive Action, a Missive from the Prince Ying's Mansion","paragraphs":["When they returned to the Ye Manor, Song Shixue was keeping watch over the sleeping Song Anhao, still awake herself. Hearing Xuetuan's low growl from the courtyard, she threw off her quilt, got out of bed, and walked out of the room.","Seeing that it was Song Jinzhao and Song Qiming returning, her face instantly bloomed into a radiant smile as she went to greet them. \"Sister, Brother.\"","Noticing how thinly dressed she was, Song Jinzhao reached out to guide her back into the room, asking with gentle concern, \"Why are you still awake so late?\"","Song Shixue rubbed her eyes. \"I couldn't sleep without you two back.\"","Song Qiming plopped down onto a round stool and immediately started pouring himself some water. Having waited outside the palace gates for over two hours and talking too much on the carriage ride back, his throat was completely parched.","The ice-cold liquid slid down his throat into his stomach. A few drops escaped the corner of his mouth, which he quickly wiped away.","He asked with eager anticipation, \"Shixue, guess what reward the Emperor bestowed upon our sister?\"","Song Shixue looked at Song Jinzhao, who was calmly sitting in a chair grinding ink. \"Did she become a Lady of the Commandery?\"","According to what they had discussed before, being promoted to a Lady of the County wasn't enough; such a massive contribution deserved the title of Lady of the Commandery.","Song Qiming shook his head with a wide grin. \"More than that! The Emperor has officially titled her as County Princess Linghui. He also rewarded her with a thousand taels of gold, a thousand acres of fertile land, and even gave her a mansion.\"","On their way back, his teacher had mentioned that even he hadn't anticipated such a generous reward, which showed just how highly the Emperor regarded their sister.","Song Shixue's mouth fell open, unable to close, and her eyes gradually grew as bright and burning as the sun.","Before coming to the capital, the phrase she had heard the most was that high-ranking officials were everywhere here—if a brick fell from the sky, it would hit someone with a red-buttoned hat. To say she hadn't been worried would be a lie.","Now that her sister was a County Princess, they no longer had to worry about being bullied when they went out.","Among the four siblings, Song Qiming and Song Shixue were so excited that it took a long time for their emotions to settle, and they didn't even know when they finally fell asleep.","Song Jinzhao and Song Anhao slept the deepest. Having been busy for several days, the matter was finally settled, and they could relax and get a good night's sleep.","Compared to the good night's sleep enjoyed at the Ye Manor, some people spent a completely sleepless night.","During the morning court session the next day, several officials sported dark circles under their eyes. Thinking about what was to happen later, they had to keep their nerves highly strung.","Emperor Xiao Chengjing said sternly, \"My beloved Minister Dong, the Court of National Granaries will be responsible for planting the one hundred and fifty catties of potatoes presented by County Princess Linghui. If there is anything you do not understand, go consult the County Princess. I want to see four thousand catties of potatoes after the new year.\"","Dong Yuanbin, the Chief Minister of the Court of National Granaries, stepped out from the ranks of civil officials, knelt on both knees, and responded with a resonant and powerful voice, \"This humble subject receives the decree.\"","\"My beloved Minister Gu, I command you to lead a team to review all historical records and texts concerning maritime affairs in the Chongwen Pavilion. Refine them based on the nautical chart provided by County Princess Linghui. I want to know where this unknown new continent is located.\"","\"This humble subject obeys the decree.\" Gu Qishan gritted his teeth and accepted the order, though he was already beginning to fret inwardly.","From ancient times to the present, no one had ever ventured into the deep ocean. Even if they found something, who would know if it was true or false? If an expedition encountered disaster and they died at sea like those foreigners, the Emperor would be furious and place the blame on him. He would be the one to suffer.","Li Qinyun's maidservant went out at the crack of dawn to gather information and hurried back half an hour later.","\"Your Ladyship, at the birthday banquet yesterday, Song Jinzhao presented a birthday gift to the Emperor. The Emperor was so immensely pleased that he conferred upon her the title of County Princess Linghui on the spot.\"","Having not slept well all night, Li Qinyun had a terrible headache. She immediately demanded, \"What birthday gift?\"","The maidservant replied, \"It is the potato that the Prince mentioned. It is said to yield a thousand catties per acre. The news has already spread throughout the bustling markets of the capital, and everyone is calling it a divine artifact.\"","Li Qinyun slumped onto the soft couch in a daze, muttering to herself, \"She became a County Princess this quickly?\"","If she had known, she would have invited Song Jinzhao to the manor the day before yesterday. Now that she was a County Princess and currently in the limelight, it would be impossible to suppress her with authority anymore.","After pondering for a long time, Li Qinyun personally wrote an invitation and handed it to her maidservant.","\"Deliver this invitation personally to Song Jinzhao at the Ye Manor. Tell her that I have missed her dearly since we parted in Anyang, and invite both her and her brother to our manor for a chat.\"","Li Qinyun was actually unsure if they would come, but since Prince Ying had given the order, she had to send this invitation whether she wanted to or not.","When Song Jinzhao received the invitation, the palace eunuchs had just left. The table in the room was covered with various rewards: trays of gold and silver jewelry, fine silks and satins, as well as two exquisite red lacquer boxes.","One of them was open, revealing it was full of gold ingots. Although not large in volume, it was very heavy. Lifting it slightly, one could estimate it weighed about forty kilograms, roughly a thousand taels of gold.","The other box contained three title deeds. The mansion was located near the center of the inner city and covered an area of fourteen acres.","As for the thousand acres of fertile land, it was actually two royal manors that added up to exactly a thousand acres.","Song Shixue stared at the elegant, neat calligraphy on the invitation and asked in confusion, \"Why does Brother have to go too?\"","Prince Ying's secondary consort was a female family member; why would she invite a male guest?","Song Jinzhao tossed the invitation onto the table. \"The one who wants to see Qiming is not Prince Ying's secondary consort, but Prince Ying himself.\"","Thinking about how Ye Liangyu was at odds with the two princes in the court, Song Shixue clenched her fists, looking somewhat worried.","\"Is Prince Ying going to deal with Brother?\" Prince Ying and Lord Ye did not get along, and since her brother was Lord Ye's student, this move felt like it would bring trouble.","Song Jinzhao closed the boxes containing the gold and title deeds. \"Perhaps he wants to recruit him, or maybe it's a warning.\"","Song Shixue frowned in distress. \"Can you just not go?\"","Song Jinzhao replied, \"Not going will only cause more trouble. Since the invitation was sent by a female family member, I will just play dumb and not bring your brother along.\"","She truly couldn't feel at ease letting Qiming face Prince Ying alone.","Song Shixue bit her lip. \"I can accompany you to see Prince Ying's secondary consort, Sister.\"","Song Jinzhao patted her head but shook it in disagreement.","\"Don't worry. I've met Li Qinyun before; she won't do anything to me. Even if she wanted to make a move, she wouldn't choose this time to do it.\"","The matter of the potatoes was not yet fully settled, and she had just been titled a County Princess. If something happened to her in Prince Ying's manor, the Emperor would definitely blame Xiao Rongyan. He wouldn't dare, nor would it be worth the cost.","After the morning court session ended, the news of the two commands the Emperor had issued back-to-back spread out. In just an hour, the fact that the Court of National Granaries was responsible for planting potatoes had already spread through every street and alley.","Especially the commoners who made a living by farming; they were all inquiring about where outside the city the Court of National Granaries would plant them, wanting to go take a look.","After court, Ye Liangyu did not go to the Censorate. Instead, he returned to the manor, found Song Qiming who was practicing martial arts, and said, \"For the next three months, the Imperial Academy will conduct a series of rigorous examinations and training for students in preparation for the metropolitan examination. I will take you to see the Chancellor this afternoon, and you will start attending the Imperial Academy tomorrow.\"","He had to attend court every day, and the Censorate also had a lot of official business.","As early as when they left Anyang Prefecture, he had already decided to have Song Qiming study at the Imperial Academy for a period, which was why he had instructed him to come to the capital immediately after the examination results were posted.","Previously, he had been worried that Song Qiming might be looked down upon by the children of officials at the Imperial Academy, given his humble background.","But now that Song Jinzhao had been titled a County Princess, Song Qiming's status had also become extraordinary by association, so he no longer needed to worry."]},{"number":221,"title":"Chapter 221: The mansion bestowed by the emperor has not yet been renovated, Wangyue Tower","paragraphs":["After finishing his conversation with Ye Liangyu, Song Qiming found Song Jinzhao and told her about his plans to attend the Imperial Academy.","Song Jinzhao, who was just about to head out to look at a residence, raised her eyebrows in pleasant surprise. \"That is perfect. Tomorrow, when I go to Prince Ying's Manor, I will tell his secondary consort that you have gone to study at the Imperial Academy and have no free time.\"","Song Qiming asked in confusion, \"Why would she invite me?\"","\"Eldest sister~\" Song Anhao called out as he ambled over slowly, riding on Xuetuan's back.","Song Jinzhao bent down to pick him up, turning her head to answer Song Qiming, \"She probably wants to recruit you, and conveniently use you to bring down your teacher.\"","Lanxi stayed behind to guard the courtyard and Xuetuan, while Qingshuang drove the carriage, taking Song Jinzhao, Song Shixue, and Song Anhao to see the courtyard bestowed by the Emperor.","Staying at the Ye residence indefinitely was not a long-term solution. Song Jinzhao had originally planned to buy a house herself after the birthday banquet, but since the Emperor had rewarded her with a ready-made one, it was best to go over early and see what needed to be tidied up so they could move in sooner.","Upon arriving, they found not only a flatbed cart parked at the entrance but also people standing on the steps wearing official uniforms, with noisy sounds coming from inside.","Qingshuang turned her head and whispered into the carriage, \"Eldest Miss, there are people inside. They look like government officials.\"","The Principal of the Ministry of Works, who was directing his subordinates to hang up a plaque, saw Song Jinzhao step down from the carriage. He immediately ran down the steps, stopped in front of her, and bowed respectfully. \"I am Fang Zhixing, Principal of the Construction Bureau under the Ministry of Works. Greetings to County Princess Linghui.\"","He gritted his teeth, feeling extremely annoyed inwardly. How did she arrive so quickly?","If he had known, he would have worked through the night yesterday. Now, he could only try to smooth things over with her for the time being.","\"Lord Fang, there is no need for such formality. What is going on here?\" Song Jinzhao looked up at the plaque suspended beneath the door beam. Carved onto it were the words 'County Princess Manor'. The black paint outlining the characters had not yet fully dried, indicating it was likely rushed.","Fang Zhixing hurriedly explained, \"To answer the County Princess, this residence originally belonged to a third-rank official in the Ministry of Personnel. During the rainy season this year, floods occurred in Jiangnan, and it was discovered that he had accepted bribes from local officials. The Emperor confiscated his estate, and this mansion was among the seized properties.\"","\"The Ministry of Works had previously finished repairing the house, but a few days ago, heavy winds and rain blew off quite a few roof tiles, and trees in the courtyard were uprooted, leaving the landscaping a bit messy. Since the Emperor's reward came so suddenly, I brought men over early this morning to fix it up and clean the place out. In just a few more days, the County Princess will be able to move in comfortably.\"","In truth, the Ministry of Works had never finished repairing the house at all. They had been busy with other matters recently and figured the Emperor would not bestow the mansion upon anyone anytime soon, so they had slacked off and delayed the work.","Who could have known that a County Princess Linghui would suddenly appear out of nowhere, and that she would be granted this exact residence? When he went to work at the Ministry that morning and found out, he was completely panicked.","Song Jinzhao's gaze swept across the blue sky. The sunlight was so bright it was almost dazzling.","For the four days since they entered the capital, the weather had been perfectly fine every day. There had been no wind or rain, so how could tiles have fallen, let alone winds strong enough to uproot trees?","Even though she knew Fang Zhixing was lying to her, Song Jinzhao chose not to expose him. It simply meant moving in a few days later; there was no need to point it out and put him in an awkward position.","\"Since that is the case, I will have to trouble Lord Fang. Once the repairs are done, just send someone to the Ye residence to let us know.\"","Fang Zhixing nodded repeatedly, seeing them off to their carriage with a face full of flattery.","Song Shixue asked, \"Sister, are we going back now?\"","Song Jinzhao shook her head and instructed Qingshuang, \"Go to the liveliest market street in the capital. I want to take a stroll.\"","Qingshuang immediately changed direction and drove south.","The most prosperous main thoroughfare in the inner city was undoubtedly Chang'an Avenue, which led straight from the city gates to the Imperial City. The buildings on both sides of the street were also the newest and most beautiful.","The four-story Moon Ascension Pavilion stood tall in the middle of Chang'an Avenue, a true testament to the prosperity of the capital.","After wandering around the area for a bit, seeing that it was nearing noon, Song Jinzhao lifted the carriage curtain and said, \"Let's go eat at the Moon Gazing Tower.\"","The carriage stopped at the entrance of the restaurant. The waiter greeting guests at the door saw Song Jinzhao step down and immediately came over enthusiastically. \"Will the young lady be sitting on the first floor or the second floor?\"","Her face was unfamiliar, so it was likely her first time here. Though her carriage was large, it lacked decoration, suggesting she was probably the daughter of an ordinary merchant family.","Song Jinzhao withdrew her gaze from the main hall. There really were quite a few people at this hour.","\"The first floor. Please arrange a table in the corner for us.\"","The waiter led the four of them to the very last table by the window. \"There are walls on both sides, so it has the fewest people here. What would you esteemed guests like to eat?\"","Song Jinzhao replied, \"Serve us a few of your restaurant's best-selling signature dishes, along with four bowls of rice.\"","\"Right away! Please enjoy some tea first, the food will be served shortly.\" The water poured from the teapot was still steaming. It had a light color and a sweet taste, clearly not made from inferior tea leaves.","After waiting for nearly fifteen minutes, the waiter began bringing out the dishes one after another.","\"Sheep Milk Fish, Fresh Stir-fried River Shrimp, Roasted Quail, Scallion Vinegar Chicken, Broth Bathed Embroidered Meatballs, Taro Soup, and Chrysanthemum Cake. These are all our signature dishes at the Moon Gazing Tower. Please take your time and enjoy.\"","Looking at the seven dishes filling the table, the plates seemed large, but the portions were quite small. The only commonality was the exquisite plating and beautiful color combinations.","Song Shixue leaned over to stare at a few dishes she had never seen before. \"The color of this fish soup is so white, it looks quite fake.\"","\"Chopstick Spring... isn't this just quail?\" The name sounded nice, but without seeing the actual dish, one really wouldn't know what it was.","It looked expensive, and gave the illusion that it wouldn't be filling at all.","Song Jinzhao picked up a spoon and first scooped half a bowl of the thick Sheep Milk Fish broth. \"Let's taste it and see how it is.\"","Since the first-floor hall could be fully seated during mealtime, the taste shouldn't be too bad.","The moment it entered her mouth, Song Jinzhao raised her eyebrows in surprise. \"It is fish stewed in sheep's milk. There is no gamey smell at all; you completely can't tell.\"","Hearing that it was sheep's milk, Song Shixue immediately took a taste. Sure enough, it was sheep's milk.","Seeing this, Song Anhao refused to let Qingshuang help him. He steadily scooped half a bowl for himself with a spoon, put his mouth to the rim of the bowl, and took a big gulp. As it slid into his stomach, he felt a warm and cozy sensation inside.","He generously gave a thumbs up. \"It is delicious! It's smooth and fresher than regular fish soup, and it seems to have the fragrance of osmanthus.\"","The waiter, who was just bringing over the rice, heard this and smiled. \"This young master has a very sharp palate. The sheep's milk used to make this dish has fresh osmanthus added just as it is about to boil. When serving, the osmanthus is filtered out, which is why it has a faint osmanthus scent.\"","The Fresh Stir-fried River Shrimp contained only scallion segments for garnish alongside the shrimp. The meat was firm, and you could tell it had been caught fresh today.","The skin of the quail was coated with honey and sprinkled with sesame seeds, giving it a bright, translucent red color and firm meat.","By the end of the meal, Song Jinzhao had already formed a good initial impression of the Moon Gazing Tower.","The ingredients were fresh, the dishes had their own unique characteristics, and the head chef not only possessed great culinary skills but also knew how to innovate. No wonder they were able to run such a large restaurant."]},{"number":222,"title":"Chapter 222: Song Gaoli Becomes Suspicious, Dong Yuanbin Pays a Visit for Advice","paragraphs":["Duan Yanhua, coming in from the door, spotted Song Jinzhao sitting in the corner at a glance. He quickly pulled Song Gaoli, who was trailing at the very back, behind him, and walked toward Song Jinzhao with a pleasantly surprised look on his face.","This humble official greets County Princess Linghui. Why are you sitting in the main hall?","Hearing the voice, Song Jinzhao looked up at Duan Yanhua. He was accompanied by seven young men, among whom was Song Gaoli.","I wanted to join the bustle, so I didn't go upstairs. Is Lord Duan bringing his students out for a meal?","Song Qiming had mentioned that Duan Yanhua had taken in many students and even housed quite a few in his residence. Presumably, these were them.","Sister Jinzhao. Song Gaoli smiled, his eyebrows twitching as he winked at Song Jinzhao. He had been startled when he learned she was titled a County Princess. If he hadn't been unable to leave that morning, he would have run to the Ye Residence long ago.","Song Jinzhao gave a slight nod in response.","The waiter standing to the side watched their exchange dumbfounded.","County Princess Linghui? The one who presented the miraculous crop yielding a thousand catties per mu?","The waiter's gaze landed on Song Jinzhao, his eyes full of adoration.","To think a County Princess was so low-profile. He hadn't noticed at all earlier, assuming she was just the daughter of some merchant who had just arrived in the capital, with no real status.","Seeing that Duan Yanhua had completely ignored them, the other six students stood frozen, unable to advance or retreat, awkwardly not knowing what to do.","Seeing that Song Shixue and Song Anhao were both present but Song Qiming was nowhere to be seen, Song Gaoli asked curiously, Did Qiming not come?","Song Jinzhao shook her head. He is reading at the residence and didn't come out.","Hearing this, Song Gaoli just wanted to press his lips together and sigh. He was already so outstanding yet still wouldn't relax. How were ordinary people like them supposed to feel?","Duan Yanhua really wanted to sit down and eat with Song Jinzhao and the others, but the food on their table was clearly almost finished, and they looked ready to leave. After careful consideration, he decided to bid farewell.","As he went upstairs, his peripheral vision remained fixed downstairs. This caused him to miss a step and nearly fall. Had Song Gaoli not pushed him from behind, he would have definitely planted his face onto the stairs and cracked his head open.","Once Song Anhao finished polishing off the rice in his bowl, Song Jinzhao called out to the waiter, Waiter, the bill.","The waiter bowed at least twice as low as when Song Jinzhao and her group had first entered, his neck almost level with the table.","In a respectful posture, he kept his head down, not daring to look directly into Song Jinzhao's eyes. His voice trembled slightly but was very clear, To answer the County Princess, it is a total of four taels and two mace of silver.","Song Jinzhao's fingers paused slightly as she reached for her coin purse. She placed the silver on the table. The food was delicious, but the price was truly steep, enough to cover a year's expenses for an ordinary family of three.","On the second floor by the window, Song Gaoli saw Duan Yanhua craning his neck to look out at the street, his eyes following Song Jinzhao's movements. Doubts inevitably arose in his heart.","Only when her figure was out of sight did Duan Yanhua withdraw his gaze. He said to Song Gaoli, Miss Song has been titled a County Princess. In the future, you must interact more with Song Qiming. I heard that Vice Minister Ye has also taught you. Tomorrow, as your teacher, I will take you to visit the Ye Residence.","The other six sitting nearby all looked at Song Gaoli. Aside from envy, a trace of jealousy sprouted in their hearts.","They originally thought that someone who came in at the bottom of the ranks would definitely be inferior to them. To their surprise, Song Gaoli actually knew Vice Minister Ye and had a deep relationship with the newly titled County Princess Linghui. They had underestimated him.","However, upon hearing this, not only was Song Gaoli unhappy, but the doubts in his heart grew even stronger.","Did he value him, or did he value Sister Jinzhao's power, or did he want to use him to get in touch with Lord Ye?","Looking back now, did Duan Yanhua really accept him as a student because of that poem? Or were there other reasons?","After leaving the Moon Gazing Tower, Song Jinzhao strolled around the vicinity for quite a while. Song Shixue asked, Sister, are you thinking of buying a shop?","The family's businesses were all in Anyang Prefecture. If they were to reside permanently in the capital, the expenses would be high, and they would definitely have to find a way to make money.","Song Jinzhao nodded. Let's first see what the commoners in the capital like and how the market is. We'll go to the broker in a few days.","By the time they returned to the Ye Residence, Ye Liangyu had already taken Song Qiming out.","Having played for several hours, Song Anhao grew sleepy as soon as he returned to his room. He simply took off his outer coat and slipped under the covers to sleep.","Song Jinzhao and Song Shixue sat on the chairs outside the room, discussing a few ancient prescriptions left behind in ancient medical texts.","The Ye Residence did not have many servants, and with Ye Liangyu as the sole master, there wasn't much work. Most of the time, it was exceptionally quiet.","Osmanthus trees were planted everywhere in the residence. It was currently their blooming season. With a light breeze, the fragrance wafted over, far richer than what they had eaten at noon, making it feel like they were soaking in an osmanthus bath.","The rustling sound of shoe soles scraping against the stone-paved path entered the courtyard. Xuetuan, who was eating meat, lifted its head, while Lanxi and Qingshuang turned to look.","The gatekeeper was breathing rapidly, his voice a bit breathless. County Princess, Lord Dong from the Court of the National Granaries is outside requesting an audience.","Song Jinzhao raised her head. Which Lord Dong?","Gatekeeper: Lord Dong Yuanbin, the Chief Minister of the Court of the National Granaries.","Let him in. It was probably regarding the planting of potatoes.","As soon as Dong Yuanbin, dressed in his official uniform, stepped into the courtyard, a hoarse roar from Xuetuan scared him so much he didn't dare to move a muscle, his eyes wide as brass bells.","Why would there be a tiger in the Ye Residence? And not locked in a cage, was it going to eat someone?","Xuetuan! Song Shixue shouted a reprimand. She stood up, walked over, and grabbed the soft flesh on the back of its neck, giving it a good rub.","My Lord, there is no need to be afraid. Xuetuan is very well-behaved and doesn't bite.","Dong Yuanbin stared at the white tiger acting spoiled like a dog at Song Shixue's feet.","To think a fierce beast had two faces. It didn't bite people, more likely, it just didn't bite her.","Giving Xuetuan a wide berth, he walked up to Song Jinzhao and bowed. This humble official greets County Princess Linghui. At the morning assembly today, the Emperor placed the matter of planting potatoes under the charge of my Court of the National Granaries. I have come today to ask the County Princess for guidance on how to plant them. Are there any areas that require special attention?","Song Jinzhao pushed the ledger she had just brought out from her room toward Dong Yuanbin. This is the growth record of the potatoes from sowing to maturity. In the winter, inside the vegetable greenhouse, one must constantly monitor the temperature to prevent the cold from freezing and damaging the stems and leaves. Otherwise, not only will the potatoes fail to grow, but they will also easily rot.","Dong Yuanbin nodded while committing Song Jinzhao's words to memory. There were only so few seeds; if they rotted in the ground, the Emperor would chop off his wretched head.","Also, eating potatoes that have turned green or sprouted will cause poisoning. I have written the antidote prescription at the very back, but it is best not to eat them at all. If consumed in excess, there might not be enough time to save them, and it could lead to death.","Dong Yuanbin nodded vigorously. At the birthday banquet yesterday, Song Jinzhao had described the symptoms of those poisoned crew members, and he had taken it to heart then.","Please rest assured, County Princess Linghui. When we have enough seeds for the commoners to plant, we will definitely remind them repeatedly.","He opened the record and began to read it word by word, asking Song Jinzhao whenever he encountered something he didn't understand. He didn't leave until Ye Liangyu and Song Qiming returned from outside."]},{"number":223,"title":"Chapter 223: Duan Yanhua's True Motive","paragraphs":["Song Gaoli walked out of the Duan residence's main gate as if nothing had happened. Once he was a good distance away, he decisively ducked into an alley and looked back. Seeing that no one was following him, he changed direction and headed toward the Ye residence.","His teacher was adamant about taking him to the Ye residence tomorrow to visit Lord Ye and Sister Jinzhao, having even prepared the gifts. He needed to go and give Qiming a heads-up first.","In the study, Song Qiming frowned and said, Are you saying that Duan Yanhua took you in as a student with ulterior motives?","Song Gaoli lowered his head, his eyelids drooping, feeling extremely disheartened.","Yeah. Today, when we ran into Sister Jinzhao at the Moonview Restaurant, his attitude toward me suddenly became exceptionally good. He even mentioned that Lord Ye used to teach me and insisted on dragging me over for a visit tomorrow.","Song Qiming turned his head to look at Ye Liangyu, who was sitting in a chair. Teacher, how much do you know about Duan Yanhua? Is he Prince Qi's man or Prince Ying's man?","If the other party had an agenda, the mastermind behind it could only be one of these two.","When Song Gaoli came over a few days ago, Ye Liangyu was not in the residence, so he did not know that Gaoli had also come to the capital.","He had passed the provincial examination in the very last place again; heaven truly treated him well. However, being taken in as a student by Duan Yanhua was a bit of bad luck.","He is neither Prince Qi's man nor Prince Ying's man. This person is full of empty ambitions and loves to daydream. He shrinks back when encountering difficulties, wants to take shortcuts but lacks ability, and has been stuck in the Hanlin Academy for over a decade without moving up or down. Neither Prince Qi nor Prince Ying thinks highly of him.","Starting from the last metropolitan examination, he began taking in students, pinning his hopes on them, thinking that one day they might strike it rich and pull him up with them.","Song Gaoli was dumbfounded. Pull him up? It is still a question whether I can even pass the exam.","Ye Liangyu continued, He likely did not take you in as a student thinking you could pass, but rather to build connections and curry favor with his superior.","Song Gaoli understood instantly. It was exactly what he had thought at noon: Sister Jinzhao and Lord Ye were the connections Duan Yanhua wanted to make. He was indeed just a stepping stone. Who is his superior? I do not know him.","Song Qiming interjected, Chancellor Fei of the Hanlin Academy has a very close relationship with Teacher.","Since Duan Yanhua was a compiler at the Hanlin Academy, his motive was already crystal clear.","However, what puzzled Song Qiming was, Teacher, when we asked around earlier, everyone said this Lord Duan had excellent character and took great care of the younger generation.","Ye Liangyu curled his lips into a smile and shook his head. Duan Yanhua cares deeply about his reputation. Three years ago, his student who failed the exam was full of praise for him when returning home, even hugging him and crying at the city gate upon leaving the capital. The scene was quite touching.","Song Gaoli and Song Qiming felt a sense of having been tricked. Was it true gratitude for the teacher's kindness and reluctance to part, or was it just an act?","Song Gaoli licked his lips. Thinking back on their interactions recently, it did not seem that exaggerated. It was quite mundane, and they spent less time together each day than he did with the teachers at the academy.","If that is the case, then it is fine. My Lord, you can just ignore him. I did not expect to definitely pass this time anyway. At worst, I will just return to Anyang Prefecture and take the exam again in three years. He still had that much self-awareness.","Ye Liangyu's profound gaze shifted between Song Qiming and Song Gaoli.","There were not many newly minted provincial graduates who were close to Qiming. Since the two had such a good relationship, and Song Gaoli had a bit of luck, he might become a helpful ally to Qiming in the future.","Tomorrow, Qiming will go to study at the Imperial Academy, his sister is going to Prince Ying's estate, and I will be at the Censorate handling the official duties left over from today. You just pretend you do not know anything and come over with Duan Yanhua. You do not need to worry about anything else.","Song Gaoli was completely baffled. Why was Qiming suddenly going to study at the Imperial Academy? Was not the metropolitan examination only a little over three months away?","Sister Jinzhao was going to Prince Ying's estate? Was not Ye Liangyu at odds with him?","The next day, when Song Gaoli went out with Duan Yanhua, his heart kept pounding. He could not help but feel a bit panicked.","Vice Censor-in-Chief Ye is not at home? Isn't today a rest day? Duan Yanhua frowned in confusion, suspecting that Ye Liangyu just did not want to see him.","In previous years, he had been shut out by Fei Yanzhang time and time again, and had been lectured by him both openly and covertly several times. These two men had the same temperament, but this time he had brought Song Gaoli with him.","Yunhe, who had been specially left behind, answered with a calm smile, There were quite a few official duties left over from yesterday, so my lord went to the Censorate early this morning.","Duan Yanhua asked, Then what about County Princess Linghui?","Yunhe shook his head again. Prince Ying's secondary consort invited the County Princess to be a guest at Prince Ying's estate, so she is not here right now either.","Duan Yanhua's expression tensed up, and he subconsciously took two steps back. Why would Prince Ying's secondary consort invite Song Jinzhao to the estate?","What about Song Qiming? Is he reading in the residence?","Yunhe shook his head for the third time. Young Master Song went to study at the Imperial Academy today and won't be back until tonight.","One blow after another, Duan Yanhua's entire body went stiff at this moment. The Imperial Academy? It had only been a few days, and they had already squeezed someone into the Imperial Academy?","Wasn't having Ye Liangyu's one-on-one guidance enough? He still had to go to the Imperial Academy!","Yunhe considerately added, Right now, only Miss Shixue and the young Master Song are in the residence. Would Lord Duan like to see them?","Duan Yanhua shook his head with a frustrated expression. No need. I will come back another day.","What was the use of seeing two children who couldn't make any decisions? One of them was still at an age of playing with mud and knew absolutely nothing.","On the way back, Duan Yanhua asked Song Gaoli, Did Song Qiming tell you that he was going to study at the Imperial College?","Song Gaoli shook his head, playing dumb. I don't know. I haven't seen him these past two days.","Meanwhile, after leading Song Jinzhao to the main hall, the maid quickly rushed back to the courtyard to report to Li Qinyun, Your Highness, only County Princess Linghui has arrived. Young Master Song did not come.","Snap. The jade hairpin in her hand fell onto the dressing table and broke into two pieces. She turned her head anxiously. How could that be? I clearly wrote on the invitation to invite both siblings.","The maid bit her lip tightly. But County Princess Linghui really only brought a single maidservant with her.","Ignoring a strand of hair that had fallen over her shoulder, Li Qinyun furrowed her brows and immediately asked, Is His Highness still in the study?","The maid nodded. Guyun, who serves by His Highness's side, already came over to ask a moment ago. Do you need this servant to go inform His Highness?","Li Qinyun took a deep breath and adjusted her collar. No need, I will go tell him myself. Instruct the servants to serve a few more pastries. I will go over shortly.","Song Jinzhao looked at the plum blossom cakes on the table, which were exactly the same as the ones served when she was a guest at Ming Garden. Was this a reminder to her? Or did the Prince Ying's Manor serve this to all their guests?","In the study, upon hearing that Song Qiming had not come, Xiao Rongyan swept his hand and pushed the brush rack off the table. One of the brushes hit Li Qinyun's white dress, leaving an ugly black ink stain. She clearly has no regard for this prince!","Afraid that Xiao Rongyan's anger would spread to her, Li Qinyun spoke softly to soothe him, Perhaps Song Qiming didn't come because it was I who invited him. After all, this is the inner courtyard of the manor, and as a male guest, he must avoid any impropriety.","Xiao Rongyan glared furiously, his spittle flying all over Li Qinyun's face.","Song Jinzhao is no fool. She definitely knows that I am the one who wants to see Song Qiming. This is a deliberate refusal. It seems she hasn't learned enough of a lesson from Ye Liangyu.","With her face wet, Li Qinyun didn't dare use her handkerchief to wipe it, terrified of stepping out of line and losing Xiao Rongyan's favor.","Unable to persuade him otherwise, she could only lower her head and let Xiao Rongyan vent his anger."]},{"number":224,"title":"Chapter 224: Song Jinzhao Drives the King of England Mad","paragraphs":["Hearing footsteps, Song Jinzhao looked up. Xiao Rongyan walked in with a displeased expression, his robes billowing high around him as if he were about to hit someone.","Li Qinyun followed behind him; though she felt miserable inside, she still had to wear a smile on her face.","\"This subject greets His Highness the Prince of Ying,\" Song Jinzhao rose and gave a slight curtsy. As she looked up, she met Xiao Rongyan's icy gaze, which looked as if it had been dipped in poison.","She looked away, pretending not to notice anything, and sat back down to leisurely sip her tea.","Provoked by Song Jinzhao's dismissive glance, Xiao Rongyan immediately demanded, \"Why didn't your younger brother come?\"","Song Jinzhao set down her teacup. \"It's not convenient to bring him to the inner courtyard of the prince's estate. After all, my brother is quite good-looking.\"","Li Qinyun looked at Song Jinzhao in disbelief. What did that mean? Did she think she would take a fancy to a thirteen-year-old brat?","Xiao Rongyan clenched his fists, feeling a stifling tightness in his chest.","He glared at Li Qinyun, then said sarcastically to Song Jinzhao, \"The County Princess worries entirely too much. As the top scholar of the Longbei provincial exam, your brother will surely place high in next year's metropolitan exam. I merely wished to meet this young talent. I wonder if he can come tomorrow?\"","Song Jinzhao pursed her lips in a fake smile. Inviting him today, then inviting him tomorrow. Staying at home every day, you really have too much free time.","\"I'm afraid not. Vice Censor-in-Chief Ye believes my brother's experience is still shallow, and next year's metropolitan exam will be full of top-tier scholars. He was worried that studying at home behind closed doors would be detrimental, so he had him enroll in the Imperial Academy. He already started today.\"","Li Qinyun peeked at Xiao Rongyan's expression from the corner of her eye. Her heart began to pound; she felt something bad was about to happen.","Xiao Rongyan sneered, \"The Imperial Academy? Getting him arranged so quickly, Ye Liangyu's power is truly vast.\"","Song Jinzhao curled her lips into a smile and immediately retorted, \"Your Highness is mistaken. It is common practice for the Imperial Academy to admit outstanding students from various provinces. My brother was already qualified. Furthermore, he is my brother; even if Vice Censor-in-Chief Ye hadn't spoken up, all I would have to do is ask the Emperor, and securing a spot wouldn't be difficult.\"","Xiao Rongyan's pupils darkened as if he wanted to chop Song Jinzhao into pieces.","\"When Yun'er returned to Anyang Prefecture to visit her family, she reminded the County Princess that a divine crop like the potato should have been handed over to me, rather than rashly presented to my imperial father. Next time you have something, please inform me in advance.\"","Hearing this, Song Jinzhao raised her eyebrows, making a highly exaggerated expression.","\"To be honest with Your Highness, before I came to the capital, I did consider telling you first. But I am a particularly vulgar person who values profit and power. Your Highness's power is certainly not as great as the Emperor's. Since it's all for the imperial court anyway, after careful consideration, I decided to present it to the Emperor myself, which conveniently saves you the trouble.\"","Li Qinyun fidgeted uneasily, her back already breaking out in a sweat. Seeing the sparks flying thicker by the second, she hastily interrupted, \"His Highness means that if he had known in advance, he definitely would have fought for a greater reward for the County Princess. Compared to Vice Censor-in-Chief Ye, His Highness's status is undoubtedly higher.\"","Song Jinzhao opened her mouth in sudden realization. \"I see! Thinking about it, the title of County Princess doesn't seem to hold much weight in the capital. Why doesn't His Highness go to the palace today and request the title of Commandery Princess for me? That should be about right.\"","Li Qinyun was speechless.","Xiao Rongyan was almost laughing out of anger.","With such a lowly background as a peasant girl, you should be deeply grateful that I am willing to toss a few hundred taels of silver your way.","A Commandery Princess? Pure wishful thinking.","\"The potatoes have already been presented to my imperial father; it is too late to talk about that now. If you can persuade Ye Liangyu to pledge his allegiance to me, I could confer the title of Commandery Princess upon you after I ascend the throne.\"","Heh! Wait until you actually become emperor before you talk.","Song Jinzhao said, \"It's not that I don't want to help Your Highness, but Lord Ye is far too upright and stubborn. I talked until my lips were chapped, but he wouldn't budge. He keeps saying that for the sake of the court, he wouldn't regret it even if he were torn apart by five horses by treacherous officials.\"","\"Actually, I think since both Your Highness and Lord Ye are acting for the good of the court, what difference does it make whether he pledges allegiance or not?\"","\"When Your Highness becomes the Emperor in the future, all the officials in the court will be your subjects. An upright, unyielding minister who does not fear the powerful like Lord Ye will surely become a steadfast pillar for Your Highness, continuing to serve our Dongzhao Kingdom.\"","By now, Li Qinyun had turned mute, unable to utter a single word.","Xiao Rongyan gritted his teeth. She was mocking him.","\"County Princess Linghui is truly articulate. You make me see you in a new light.\"","When he became emperor, he would definitely make her and Ye Liangyu pay.","Song Jinzhao smiled and nodded. \"Thank you for the praise, Your Highness. I am merely a common woman born to a farming family. I haven't read many books and my knowledge is shallow. If I have said anything wrong, I beg Your Highness's forgiveness.\"","The main hall was dead silent, making the sound of Li Qinyun swallowing her saliva exceptionally distinct.","The moment Song Jinzhao stepped out, Xiao Rongyan flipped the table over. He cursed furiously at the air, \"She really is an uneducated village woman! No one would want a woman like her even if she were given away for free. It serves her right that she's still unmarried.\"","Li Qinyun's delicate shoulders trembled in fear, not daring to breathe loudly.","If she had known Song Jinzhao was this difficult to deal with, she wouldn't have gone back to visit her family in the first place, and then none of this would have anything to do with her.","The maid leading the way walked extremely fast, practically flying.","After escorting Song Jinzhao to the door, the maid decisively bolted.","Having angered the Prince, County Princess Linghui would probably never be allowed through the gates of the Ying Prince's Estate again. It was better to stay far away from her.","Qingshuang stared at the maid's retreating back, then turned and whispered into Song Jinzhao's ear, \"Eldest Miss, have we thoroughly offended the Prince of Ying?\"","With the way things looked just now, she had been worried they wouldn't make it out today.","Song Jinzhao replied, \"From the moment Qiming took Mr. Ye as his teacher and I personally presented the potatoes to the Emperor, we had already offended him. Since we are not on the same path, why swallow our pride? Otherwise, they'll just think we're easy to bully.\"","\"Hurry up and unload these things! The Princess Consort urgently needs them tomorrow.\"","A woman dressed in maid's clothing stood on the steps with her hands on her hips, bossing around the servants who were moving boxes. Her attitude was extremely arrogant.","Song Jinzhao, who was just about to leave, shifted her gaze. She deliberately slowed her pace and raised her voice.","\"The Prince of Ying dotes so heavily on his Secondary Consort; the Princess Consort must just be a mere decoration.\"","Qingshuang blinked and instantly understood. She immediately chimed in, \"That's probably the case. Otherwise, His Highness wouldn't have brought only the Secondary Consort to the main hall and left the Princess Consort behind. The Secondary Consort is both intelligent and beautiful. If her background weren't a bit low, she would be more than qualified to be the official Princess Consort.\"","Song Jinzhao stepped onto the carriage, lowering her voice but keeping it just loud enough for the maid on the steps to hear.","\"She's a Secondary Consort now, but that might not be the case in the future. If the Prince of Ying ascends the throne one day, whoever he wants to make Empress will be Empress.\"","Since Xiao Rongyan had so much free time to cause trouble for others, she would set a fire in his own backyard and keep him too occupied to bother her."]},{"number":225,"title":"Chapter 225: The Unhappy British Princess, the Soaring Song Gaoli","paragraphs":["Watching the carriage gradually pull away, the maid's face puffed up with anger.","She stormed over to the gatekeeper, pointed at the back of the carriage, and demanded, \"Who was that just now?\"","The gatekeeper was so frightened that his lips trembled. \"It was County Princess Linghui, the esteemed guest invited by the Secondary Consort today.\"","The maid slapped the gatekeeper across the face. \"What Secondary Consort? There is only one mistress in Prince Ying's Manor, and that is the Princess Consort.\"","\"And why wasn't the Princess Consort informed of County Princess Linghui's visit today?\"","The gatekeeper clutched his face, his legs turning to jelly, and his voice shook violently. \"It was the Secondary Consort—no—Secondary Consort Li who personally gave the order. She said County Princess Linghui is an old friend of hers, and that this was also Prince Ying's intention, which is why the Princess Consort wasn't notified.\"","The maid ground her back teeth and glared fiercely in the direction of Li Qinyun's courtyard.","Upon returning to her own courtyard, she immediately reported the matter to the Princess Consort.","\"Your Highness, if this continues, Secondary Consort Li will surely walk all over you.\"","According to the rules, whenever female guests visited, regardless of whom they were looking for, they had to pay their respects to the official wife first.","The imperial family maintained strict hierarchies. As a secondary consort, Li Qinyun was required to inform the Princess Consort before inviting anyone into the manor, and she could only do so with the latter's permission.","Song Jinzhao had stayed in the manor for such a long time, yet the Princess Consort only found out after she had already left. This incident was an outright challenge to her status as the primary wife. After all, she was the rightful mistress of the manor; Li Qinyun was merely a concubine.","\"Did you just say Prince Ying was also there?\"","The maid lowered her head, feeling aggrieved and full of resentment.","\"The gatekeeper said it was Prince Ying's intention. Song Jinzhao is a county princess, after all. His Highness didn't even call for you to help host the guest; when she left, she probably thought you had fallen out of favor.\"","If the master fell out of favor, the servants would be looked down upon as well. She certainly did not want to be suppressed by Secondary Consort Li's personal maid in the future.","The Princess Consort took a deep breath, thinking of how Prince Ying had allowed Li Qinyun to travel thousands of miles back home to celebrate her father's birthday.","He doted on her so much that, fearing she wouldn't be used to the food outside the manor, he specifically sent a chef along for the journey. The jealousy she had long suppressed began to surge within her.","If this continued, wouldn't Li Qinyun truly overpower her if she gave birth to an imperial grandson one day?","Let alone whether the position of Empress would be snatched away by her, the position of Crown Prince alone could not fall to anyone else; it had to be her own son.","The next day, the Princess Consort went to her maiden home for reinforcements. When she returned, Prince Ying's Manor gained two exceptionally beautiful maids. In just three days, these maids became concubines, causing Xiao Rongyan to stay away from Li Qinyun's courtyard for an entire month.","Meanwhile, Song Gaoli originally thought that since no one was at the Ye Manor, Duan Yanhua would head back. However, halfway there, Duan suddenly changed his mind and took him to visit Hanlin Academy Scholar Fei Yanzhang.","Standing at the unfamiliar entrance of the Fei Manor, Song Gaoli wore a bitter expression, truly not wanting to go in. He felt a shameful sense of brazenly begging at someone's door.","\"Be smart when you see Lord Fei. Mention your relationship with Song Qiming and Vice Censor-in-Chief Ye more often,\" Duan Yanhua whispered to Song Gaoli just before entering, his strict tone carrying a hint of warning.","Song Gaoli didn't say a word and could only nod. Yesterday, Teacher Ye had told him not to worry about anything else, so what should he do now?","Would he be kicked out by Fei Yanzhang?","The two were led to the main hall and sat for quite a while before Fei Yanzhang finally arrived.","His appraising gaze lingered on Song Gaoli for a long moment before shifting away; compared to Song Qiming, this one looked a bit lacking.","\"This humble official greets Your Excellency.\"","Song Gaoli hastily followed suit, bowing with cupped hands. \"Student Song Gaoli pays his respects to Lord Fei.\"","Good heavens, his aura was even more intimidating than Mr. Ye's. Just one sweeping glance made his heart palpitate with fear.","Fei Yanzhang looked displeased as he spoke to Duan Yanhua, \"Is there something that couldn't wait until we are on duty tomorrow? And what are these things for? Remember to take them with you when you leave.\"","Song Gaoli held his breath and swallowed hard. The opening atmosphere was not great; it seemed his teacher's relationship with Lord Fei was truly quite ordinary.","There was not a trace of displeasure on Duan Yanhua's face, as if he were long accustomed to the other party's attitude.","\"Your Excellency, this humble official indeed has a favor to ask of you today.\"","He pointed at Song Gaoli and continued, \"This is my newly accepted student. Although he is a fellow townsman, classmate, and bosom friend of County Princess Linghui's brother, Song Qiming, their academic knowledge is worlds apart. Song Qiming placed first in the provincial exams, while he came in dead last. Seeing as the metropolitan examination is only a few months away, I was hoping Your Excellency could give him some guidance so he can perform better next year.\"","Fei Yanzhang cast a critical glance at Song Gaoli. \"Since you took him on as a student, you should teach him well yourself. Or are you saying you lack even that bit of ability?\"","Duan Yanhua slapped his thigh forcefully, sighing as if frustrated by an underachiever. \"This humble official taught him for over a month on the way back to the capital, but his progress was very mediocre. I suppose it is because he once studied under Vice Censor-in-Chief Ye and has grown accustomed to his teaching methods.\"","\"Back then, this humble official passed the imperial examination in last place, falling far short of Vice Censor-in-Chief Ye. After thinking it over, only Your Excellency can compare to him, which is why I specially came to visit today.\"","Song Gaoli's mouth twitched, and he could only nod in agreement to go along with Duan Yanhua's words.","On the way to the capital, Duan Yanhua had been sleeping the entire time and hadn't even opened a book. Where did this guidance come from?","He spun lies effortlessly, making them sound completely true. If he hadn't experienced it firsthand, he really would have thought Duan Yanhua was a good teacher who cared about his student's future.","\"Oh? Ye Liangyu taught you?\" Fei Yanzhang looked at Song Gaoli, his eyes fixed on him in a way that made one too guilty to dare tell a lie.","Duan Yanhua shot Song Gaoli a look.","Quick, do as I said.","Song Gaoli opened his mouth to explain, \"My enlightenment teacher was a classmate of Lord Ye. Before participating in the prefectural examination, he entrusted Qiming and me to Lord Ye to be taught for two months.\"","\"So that's how it is.\" Fei Yanzhang tapped his fingers lightly against his teacup twice.","Last night, Ye Liangyu had suddenly sent someone over asking for his help. It seemed Song Gaoli's character had passed his test.","Seeing that Fei Yanzhang was finally interested, Duan Yanhua hastily struck while the iron was hot. \"Your Excellency, this child is not highly talented, but he is eager to learn and can endure hardship. If it weren't for my limited abilities, I wouldn't have come begging to you.\"","Fei Yanzhang said, \"I heard that Ye Liangyu has already sent Song Qiming to study at the Imperial Academy. Since you are good friends with him, you should go together.\"","\"My relationship with the Chancellor is fairly good; he should do me this favor. There are many instructors inside, so surely there will be someone who can teach you.\"","Now, not only was Song Gaoli dumbfounded, but even Duan Yanhua was caught completely off guard.","Originally, he only wanted to use this matter to let Fei Yanzhang know that his newly accepted student had a good relationship with Ye Liangyu. Who knew the other party would make such a grand gesture right off the bat?","Sending Song Gaoli to the Imperial Academy? Fei Yanzhang valued Ye Liangyu this much; his move was absolutely right!","\"Gaoli, hurry up and thank Lord Fei.\" He hurriedly patted Song Gaoli's arm.","At this moment, Song Gaoli's mind was blank. Snapped out of it by Duan Yanhua, he hastily stood up and thanked Fei Yanzhang: \"Thank you, Lord Fei. This student will never forget your kindness today.\"","Fei Yanzhang waved his hand. \"As long as you know how to be grateful. Ye Liangyu and I often drink and converse happily together. Since you were able to receive his guidance, you must have some merits.\"","Go back for today. Once I have everything arranged, I will inform Lord Duan. When the time comes, you just need to head over there with Song Qiming.","If it hadn't been too conspicuous to sneak two people in at once, Ye Liangyu would never have asked for his help.","Ranking dead last, with only a little over three months left... could this kid really pass the imperial examination?","He could only hope that all this effort wouldn't be in vain."]},{"number":226,"title":"Chapter 226: Audit, Is There an Issue with Zhuangzi","paragraphs":["Upon leaving the Fei residence, Duan Yanhua felt a surge of excitement, but the look he gave Song Gaoli also carried a hint of jealousy.","\"You are a lucky kid. If I had been able to enter the Imperial Academy to study at your age back then, I wouldn't have dragged on until I was nearly forty to pass the imperial examination.\"","Song Gaoli chuckled twice and rubbed the back of his head with an unnatural expression.","\"It is all thanks to you, Teacher. If you hadn't brought me to visit Lord Fei today, your student wouldn't have had this opportunity.\"","After calming down, Song Gaoli had a suspicion in his heart. Perhaps today's matter was not as simple as it appeared on the surface.","It was highly likely that Ye Liangyu had planned this, which was why he had specifically instructed him not to interfere with anything when he left yesterday.","Duan Yanhua reached out and patted Song Gaoli's shoulder. He said earnestly, \"I am very gratified that you can think this way. My efforts in planning this for you were not in vain. After entering the Imperial Academy, you must study hard and pass the imperial examination next year.\"","\"You must also pay attention to one thing. There are many children of officials in the Imperial Academy, and among them are people of noble status. In your spare time, remember to interact more with them. It will be beneficial for your future official career.\"","\"If you hear any particularly important news, you must tell me immediately. I will help you plan, lest your youthful arrogance causes you to offend someone without even realizing it.\"","Song Gaoli nodded on the surface, but in his heart, he thought about going to the Ye residence tonight to ask Song Qiming if today's show was arranged by Ye Liangyu.","After Song Jinzhao returned to the Ye residence, she took out the box containing the land deeds and spread a thick stack of slavery contracts from inside onto the table.","These were all the servants who lived depending on the estate. They were rewarded along with the estate, totaling more than twenty people.","She hadn't brought a single servant from the farm in Anyang Prefecture. Now, if she wanted to sort out these two estates as soon as possible, she would either have to buy new servants or use the old ones.","Qingshuang brought out another old, large wooden box. There were a few wormholes on the four bottom corners.","When the Internal Affairs Department brought the rewards over that day, they threw this box into a corner. By the time Qingshuang found it, she saw that the outside was covered in a layer of grime, as if it hadn't been opened in over a decade.","\"Eldest Miss, when your servant opened it, it was full of account books. They look quite complete, and the age of the paper and ink match up. They don't look like fake accounts, but they also seem incredibly fake.\"","\"These two estates have never made any money. The income and expenses are unusually balanced. You could say they are self-sufficient; they have never asked the owner for subsidies, nor have they ever given the owner a single coin.\"","In the inner room, Song Shixue, who was sticking needles into a strawman, looked up in astonishment.","If two estates totaling a thousand acres couldn't make money while supporting twenty-odd servants, wouldn't the farm her eldest sister bought in Anyang Prefecture require her to lose money every year? This was a huge problem.","Standing nearby, Lanxi hesitated and said, \"Could it be that the estate managers embezzled the funds? There are countless royal estates, big and small. Without careful inspection, it is very easy for such problems to occur.\"","When he was in the imperial palace of the Shuobei Kingdom, his food and supplies were often stolen by maids and eunuchs. Even his monthly allowance was withheld by the Internal Affairs Department.","Song Jinzhao took the account book Qingshuang handed her. It clearly recorded how much grain the tenant farmers handed over each year, and the reasons for any shortages. Droughts, floods, and locust plagues were written down clearly with ample justification. However, the yields were simply unpresentable. As long as they worked hard, they shouldn't have harvested so little grain.","Song Jinzhao said, \"Find the contracts signed between the estate and the tenant farmers and show them to me.\"","Qingshuang and Lanxi immediately walked to the box and bent down to search through it. The rising dust created a hazy fog. It wasn't until they had pulled out all the account books from the box that the two found a thick stack of contracts at the bottom. They had been badly bitten by insects, covered in wormholes and yellow spots.","\"I will go outside and clean them off first.\" Lanxi took the contracts into the courtyard and swung his arms forcefully. What fell off was not just dust, but also insect corpses and droppings.","After he had cleaned them up enough, he handed them to Song Jinzhao. By this time, Song Shixue had also walked over. She casually picked up a contract and saw that the signing date was twenty years ago.","In other words, these two estates hadn't changed their tenant farmers in twenty years. Furthermore, according to the terms written on the contract, no matter how much the tenants harvested, in the absence of a grain tax, they only needed to hand over thirty percent. And there was no minimum yield requirement.","Song Jinzhao's curiosity was thoroughly piqued.","She tapped her fingertip against the string of recorded droughts and rainstorms in the account book and instructed Qingshuang and Lanxi, \"Go immediately and find someone to ask around. First, see if what is written here is true.\"","\"Anyway, there is nothing to do these next few days. Since we can't move houses, we might as well go to the estate and take a look. We will go tomorrow.\"","Hearing this, Song Shixue became interested. She raised her hand and said, \"Sister, I want to go too. I am going to grow moldy staying in my room all day.\"","Song Jinzhao nodded. \"Bring Anhao and Xuetuan along too.\"","Even an intellectually challenged tiger was still a tiger. They had few people and couldn't intimidate others, so bringing Xuetuan over would be just right.","Staying motionless in the courtyard these past few days, the tiger's muscles had grown slack."]},{"number":227,"title":"Chapter 227: Oriental Yukun: The Stricken Song Qiming","paragraphs":["When Song Qiming returned from the Imperial Academy in the evening, he was feeling quite down and looked to be in a bad mood.","\"Brother, what's wrong?\" Could it be that someone at the Imperial Academy was bullying him?","Song Qiming shook his head, sighing with a disappointed expression, \"Today I finally learned what it means that there is always someone better out there. I feel like getting the top scorer position is a bit unlikely now.\"","Song Shixue asked in confusion, \"Top scorer? Weren't you aiming for the second tier?\"","She had never thought her brother could become the top scorer. After all, he was too young and there were too many competitors. Passing the imperial examination to become a Jinshi would already be excellent.","It seemed their older sister hadn't demanded that he must take first place, either.","Song Qiming rested his head on the table and sighed, \"This is a goal I set for myself. I want to be the top scorer.\"","Song Jinzhao smiled faintly and said, \"Did you meet someone better than you at the Imperial Academy?\"","Song Qiming nodded and let out another depressed sigh. \"Yeah! I took a bit of a blow.\"","\"Did you meet Dongfang Yukun?\" Ye Liangyu, walking in with a relaxed smile, observed Song Qiming's reaction meaningfully.","Song Qiming suddenly straightened his back, staring intently at Ye Liangyu as he nodded vigorously. \"I did. He is simply unprecedented, stunningly brilliant, and as handsome as Pan An. Teacher, did you do this on purpose?\"","He thought that coming in first in the provincial exams at thirteen was already impressive, making him a genius among geniuses. Who knew there was someone even better, and the gap wasn't just a little bit. He was truly quite discouraged.","Ye Liangyu sat down with a smile and drank some tea. \"Compared to Dongfang Yukun, you are indeed lacking a bit. There are too many capable people in the world, not just in the Imperial Academy, which is why my requirement for you is only the second tier.\"","Song Jinzhao grew more interested as she listened, opening her hand to gesture for someone to explain.","\"So, could someone tell me who exactly this Dongfang Yukun is?\"","Song Qiming puffed up his cheeks and said, \"Sister, you have no idea. As soon as I stepped one foot into the classroom, I was blinded by a man who looked even prettier than a woman. He is truly too handsome, I've never seen anyone like him.\"","\"Then I caught them competing in the arts. That refinement, that posture, and his zither playing was so beautiful it sounded like music from the heavens.\"","\"He rides like the wind and shoots with unerring accuracy. His archery could almost rival Shixue's, and his running script calligraphy flows like a swimming dragon, having reached the pinnacle of perfection.\"","Suddenly thinking of something, he quickly ran back to the next room and brought out a piece of calligraphy to hand to Song Jinzhao. \"This is the calligraphy he gave me, a poem he composed on the spot in class today. Sister, take a look, isn't it as graceful as floating clouds and as vigorous as a startled dragon!\"","Song Jinzhao and Song Shixue both leaned in to look. Even Song Anhao, who had been playing outside with Xuetuan, was drawn over. He stood on tiptoe, grabbing the edge of the table, until Ye Liangyu scooped him up by the waist and set him on his lap so he could see clearly.","Song Jinzhao blinked. To be honest, this handwriting looked a bit like Wang Xizhi's.","She had been to museums and seen many copies of the Preface to the Poems Collected from the Orchid Pavilion, and she could say there was a ninety percent resemblance.","At first glance, it was somewhat elegant; at second glance, the elegance carried strength; at third glance, it was rather beautiful; at fourth glance, it was absolutely stunning.","It gave off a feeling of fiercely restrained ambition. That madness that seeped through yet couldn't fully break out was what struck the appreciator's soul the hardest, making it unforgettable at first sight, rendering one unable to look at any other calligraphy ever again.","\"The brushwork is profound. One couldn't achieve this without over a decade of practice. The poem is written well too, blending emotion with scenery to create a strong visual image.\"","Ye Liangyu asked, \"He gifted you his calligraphy and personally wrote a poem; it seems you two get along quite well?\"","Song Qiming pondered for a moment and nodded hesitantly. \"I suppose so. I sit right behind him, and he was the one who initiated the conversation with me.\"","\"A modest gentleman as gentle as jade—I think that describes him perfectly.\"","Song Qiming held up a finger, his eyes shining. \"No, those eight words are far from enough.\"","Having never seen the person, Song Shixue didn't know whether to laugh or cry. \"Brother, you've praised this Dongfang Yukun to the heavens. Now I'm extremely curious about what he actually looks like.\"","Lanxi, standing at the door of the room, looked up at Song Shixue, his pupils shrinking as if pricked by a needle.","He gritted his teeth hard, forcefully suppressing the bitterness in his heart.","If he was truly as handsome as the eldest young master described, would she like him?","Ye Liangyu gazed gently at Song Qiming, as if in his heart, no matter how outstanding Dongfang Yukun was, he could not compare to the student before him.","Encountering a competitor more talented than oneself, being able to see their strengths with an appreciative eye, not being stingy with praise, and feeling admiration rather than jealousy—this was very good.","\"Dongfang Yukun is the grandson of the Secretariat Director, Dongfang Yuanbin. Although he is currently sixteen and still studying at the Imperial Academy, he actually passed the provincial exams and came in first place when he was only ten.\"","Song Shixue immediately asked in return, \"Then why hasn't he passed the metropolitan exams to become a Jinshi yet? Are the metropolitan exams that difficult?\"","Song Qiming replied, \"I heard from my classmates at the Imperial Academy that Dongfang Yukun deliberately didn't take them. I don't know anything beyond that.\"","On his first day, not many people had spoken to him, so he didn't know much either.","Ye Liangyu patiently explained to them.","\"Dongfang Yuanbin is a veteran official of two reigns and has been in the position of Secretariat Director for many years. Dongfang Shaoting, who is Dongfang Yukun's father, is the Minister of Personnel. The father and son can be said to hold high positions and wield immense power.\"","\"Six years ago, when Dongfang Yukun came in first in the provincial exams, the common people rumored that he was the reincarnation of the Wenqu Star. If he had participated in the metropolitan exams, he would surely have placed in the top tier, and at just ten years old, it was indeed possible for him to achieve that.\"","Song Jinzhao said lightly, \"Three generations of descendants serving as officials in the same court, already holding great power, plus a once-in-a-millennium prodigy—the Emperor would be wary.\"","Ye Liangyu shook his head and smiled. \"It is truly a pity that the Princess cannot enter the court as an official. For the games of the court and the struggles of the state, you are even more suited than Qiming.\"","Song Jinzhao was born into a farming family and had not been immersed in such matters from a young age like the children of officials. Yet, she could hit the nail on the head so quickly based on just two sentences. It could only be said that it was innate, but unfortunately, she was born the wrong gender.","Song Jinzhao recalled the people she had seen at the birthday banquet that night, unable to figure out which one was Dongfang Yuanbin.","\"Since Dongfang Yukun will be participating in next year's metropolitan exams, will either his grandfather or his father have to step down?\"","Ye Liangyu nodded. \"Dongfang Yuanbin is already elderly; he will retire next year. Currently in the court, Chancellor Gu Qishan is acting head of the Department of State Affairs. For the time being, Dongfang Shaoting will not be able to surpass him.\"","Song Qiming's tightly furrowed brows slowly relaxed. \"So Dongfang Shaoting will become the new Secretariat Director?\"","Ye Liangyu nodded. \"If there are no surprises, it is highly likely.\"","Song Qiming's chest involuntarily relaxed. With such an outstanding grandfather and father, it was no wonder they could produce a one-in-a-million genius like Dongfang Yukun.","Being so young now, his official career would definitely not be simple; it was bound to be an unstoppable, broad path to success.","\"Awooo—\" A low tiger's roar echoed in the courtyard. A servant hugged the wall, taking a detour to the room's door to report.","\"Master, Young Master Song is outside requesting an audience.\"","Ye Liangyu stood up and went to the door. \"I imagine he has already been to the Fei residence.\"","Song Qiming blinked. Who had been to the Fei residence? Gao Li?","Watching the retreating figures of the master and disciple, Song Jinzhao picked up the calligraphy on the table and handed it to Lanxi. \"Put this in the eldest young master's room.\"","Lanxi took the scroll and slowly pushed it open, his fingers subconsciously tightening around it. After arriving in the next room, he couldn't help but spread the scroll out and examine it carefully a few more times.","It was just semi-cursive script; he could write it too, and definitely much better than Dongfang Yukun.","\"Achoo~\" The beautiful youth, who was practicing archery at home, suddenly felt an itch in his nose and couldn't hold back a sneeze. His hand slipped, and the arrow flew out, hitting the bullseye dead center.","\"Young Master, put on your coat quickly, lest you catch a cold,\" the servant waiting beside him immediately picked up the clothes resting on a chair and was about to dress Dongfang Yukun.","The beautiful youth waved his hand and said with a proud face, \"No need. Someone is probably missing me.\"","The servant: \"...\"","In the slightly dim study, a lamp was missing, and Song Gaoli widened his eyes as he looked at Ye Liangyu.","\"So Lord Fei recommending me to study at the Imperial College was really arranged by you?\"","Song Qiming was taken aback at first, then looked at Ye Liangyu in pleasant surprise. If Gaoli could enter the Imperial College, he would have an acquaintance inside.","Ye Liangyu nodded. \"Inserting two people at once would attract too much attention, so I just gave Fei Yanzhang a heads-up. He can handle it.\"","\"Thank you, sir, for taking the trouble to arrange this. I'm just worried that if I enter the Imperial College and fail the exam next year, this quota will be wasted for nothing.\"","Song Gaoli looked down at the floor in embarrassment, his mouth saying no but the corners of his lips refusing to stay down.","Ye Liangyu stared at the top of his head and said, \"As long as you give it your all, it's not a waste. You can learn a lot at the Imperial College. Even if you don't pass next year, you can continue studying there after failing, and you will definitely pass in three years.\"","Every time he barely passed the line; who could really say for sure when it came to luck?"]},{"number":228,"title":"Chapter 228: Dong Yuanbin Frightened Out of His Wits by a Tiger's Roar","paragraphs":["Morning light filtered through the thin mist. Outside the window, on the withered yellow grass, Xuetuan impatiently pawed at the dirt. Its anxious whimpers seemed to be urging Song Jinzhao and the others to hurry up.","\"Stop making a fuss, or we won't take you out,\" Song Shixue, who was currently combing Song Anhao's hair, shouted outside with a glare.","Xuetuan lowered its tiger head in grievance, whimpering softly as it lay back on the ground and buried its face in its paws.","By the dining table, Qingshuang held an account book and reported, \"I have already asked the farmers in the city. The droughts and rainy seasons recorded in the account book did indeed happen, but the actual situation was much milder than what is written. It was nowhere near a fifty percent reduction in crop yield, at most ten percent.\"","Song Jinzhao put down her spoon. She suddenly felt that the fresh meat wonton she was chewing wasn't as delicious as before. It had a bitter taste that made it hard to swallow.","Did the Emperor reward them with these two estates on purpose, or was he himself unaware of this situation?","Now that they had fallen into her hands, there was no way she would let a thousand acres of land remain unprofitable. She absolutely had to go take a look this time.","By the time they finished packing, the sun had already leapt out from behind the clouds. Song Shixue picked up her younger brother and got into the carriage. Xuetuan, wearing a collar, jumped onto the carriage frame, waiting to be let loose once they were out of the city.","The carriage slowly headed toward the outer city. According to the location marked on the deed, it would take a little less than two hours to reach the estate after leaving the city.","After leaving the city, Xuetuan couldn't hold back and jumped down from the carriage. Lanxi hurriedly tied a rope to it and handed it to Song Jinzhao. Even though it was only eleven months old, its body was already the size of half a cow. If it really exerted its strength, a single person wouldn't be able to hold it back at all.","\"Aooo~\" It howled as it ran, scaring the migratory birds in the surrounding woods into taking flight for their lives.","In a nearby official estate, Dong Yuanbin, who was personally leading people to build a greenhouse, alertly straightened his back and looked around. \"Why does it sound like I just heard a tiger's roar?\"","A subordinate with hands full of mud roughly wiped the smelly sweat off his face. \"My Lord must have heard wrong. How could there be tigers around here?\"","For dozens of miles around, it was all farmland. Not even the shadow of a mountain could be seen, so where would a tiger come from?","Dong Yuanbin thought about it and agreed. \"I probably misheard. A few days ago, I went to the Ye residence to seek advice from County Princess Linghui. They actually raise a tiger, a white one at that. It's incredibly fierce, with teeth longer than my fingers.\"","He had a nightmare that very night after returning.","He dreamed that he was eaten by that white tiger, without even a bone left behind. The scene was extremely bloody.","He was jolted awake in terror, covered in a cold sweat, and couldn't fall back asleep for a long time. Even now, it still cast a shadow over him.","Subordinate: \"I heard that County Princess Linghui started out as a hunter. She has killed hundreds, if not thousands, of fierce tigers and bears, so it's not surprising that she raises a tiger.\"","\"Exactly. You didn't see it, but even County Princess Linghui's youngest brother, a mere three-year-old child, dared to ride on the tiger's back and show off. He really has guts.\"","\"Aooo~\"","Dong Yuanbin, who was just about to look at the blueprints, abruptly looked up into the distance and scolded with a solemn expression, \"Nobody make a sound. Be quiet.\"","The people busy working around him instantly froze in place, motionless.","What was wrong? Why was he getting angry out of nowhere?","\"Aooo~\" This time the sound was much clearer, and quite a few people heard it.","The subordinate's eyes widened in horror, looking as if they were about to pop out.","\"It really is a tiger's roar!\" In broad daylight, and so close to the city walls, how could there be a tiger?","After confirming it was indeed a tiger, Dong Yuanbin hurriedly started running and urged the crowd, \"Quickly put down your things and hide inside the house.\"","A large group of people swarmed toward the nearby brick house, tightly shutting the front door and blocking it with cabinets.","They looked outside through the windows, their hands tightly gripping the window frames, ready to lock them at a moment's notice.","Seeing people in the distance running out of the greenhouses to look around, Song Jinzhao shook the rope. \"Xuetuan, stop howling.\"","Last year, the imperial court popularized the methods for building vegetable greenhouses among the commoners. This year, as winter approached, some people in the capital had already started building them.","\"Awoo.\" Xuetuan shook its head reluctantly.","Its eyesight was poor to begin with, and with this movement, it stumbled and fell straight into a nearby ditch.","By the time it climbed out, it was covered in dirt, its white fur soiled, and it rolled on the ground in grievance.","Song Jinzhao furrowed her brows and shouted behind her, \"Shixue, let Anhao come down.\"","Song Shixue pitied the little white tiger for being born with impaired vision and low intelligence, so she spoiled it rotten and indulged it in everything.","Song Qiming was too busy to get close to it, and Song Jinzhao liked to suppress it with force.","Instead, it was the youngest, Song Anhao, who could subdue the white tiger without lifting a finger. The child was full of energy, and since there were no other children in the family, he wanted to play with Xuetuan all day long. Over time, even the tiger wanted to hide from him.","After getting out of the carriage, Song Shixue saw Xuetuan covered in dirt and helplessly went over to brush it off with her hands. \"The road is so wide, yet you still managed to fall into a ditch. When we get back, I really need to give you some acupuncture.\"","Xuetuan nuzzled its head into Song Shixue's embrace, acting spoiled.","Once it was clean, Anhao couldn't wait to climb onto the tiger's back. Grinning widely, he grabbed the collar around its neck and patted the tiger's rear with his hand.","Waving his short arm forward like a general, he cried, \"Charge, Xuetuan~\"","After hiding for quite a while without seeing any tiger approach and hearing no more sounds, the people inside the house looked at each other in dismay. Some began to doubt if they had misheard, wondering if it was a wild dog barking instead of a tiger roaring.","Another long moment passed, and there was no movement outside at all.","Dong Yuanbin thought for a moment, pointed at the door blocked by the cabinets, and said, \"Open the door.\"","Everyone huddled together as they walked out of the room. Dozens of heads looked around everywhere, and after waiting a good while longer, they finally relaxed.","The subordinate scratched his head and muttered, \"We probably misheard. It might have just been a dog barking.\"","Dong Yuanbin shook his head and insisted, \"It was definitely a tiger's roar. I heard it several times, there's no way I heard wrong. Let's get back to work, but assign two people to keep watch nearby, just in case.\"","The subordinate nodded in agreement. Whether it was a wild dog or a tiger, having someone on lookout would bring peace of mind.","With Song Anhao riding on its back, Xuetuan didn't dare move recklessly for fear of throwing him off. Its tiger head kept pace with the horse's head, and it didn't raise its head to howl anymore.","As a result, their speed slowed down. By the time they arrived at the estate, another two hours had passed."]},{"number":229,"title":"Chapter 229: Shocking: All Tenants Are Disabled","paragraphs":["The sun hung high overhead, its rays casting a surprising warmth upon them.","On the endless ridges of the fields, dozens of people could be vaguely seen working. In the distance, several extremely small houses were scattered about, looking somewhat like makeshift thatched huts.","Although Song Jinzhao's group consisted of only five people and they were still far away, their carriage was conspicuous. Coupled with the fact that people rarely visited this place year-round, the men and women working in the fields couldn't help but stop their labor and look up.","The path along the field ridge was too narrow, only allowing one person to pass at a time.","Song Jinzhao had the carriage parked by the roadside, tying the horse to a willow stump.","Anhao had already been lifted down from the tiger's back by Song Jinzhao, and Song Shixue walked in the middle, holding the leash.","As the distance closed, the people in the fields finally got a clear look at the group before them.","Of the group of four walking, three were women. Two were clearly quite young, and they had a child with them.","Seeing the white tiger stretching its neck to look around, the men quickly shielded the women and children behind them, staring at Song Jinzhao's group with vigilant faces.","At this moment, however, Song Jinzhao's brows were tightly furrowed.","From a distance, she couldn't see clearly, but up close, she realized that nearly half of the dozens of people were disabled, and all of them were men. They were missing arms or legs; some were blind in one eye with scars on their faces, and even the hands gripping the hoes were missing several fingers.","Were these the tenant farmers of the estate?","Song Shixue stared at a man missing both arms, lying on the ground and using his feet to dig the earth. All the color drained from her face, her skin turning an ashen white, her eyes filled with disbelief.","What was wrong with these people? Even during her family's hardest times, she had never seen such a scene. Subconsciously, she whispered, Sister.","Held in her arms, Song Anhao tightly hugged Song Jinzhao's neck. Her innocent gaze met that of the child hiding behind the woman, one filled with curiosity, the other with fear.","Sweeping her gaze over the crowd, Song Jinzhao astutely noticed that the eyes of these men were not like those of ordinary people. Instead, they resembled trained soldiers, their vigilance mixed with defensiveness, and a trace of murderous intent hidden deep in their eyes.","The two sides stood in a stalemate for a moment, neither taking the initiative to speak, until an able-bodied man from the other side stepped forward and asked Song Jinzhao's group, Who are you people, and what are you doing here?","If one ignored his right hand, which was missing three fingers, he could indeed be considered able-bodied among this group.","Qingshuang was about to ask if they were the estate's tenant farmers, but Song Jinzhao beat her to it.","I heard there is surplus land sitting idle on this estate. I want to find your manager and ask if it's for rent.","The man froze. The people standing behind him nervously clamped their mouths shut, their lowered brows tinged with worry.","After a moment of silence, the man pointed toward the east and said, Walk ahead for half an hour, and you will see five tile-roofed houses clustered together. The estate manager lives there.","The fields haven't been sown yet, so you can ride your horses over.","Song Jinzhao nodded in thanks. Thank you, brother.","She didn't ride the horse, but instead led her people on foot, continuing along the field ridges.","Seeing them walk far away, a woman with a child got red-rimmed eyes.","She looked worriedly at the man who had just spoken. Husband, if the manager rents the land to others, does that mean he won't rent it to us anymore?","Other estates demanded sixty percent of the annual grain harvest, whereas theirs was only thirty percent. If they lost this, they would never be able to rent such cheap land again.","The man turned and comforted the crowd. Don't worry. The manager is kind-hearted and won't just arbitrarily stop renting to us.","It's probably because some fields on the estate are empty and the manager doesn't want them to go to waste. Since we don't have the energy to farm them, he wants to rent them out.","The worry in everyone's eyes did not fade because of this. Would the land really not be taken away? They had no certainty in their hearts.","After walking a distance, Song Jinzhao successively saw quite a few more people.","Like the dozens of people from earlier, the men were not quite sound in body, the women were emaciated, and the children were sallow and thin, looking only slightly better in complexion than the adults.","Walking behind, Qingshuang and Lanxi remained silent. Even Song Anhao, who usually talked the most, quieted down, obediently resting her hands on Song Jinzhao's neck and looking straight ahead.","If these people were truly the tenant farmers of the estate, then the yields recorded in the ledger might not be fake. But why would the manager rent all the land to families with disabled members? And where did he find all these people? There were simply too many of them.","Filled with doubts, Song Jinzhao found the place the man had mentioned.","To be honest, the houses were a bit dilapidated. It was obvious they had been built decades ago and patched up many times; even the colors of the walls and roof tiles were mismatched.","After entering the courtyard, they didn't see a single person. Only the chimney on the roof was emitting smoke.","Walking to the kitchen door, they found only a woman inside cooking.","Seeing strangers suddenly appear in her home, the woman was stunned for a moment.","She sized up the attire of Song Jinzhao and Song Shixue, guessing they were masters of some household. Seeing that they were young girls and seemed harmless, she put down her spatula, walked out, and asked, Is there something I can help you two young ladies with?","It wasn't until she reached the door that she saw Xuetuan standing behind the four of them, and she immediately let out a terrified scream.","She quickly turned around, dodged into the kitchen, and slammed the door shut with a bang, her figure moving so fast it was almost a blur.","Xuetuan, whose chin was currently locked in Song Anhao's grip, stared at the kitchen door with a bewildered expression. It seemed something had just scurried inside.","Song Jinzhao was rendered speechless. Had she known the estate would be like this, she wouldn't have brought Xuetuan along.","Song Shixue stepped forward and knocked on the door. Auntie, Xuetuan is my pet. He doesn't bite.","The woman leaning against the door trembled in fear. Raising a tiger as a pet? This young girl was far too bold.","Auntie, he really doesn't bite.","Under Song Shixue's continuous reassurances, the woman slowly opened a crack in the door.","Seeing that it was peaceful outside and the tiger was still being held by the child, standing in place without moving a single step, she gradually opened the door.","Who are you looking for?","Song Jinzhao: I'm looking for the estate manager. The tenant farmers we met said he lives here.","The woman nodded. They are working in the fields and haven't returned yet. What do you need?","Yuniang, a rough male voice sounded from behind.","Turning around, they saw over a dozen men carrying hoes and shovels standing at the entrance. Their thick homespun clothes almost all had one or two patches, with straw ropes tied around their waists. They had sturdy builds, and their weather-beaten faces were rough and tinged with deep red, clearly not people who lived a life of luxury.","The fifty-year-old man standing at the very front had his pupils shrink when he got a clear look at Song Jinzhao and the others, nearly dropping the hoe in his hands.","The woman quickly hurried over, pointed at Song Jinzhao's group, and said, Husband, these guests said they are looking for you.","The old man gritted his back teeth, his heart filled with immense bitterness.","He took a deep breath to brace himself, put down the hoe, walked up to Song Jinzhao, and knelt down. This lowly one, Chen Fu, manager of Daohua Estate, pays his respects to County Princess Linghui.","The air suddenly froze. The woman cast her gaze toward Song Jinzhao and hurriedly knelt down as well.","Although the others were completely bewildered, they also followed suit, kneeling and kowtowing.","Song Jinzhao stared at him. You know me?","The old man raised his head and smiled bitterly. \"Other than you, County Princess, this humble one cannot think of anyone else.\"","The simple main hall had no decorations at all. The old mahogany table had lost its original luster, looking as though it had been used for many years.","Three dishes and a soup were laid out on the table. They were all vegetarian dishes, with only a little egg drop floating in the soup. The woman called Yuniang was currently leading people in the kitchen to prepare more food.","Chen Fu knelt on the floor below the steps. \"The manager of Shiquan Estate is still in the fields and hasn't returned yet. This humble one has already sent someone to call him, so he should be here shortly.\""]},{"number":230,"title":"Chapter 230: Not Like Corruption, Questioning","paragraphs":["Li Hou ran all the way back. With sweat and mud mixed together on his body, his cheeks and neck were stained completely black.","Upon entering the door and seeing Song Jinzhao sitting upright on the long wooden bench, his legs gave way. How did she arrive so quickly! They had not even had time to prepare.","\"This lowly one, Li Hou, manager of Shiquan Manor, pays his respects to the County Princess Linghui.\" His knees struck the wooden floorboards with a heavy thud that sounded painful just to hear.","Song Jinzhao looked at the two men, already certain in her heart that they had not embezzled anything. There was nothing to embezzle, nor could they have done so.","It was just that there were too many questionable things about these two manors, and the truth was likely known only to these two men before her.","\"I have already reviewed the account books and deeds sent over by the Internal Affairs Department. Do you not plan to say anything?\" Song Jinzhao picked up the boiled water from the table and took a small sip, her tone as placid as a still pool.","Yet, such a calm voice fell upon the ears of Chen Fu and Li Hou like a death warrant. The two men exchanged a glance and simultaneously knocked their heads against the ground.","\"County Princess, please forgive us. It was this lowly one's greed. We embezzled the grain that should have been handed over. We beg the County Princess to spare our lives.\"","Song Jinzhao remained expressionless. \"Coarse tea, bland food, and tattered clothes. Where is the grain you embezzled? Why hasn't this County Princess seen any of it?\"","Chen Fu's heart pounded nervously. \"This lowly one sold the grain and purchased a residence in the neighboring city. Our current appearance is just a disguise, as we were afraid the people from the Internal Affairs Department would come to inspect.\"","Song Jinzhao's tone rose as she said lightly, \"Is that so? You put on quite a convincing act. Doing all the farm work yourselves must be very exhausting, isn't it?\"","The two men were panicked to the extreme. They did not utter a word, simply remaining kneeling on the ground without raising their heads, their hearts pounding so hard it felt as if they would burst bloodily from their chests.","Seeing their silence, Song Jinzhao continued, \"Bring the deed of the house you bought for me to see. This County Princess will send someone to the neighboring city to verify it. Since it is stolen property, it must be confiscated.\"","Li Hou raised his head and slammed it against the wooden floorboards again with a thud. \"County Princess, please forgive us. In recent years, the two of us became addicted to gambling and lost the residence.\"","Lanxi, who was standing by the pillar, could not help but roll her eyes. They truly refused to give up until the bitter end; not even a ghost would believe such words.","Song Jinzhao's expression darkened, and she said in a deep voice, \"On the way here, this County Princess saw many disabled tenant farmers. They have all served in the military, haven't they?\"","A chill shot from the top of their heads to the soles of their feet. The hands they had placed on the ground began to tremble, and they answered with quivering voices, \"They haven't served in the military. This lowly one only manages the renting of the land and never paid attention to whether they were disabled or not. As long as they can pay the rent on time, it doesn't matter if they are disabled.\"","A pair of chopsticks slammed onto the table with a loud smack. A woman who was bringing in dishes was startled, dropping the plate in her hands and spilling soup and vegetable leaves all over the floor.","\"Do you take this County Princess for a fool? It would be one thing if only one or two were disabled, but every single male in the more than two hundred tenant households of this entire manor is crippled. Where did you find these people? From which military camp did these soldiers collectively retire?\"","\"For twenty years, Daohua Manor and Shiquan Manor have not handed over a single coin, and the Internal Affairs Department has turned a blind eye. Shouldn't this County Princess ask the head of the Internal Affairs Department if there is a hole in his head, or if you bribed him with money?\"","Cold saliva slid down their throats into their stomachs. Chen Fu and Li Hou's hands and feet were freezing; at this moment, they were terrified to the extreme.","Wasn't it said that this County Princess Linghui came from a humble background? How could her aura be so intimidating? How did she see that those people had served in the military?","Song Jinzhao stood up, resting one hand on the table. \"If you refuse to tell the truth, I will have no choice but to handle this impartially according to the law.\"","\"A rent of three tenths is too little; it must be raised to at least six tenths. If the current tenants cannot afford it, I will rent it to others. As for you two.\"","\"Qingshuang, go back and find a human trafficker to sell off their entire families. This County Princess will not tolerate subordinates who deceive their superiors and steal what is entrusted to their care.\"","The woman frozen in place turned pale, hastily kneeling and kowtowing for mercy. \"County Princess, spare our lives. I beg you not to sell us.\"","The cries drew a child who had been playing outside the house to run inside.","Seeing the woman's forehead bleeding and his grandfather kneeling on the ground, he immediately grabbed the woman's sleeve and cried out, \"Grandma, what's wrong with you?\"","He pointed at Song Jinzhao and shouted, \"You are all bad people! You're bullying my grandpa and grandma! I'm going to hit you!\"","A younger woman scrambled in on her knees, tightly pulling the child into her arms and kowtowing incessantly.","\"County Princess, please forgive us. The child is young and speaks nonsense. Please do not take it seriously.\"","Unable to bear the sight, Song Shixue secretly tugged at Song Jinzhao's sleeve under the table.","A surge of frustration swelled in Song Jinzhao's chest. Even faced with being sold, they still refused to tell the truth. What exactly were they trying so hard to hide?","The more they refused to speak, the more Song Jinzhao felt that the matter behind this was massive.","She ordered Qingshuang, \"Take the women and children outside, and close the doors.\"","As the main doors were closed, the room instantly darkened. Lanxi took out a fire starter and lit the candles.","The flickering candlelight cast shadows on everyone's faces. Song Jinzhao spoke, \"This County Princess is not an unreasonable person. Once this is reported to the authorities and blown out of proportion, everyone will know. By then, whatever you are trying to hide will be exposed, and it will be too late.\"","Hearing that Song Jinzhao intended to report them to the authorities, the two men who had kept their heads lowered suddenly looked up, their eyes filled with sheer terror.","Their eyes met, and silence spread throughout the room. After an unknown amount of time passed, Chen Fu lowered his head as if resigning himself to his fate."]},{"number":231,"title":"Chapter 231: The Status of Tenant Farmers is a Major Problem","paragraphs":["The fewer people who know about this, the better. I must ask the County Princess to dismiss your attendants.","Before Song Jinzhao could speak, Song Shixue picked up Song Anhao, handed the rope to Lan Xi, and the four of them left the room without any delay, closing the door behind them.","You may speak now.","Chen Fu let out a heavy sigh, looking as if he had aged more than ten years in an instant.","This matter begins over twenty years ago. Has the County Princess ever heard of the Wu family army?","Song Jinzhao shook her head. No, I haven't. More than twenty years ago, not only had she not yet transmigrated to this world, but even the original owner of her body had not been born.","Chen Fu spoke with a heavy tone, Twenty-five years ago, the Kingdom of Shuobei started a war at the border. The late Emperor decreed that Marquis Wuying lead the Wu family army to the border to provide support. The two sides fought for a year without a clear victor. It was not until the Battle of the Chiwu River in the spring of the following year that the Wu family army suffered a crushing defeat and was nearly wiped out. The reason was that Marquis Wuying committed treason and leaked military secrets.","The Emperor was furious and ordered the execution of the entire Wu family. Even the remaining two hundred or so soldiers of the Wu family army were to be beheaded. At that time, my master and Marquis Wuying were close friends. He did not believe the Marquis would commit treason, but the disaster of the family extermination was already irreversible. Unable to save those in the capital, he sought to preserve the lives of these two hundred men. Regardless of whether Marquis Wuying committed treason, these ordinary soldiers were innocent.","Thus, he sent people to the border to spend silver and secretly substitute them, saving these men's lives. Because they were all disabled to varying degrees and would struggle to survive, and fearing their identities would be exposed and discovered, he secretly arranged for them to stay in his own agricultural estate, giving them land to farm.","Later, when the Chen family was destroyed, the estate was confiscated and turned into an imperial estate. Li Hou and I, as the managers, kept these men hidden. If outsiders were to learn of this, they would undoubtedly be put to death.","Song Jinzhao's thoughts were a bit chaotic. There were too many mysteries surrounding the whole affair, and many things she did not understand.","Who else knows about this besides the two of you?","Chen Fu and Li Hou shook their heads simultaneously. No one else knows but us. The master did not tell anyone else.","Song Jinzhao asked, Do those tenant farmers know that they are legally dead?","From the brief encounters she just had, they did not look like they knew.","Chen Fu shook his head, his eyes showing immense complexity as he said, They do not know. When the master brought them back, he registered new household identities for them. The contracts were signed using the new identities, but the tenant farmers still hold their old household registration papers.","Song Jinzhao furrowed her brows deeply. Has no one noticed in over twenty years? Have they never contacted their former families?","Surviving a great disaster, they would certainly want to reunite with their families. How could they not reach out?","Li Hou replied, They have no families. Their homes were trampled flat by the Shuobei army long ago. The fighting was fierce back then, with people dying every day. These men were all new recruits who joined the army at the border.","Being disabled, they naturally felt inferior and almost never left the estate. The master also forbade them from going out, so they did not know the Emperor had ordered their execution. Later, the two countries called a truce, and as time passed, people gradually stopped bringing the matter up.","Song Jinzhao asked, When they took wives, didn't the women ask what they used to do?","Chen Fu explained, Li Hou and I found matchmakers from out of town to arrange their marriages. Moreover, we told them that because Marquis Wuying committed treason, the Wu family army had a bad reputation, so they shouldn't tell others they were once part of the Wu family army. We told them to just say they were ordinary garrison guards.","Song Jinzhao rubbed her temples, feeling a headache coming on. Before the Chen family was raided, did you collect rent?","Chen Fu and Li Hou shook their heads together. We didn't collect rent back then; we just told them they could farm the land for free. Later, when it became an imperial estate, we had no choice but to collect rent, which is why the contracts were made.","And what about the Internal Affairs Department? A thirty percent rent, with occasional crop reductions due to droughts and floods. Why have they tolerated you for so many years?","Unless the people in the Internal Affairs Department were all useless fools, given the situation recorded in the ledgers, Chen Fu and Li Hou would have been sold off long ago.","Chen Fu swallowed hard. It's exactly as the County Princess guessed. We bribed the stewards of the Internal Affairs Department.","We told them that the contract stated thirty percent, but we actually collected sixty percent, and the extra thirty percent was what we embezzled.","Song Jinzhao asked, How much did the Internal Affairs Department steward take?","Chen Fu replied, We originally planned to give them ten percent, but they were insatiably greedy and insisted on twenty percent. Li Hou and I had no choice but to agree, so we've always given them twenty percent.","Song Jinzhao closed her eyes, not wanting to hear any more. She found it somewhat hard to accept.","They only collected thirty percent rent in total. If they gave away twenty percent, they were left with a mere ten percent.","There were more than twenty people to feed on the estate, and during holidays and festivals, they still had to send tributes to the palace. No wonder these people were so poor.","If they didn't work the fields themselves, they probably wouldn't even be able to afford a decent set of clothes to wear when meeting the Internal Affairs Department steward each year.","Seeing Song Jinzhao remain silent, Chen Fu and Li Hou felt extremely anxious, worried that she would expose them for harboring imperial criminals.","Their old master had shown them great kindness. If they could not protect these men and let them die, they would truly fail to live up to their master's dying wishes.","County Princess, these men are innocent. It was to defend the Dongzhao Nation that they had their limbs severed and eyes blinded by the enemy. They truly shouldn't be killed.","So many years have passed, and no one in the capital recognizes them. As long as you don't say anything, no one will find out.","Originally, Daohua Estate and Shiquan Estate were imperial properties, and they worried the Internal Affairs Department would discover them one day. But now, these two estates had been bestowed upon County Princess Linghui by the Emperor. As long as she kept quiet, no one would ever know.","Song Jinzhao's shadowed eyes were as deep as an ancient well, her fingers continuously tapping against the tabletop.","Today, this County Princess only came to see if the vegetable greenhouses promoted by the imperial court have been implemented on the estate. I haven't heard anything else.","The anxiety in Chen Fu and Li Hou's eyes was replaced by pleasant surprise. Before they could even bow in gratitude, Song Jinzhao stood up and left.","Looking at her slender back, Chen Fu felt her figure seemed incredibly tall, as if she could hold up the entire sky.","As the door was opened, the eyes of everyone in the courtyard focused on Song Jinzhao. Looking past her, they saw the two managers still kneeling on the ground.","Those who were unaware were full of confusion. What exactly had happened?","A new official applies strict rules upon arrival; was the new owner here to establish her authority?","Song Shixue came forward and called out, Sister.","She didn't know the truth, only that her sister's expression was very serious at the moment, clearly indicating something was wrong.","Song Jinzhao didn't explain. She looked up at the sky, feeling as if the dazzling sunlight was now covered by a layer of shadow.","After a moment of silence, when she spoke again, her voice sounded as if it had been soaked in water. We have finished inspecting the estate. Let's go back first.","There is no wall in the world that does not leak wind. Soldiers are naturally more vigilant than ordinary people. Did truly none of them know the truth? Or were they pretending to be ignorant to save their own lives?","Walking along the field ridges and encountering those disabled men again, Song Jinzhao's eyes held a hint of scrutiny, alongside the imagined scenes of these men losing their heads if the matter were to be exposed.","Among the crowd, a few men standing together stared vigilantly at Song Jinzhao, their tense backs looking as if they might lunge forward in the next second.","Feeling a prickle on her back, Song Jinzhao suddenly turned around, her eyes meeting the gaze of the man who had just pointed the way for them.","The moment their eyes met, the man quickly darted his gaze away as if he had been electrocuted. Song Jinzhao's fingers, hanging by her side, twitched slightly. This matter indeed needed further investigation.","On the way back, Song Jinzhao instructed, Do not say a single word about what happened today when we return. Do not tell anyone.","Yes. Qingshuang and Lanxi nodded in agreement. Even though they were curious, they held their tongues and did not ask any questions.","After the greenhouse frame was set up and all instructions were given, Dong Yuanbin finally left in his carriage.","Having experienced such a thrilling and exhausting morning, he now just wanted to lie down and not say a single word.","The sound of galloping hooves came from behind. The servant riding at the rear turned his head to look. His pupils shrank, and he opened his mouth to scream in terror. Tightening his grip on the reins, he urged his horse to sprint wildly forward.","A tiger! There really is a tiger! A tiger is coming!","Dong Yuanbin, who had been resting with his eyes closed, suddenly snapped them open. Startled, he and the Deputy Minister of the Court of Agricultural Review lifted the window curtains to look outside, only to be hit in the face by the dust kicked up by the hooves.","By the time they could see clearly, the tiger was only about thirty paces away from them.","A white one? Dong Yuanbin blinked, pulled his head back in from the window, and shouted to the driver, who was frantically whipping the horses, Stop the carriage!","The subordinate sitting next to him looked at him in astonishment. My Lord, the few of us cannot fight off a tiger.","Seeing that the driver merely slowed down instead of stopping, Dong Yuanbin raised his voice and commanded again, Did you not hear what this official said? Stop the carriage!","Who said anything about fighting? That is the tiger raised by County Princess Linghui. Did you not see the people following behind it?","The Deputy Minister of the Court of Agricultural Review froze. After coming to his senses, he lifted the curtain and looked out the window once more.","There were indeed people following it, and the tiger was even on a leash."]},{"number":232,"title":"Chapter 232: Exploration or Party Strife","paragraphs":["After the carriage came to a steady halt, Dong Yuanbin stepped down with his subordinates. \"I pay my respects to County Princess Linghui.\"","Looking at Xuetuan, who was raising its head and roaring, the two men tacitly refrained from approaching. Instead, they stopped ten paces away and bowed with cupped hands.","Seeing that they were covered in mud, Song Jinzhao asked, \"Did Lord Dong personally lead your men to plant potatoes?\"","Dong Yuanbin smiled and nodded. \"With so few potato seeds, I couldn't set my mind at ease, so I had to oversee it personally. We haven't planted them yet. The weather is getting colder, so we are setting up the greenhouses first. Where is the County Princess coming from? You look travel-worn.\"","Song Jinzhao replied, \"The Emperor rewarded me with two estates. Since I had some free time, I went to take a look.\"","He figured that the tiger roar he heard in the morning must have come from this white tiger; County Princess Linghui must have been passing by the imperial estate at that time.","Dong Yuanbin ordered his subordinates to clear the way and let Song Jinzhao and her group pass first. After they had gone far, the subordinate standing to the side couldn't help but shiver.","\"This is the first time I've seen a white tiger. How did the County Princess tame it?\"","Glancing at his subordinate's timid appearance, Dong Yuanbin retorted, \"With your legs trembling and your inability to even speak clearly, you definitely couldn't tame one anyway.\"","The subordinate shut his mouth, muttering in his heart: It's not like I want to raise a tiger anyway.","After returning to the Ye Manor, Song Jinzhao kept Qingshuang behind alone. \"Go to the neighboring city and inquire about something. Don't let anyone know.\"","Qingshuang leaned close to Song Jinzhao and listened attentively.","The sunlight outside the window was obscured by white clouds, the shadows in the courtyard gradually deepened, and a chill seeped into the air.","...","In just one day, Fei Yanzhang had arranged for Song Gaoli to study at the Imperial Academy.","In the evening, when the servant went to the Duan Manor to pass on the message, the other people in the courtyard all looked towards Song Gaoli, their eyes practically overflowing with jealousy.","\"Some people are just born lucky. Pies fall from the sky even without them lifting a finger.\"","\"Who says otherwise? We've been in the manor for a year, and the teacher never thought about sending us to the Imperial Academy. But a certain someone gets in right after arriving. What great schemes.\"","Facing the cold ridicule of the others, Song Gaoli retorted with a calm expression, \"If you want to study at the Imperial Academy, you can go and ask the teacher yourselves. There's no need to make sarcastic remarks in front of me.\"","If he had the ability, he would have gotten you in, but unfortunately, he can't.","A man dressed in a white scholar's gown took a step forward and sneered at Song Gaoli. \"With your abilities, even if you enter the Imperial Academy, you won't pass the exams. You might as well give up your spot. When I pass the imperial examination and become a Jinshi, I might be able to find a way to give you a hand.\"","A strong sense of humiliation colored Song Gaoli's face. He clenched his fists and gritted his teeth, saying, \"There's no need. I will absolutely pass.\"","His retreating back carried a sense of determination, his shoe soles stomping forcefully on the ground as if venting his anger, leaving behind six resentful people sulking in place.","It was already midnight when Qingshuang returned, yet the candlelight in Song Jinzhao's room was still lit.","\"It is exactly as you said, Miss. In the autumn of the 74th year of Jianyuan, the late Emperor decreed that the Marquis of Wuying lead the Wu family army to the border to resist the enemy. In the first year of Yongyuan, the Wu family army was defeated at the banks of the Chiwu River, and the Emperor ordered the execution of their entire family. The previous owner of Daohua Estate and Shiquan Estate was the then-Chancellor Chen Yan. Two years later, Chen Yan was condemned for disrespecting the Emperor, and his entire family was exiled to the southwest. Rumor has it that they encountered a landslide on the way and no one survived, but Chen Yan is definitely dead.\"","\"Why are the era names different? Wasn't it the late Emperor who ordered the execution of the Wu family?\" Song Jinzhao asked, furrowing her brows. She had thought it was the same emperor.","Qingshuang shook her head. \"The late Emperor passed away in the twelfth lunar month of the 75th year of Jianyuan. Later, the new emperor ascended the throne, who is the current Emperor Chengjing. He was the one who issued the decree.\"","\"Some also say that the Emperor insisted on ordering the execution of the Wu family because the Wu family was the maternal family of the late Prince of Jin, and the Emperor wanted to pull up the weeds by the roots. The Chen family also supported the Prince of Jin back then, which is why they ended up being exiled. However, the people your servant asked all said that Chancellor Chen was a good official who wholeheartedly served the people.\"","Song Jinzhao's brows furrowed even tighter. How did this get tangled up in factional disputes? The matter was becoming increasingly complicated.","The first year of Yongyuan... Ye Liangyu passed the imperial examination and became a Jinshi in the third year of Yongyuan. He must have experienced the exile of the Chen family at that time and might know some inside information."]},{"number":233,"title":"Chapter 233: Waiting for Twenty-Five Years, Qiaowen and Ye Liangyu","paragraphs":["The night shrouded the Daohua Estate in pitch-black darkness. The narrow back door of the estate was opened from the inside, and a thin, small man slipped away into the dark.","Inside a cluster of thatched cottages where the tenant farmers lived, a man missing three fingers and another one-eyed man sat around a fire. The firelight illuminated their faces, yet offered no warmth.","The bamboo door was pushed open from the outside, and the two men instantly stood up, staring intently at the newcomer.","\"What were those people here for today?\"","Chen Jiu looked at the two men, sighed, closed the door behind him, and sat down.","\"The girl who came wearing a green dress today is the newly titled Linghui County Princess. The Emperor has already rewarded her with the Daohua Estate and Shiquan Estate.\"","The two men's expressions changed drastically. This was not good news for them; it was an absolute disaster.","Qu Ya frowned deeply. Recalling the few glances he had exchanged with Song Jinzhao, she did not look like an ordinary sheltered noble young lady.","\"Linghui County Princess... Why does this title sound so familiar? I feel like I've heard it somewhere before.\" Guan Nianshan concentrated on recalling but just couldn't remember.","Chen Jiu said, \"She is the Linghui Township Princess who invented the waterwheel, proposed off-season planting, and built vegetable greenhouses.\"","\"Steward Chen said that at the Emperor's birthday banquet, she presented a type of crop that yields a thousand catties per acre, called potatoes. It has already spread all over the capital. Only those of us who stay on the estate all day didn't know.\"","Qu Ya's pupils darkened. \"As far as I know, does this County Princess know martial arts?\"","Chen Jiu nodded. \"Not only does she know them, but her martial arts are highly formidable. She has killed quite a few people.\"","Guan Nianshan picked up a piece of firewood, added it to the fire, and slowly said, \"If her martial arts weren't high, she wouldn't keep a tiger as a pet. She definitely noticed us today. Did Chen Fu and Li Hou tell her about our identities?\"","Chen Jiu shook his head. \"I don't know. When the Linghui County Princess found issues with the account books, Steward Chen and Steward Li claimed they embezzled the money themselves to buy houses in the neighboring city. The County Princess told them to produce the property deeds, but since they never bought any, they couldn't produce them and claimed they lost the houses gambling.\"","\"The Linghui County Princess said she would raise the rent and sell off Steward Chen's and Steward Li's entire families. After that, Steward Chen's grandson started crying. Later, the two stewards were kept in the room to talk for a long while. I was standing outside and couldn't hear. They didn't say anything when they left, but what I can confirm is that she saw that you both used to be soldiers.\"","Qu Ya used his mangled right hand to touch his chest until he felt the hard bulge.","\"I crossed paths with her twice today. She is highly alert and not an ordinary person. Steward Chen and Steward Li couldn't have kept it hidden; they definitely already told her.\"","Guan Nianshan stood up and paced back and forth in the thatched cottage. \"If she reports us to the authorities, we are dead for sure.\"","Chen Jiu spoke with uncertainty, \"Although the two stewards looked pale, they didn't act like the sky was falling. They did nothing out of the ordinary. There might still be room to turn this situation around.\"","Qu Ya nodded. \"Chen Jiu is right. If she had reported it, the Imperial Guards would have arrived in the afternoon. Since there's been no movement at all, she definitely didn't report it.\"","Guan Nianshan said, \"What should we do now? We can't just sit and wait for death, putting our lives in the hands of a stranger.\"","\"We have no choice but to wait. If she reports to the authorities, the people outside absolutely cannot escape the government's pursuit.\" Qu Ya looked up into Guan Nianshan's eyes. If they left the estate, what if the young master returned one day and couldn't find them?","As if reading the meaning in Qu Ya's eyes, Guan Nianshan's eyes turned red. He sat down dejectedly and said no more.","After Chen Jiu left, he finally raised his head, his moist eyes filled with tears. \"Do you think the young master is still alive?\"","Qu Ya remained silent for a long time before replying, \"Chancellor Chen would definitely protect the young master with his life. He must still be alive.\"","Men do not shed tears easily, but after waiting so many years without any news, Guan Nianshan felt an agonizing pain in his heart.","He spoke in a hoarse voice, asking Qu Ya as much as he was asking himself.","\"If he's alive, why hasn't he come looking for us? Twenty-five years is too long, so long that I'm almost losing hope.\"","Qu Ya reached into his robe and took out the token hidden in his chest. A large character for Wu was prominently carved on it. \"I believe he will come.\"","His gaze falling on the token, Guan Nianshan sadly turned his head away, trying to swallow back his tears.","The next day, after Ye Liangyu returned from his duties at the Censorate, Song Jinzhao sought him out and feigned an inquiry, \"Lord Ye, yesterday I went outside the city to inspect the farmland rewarded to me by the Emperor. I found that the stewards on the estate are old servants left behind by the Chen family. The Imperial Household Department kept them on the estate. If I don't want to use them, can I dispose of them as I please?\"","Ye Liangyu's right hand paused slightly. He lowered his eyes and said, \"According to the rules, since the estate was rewarded to you, you hold their indentures and can deal with them however you wish.\"","\"However, you don't have many people in the capital, and training new servants in a short time is quite troublesome. For the Chen family's servants to become stewards, they must have some ability. You could try to take them in for your own use.\"","Song Jinzhao nodded. \"I heard they used to be trusted aides of the former Chancellor Chen Yan. They have ability, but I'm worried their character might be flawed.\"","Given Ye Liangyu's personality, if the Chen family was exiled innocently and Chen Yan was a good official, he definitely wouldn't be able to stand hearing her say such things.","Just as Song Jinzhao expected, before she could even finish her sentence, Ye Liangyu interrupted her, his tone even a bit aggressive.","\"The Chen family's exile does not mean Chancellor Chen's conduct was flawed. He was framed.\"","Song Jinzhao was taken aback for a moment, not expecting Ye Liangyu to react so strongly.","\"What do you mean by that, my Lord?\"","Ye Liangyu asked her in return, \"Currently in the court, Prince Qi and Prince Ying stand as equals in opposition. No matter who ascends the throne in the future, does the County Princess think they will treat the officials who once stood against them kindly?\"","Song Jinzhao shook her head. \"I have witnessed the character of these two princes. They are narrow-minded and likely won't be kind.\"","The corners of Ye Liangyu's mouth curled up in pure bitterness. \"It was the same for Chancellor Chen back then. Although he didn't directly align with Prince Jin's faction, he and Marquis Wuying were close friends who grew up together, and the Wu family was Prince Jin's maternal family. So, in the eyes of outsiders, he was also part of Prince Jin's faction.\"","\"When Marquis Wuying was executed with his entire family for treason, Chancellor Chen firmly believed that the Marquis was wronged. He repeatedly submitted memorials requesting a reinvestigation of the case, but was rejected by the Emperor every time.\"","\"It wasn't until two years later, when Chancellor Chen's disciple, Gu Qishan, found a journal in the Chen manor's study. It was filled with curses directed at the Emperor for not letting him reinvestigate the case. As a result, the charge of disrespecting the Emperor fell upon him, and the outcome was that all thirty-six members of the manor were exiled.\"","Song Jinzhao blinked. So Gu Qishan had become the Chancellor by reporting his own teacher.","\"Did he really write it?\"","Ye Liangyu said indignantly, \"This was clearly a deliberate frame-up by Gu Qishan, that traitor who deceived his master and destroyed his ancestors, just to climb the ranks. The current Emperor had long been unable to tolerate Chancellor Chen because of the matters concerning Prince Jin and the Wu family. Gu Qishan saw this clearly, which is why he made his move.\"","\"It's just hateful that I had only just entered the Hanlin Academy at the time. My position was low and my words carried no weight, otherwise I would have impeached him to death.\"","Song Jinzhao: \"...\"","If Xiao Chengjing had made up his mind to condemn Chen Yan, it was only fortunate that Ye Liangyu had not yet entered the Censorate at that time. Otherwise, given his outspoken nature and his stubborn tendency to walk down a single path until it went dark, he definitely would not have survived to this day.","\"Chen Yan was so determined to overturn the verdict for the Marquis of Wuying. Could it be that the events of those years were truly a wrongful accusation?\"","Ye Liangyu, who had just been speaking with righteous indignation, so agitated that his white beard was practically flying, instantly became mute.","Song Jinzhao could not read his attitude regarding this matter from his face.","After a long silence, Ye Liangyu slowly shook his head. \"The witnesses and material evidence were all present. The Wu family truly had no way to refute it. The only flaw in this case was that the Marquis of Wuying never pleaded guilty; instead, he was shot to death while fleeing. That is why Prime Minister Chen, who had a very deep friendship with him, always insisted on his innocence. But to say that he harbored treasonous intentions just because the Emperor refused to let him reopen the case, that I do not believe.\"","Song Jinzhao blinked. After so many years, the man was already dead, yet Ye Liangyu still referred to Chen Yan as Prime Minister Chen with every breath, showing his deep respect for him.","When the Chen family was exiled in the third year of Yongyuan, Ye Liangyu had only recently passed the imperial examination and entered the court as an official. There must have been some interaction between the two of them back then to earn such deep trust.","\"Your Excellency just mentioned that the Wu family was the maternal family of the Prince of Jin. Holding such heavy military power, if he did not die, the Emperor's dragon throne would likely not be secure.\"","\"Speak cautiously, County Princess,\" Ye Liangyu's eyes widened sharply as he stood up to make sure no one else was outside the room. \"You cannot speak such words recklessly. It will bring a fatal disaster.\"","Song Jinzhao covered her mouth, pretending to have misspoken. She looked frightened, but her mouth did not stop.","\"I was just making a random guess. If the Emperor could not even tolerate Chen Yan, how could he possibly spare the Wu family?\"","To behead even the disabled ordinary soldiers, Xiao Chengjing must have been quite ruthless back then.","Ye Liangyu stood before Song Jinzhao with his hands behind his back. \"There was a reason why the Emperor refused to let Prime Minister Chen reinvestigate the case back then. After the Wu family was entirely executed, the Yuecheng Army stationed in Yuecheng unexpectedly defected to the foreign tribes in the southwest.\"","\"Although the southwest is also the territory of the Dongzhao Kingdom, these foreign tribes have always been restless, frequently recruiting soldiers and buying horses in an attempt to establish a separatist regime. The Yuecheng Army's actions were tantamount to treason. The commander-in-chief of the Yuecheng Army, Zeng Qing, was single-handedly promoted by the Marquis of Wuying, and half of the Yuecheng Army had served in the Wu Family Army. How could the Emperor not be furious?\"","Song Jinzhao frowned in confusion. \"If that was the case, why did they not attack back then? There was a ready-made excuse to deploy troops.\"","Ye Liangyu replied, \"At that time, the Wu Family Army had been defeated at the border, and the Duke of Zhenguo led the remaining troops to resist the enemy. The imperial court had no more soldiers to deploy. It was a blessing that the southwest did not take advantage of the crisis to strike; how could the Emperor have the energy to deal with them?\"","\"After the peace talks between the two countries, the imperial court lost almost half the silver in its treasury. Coupled with the depletion of military strength, they could not afford another war in the short term. They could only let the foreign tribes in the southwest do as they pleased. Over the years, their military power has gradually expanded, and they have already become a major threat to the court.\"","Song Jinzhao remained silent. The commander of the Yuecheng Army must have worried that Xiao Chengjing would come after him, which was why he preemptively led his troops to flee.","With so many troops at hand, if the Wu Family Army had not gone to the border, the Prince of Jin could have easily conquered this empire by force.","She just did not know what exactly happened during the battle for the throne back then. The schemes involved were probably only known to the players deeply entrenched in the struggle.","Those disabled soldiers at the estate could only be considered collateral damage, innocent fish in the moat; already crippled, they still had to suffer the blade.","There must be someone among them who knew the Emperor wanted to kill them, which was why they hid in the estate behind closed doors, dragging out their ignoble existence."]},{"number":234,"title":"Chapter 234: Determined to Conceal, Housewarming Banquet","paragraphs":["Returning to Daohua Estate and Shiquan Estate, Song Jinzhao stood on the ridge of the field and stared at the physically disabled soldiers for a long time. Her gaze fell on their wives and children. If she were to report this to the authorities, these people would probably lose their lives as well.","After pondering for a long time, Song Jinzhao seemed to have made a very important decision.","Never mind. Even if the matter was exposed one day, it would be the fault of the Internal Affairs Department. She had not even been born back then; she was just an innocent scapegoat who inherited the mess.","The estates were bestowed by the Emperor, so the blame could not fall on her anyway. It would not go so far as to cost the lives of these disabled soldiers, women, and children when the matter had passed for over twenty years.","However, with a thirty percent rent, she would not be able to earn a single penny. Besides, their labor force was very weak. She still had to think of a way to resolve this.","Staring at Song Jinzhao's dashing figure as she rode away on horseback, Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan felt extremely heavy-hearted.","Why did the Linghui Princess of the County come again? Did she still want to expose them?","Over the following days, the two waited anxiously day after day, but everything on the estate remained as usual.","If there was any change, it was that Chen Fu and Li Hou went from door to door, informing them that the estate had a new owner and telling them to work hard and absolutely not slack off, striving to harvest more grain to pay the rent.","It seemed that this Linghui Princess of the County did not intend to expose the matter. The two men's uneasy hearts gradually relaxed as the days passed.","A few days after Song Jinzhao returned from the estate, Fang Zhixing, a director from the Ministry of Works' Construction and Repair Department, came to inform her that the Princess's residence had been fully repaired and cleaned. He also reminded Song Jinzhao that the day after tomorrow would be an auspicious day for moving.","The next day, Song Jinzhao took her younger brother and sister out to buy many gifts to thank Ye Liangyu for letting them stay at the Ye Manor during this time.","Looking at the famous teas and fine wines on the table, Ye Liangyu actually felt somewhat reluctant to see Song Jinzhao and the others leave.","Since his parents passed away, he had lived alone in the mansion as a solitary man. Although Song Jinzhao and her siblings had only stayed in the backyard for ten days, the sounds of their playful banter in the courtyard when he returned from court every day always drew him to speak a few more words. Even the dining table was much livelier than before, unlike the cold and desolate atmosphere when he was all alone.","But he also knew he could not stop them. After having Yunhe accept the gifts, he said, Miss Song, as a Princess of the County now, you have essentially stepped half a foot into the capital's aristocratic circles. Moreover, your residence was a gift from the Emperor. After moving, it stands to reason that you should host a housewarming banquet and invite the high officials and nobles in the capital to your home to celebrate.","This matter concerns the future prestige of the Song Manor in the capital. The guest list must be comprehensive. Whether they come or not, the invitations must be sent out. You absolutely cannot afford to offend anyone over this.","After all, the Song family came from commoner origins. Ye Liangyu was not worried about simple social interactions, but he was truly concerned that Song Jinzhao did not understand the rules among such noble families.","The housewarming banquet was not only an expression of gratitude for the Emperor's gift, but also the first step for the Song family to establish a firm foothold in the capital. There especially could not be any mistakes, otherwise, people would say she lacked manners and was indeed someone from a small place with an unchangeable baseness in her bones, thereby looking down on the Song Manor even more.","Before Song Qiming entered the court as an official, the lintel of the Song Manor could be said to be entirely supported by Song Jinzhao's title as the Linghui Princess of the County; she absolutely had to hold it up.","Song Jinzhao blinked. She had thought about hosting a housewarming banquet, but she merely intended to invite a few familiar people over for a casual meal.","Inviting all the high officials and nobles in the entire capital, ninety-nine percent of whom she didn't even know, would not only be troublesome, but she also wouldn't know what kind of chaos might ensue.","However, meeting the serious and earnest look in Ye Liangyu's eyes, Song Jinzhao could not help but start thinking about this matter.","A wise person does not fight a losing battle. Since they had come to the capital, they had to establish a foothold here eventually. They still needed to go through the motions of making connections and socializing.","In the future, when Qiming entered the court as an official, he could not be completely without social ties. Although a lone minister was commendable, a single tree cannot make a forest, and it is easily broken and snapped.","Song Jinzhao said, To be honest with you, Lord Ye, I really do not understand the relationships and social interactions among the various manors in the capital. I'm afraid the housewarming banquet will be difficult to handle.","Ye Liangyu reached out his hand, and Yunhe, who was standing to the side, immediately took a step forward.","There are no female family members in my manor. Yunhe manages all external social relations. Let him explain it to you. During the housewarming banquet, you can freely assign the servants in my manor as you see fit, and just return them after it's done.","Ye Liangyu had no heirs. Now that he had accepted Song Qiming as his student, and seeing how promising the boy was, he would naturally do everything possible to pave the way for him. Otherwise, he would not have repeatedly used his own network of connections to help Song Jinzhao. While there was certainly the favor of treating his legs involved, it was mostly for Song Qiming's sake.","With a family backing him up, he would always be able to walk a steadier path.","Moreover, Song Jinzhao was unlike ordinary women. She was truly too capable, and the assistance she would bring to Song Qiming in the future would be immeasurable.","The Song family had not brought much luggage on their journey to the capital this time. Adding what they had purchased these past few days, two carriages were enough to transport it all.","The Princess's residence covered an area of fourteen mu. Their belongings could not even fill a fraction of the more than seventy rooms.","Including the gardens, rockeries, and ponds, Song Jinzhao and her siblings, along with Lanxi, Qingshuang, and Qingshui who was responsible for cooking, totaled only eight people, plus a tiger.","Walking through the mansion, one could shout without anyone hearing it. It felt extremely desolate, and furthermore, there was no one to clean it.","The house was large, but tidying it up was also troublesome.","On the day of the move, Ye Liangyu walked around the mansion and couldn't help but nod continuously.","If it weren't for the former Vice Minister of Personnel's corruption and bribery, even if the Internal Affairs Department had repaired it perfectly, it wouldn't have such diverse scenery where the view changes every seven steps. He even secretly expanded the area by several mu back then. That small vegetable garden at the back used to be the houses of nearby commoners. He later secretly bought them and converted them into a backyard. I heard it was used for raising cattle, just so he could have fresh beef to eat every day.","The imperial court explicitly prohibited the arbitrary slaughter of draft cattle; even if one raised them themselves, it was not allowed.","But when that Vice Minister of Personnel's estate was confiscated, there were eighty head of cattle kept in the manor. Just the cattle bones buried beneath the vegetable patch amounted to more than two hundred excavated. If the evidence hadn't been irrefutable, no one would have believed the truth if it were spoken.","Song Jinzhao also felt that the scenery inside the mansion was beautiful, but no matter how good the scenery was, it needed someone to maintain it. Otherwise, after a month, it would definitely look terribly ugly.","Buying one or two servants this time would certainly not be enough; they had to be bought by the dozens.","She would also have to pay these people their monthly wages. Once the housewarming banquet was over, she still needed to hurry and think of ways to generate new sources of income. The more money she earned, the better.","Ten days had passed since Song Qiming entered the Imperial Academy to study. The most common discussion among his classmates was comparing him with Dongfang Yukun.","Originally, most people had already decided that the top scholar of next year's spring imperial examination would be Dongfang Yukun. After all, he had passed the provincial examination to become a Juren at the age of ten, and was even the Jieyuan, the first-place winner.","But now a Song Qiming had popped up. He started his education at the age of ten and, in just three years, passed the provincial examination to become a Juren, also securing the title of Jieyuan.","Both were young geniuses. With two of them appearing at once in this special imperial examination, it was absolutely a clash of the titans.","Just when everyone was watching and expecting them to dislike each other and fight to the bitter end, the relationship between these two people progressed surprisingly rapidly.","Only ten days had passed, and they had already begun to come and go together. They even stayed together for lunch, after class, and when going to the latrine, leaving everyone absolutely dumbfounded.","You have to know that although Song Qiming's older sister was now a County Princess, the Song family had risen to power too quickly and lacked a solid foundation. Aside from Song Jinzhao, they had no one backing them.","But the Dongfang family was different.","Dongfang Yukun's grandfather was a veteran minister who had served two emperors. Both his grandfather and his biological father held high-ranking positions at court. Even Prince Ying and Prince Qi wouldn't dare offend them easily.","It truly dropped many people's jaws that two individuals with such vastly different family backgrounds, who were also competitors, could become friends in such a short period.","After entering the Imperial College, Song Gaoli did not follow Duan Yanhua's instructions to socialize with the rich and powerful to gather information. Instead, he chose to stick closely to Song Qiming. Over time, everyone naturally assumed he was Song Qiming's lackey.","However, Song Gaoli didn't care about this at all. His only goal right now was to pass the imperial examination and become a Jinshi. Being called a lackey was far better than being bullied.","On his very first day at the Imperial College, everyone found out that he had placed dead last in the Longbei Provincial Examination. The disdainful looks they gave him then were still vivid in his mind.","Every time he recalled it, it was like reliving the scene all over again. He could almost see people pointing at his nose, cursing him for having no real talent and getting in through the back door. That sense of inferiority and humiliation was so awful that he wished he could dig a hole and bury himself on the spot.","Moreover, after entering, Song Gaoli discovered that there were many students from ordinary backgrounds in the Imperial College.","Not only were they bossed around like servants by the young masters of noble families, but they didn't even dare to outperform them in class or in writing essays. They were oppressed anytime and anywhere, and he definitely didn't want to end up like that.","By following Song Qiming, he was treated as a brother. If he followed anyone else, he would truly be a servant, serving them tea, pouring water, and constantly flattering them. How could he possibly focus all his energy on studying then?","At this very moment, standing before the flowerbed, Song Qiming and Dongfang Yukun were composing poems about the blooming yellow chrysanthemums, while Song Gaoli stood by and observed.","He savored and analyzed their poems while reciting his own, waiting for Song Qiming and Dongfang Yukun to offer their guidance.","Song Qiming's feedback was relatively tactful, but Dongfang Yukun had a truly venomous tongue. The moment he spotted a flaw, he would point it out mercilessly, always following up with: You just change it exactly as I said, and I guarantee the teacher will praise you.","After critiquing Song Gaoli's poem, Dongfang Yukun turned to Song Qiming. Your family is hosting a housewarming banquet? My mother said she received an invitation.","Song Qiming nodded. My teacher had my sister send invitations to everyone. I am just not sure how many will actually come.","Dongfang Yukun proudly threw an arm over Song Qiming's shoulder. Don't worry, I will definitely make my parents go. I absolutely won't let your Song family lose face.","Song Gaoli's eyes lit up. If the Dongfang family attended, many court officials would definitely give them face and show up. At the very least, it wouldn't end up with half of the dozen tables empty, that would be far too embarrassing.","Song Qiming smiled gently. It would be best if your parents could grace us with their presence, but if they cannot make it, just having you there is enough. I have already boasted to my sister and younger sister about how incredibly talented and devastatingly handsome you are, like Pan An himself. They have to see you with their own eyes this time.","Dongfang Yukun removed his hand from Song Qiming's shoulder and lifted his chin with a look of defiance. When it comes to talent and looks, how could Pan An possibly compare to me?","Song Qiming met his gaze, while Song Gaoli stifled a laugh beside them.","I was just giving an example. You are definitely a thousand times better than him.","When they first met, Song Qiming thought the other boy was an aloof, brilliant, and stunningly handsome flower on a high peak. But after spending time with him, he realized the guy was not only arrogant but also incredibly narcissistic, absolutely reveling in having others swoon over him.","The Dongfang family wasn't the only one to receive an invitation; the families of many students at the Imperial College received them as well.","Upon hearing that the Dongfang family was attending, many students went home and told their parents.","News spread quickly among the officials. The very next day at morning court, an acquainted minister asked the Minister of Personnel if he had received an invitation from the Song residence.","Dongfang Shaoting nodded without the slightest hesitation. Not only did he confirm it, but he also turned the question around on the others.","I have heard the scenery at the County Princess's estate is quite lovely. Since it was bestowed by the Emperor and the County Princess has extended an invitation, as an official, I naturally must bring my family to offer our congratulations. Are you gentlemen not going?","The group looked at a loss, turning their heads to glance at Prince Qi and Prince Ying standing not far away. Could they go?","Xiao Rongche and Xiao Rongyan's faces darkened. Whoever attends is making an enemy of us princes.","The Song family wants to integrate into the capital's noble circles? Keep dreaming!","On the day of the housewarming banquet, almost all the servants from the Ye residence were at the County Princess's estate helping out, and Ye Liangyu arrived very early.","Song Jinzhao had even spent a fortune to hire the head chef from the Moon Gazing Pavilion to oversee the kitchen, determined to ensure no one could find a single fault.","As the Si hour approached, guests began to arrive one after another with gifts to offer their congratulations. Most of them were minor officials, such as Dong Yuanbin, the Chief Minister of the Court of National Granaries, and Duan Yanhua, a compiler at the Hanlin Academy. Song Gaoli arrived with him.","It wasn't until halfway through the Si hour, when Ou Shinian, the Minister of Works, and Fei Yanzhang, a scholar of the Hanlin Academy, arrived with their families that the situation underwent a subtle shift.","Officials who were currently exchanging pleasantries looked in surprise at Ou Shinian, who was speaking with Song Jinzhao with a face full of smiles. The Minister of Works is actually the first to arrive. When did the Linghui County Princess establish a connection with him? Do you think the other five Ministers will come?","The official he was talking to whispered back, You must be out of the loop. The Ministry of Personnel will definitely come. As for the others, it is hard to say.","Ou Shinian cheerfully handed over his gift. As expected of an estate bestowed by the Emperor, the County Princess's residence is much grander than my ministerial manor.","Song Jinzhao smiled warmly. Lord Ou is too generous with his praise. It is all thanks to the excellent renovations done by the Department of Construction.","Sitting at a table in the back, Fang Zhixing heard Song Jinzhao praising his work and proudly lifted his chin. It was a pity Minister Dongfang hadn't arrived yet; it would have been great if he could hear it with his own ears.","Seeing Song Jinzhao smiling, Ou Shinian quietly stepped to her right side and spoke in a hushed tone.","If the County Princess invents anything else to present to the Emperor next time, could you please send me a message first? I don't want the credit; I only ask that when the Emperor questions me, I can at least say a few words. To be honest with the County Princess, my salary for next year has already been completely docked.","Song Jinzhao curled her lips into a teasing smile. Surely Minister Ou isn't lacking this one year's salary?","Ou Shinian: ...Actually, I really am.","Their eyes met, and they shared a silent smile, as if they had reached a mutual understanding, or perhaps not.","On the other side, Fei Yanzhang walked up beside Ye Liangyu, observing Song Qiming, who was standing at the door greeting guests. He was elegant in his bearing and proper in his speech. Although he was still young, he knew exactly how to advance and retreat, and was quite steady.","Even when facing important court officials, he was neither haughty nor humble. He was a promising young talent worth nurturing. His good friend had indeed taken on the right student.","Seeing that Fei Yanzhang's gaze was fixed on Song Qiming, Ye Liangyu smiled and nudged his friend's arm. Well? This student of mine isn't bad, is he?","Fei Yanzhang nodded. He is indeed quite good. If you weren't so anxious for him to enter the court, this child should have waited another three years. Thirteen is ultimately too young."]},{"number":235,"title":"Chapter 235: Princess Yongjia and Duke Qing Arrive at the Scene","paragraphs":["Ye Liangyu's straight back slumped slightly.","\"I also wanted him to temper himself for another three years, but on one hand, the child himself wants to enter the court as an official as soon as possible. I guess he doesn't want his sister to work so hard supporting everything alone.\"","\"On the other hand, I really don't know if I'll still be around in three years. What if I can't help him then?\"","Fei Yanzhang glared at him with tiger-like eyes. \"What nonsense are you spouting? You're only in your forties, what do you mean you don't know if you'll be around? You have to live to at least eighty before you can die.\"","Ye Liangyu's fingers slid from his white beard to his white eyebrows, finally grasping his head full of white hair.","His hair turning white overnight was a true reflection of the utter despair he felt when he learned he was crippled back then.","\"Who knows when an accident might suddenly happen. It's better to make preparations early. This child is neither anxious nor rash; he is calm and patient when facing issues. I believe he can do it.\"","Thinking of what happened at the hunting grounds back then, Fei Yanzhang could only remain silent. If only the Emperor had fathered a few more princes.","The number of guests arriving to offer their congratulations gradually increased. With the appearance of Dongfang Shaoting bringing his wife and children, the banquet truly began to liven up.","At a glance, although not many officials from the factions of the Prince of Ying and the Prince of Qi came, half of their female family members had arrived.","Her gaze fell upon the young man whose skin was so white it seemed to glow. A flash of amazement crossed Song Jinzhao's eyes; Qiming truly hadn't exaggerated.","Dressed in a crescent-white brocade jacket, the young man was dazzling among the crowd. The others couldn't even serve as a foil to him, completely fading from sight.","Song Shixue blinked, staring at him with the thought that he was someone to be admired from afar but not approached lightly.","Seeing this, Dongfang Yukun was secretly pleased, though on the surface he maintained the aloof demeanor of a modest gentleman.","Faced with such a handsome man, Song Jinzhao merely appreciated him briefly before moving on. Instead, it was Song Shixue who kept stealing glances at him.","This caused Lanxi, who was bringing things over, to look extremely displeased.","Once the hour arrived, even though the tables weren't full, Song Jinzhao didn't wait any longer and directly announced the start of the banquet.","She took Song Shixue to host the women's tables, while the men's tables were left in the charge of Song Qiming. With Ye Liangyu guiding him, nothing would go wrong.","Young Song Anhao was arranged to sit at a table full of female guests, showing no stage fright at all.","His mouth never stopped moving. Not long after the banquet began, he had already praised every lady at the table. The madams all complimented him for being clever and adorable, and some even gave him small gifts on the spot.","Just when everyone thought today's housewarming banquet would pass by just like this, Yunhe hurriedly ran in and said to Song Jinzhao, \"County Princess, the carriages of Princess Yongjia and the Duke of Qing have already stopped at the estate's entrance.\"","Although his voice wasn't loud, the madams at the table all heard him.","Their eyes were filled with astonishment, unable to believe that Princess Yongjia would come.","\"Please enjoy your meal, ladies.\"","Song Jinzhao stood up and had only taken a few steps when she heard the servant standing outside the front hall shout loudly: \"Princess Yongjia has arrived! The Duke of Qing has arrived!\"","The men's tables, previously bustling with clinking glasses, instantly fell silent. Everyone looked up in unison, and sure enough, they saw Xiao Yongjia and Chu Liuyun step over the threshold one after the other.","\"Your subject greets Her Highness the Princess.\"","\"Your humble official greets Her Highness the Princess.\"","\"Your subject's wife greets Her Highness the Princess.\"","\"Your commoner greets Her Highness the Princess.\"","...","In the blink of an eye, a whole swath of people knelt in the front hall. Only two Ministers and Ye Liangyu remained standing, offering a bowing salute.","\"You may all rise.\"","\"Imperial Father heard that the County Princess of Linghui is hosting a housewarming banquet at her estate today, and specially sent this princess to offer congratulations.\"","Song Jinzhao: \"Your subject bows in gratitude for His Majesty's profound grace.\"","Something wasn't right. Why would the Emperor specifically send a princess to deliver gifts for a mere County Princess's housewarming banquet? Even if he wanted to send gifts, a eunuch would have sufficed.","Thinking of the relationship between Princess Yongjia and Chu Liuyun, Song Jinzhao already had a theory in mind.","If this matter wasn't handled well, it might truly become a troublesome issue.","Chu Liuyun swept his gaze over the officials sitting at the men's tables.","Two out of the Six Ministers had come, and there were also people from the Hanlin Academy and the Censorate. After today, the Song family could be considered to have firmly established their footing in the capital.","One truly could not underestimate this woman. Her rise was even faster than that of civil officials making their fortunes. Her next step would likely be aiming for the title of Commandery Princess.","\"This official was busy with public affairs and arrived a bit late. I wonder if the County Princess still has a seat available.\"","Song Jinzhao smiled faintly and said, \"With Her Highness the Princess and the Duke of Qing gracing us with their presence, even if there were no seats, we would have to make some. Qiming, host the Duke of Qing well.\"","After speaking, she extended her hand toward Xiao Yongjia. \"Your Highness, please take the seat of honor.\"","Seeing that Song Jinzhao's gaze did not linger on Chu Liuyun, Princess Yongjia walked toward the women's tables with peace of mind.","Duan Yanhua, sitting in his chair, tightly pinched his thigh with the hand hidden under the table. The Song family was truly formidable!","If those who hadn't come knew that the Emperor had sent the Princess to deliver gifts, and that even the Duke of Qing had arrived, what would they think?","They would probably be terrified to their cores."]},{"number":236,"title":"Chapter 236: Business Plan","paragraphs":["After the banquet dispersed, the list of guests who attended today quickly spread through the various estates. Prince Ying, Xiao Rongyan, stared in disbelief at the servant who brought the news and questioned, Are you saying Imperial Father sent Yongjia to the Song Estate to congratulate Song Jinzhao on her housewarming?","The servant nodded vigorously and said with absolute certainty, This servant saw Princess Yongjia's carriage parked at the entrance of the County Princess's estate with my own eyes. Everyone who went to the banquet is saying so.","Xiao Rongyan frowned, looking slightly anxious. To think Imperial Father values Song Jinzhao so much that he even sent a gift for a mere housewarming banquet!","When Prince Qi, Xiao Rongche, found out, he was so furious that he smashed a tea set on the spot. They are all just a bunch of sycophants, actually rushing to curry favor with a County Princess of a different surname.","Prime Minister Gu Qishan stood before Xiao Rongche and consoled him, She is but a County Princess and cannot make any real waves. Since the Emperor currently favors Song Jinzhao, Your Highness should not act rashly, lest Prince Ying and Ye Liangyu catch onto anything to use against you.","Xiao Rongche took a deep breath and slammed his fist onto the table. His whole person was like an ignited powder keg, ready to explode at any moment.","Upon returning to the palace, Princess Yongjia immediately went to the Imperial Study to report back to Emperor Xiao Chengjing.","Imperial Father, I have delivered the gift you asked me to send.","Xiao Chengjing put down the memorial in his hand and beckoned Princess Yongjia to his side. How was it? How did you get along with County Princess Linghui today?","Xiao Chengjing had not really cared about a housewarming banquet. This morning, Princess Yongjia came to him saying she wanted to leave the palace to attend the Song Estate's housewarming banquet and get to know Song Jinzhao, so he casually asked her to bring a gift along.","Princess Yongjia replied, There were so many guests at the County Princess's estate today that I didn't have any time alone with her. I want to leave the palace and play with her next time.","She only went to the Song Estate because she knew Brother Liuyun was going, and she followed along out of worry.","Throughout the entire banquet, Brother Liuyun only exchanged two sentences with Song Jinzhao, which was even less than what she herself had spoken to her. Today's trip was truly a bit unnecessary.","Xiao Chengjing smiled affectionately at his daughter. There aren't many girls your age in the imperial clan. If you like her, you can visit County Princess Linghui more often so you won't get bored staying in the palace.","Thank you, Imperial Father. Princess Yongjia smiled and nodded at the Emperor. It would be nice if she could leave the palace frequently.","Xiao Chengjing's tone shifted as he suddenly asked, You mentioned there were many guests at the County Princess's estate today. Who all was there? Tell me.","Princess Yongjia focused her mind to recall. There was the Minister of Works and his wife, the Minister of Personnel and his wife, and Dongfang Yukun was there too. He seemed to have a very good relationship with the County Princess's younger brother.","There was also Lord Fei from the Hanlin Academy and Lord Ye from the Censorate. I also heard that all the servants in the County Princess's estate today were temporarily called over from the Ye Estate to help. Even on the male guests' side, Lord Ye took Song Qiming around to entertain them.","There were also some officials I didn't quite recognize. More than half of the dozen or so tables were full. When I arrived, I even bumped into Duke Qing at the entrance; he went too.","Xiao Chengjing looked at his daughter with a playful expression. Tell your Imperial Father the truth. Did you go to the Song Estate today because you wanted to see Chu Liuyun?","Princess Yongjia stopped talking, and two blushes of red dyed her cheeks. She stamped her foot coquettishly and said, Imperial Father, what are you saying? I already told you it was a chance encounter.","Watching Princess Yongjia's small figure fleeing in shyness, the Emperor gave a doting smirk. At sixteen, she was indeed reaching the age for marriage.","Neither Duke Zhenguo nor Chu Liuyun was involved in partisan politics, making him a pretty good choice.","After the housewarming banquet ended, the County Princess's estate became completely quiet. With few people walking about, it felt empty everywhere, and a gust of cold wind made it seem somewhat desolate.","However, Xuetuan liked it very much, running around everywhere every day. Sometimes even Shixue and Anhao couldn't find it.","At night, in the study connected to the bedroom, the bright candlelight shone brilliantly. Song Jinzhao was sitting in her chair, fully engrossed in writing a business proposal.","The braised food shop, milk tea shop, and barbecue shop from Anyang Prefecture could be copied over to open a few more branches in the capital. Luosifen and hot pot restaurants could also be prepared.","She also planned to take back the fields of Daohua Farm and Shiquan Farm after spring next year.","Daohua Farm was close to the river and had better soil, so she planned to use it to grow flowers. Shiquan Farm was located further back and would be used to build a farmstead and a perfume processing factory. By adopting a recruitment method to support these tenant farmers, she could solve their livelihood issues while ensuring her own interests were not compromised.","The number of wealthy people in the capital was several times that of other prefectures, and every woman loved to dress herself up beautifully.","The inner courtyards of high officials and nobles spent countless amounts of silver on clothes and jewelry every year. Bathing in flower petals was also extremely common, but the fragrance from this method lasted for a very short time, often dissipating within a night.","But if there was perfume, the fragrance could be maintained all day without fading. Thinking of the exorbitant prices and terrifying sales volumes of those big-name perfumes in the modern world, Song Jinzhao felt this was a business she absolutely had to do.","The first step was to buy a shop and get the business running. There were enough people on the farms, but what she needed now were workers to labor in the shop. Also, the number of servants in the estate needed to be increased by at least a dozen, so she still had to buy more people.","During the early morning court session the next day, Xiao Chengjing's intimidating gaze circled over the hats of the ministers below. Court of National Agricultural, what is the progress of the potato planting at the imperial farm outside the city?","Dong Yuanbin, the Chief Minister of the Court of National Agricultural, immediately stepped out from the crowd. To reply to Your Majesty, the greenhouses for planting potatoes have all been constructed. The potato tubers have all sprouted eyes, and planting can begin tomorrow.","Xiao Chengjing nodded in satisfaction, his sharp gaze sweeping toward Gu Qishan, who stood at the very front of the officials. My beloved Minister Gu, how is the refinement of the nautical chart coming along, and when can we set sail?","Gu Qishan's passionate heart instantly turned ice-cold. He took a step forward, cupped his hands, and said, To reply to Your Majesty, this subject has led people to look through all the ancient texts in the Chongwen Pavilion. Among them, records regarding maritime affairs are extremely scarce, and none of them match the parchment map submitted by County Princess Linghui. Presumably, it is so far from the coast that our predecessors have never explored it.","Xiao Chengjing was very dissatisfied with Gu Qishan's answer, and his tone grew heavier. I do not care whether our predecessors have explored it or not. Since potatoes could be found in that place, perhaps there are even more astonishing products. If the Chongwen Pavilion cannot find relevant historical records, then we shall personally send people out to sea to search. What do my beloved ministers think?","...","For a moment, no one spoke.","The fierce winds, massive waves, and torrential downpours on the sea could claim a life at any time. At a moment like this, whoever spoke first would be the unlucky one. If things went wrong, they might end up dying in the sea just like those foreigners who traveled across the ocean.","Seeing that no one responded after a long while, Xiao Chengjing's eyes gradually darkened. Prince Qi, what do you think?","Feeling very helpless inside, Xiao Rongche stepped forward. To reply to Imperial Father, this son believes that since the Chongwen Pavilion cannot find relevant historical records, we should send people to search among the common folk. Perhaps someone will know.","Xiao Chengjing was not satisfied with this answer. Who knew if folk histories were true or false? Prince Ying, what is your opinion?","The parchment nautical chart was obtained by Song Jinzhao, and the matter was handed over to Gu Qishan to handle. Even if a new continent was found, the credit would not belong to him; instead, it would only make Song Jinzhao and Prince Qi's faction more smug. Xiao Rongyan wished for nothing more than for this matter to fail.","\"I humbly believe that what Eldest Brother said is not without reason. However, I think we should send envoys to the coastal prefectures to make inquiries. The commoners there spend their years sailing the seas; perhaps they know things that others do not.\"","Xiao Chengjing's expression softened slightly. Seeing that the rest of the court remained silent, he declared, \"We shall do as the Prince of Ying suggests. Order the officials of the coastal prefectures to gather information among the people.\"","The ministers dropped to their knees and chanted in unison, \"Your Majesty is infinitely wise.\"","Standing amidst the crowd, Ye Liangyu lifted her head to steal a glance at the Emperor seated high upon the dragon throne. With progress moving at such a glacial pace, heaven only knew how long it would take to find the true origin of the potatoes.","Now that they already possessed the potato seeds, she feared this whole endeavor would ultimately be left unresolved and forgotten."]},{"number":237,"title":"Chapter 237: Song Jinzhao's Suggestions","paragraphs":["Half an hour after breakfast, the people from the agency led a long line of maids and servants into the outer courtyard of the County Princess's estate. They stood in exactly five rows below the steps, fifty people in total, ranging in age from sixteen to forty.","The agency manager said, \"To answer the County Princess, these are the best batch selected from the human market according to your estate steward's requirements. Every one of them has a clean background and is smart and diligent. Would you like to take your pick, County Princess?\"","Qingshuang bent down and placed a stack of servitude contracts on the table in front of Song Jinzhao. \"Miss, these servants have already been screened once.\"","Originally, the agency had selected a hundred people, but she had directly screened out half of them.","With Fushun absent and Lanxi still young, Song Jinzhao simply let Qingshuang act as the steward of the County Princess's estate, waiting until Fushun came over next year to switch.","\"Meihua.\" Every time Song Jinzhao flipped to a servitude contract, Qingshuang would call out a name, and the corresponding person would step forward from the ranks.","Her gaze swept from their hair down to their shoes, keeping the time spent on each person to under three minutes. It took Song Jinzhao over two hours to finish questioning the fifty people, and in the end, she kept forty.","After the people were led away, the agency manager pulled out another stack of land deeds and floor plans from his chest and handed them to Qingshuang. \"These are the shops selected according to the County Princess's requirements. All the ones on the capital's main street that meet the conditions are here. They can be viewed at any time. Please take a look, County Princess.\"","Song Jinzhao calculated the money in her hands. The profits from the shops in Anyang Prefecture for the past half year wouldn't be in her hands until she went back in February next year. Keeping the thousand taels of gold rewarded by the royal family, the rest had to be put into circulation.","The shops selling milk tea and braised snacks didn't need to be too big. Thirty-something square meters was enough for the luosifen shop. The location for the barbecue restaurant could be a bit cheaper, while the hot pot restaurant was best situated in the liveliest area possible. After picking and choosing, Song Jinzhao selected a small portion to go and see in the afternoon.","After returning from the Censorate at noon, Ye Liangyu didn't go home. Instead, he came to the County Princess's estate to freeload a meal.","\"During the morning court session today, the Emperor asked about the maritime maps. Gu Qishan couldn't find any relevant historical records. Prince Qi and Prince Ying suggested gathering information from the commoners in the coastal prefectures. I'm afraid the matter of finding a new continent won't be accomplished anytime soon.\"","\"This wasn't an easy task to begin with; it easily takes decades just to start. If the Emperor doesn't have firm resolve, it will likely be difficult.\"","Song Jinzhao thought of the maps of the Dongzhao Kingdom and the Beishuo Kingdom she had seen. The territories of both countries were entirely on land, and there were no other countries. They hadn't even had a naval battle before, so they had no navy.","From the routes on the parchment map, she could roughly deduce that those foreigners must have come from the east. She just didn't know if the global map of this world was the same as Earth's.","\"Giant waves, storms, ocean currents, and whirlpools; the sea is full of danger everywhere. Not seeing land for a long time will make people feel lonely and panicked, and losing one's direction can be fatal. If it isn't someone who sails the sea year-round, not only will they fail to find the new continent, but they will also easily lose their lives.\"","\"If the Emperor has truly made up his mind to search, my suggestion is to first establish a navy and train a group of excellent sailors. They can be selected from the commoners and soldiers in the surrounding coastal prefectures, as they are good swimmers.\"","\"Having people alone isn't enough; there must also be ships. Dongzhao Kingdom's current merchant ships are insufficient to handle the sea's monstrous waves and extreme weather. If you take them out to sea, a single giant wave will flip them over. Larger and sturdier ocean-going sailing ships need to be built.\"","Watching Song Jinzhao speak with such assurance, Ye Liangyu raised his eyebrows in surprise, and his right hand holding the chopsticks paused.","\"How do you know so much?\" Anyang Prefecture wasn't by the sea, and he himself had never even seen the ocean.","Song Jinzhao said frankly, \"When I was saving someone at the docks last time, I chatted with the captain about some situations at sea.\"","\"I see,\" Ye Liangyu realized.","\"Training sailors is a small matter, but establishing a navy is a major undertaking. Building sailing ships requires even more money. I'm afraid neither the Ministry of War nor the Ministry of Revenue will agree.\"","The national treasury was empty, and there wasn't enough money to spend as it was. For something that wasn't a necessity and wouldn't show visible benefits in the short term, it would be very difficult to get the Emperor and the Ministry of Revenue to fork over the money.","\"Lord Ye, have you ever considered that since people from other places are already trying to come here, perhaps there are countries in other places too? How many people do they have? How is their national strength? Is their military powerful? If they have intentions to invade, and our Dongzhao Kingdom's military isn't skilled in naval warfare, I'm afraid we won't be able to defeat them when they arrive.\"","Ye Liangyu froze; he had never thought of this point. \"In that case, wouldn't it be easier for us to be discovered if we took the initiative to go looking for them?\"","Song Jinzhao put down her bowl and chopsticks. Qingshui was getting better and better at cooking. She could have her train a few more people so they could be used when she opened a restaurant in the future.","\"Haven't their people already found their way here first? It just depends on whether we take the initiative to strike or defend passively. But that's the worst-case scenario. Perhaps the other party has no ill intentions and just wants to communicate. With a vast ocean between us, invading wouldn't be that easy anyway.\"","Song Jinzhao's words plunged Ye Liangyu into deep thought. His attention completely drifted away, and he didn't even have the mind to continue eating.","Seeing that he was about to leave without finishing his meal, Song Anhao, with a grain of rice stuck to the corner of his mouth, rolled his eyes around and mumbled, \"Sister, didn't you say 'who knows that every single grain on the plate comes from hard work' and forbid me from wasting food? Why don't you scold Uncle Ye when he has so much left in his bowl?\"","Ye Liangyu, who had just stepped over the threshold, slammed on the brakes.","He turned around and looked at the large bowl of rice left in his bowl, meeting Song Anhao's big, disapproving eyes, and couldn't help but feel a wave of shame in his heart.","Song Jinzhao smiled and wiped the grain of rice from the little boy's mouth. \"Lord Ye, please don't take offense. Last time, this child was being greedy. He was almost full but still wanted to fill a large bowl with rice. In the end, he couldn't finish it, so I scolded him a bit.\"","Ye Liangyu returned to the table and sat down, shaking his head as he picked up his chopsticks and started eating again.","\"Anhao is right. Every grain comes from hard work. I shouldn't leave leftover food.\"","Actually, he wasn't full either, but his mind was in a mess right now and he wasn't in the mood to eat. Plus, if he got hungry in the afternoon, there would be pastries, so he hadn't cared.","After finishing the rice in his bowl with the mutton soup, Ye Liangyu suddenly looked at Song Anhao, who was currently battling a lamb chop.","\"Shouldn't Anhao start his early education?\" Being able to blurt out a line of poetry showed he had a good memory. If he started his education from a young age, he might even be more formidable than Qiming.","Song Jinzhao and Song Shixue looked at Song Anhao at the same time. \"He's only three years old. Isn't that a bit too early?\"","Ye Liangyu shook his head. \"It's not early. Children from wealthy families all begin their early education at three or four years old, and they can enter a private school to study at six. Anhao is smart and clever, and his memory is quite good. You can try hiring a tutor to start teaching him.\"","Looking bewildered, Song Anhao gripped his lamb chop and asked, \"Does early education mean going out early and coming back late every day like my older brother? I see him studying until very late every day. It's so exhausting.\"","Hearing this, Ye Liangyu immediately transformed into a teacher and began to preach, \"Studying is the most interesting thing. In books, you will find houses of gold; in books, you will find beauties of jade. As long as you immerse yourself in reading, you will discover the joy within, and you won't find it exhausting.\"","\"If you don't believe me, you can ask your brother. He loves studying the most and never finds it tiring.\"","Song Jinzhao's brow twitched. For a moment, she didn't know whether she should agree or refute him."]},{"number":238,"title":"Chapter 238: Enlightenment for Song Anhao","paragraphs":["Ye Liangyu continued, \"However, since you're still young, you don't need to study from dawn till dusk. Just one two-hour lesson every morning will suffice, mainly to build a foundation for when you enter an academy later on.\"","Song Anhao put down his lamb chop and began counting on his fingers. \"If I wake up at the hour of Chen, by the time I finish eating it'll be almost the hour of Si. Then lunch is at the hour of Wu. That only leaves about three hours in between. The whole morning will be gone just like that.\"","Ye Liangyu frowned disapprovingly. \"The best time of the day is the morning. Classes should be finishing up by the hour of Chen, which means you need to wake up at the hour of Mao.\"","\"Ah... can't it be a bit later?\" Song Anhao's chubby little lips pouted so high they could touch the sky. The hour of Mao was far too early; he wouldn't be able to get out of bed.","Ye Liangyu put on a stern face. \"Studying requires diligence. There is no room for laziness. You need to learn from your older brother in this regard.\"","Turning to look at Song Jinzhao, he added, \"County Princess, all three of you siblings are quite exceptional. Song Anhao will surely take after his brother. If Qiming had begun his early education sooner, he might have even passed the provincial exams and become a Juren earlier than Dongfang Yukun. While the title of top scholar might be out of reach for him now, we absolutely cannot let Song Anhao be delayed as well.\"","Song Jinzhao blinked. It was true that in the modern world, a three-year-old child was old enough to attend kindergarten.","However, there were no kindergartens here. She had originally planned to wait until Song Anhao turned four before hiring a private tutor to teach him at home. Still, starting a bit earlier wouldn't hurt.","\"If we were to hire a tutor to come teach at the house every day, does Lord Ye have any suitable candidates in mind?\"","The ideal person for a three-year-old's early education would be an older scholar who had passed the county exams. Ye Liangyu mentally sifted through everyone he knew. The older scholars he was acquainted with were not in the capital, and those who were in the capital currently held official posts, making them unavailable to serve as tutors.","His mind worked rapidly. When he looked up, his gaze happened to land on Song Jinzhao's gentle face, which remained composed no matter what happened. Suddenly, a bright light sparked in his eyes.","Wasn't the perfect tutor sitting right in front of him?","Qiming and his younger sister's early education had been entirely handled by Song Jinzhao. She had already successfully produced two excellent students, proving that she was a highly capable teacher.","Seeing him staring at her so intently, Song Jinzhao asked hesitantly, \"Lord Ye?\"","Ye Liangyu replied, \"Actually, County Princess, you could teach him yourself. With your talents, providing early education for a three-year-old is more than within your capabilities. The results would likely be far better than hiring an outside tutor. Qiming is a perfect example of this.\"","Song Jinzhao gently stroked her young brother's soft little braid. \"I'm afraid I won't have the time. It would be better to hire a tutor.\"","She was going to be very busy in the near future, and teaching a child to read required a great deal of patience. She worried that once she got busy, she wouldn't be able to give him the attention he needed.","Song Shixue, who had been quietly observing for a while, tentatively raised her hand. \"If Older Sister doesn't have the time, I can teach him. Every day I just stay at home reading medical books or practicing martial arts. I actually have quite a bit of free time. I could give Song Anhao his lessons after my morning training.\"","Ye Liangyu's gaze paused before he nodded hesitantly. \"Actually, that could work. The material during the early education phase is quite simple. It's about teaching by example, integrating lessons into daily life, and instilling virtues and manners. It would be wonderful for you two sisters to handle it. Once Qiming finishes the metropolitan exams and enters the court as an official, he can also offer some daily guidance when he has the time.\"","Song Anhao reached out and grabbed Song Shixue's arm. \"I want Eldest Sister and Second Sister to teach me.\"","Song Jinzhao offered Ye Liangyu a faint smile. \"Early education will be no problem at all for Shixue. Even though she mostly reads medical texts, she has read plenty of other books as well. In terms of the Four Books and Five Classics, if she were to practice writing eight-legged essays just a little, she would be more than capable of passing the county examinations.\"","Hearing this, Song Shixue lowered her eyelashes, the tips of her ears growing slightly warm.","Ye Liangyu couldn't help but smile upon hearing this. What he admired most was the bond between the four Song siblings. They truly embodied deep familial affection. It was a stark contrast to Prince Qi and Prince Ying, who didn't act like brothers at all and seemed to wish nothing more than to kill each other. They completely ignored Princess Yongjia, showing absolutely none of the care expected of older brothers."]},{"number":239,"title":"Chapter 239: Beijing's Housing Prices Are as High as Gold","paragraphs":["In the afternoon, Song Jinzhao went out to look at shops. Song Anhao, whose interest had been piqued, couldn't wait until the next morning. Right after waking up from his afternoon nap, he dragged Song Shixue over to teach him how to read. Unfortunately, this burst of enthusiasm only lasted for half an hour before he collapsed onto the desk.","The manager of the brokerage personally led Song Jinzhao around the inner city. On the bustling streets, he bowed slightly as he introduced the area to her. His facial expressions were lively as he spoke, making him appear both professional and enthusiastic.","\"County Princess, the shops on this street are not large, and they sell high-quality, inexpensive goods. Food stalls make up forty percent of them. The east side leads straight to the capital's central axis, while heading south, west, or north will take you to modest residential houses. A considerable number of people pass through this street every day.\"","\"As you can see, even though the lunch hour has passed, there is still an endless stream of commoners coming and going. If you open an eatery here, you definitely won't have to worry about not making money.\"","At a glance, both sides of Qipan Street were lined with small shops facing each other. The doorways were about three to four meters wide, and looking inside, the layout seemed to be a straight, narrow line.","Stepping into an empty shop, there was a lot of rubbish left behind by the previous tenant on the shelves and the floor. The tables only had a thin layer of dust, and there were no cobwebs on the ceiling, suggesting it hadn't been vacant for long.","The brokerage manager walked in front of Song Jinzhao, pointing at the floor and gesturing. \"Behind this door used to be a warehouse. Since you are going into the food business, County Princess, it can be converted into a kitchen. Setting up ten tables in the front would be absolutely no problem. It faces south, so the lighting is good. The only drawback is that there is no water well. Water has to be fetched from the well up ahead, which is about ninety zhang away.\"","Through the back door of the warehouse was a small courtyard of about six square meters. The ground was cluttered with various odds and ends, and it was walled off on the side.","The manager pointed to the left courtyard wall and said with a smile, \"However, if you plan to buy several storefronts, County Princess, the place next door used to be a noodle shop, and they have a well in their courtyard. You could knock through the wall, making water access convenient.\"","In order to satisfy Song Jinzhao, the brokerage manager had taken the stack of selected title deeds right after leaving the County Princess's estate that morning and physically inspected the ones he wasn't very familiar with again.","What kind of shop could be opened? How could it be decorated conveniently? He had already thought it all through in his mind when he came to inspect them.","After walking around, they went next door. This shop had clearly been cleaned, and there really was a well in the backyard.","Song Jinzhao walked to the edge of the well and looked down. The water was very clear, without even a single fallen leaf.","A milk tea shop next door, this one for a Luosifen noodle shop, and still needing a braised food shop—it would be best if they could all be connected.","Luosifen paired with braised food, a perfect match!","It would also be convenient for fetching goods regularly.","\"I see the two shops next door are both open. Is anyone looking to transfer their lease?\"","The brokerage manager paused for a moment. \"I will have to go and ask about that.\"","Song Jinzhao nodded. Then, the group went to see one south-facing and two north-facing shops, all on Qipan Street. The only issue was that the remaining south-facing one was at the end of the street, a bit far from the two they had just seen.","Leaving Qipan Street and turning two corners brought them to Wuyi Alley. There were noticeably fewer people here than on Qipan Street, and the shops were much larger, mostly around a hundred square meters.","The brokerage manager said, \"County Princess, don't mind that there aren't many people here right now. There are two academies up ahead. Once school is let out, the crowds will swell. Moreover, the prices are cheap. A shop this big is only three hundred taels of silver more expensive than the one with the well we just saw.\"","Over the course of the afternoon, Song Jinzhao visited all the storefronts she had eyed in the morning. Zhuque Street, located on the central axis, had the most pedestrians. Wangyue Pavilion was on that street, and the prices there were also the most expensive.","A two-hundred-square-meter shop sold for ten thousand taels of silver, a forty-square-meter space on Qipan Street was seven hundred taels, and a hundred-square-meter place in Wuyi Alley cost one thousand taels.","These prices made Song Jinzhao fully realize just how expensive real estate in the capital was.","The County Princess's estate covered fourteen mu of land and was located right in the middle of the inner city. If it hadn't been a reward from the Emperor, she certainly wouldn't have been able to afford it.","She originally thought the silver she had on hand was quite a lot, but thinking about it now, it was completely insufficient.","Just as Song Jinzhao was looking at properties that afternoon, an unexpected guest arrived at the County Princess's estate.","Lanxi, who was training the servants in the front hall, heard the report from the gatekeeper and hurriedly sent someone to the backyard to invite Song Shixue. \"Quickly go find the Second Miss and tell her that Princess Yongjia has arrived.\"","The housewarming banquet had passed several days ago. Why would Princess Yongjia suddenly come over?","When the servant ran into the backyard to call for Song Shixue, she was sitting in the study writing a teaching plan.","Her younger brother was too young to sit still for long periods, so she planned to divide the daily two-hour session into three time slots for teaching.","Early morning, late morning, and afternoon, with each lesson lasting half an hour.","\"Second Miss, Princess Yongjia has suddenly visited. She says she is here to see the County Princess. Please hurry over and take a look.\"","The ink that had just coated the tip of her brush dripped onto the inkstone, splashing specks of black across the desk.","Song Shixue immediately put down her brush and stood up. Her pale yellow cloak fluttered against the doorframe as she hurried out of the courtyard. \"Quickly send someone to find my elder sister and have her come back.\"","Why would the princess come out of nowhere in the dead of winter? There was no prior notice at all.","By the time Song Shixue reached the front hall, Princess Yongjia was sitting in a chair drinking tea.","\"Commoner Song Shixue pays her respects to Her Royal Highness the Princess.\"","\"Rise.\" Princess Yongjia put down her teacup, her gaze sweeping over Song Shixue's somewhat youthful face.","Even though one sister possessed a natural heroic spirit and the other was sweet and delicate, the calm composure in their brows was remarkably similar. Looking closely, they really did resemble each other as sisters."]},{"number":240,"title":"Chapter 240: The Heartfelt Longings of Princess Yongjia","paragraphs":["\"Where did County Princess Linghui go?\" As the weather grew colder after the onset of winter, she wouldn't have left the palace at all if it weren't for her desire to see Brother Liuyun. The Song family had no relatives in the capital, so it was surprising that Song Jinzhao was not at home in such weather.","Standing respectfully five steps away from Princess Yongjia, Song Shixue replied, \"My eldest sister wants to buy a few shops in the capital. She made an appointment with the manager of the brokerage to look at properties this afternoon and left at the hour of Wei.\"","Xiao Yongjia frowned in confusion, her slender willow-leaf eyebrows knitting together. \"Is a County Princess's stipend not enough for County Princess Linghui to spend? I remember my Imperial Father also rewarded her with a thousand acres of fertile land. The annual rent is quite a substantial amount, so why does she still need to buy shops and engage in commerce?\"","She had heard that Song Jinzhao used to set up street stalls and even opened a shop to do business in Anyang Prefecture. But now that she held the noble title of County Princess, doing such things would inevitably invite criticism and mockery.","Song Shixue kept her eyes lowered submissively and said, \"Our family has been farming for three generations and truly doesn't have much wealth. His Majesty bestowed this County Princess estate upon us with great grace, and now there are over forty servants just for cleaning and serving. The capital is not like our hometown; if my sister doesn't make money, things will inevitably become tight over time.\"","She couldn't possibly tell her that they couldn't even collect ten percent of the rent from the thousand acres of fertile land rewarded by the Emperor.","Besides, they didn't think commerce was lowly. Farming could never bring in money as quickly as doing business. None of the shops her sister opened ever failed to make a profit. Of course she had to open them; no one would ever complain about having too much money.","Xiao Yongjia didn't know Song Shixue's true thoughts. Hearing her helpless and resigned tone, and thinking about how they had lost their parents at a young age and relied solely on a teenage Song Jinzhao to support the household, she couldn't help but feel a pang of pity.","She offered comforting words: \"Once your brother passes the imperial examination and becomes a Jinshi in the future, you won't have to worry anymore. Having two people to support the family is always better than your sister doing it alone.\"","The shops being viewed that afternoon were scattered all over the inner city, so the people Lan Xi sent out couldn't find Song Jinzhao right away.","After waiting for a short while, Xiao Yongjia stood up to leave. \"Since County Princess Linghui is not at home, I will come back another day.\"","She had originally used the excuse of seeing Song Jinzhao as a cover to visit the Duke Zhenguo's estate.","Now that the person wasn't home and she had sat for a while, it was the perfect time to leave and come back in a couple of days.","Song Shixue was momentarily stunned. Leaving already? Wasn't she here to look for her sister? It hadn't even been the time it takes to drink a cup of tea.","Despite her doubts, she still escorted the guest out of the estate gates.","Watching the carriage gradually move away, Lan Xi asked, \"Second Miss, should we still have the County Princess come back?\"","Song Shixue looked up at the slightly gloomy sky. It had been getting colder these past few days; it looked like it was going to snow.","\"No need. Go call our people back.\"","After leaving the County Princess's estate, the carriage headed straight for the Duke Zhenguo's estate in the eastern part of the inner city. Seeing that the driver and the attendants walking alongside were all from the palace, the guards standing at the door hurriedly sent someone inside to report.","\"Greetings to Princess Yongjia.\" A crowd of people knelt down at the entrance.","The wife of Duke Zhenguo came out to welcome her, accompanied by maids and older servant women. \"This subject's wife pays her respects—\"","Just as her knees were about to bend, Xiao Yongjia caught her arms. \"Madam Duke Zhenguo, there's no need for such formalities. I just came from the County Princess's estate, but unfortunately, Song Jinzhao wasn't home. I remembered hearing my Imperial Mother say yesterday that the Old Madam had caught a slight chill and summoned an imperial physician, so I decided to drop by and check on her.\"","The smile that spread across Madam Duke Zhenguo's face was as steady as calm waters. \"The imperial physician came yesterday, and my mother's illness has improved greatly. She will be absolutely delighted to know you've come.\"","Xiao Yongjia smiled while her gaze swept past the madam's shoulder. Not seeing Chu Liuyun anywhere, she felt a bit disappointed.","\"Auntie, are neither Duke Zhenguo nor Duke of Qing at home?\"","Madam Duke Zhenguo replied, \"The weather is getting colder, and it looks like it will snow in a few days. The father and son went to the military camp this morning. Prince Ying went as well.\"","Thinking of what happened at the birthday banquet, Xiao Yongjia nodded in silence.","It was best that Duke Zhenguo could go. With him there, her Second Imperial Brother wouldn't be able to give Brother Liuyun a hard time.","In the western suburban military camp, fifty kilometers outside the city, Prince Ying's backside was completely numb after being jolted in a carriage for hours. The biting cold wind scraped against his face like blades.","\"Duke Zhenguo, a trivial matter like distributing winter clothes can be left to others. Do we really need to keep watching over it?\"","The cold wind howled outside the city, making it much colder than inside the capital. Xiao Rongyan wanted to go into a tent to warm up.","Standing nearby, Chu Liuyun said, \"Your Highness might not know, but this is the final distribution of winter clothes before winter fully sets in. Once it's finished, we must adjust the defense deployments. The weather is poor, so it must be completed before the snow falls.\"","Xiao Rongyan took a deep breath. Even though he was wearing a heavy cotton coat under his armor, he couldn't help but shiver several times in a row.","Duke Zhenguo swept a dissatisfied glance over his trembling legs. With such delicacy, could he really be trained into the commander-in-chief of the three armies?","The Emperor was simply blind.","By the time the supplies were distributed, it was already getting dark. Hearing that they had to spend the night at the military camp, Xiao Rongyan's face darkened, and he nearly ground his back teeth to dust.","He walked into the tent Chu Liuyun had arranged for him. It was almost the same size as the commander's tent, yet Xiao Rongyan still found it too crude and unworthy of his noble status as a prince.","He demanded coldly, \"Change the quilt cover to silk. I am not accustomed to sleeping on such coarse cotton.\""]},{"number":241,"title":"Chapter 241: The Perplexed Oushi Nian","paragraphs":["Chu Liuyun explained, \"Silk isn't as warm as cotton.\"","Xiao Rongyan patted his arm with his fingertips, his face full of disgust. \"Cotton is rough. I have never used it.\"","Chu Liuyun pressed his lips together and gritted his teeth, forcing the words out one by one. \"The military camp doesn't have silk duvet covers. Please forgive us, Your Highness.\"","Thinking about how he had been freezing all afternoon and how shabby his sleeping quarters were, Xiao Rongyan's suppressed dissatisfaction grew even stronger.","\"Last year, the Duke of Qing hunted a spotted tiger at the hunting grounds. I heard the pelt was tanned into a blanket and placed in your tent. Since there are no silk duvet covers, a tiger pelt will do just as well.\"","Looking at his arrogant expression, Chu Liuyun chuckled softly, pushing his sarcasm down to the bottom of his heart.","\"Men, go to my tent and fetch the tiger pelt laid at the foot of my bed for resting my feet, and bring it here for His Highness Prince Ying to use.\"","Xiao Rongyan's face instantly froze. Used for resting feet?","The subordinate brought the tiger pelt and laid it on the bed. Xiao Rongyan didn't want to sit on it or cover himself with it. He couldn't help but picture Chu Liuyun's bare feet resting on it, imagining a foot odor.","Song Jinzhao didn't return to the estate until nearly evening, only to be told that Princess Yongjia had visited today. \"Did she say what it was about?\"","Song Shixue shook her head. \"She waited for a short while and then left, saying she would come find you next time.\"","\"Sister, when did your relationship with Princess Yongjia become so good?\" Otherwise, why would a princess come over time and time again without even giving notice?","Thinking of the relationship between Chu Liuyun and Xiao Yongjia, Song Jinzhao helplessly curled her lips into a wry smile. \"It's not that our relationship is good. She's just treating me as an imaginary enemy.\"","Speaking of which, Princess Yongjia was already sixteen this year, and Chu Liuyun was no longer young either. At the housewarming banquet, there seemed to be a hint of mutual affection between them. If she really liked him, she could just ask the Emperor to issue a marriage decree. After all, the Dongzhao Kingdom didn't have a rule forbidding prince consorts from serving as court officials.","\"Ah!\" Song Shixue raised her eyebrows in confusion. What imaginary enemy?","With the shop purchased, Song Jinzhao started drawing blueprints that evening. If she wanted good business, renovations were essential.","Especially for a hotpot restaurant. The people who could afford to shop on Vermilion Bird Street were all wealthy. The place had to be high-end while maintaining its own unique characteristics.","There was also the matter of suppliers, which needed to be finalized during the renovation period. The staff and chefs also required comprehensive training.","Ye Liangyu thought about it all afternoon, and finally went to see the Emperor privately after the morning court session the next day.","Xiao Chengjing remained silent for a long time after reading the memorial. \"Did County Princess Linghui tell you all this?\"","Ye Liangyu nodded. \"Yesterday during lunch, we happened to bring up the maritime maps, and the County Princess casually mentioned a few things.\"","Xiao Chengjing placed the opened memorial on the desk. \"I wonder if Song Qiming will have his eldest sister's talents once he enters the court as an official.\"","Ye Liangyu lowered his head, his tone somewhat hesitant. \"Being blood siblings, he must have inherited some of it, but someone as intelligent as County Princess Linghui is likely rare.\"","Xiao Chengjing lowered his eyes, staring at the memorial. \"Do you think Song Jinzhao knows how to build an ocean-going sailing ship?\"","\"...\"","This single question stumped Ye Liangyu. Making a suggestion and actually implementing it were two different things. Wasn't this the Ministry of Works' job?","\"I'm afraid it would be difficult. The County Princess has never even been on a ship; she probably couldn't build one.\"","Xiao Chengjing was half-skeptical of Ye Liangyu's words. If Song Jinzhao could bring it up, she definitely had some ideas in her head.","\"Alright, you may step down for now.\"","No sooner had Ye Liangyu stepped out of the imperial study than Ou Shinian was summoned into the palace by the Emperor.","Holding the heavy memorial in his hands, he couldn't help but close his eyes and groan inwardly after reading it.","Building a gorgeous and beautiful ship was easy, but making it capable of withstanding massive ocean waves was difficult.","It was a massive project, and he felt completely unsure.","\"Your Majesty, this humble subject has never been out to sea. What must this ocean-going sailing ship look like to be considered qualified?\"","Xiao Chengjing thought about it and agreed. To build it, there had to be a standard at the very least.","\"There are many officials in the court who have served in coastal prefectural cities. They must have seen the sea. You can go ask them for advice.\"","\"The idea of building an ocean-going sailing ship was told to Ye Liangyu by County Princess Linghui. If you can't figure out how to build it, try going to the County Princess's estate to ask for her guidance.\"","Watching the Emperor get up and leave the imperial study, Ou Shinian held the memorial, opening and closing his mouth for a long time. Finally, he could only go out to ask around with a distressed look on his face.","He wouldn't have known if he hadn't asked, but once he did, he was startled.","After asking around, Ou Shinian learned that maritime weather was divided into calm periods and flood periods.","During the calm period, the maritime climate was relatively stable, with clear weather, small waves, and a relatively placid sea surface.","The commoners living by the sea usually chose this time to go out and fish.","However, during the flood period, there were frequent typhoons and rainstorms. At this time, let alone going out to sea to fish, fishermen wouldn't even step out of their doors.","In severe cases, both people and houses would be blown away. Ships at sea would only be capsized, not even leaving a single plank behind.","Hearing these words, Ou Shinian almost fainted on the spot. If living on the shore was this dangerous, wouldn't being out on the sea, surrounded by water on all sides, mean simply waiting for death?","If they couldn't find land, the ship would have to sail on the sea for several months, and it would definitely encounter the sea flood period.","He stammered as he asked his colleagues, \"The coastal prefectural cities have a developed fishing industry. Are there any ships that can withstand a tsunami?\"","The official said expressionlessly, \"If there really were, there wouldn't be fishermen leaving no bones behind after going out to sea every year.\"","Ou Shinian instantly fell silent. He lowered his head and returned to the Ministry of Works to convene a meeting with his subordinates.","\"The Emperor has ordered us to build an ocean-going sailing ship. One ship must carry at least five hundred people, and it must also have enough space to store provisions to feed these people for three months.\"","\"It needs to sail freely in the sea, be able to withstand violent storms and monstrous waves fifty feet high, and its speed must be fast. Everyone, express your opinions. If you have any ideas, feel free to speak up.\"","At first, no one in the room spoke. Then, the Vice Minister of Works asked uncertainly, \"My Lord, are you sure it's fifty feet high?\"","Ou Shinian nodded vigorously with a serious face. \"I heard that in severe cases, the waves can reach hundreds of feet. I know you have no way to handle that, so I didn't set the requirement that high. If we really encounter them after going out to sea, we can only accept our fate. But it must be able to withstand ordinary waves. Fifty feet is already the lowest requirement.\"","The scene fell into a dead silence again. After a long while, someone raised a hand. \"My Lord, the capital is not near the sea. Even if we build it, there's no way to test sail it. How can we be sure it can withstand fifty-foot waves? Will we have to go to the seaside when the time comes?\"","Ou Shinian: \"...\"","He hadn't thought about this problem yet. Such a massive project definitely required a test sail on the sea. The moat in the capital wasn't wide enough, nor did it have waves. At most, a few splashes would be blown up during a violent storm, not even reaching three feet high.","\"First gather the best shipbuilders in the capital to build the ship. We'll talk about the test sail when the time comes. At worst, we'll just take a trip to Mingzhou.\"","Everyone looked at each other in dismay, only feeling that the sky over the Ministry of Works had already begun to darken.","The sky was gloomy, and gusts of cold wind blew across the barren dirt slopes. Xiao Rongyan, who was leading men to change the guard along with Chu Liuyun, was freezing from head to toe; even his heart felt like ice.","Last night, Xiao Rongyan had insisted on having his guards return to the city overnight to fetch his bedding, and they had brought many other things over as well.","He was clearly wearing a thick leather jacket under his armor, so why was he still so cold?","Seeing his shoulders hunched unnaturally, Chu Liuyun couldn't help but turn his head and roll his eyes.","This morning, when he went to the tent to wake him, he discovered that the candles had been replaced by luminous pearls, silk blankets had been laid on the ground as foot mats, and even tea sets and chairs had been brought in. He felt the entire situation was so utterly absurd that he nearly spat out a mouthful of blood on the spot.","Was he here to endure hardship or to enjoy luxury? Decorating a military tent like a bedroom in the Prince of Ying's estate—what would the ordinary soldiers think? It was an absolute corruption of military discipline.","\"Your Highness, if you feel cold, you can return first and come back to the military camp next spring.\"","Xiao Rongyan shook his head, his lips trembling. \"I do not feel cold.\"","His Imperial Father had only given him one year. He had to take complete control of the Western Suburbs Camp within this time and, ideally, recruit a few trusted subordinates. If he waited until spring, three or four months would already be wasted.","Chu Liuyun squeezed his horse's flanks and leaned forward.","\"Since Your Highness is not cold, let us go up ahead and take a look. The view there is the most open.\" And the wind was the strongest.","Suddenly, a cold sensation landed on Chu Liuyun's brow. He looked up and saw snowflakes falling thickly from the sky, drifting down like goose feathers.","Their tasks were not yet finished, but it was already snowing—a full day earlier than they had estimated.","The snow fell heavier and heavier. In just a moment, the ground was painted white.","Ignoring the wind and snow lashing against his face, Chu Liuyun followed beside the troops with a solemn expression, keeping a close eye on them and occasionally shouting out to urge them to move faster.","Xiao Rongyan, who had never endured such hardship in his life, desperately wanted to go back at once. However, he had suggested it twice and Chu Liuyun still refused to leave, leaving him with no choice but to follow along.","\"Return to the capital immediately and tell Pan Yong about my current situation at the Western Suburbs Camp. Have him sing my praises a bit more during the morning court session.\"","If he had to suffer, others needed to know about it, otherwise wouldn't the suffering be entirely in vain?","\"Understood.\" The guard cupped his hands in obedience, immediately turned his horse around, and galloped wildly toward the capital."]},{"number":242,"title":"Chapter 242: The Extravagant English King and the Minister of Works with Singed Hair","paragraphs":["The snow fell heavier and heavier with no sign of stopping. Since the military affairs were not yet finished, they had to stay in the military camp for a few more days.","Worried that Xiao Rongyan might catch a cold and fall ill, Chu Liuyun took the initiative to find him. \"Your Highness, it looks like it will snow for a few more days. If the heavy snow blocks the roads, it will be hard to return to the city. Why don't you head back first?\"","Xiao Rongyan really wanted to leave, but he also wanted to earn a good reputation for sharing the hardships of the soldiers and citizens.","\"How can I leave when the military affairs aren't finished? I will return with you when the time comes.\"","Chu Liuyun replied, \"If the snow doesn't stop, my father and I might have to stay in the camp until the New Year. Will Your Highness be alright with that?\"","Xiao Rongyan gritted his teeth. \"No problem. The snow will probably stop in a few days anyway.\"","Seeing his firm attitude, Chu Liuyun had no choice but to drop the matter.","It kept snowing. Even by the next day, it hadn't stopped; instead, it grew heavier and denser.","The generals rode on horseback braving the wind and snow, while the soldiers marched in three columns. At first, Xiao Rongyan and Chu Liuyun rode horses together, but later, unable to bear the cold, Xiao Rongyan hid inside a carriage where extra charcoal basins had been added.","Xiao Rongyan's guards quickly relayed the news to Pan Yong, the Minister of War.","The next day during the morning court assembly, when the topic of the troop rotation at the western suburbs camp amidst the snow came up, he immediately stepped forward to report.","\"The day before yesterday, His Highness Prince Ying, along with the Duke of Zhenguo and his son, went to the western suburbs camp to supervise the military rotation. This is the military report delivered this morning.\"","The Emperor opened the military report. It stated that Xiao Rongyan braved the wind and snow, working day and night alongside Chu Liuyun to supervise the troops, observe the military conditions, and even eat and sleep alongside them.","Glancing at the vast expanse of white snow outside the hall, Xiao Chengjing smiled and nodded in praise. \"Prince Ying has done well this time. He has finally lived up to my expectations.\"","Pan Yong happily stepped back to his place.","Currently, neither of the two princes in the court held military power. If Prince Ying could gain the Emperor's approval, he might be able to compete for military authority in the future.","Standing in front of Gu Qishan, Prince Qi turned his head with a gloomy expression and glared at Pan Yong, his heart filled with regret.","He shouldn't have said what he did at the birthday banquet. His cleverness had backfired, indirectly helping Xiao Rongyan instead.","Why hasn't the Northern Shuo Kingdom attacked yet? It would be best if he went to the battlefield and died.","While resting at night, a guard lifted the flap of Chu Liuyun's tent, carrying a charcoal bucket with an aggrieved expression.","\"Young Master, I just went to the storehouse to fetch charcoal. The official in charge said that His Highness Prince Ying took three days' worth of supplies all at once last night, sent someone to take more at noon today, and just went again. You and the Master only have half of your charcoal allowance left for this month.\"","Chu Liuyun was very strict in his military governance. Food and military supplies in the camp were strictly allocated, with no exceptions, not even for himself and the Duke of Zhenguo.","Xiao Rongyan was an unexpected addition. To avoid affecting the others, his expenses were deducted from the quota of the Chu father and son.","The more he used, the less Chu Liuyun and the Duke of Zhenguo had.","Looking at the charcoal bucket that was less than half full, Chu Liuyun sighed and instructed, \"Tell the official to advance next month's allowance first. I will personally replenish it in a few days.\"","The guard nodded helplessly. At this rate, let alone next month's, even the month after next's allowance would be used up.","Outside the window, the wind and snow continued endlessly, painting the world in a vast expanse of white. However, the officials inside the Ministry of Works office were sweating profusely with anxiety.","The desks and floor were covered in half-drawn, rejected drafts, and even the walls were plastered with all sorts of bizarre sailboat design blueprints.","Everyone had been brainstorming in the office non-stop for three days and three nights. They had pulled out tens of thousands of strands of hair and were nearly going bald.","The exhausted Vice Minister of Works struggled to lift his head from the desk, the heavy dark circles under his eyes making it look like he had been punched twice.","\"My Lord, we really can't hold on any longer. During the morning court today, I almost fell asleep in the Hall of Supreme Harmony.\"","Ou Shinian's fingertips trembled as he picked up his teacup. \"We still don't have a single clue. How do you expect me to explain this to the Emperor?\"","Hearing this, the others slumped dejectedly onto their desks. The strong scent of ink in the air made them dizzy.","Looking around at the messy floor and a group of exhausted subordinates, Ou Shinian took a deep, trembling breath.","\"Forget it. Everyone go back and rest. I will try to think of another way.\"","The crowd slowly raised their heads, froze for two seconds, and then stood up to leave one after another.","They ran faster than rabbits; in just a few blinks, the room was empty.","Only the two Vice Ministers were left, who apologetically said, \"We will take our leave,\" before decisively slipping away as well.","Ou Shinian looked at the empty room with a splitting headache. He was so sleepy he could barely keep his eyes open, so he simply lay down on the floor and fell asleep basking in the warmth of the charcoal basin.","An hour passed, and suddenly, a hoarse scream echoed through the Ministry of Works office.","The imperial guards stationed nearby hurried in with their swords drawn, only to find the Minister of Works, Ou Shinian, clutching his burning hair and jumping up and down in place.","Looking down, they noticed several pieces of paper scattered on the floor were also on fire, and they quickly stomped them out.","Fortunately, the fire had just started, and it was extinguished after a few stomps.","The air was filled with the smell of burnt feathers. Ou Shinian's hair, scattered over his shoulders, was curled out of shape, looking worse than a chicken coop.","The imperial guards looked at each other in dismay, not knowing how to comfort the Minister of Works, whose hair was half-burnt. Since it was ruined like this, he would probably have to cut it off.","When Ou Shinian left the palace, his eyes were vacant. The servants waiting outside the palace almost didn't recognize him when they saw his scorched hair.","\"What did you say? Ou Shinian's hair was burned off?\" Xiao Chengjing, who was reviewing memorials in the imperial study, stared at his personal eunuch in disbelief.","The head eunuch replied, \"The imperial guards saw it with their own eyes. The bottom of his hair exploded like a large broom; he's practically bald.\"","Xiao Chengjing couldn't imagine what Ou Shinian looked like now. \"Charcoal fires are used frequently in winter. Tell the maids and eunuchs to be more careful to prevent fires.\"","The head eunuch nodded. \"Your Majesty is far-sighted. I will give the orders right away.\"","In truth, after the incident, both the imperial guards and the Internal Affairs Department had already increased patrols in their respective areas.","The news of Ou Shinian's hair catching fire spread quickly. After passing through dozens of mouths, the rumor eventually turned into Ou Shinian becoming completely bald, and some even claimed he had been burned to death.","The Ministry of Works officials, who had gone home and slept soundly, only woke up the next day to find out that their office had nearly caught fire yesterday and had even burned their superior."]},{"number":243,"title":"Chapter 243: European Times Reporter Visits for Advice","paragraphs":["When Ou Shinian stepped into the Hall of Supreme Harmony during the morning assembly, everyone's eyes uniformly darted toward the top of his head.","He was wearing a brand-new official's hat, completely concealing what lay underneath.","Facing the stares of others, Ou Shinian did not say a single word nor look at a single person. As soon as the morning assembly ended, he left immediately, not even bothering to go to the Ministry of Works office.","In the study, Song Jinzhao was calculating the renovation costs for four shops. Separated only by a wall, Song Anhao's stuttering recitation drifted into her ears, with Song Shixue chiming in from time to time to correct him.","Even though the County Princess's estate was large enough, boasting seven or eight courtyards alone, the three Song siblings were unwilling to live in separate courtyards.","Fortunately, Song Jinzhao's courtyard was the largest in the estate, with twelve rooms in total, so it didn't feel crowded even with four people living there.","The heavy snow continued to fall. Every four hours, the servants had to come over with iron shovels to clear the snow, and even the roofs had to be swept clean using bamboo poles.","Qingshuang ran under the eaves, clutching a freshly issued land deed to her chest. She shook the snowflakes off her body before entering the room.","\"Miss, here is the land deed for the last shop on Qipan Street.\" She took the deed from her robes and placed it on the table.","Song Jinzhao glanced at the deed, then looked up at Qingshuang. \"Has that Miss Wei finalized her divorce?\"","Qingshuang replied, \"She got the divorce papers yesterday. The managing mama said her young lady is preparing to leave the capital and return to her maiden home, so she is urgently selling all the shops under her name. This shop was fifty taels of silver cheaper than the original price. The other party mentioned that there are still people occupying it, and it might take some effort on your part to drive them out.\"","Song Jinzhao put the deed away in a drawer. \"There is no rush. Once they know the buyer is me, they will naturally move out. After the snow stops, have Lanxi take some people to claim the shop.\"","Qingshuang nodded in compliance.","Footsteps approached, and a servant stood outside, knocking before entering.","\"County Princess, the Minister of Works, Ou Shinian, has come to visit and is waiting quietly at the entrance.\"","Why would he come in such heavy snow? At this hour, he should have just finished the morning assembly.","Song Jinzhao said, \"Let him wait for me in the front hall.\"","\"Yes.\"","In the front hall, Ou Shinian sat in a chair with freezing hands and feet, yet his heart felt like it was burning in a furnace of firewood, crackling and popping in his ears.","Seeing Song Jinzhao enter, he hastily stood up and greeted her, \"Greetings to County Princess Linghui.\"","Song Jinzhao gave a slight nod. Seeing that the dark circles under his eyes were darker than a giant panda's, she asked in surprise, \"We haven't seen each other for a few days, why does Lord Ou look so haggard?\"","His skin was sallow, his face gaunt, his eyelids swollen, and his eyes completely bloodshot.","Ou Shinian let out a heavy sigh and sat back down limply, leaning against the chair. \"To be honest with the County Princess, I haven't slept for several days.\"","\"Why is that?\" With the end of the year approaching, was the Ministry of Works really this busy?","Ou Shinian sighed again. He struggled to lift his eyelids to stare at Song Jinzhao, his eyes filled with not only blame but also grievance, nearly brimming with tears.","\"A few days ago, Vice Censor-in-Chief Ye wrote a memorial detailing the County Princess's ideas about finding a new continent and submitted it to the Emperor. The Emperor ordered our Ministry of Works to build an ocean-going sailing ship. I led everyone in the Ministry at the office, brainstorming for three days and three nights, but we haven't even finalized a blueprint.\"","He took off his hat, revealing a rat's nest of hair that stuck out wildly no matter how it was tied. \"I was so exhausted that I lay down next to the brazier for a while. As a result, I rolled over and my hair turned into this. In a few days, the Emperor will ask about the shipbuilding progress. I implore the County Princess to guide me out of this confusion.\"","Song Jinzhao stared blankly at his hair, which looked like withered grass. She could almost smell the scent of burning hair at the tip of her nose.","After a long moment of meeting his gaze, Song Jinzhao asked hesitantly, \"May I ask what difficulties you have encountered, my lord?\"","Ou Shinian replied, \"There are difficulties everywhere.\"","\"...\"","Seeing that Song Jinzhao had fallen silent, Ou Shinian took out three ship design blueprints from his robes and spread them out on the table next to her.","\"These are a few design blueprints the Ministry of Works drew up over the past three days, but all of them were rejected.\"","\"They can't withstand tsunamis, the speed is too slow, the sea breeze will overturn them, they can't continuously sail in the ocean for months, the ship's bottom will corrode, they can't carry too much cargo... A whole series of problems cannot be solved. I beg the County Princess for guidance.\"","With every word Ou Shinian spoke, Song Jinzhao's brows knitted tighter. She picked up the design blueprints on the table and observed them carefully.","They were very ordinary blueprints. The structure was simple, and nothing special stood out. They looked no different from the merchant ships sailing on the canals, except the dimensions marked on the side were much larger, roughly equivalent to an enlarged version of a merchant ship.","Song Jinzhao recalled the sailing ship models and information she had seen in the maritime museum. The difference was quite significant; these were clearly much more primitive.","However, she was not a professional. She didn't know where to start explaining, and it would be disastrous if she said something wrong!","After pondering for a moment, Song Jinzhao turned to look at Ou Shinian, whose fervent gaze looked as if he wanted to eat her alive.","\"Minister Ou, I have not dabbled much in this field. Although I have some ideas, the Ministry of Works will still need to verify for yourselves whether they can be put into practice. Please consider them carefully, my lord.\"","Ou Shinian's pupils lit up brightly. He heard nothing else except Song Jinzhao saying she had some ideas.","\"Please speak quickly, County Princess. I will judge what is right or wrong for myself.\"","Song Jinzhao took a deep breath, pointed at the design blueprints, and began to explain in detail.","\"Although flat-bottomed ships are spacious, their large water-contact area leads to slow sailing speeds and poor wave-resistance. They are only suitable for navigating calm lakes and canals. I suggest changing to a V-shaped hull to reduce the water-contact area. With less resistance, it can cut through the water more efficiently.\"","\"The ship's hull can be supported by a keel structure, which can make the vessel sturdier. In addition, the keel adds weight and deepens the draft, which improves the ability to withstand wind and waves. The entire hull can also be reinforced with iron rings.\"","\"Then there are the sails. A single sail has too little effect and poor upwind capability. In fact, you can have three sails: a headsail, a mainsail, and a fore-and-aft sail.\"","\"The headsail is for traction and steering, the mainsail is the primary source of power, and the fore-and-aft sail helps maintain balance. You could even add a few more without issue.\"","\"The ships you are making right now are all different from one another. If they suddenly break down at sea, they can't be repaired at all. You need to make identical, standardized parts. That way, no matter what breaks, it can be immediately repaired with universal parts.\"","\"As for the issue you mentioned about the ship's bottom rotting, first, you must choose wood with strong corrosion resistance, like teak, oak, and so on. Their high density makes it difficult for seawater to penetrate. Then, apply tar to form a waterproof coating. You could even nail a layer of lead sheeting to the bottom of the ship. Lead is toxic and will keep corrosive marine organisms, such as barnacles and shipworms, away...\"","Song Jinzhao spoke intermittently about many things. Some points she explained clearly, while others she only gave a general outline of, leaving the Ministry of Works to figure them out on their own."]},{"number":244,"title":"Chapter 244: Introducing Scale Ship Model Testing","paragraphs":["Ou Shinian looked at Song Jinzhao with eyes full of amazement after hearing her words. This was what she called \"not dabbling too much\"? The entire Ministry of Works combined didn't have as many ideas as she had proposed alone.","\"The County Princess possesses world-shocking talent. I am truly ashamed of my own inferiority.\"","\"Do you have paper and pen? I want to write all of this down, lest I forget and miss something after I go back.\"","Song Jinzhao instructed Qingshuang to fetch a brush and ink.","\"The Ministry of Works has many capable people. Building an ocean-going sailing ship is only a matter of time. You do not need to be too anxious, My Lord.\"","Tears shimmered in Ou Shinian's eyes. \"I may not be anxious, but the Emperor is. Fortunately, the County Princess is here; otherwise, I really wouldn't know what to do.\"","His brush flew across the paper, writing down everything Song Jinzhao had just said. \"County Princess, please take a look. Is there anything missing?\"","Song Jinzhao took the paper, read it, and handed it back. \"Not a single word is missing. That is all of it.\"","\"You can make a model of the ship first, and then build a pool that simulates the ocean environment. After successful testing in it, you can build the ship to scale, to avoid wasting too much time and cost in case of failure.\"","Ou Shinian's hand paused as he took the paper. He looked at Song Jinzhao blankly. \"What model? How do we simulate the ocean environment?\"","Song Jinzhao hesitated for a moment before asking in return, \"How did you originally plan to ensure that the ship would have no problems after going to sea, and could sail in the deep ocean and withstand wind and waves?\"","\"Of course, by transporting it to the sea to test it after it is built.\"","Song Jinzhao: \"Then the cost of trial and error would be so high! Just building such a big ship takes several months.\"","Ou Shinian pressed, \"So what are the model and simulated ocean environment that the County Princess just mentioned?\"","Song Jinzhao stretched out her hands to gesture the size.","\"Make an identical ocean-going sailing ship to scale, and specially make a large wooden barrel to act as the ocean. Artificially create waves, wind, and rain to simulate a real ocean environment. You can also add salt to the water to determine the degree of corrosion of the seawater on various parts of the hull. Wait until there are no problems before building the ship for sea trials. This can effectively save time and trial-and-error costs.\"","Ou Shinian blinked and froze in place like a mummy.","How exactly did Song Jinzhao's brain grow! Why couldn't he think of such a good idea?","Ou Shinian stepped back and solemnly bowed to Song Jinzhao. \"The County Princess is brilliant. I am in complete awe.\"","\"You overpraise me, My Lord. It is my honor to be able to help the Ministry of Works.\"","Ou Shinian smiled brightly, his admiration for Song Jinzhao growing. An idea sprouted in his mind.","Once Song Qiming passed the imperial examination and became a Jinshi, he had to poach him to the Ministry of Works. With him there, County Princess Linghui would be there, and he wouldn't have to worry about anything in the future.","When Ou Shinian arrived, his face had been full of sorrow; when he left, he looked as if he were walking on auspicious clouds, his whole person feeling light and brisk.","At the same time, in the western suburbs military camp, Chu Liuyun angrily flipped his table over with a slap after receiving a letter from the capital.","\"Boasting, faking, shameless, and fishing for compliments!\"","He spent two and a half out of three days enjoying himself in his tent and carriage. The charcoal fire burned so hot that even the servants standing outside could feel the heat.","Supervising the army day and night, eating and living with the soldiers? Bullshit! He tells lies as easily as breathing. So shameless.","Duke Zhenguo came in and saw Chu Liuyun cursing with a livid face. He frowned and scolded, \"I have taught you to be steady since childhood, yet your mind is still so unsettled. Prince Ying is right here in the military camp. Endure it for a year and it will pass.\"","Chu Liuyun turned around expressionlessly and handed the letter to Duke Zhenguo. \"Father, please take a look.\"","Duke Zhenguo took the letter in confusion. When he read the third sentence, his fingers gripped so hard that the letter paper was torn in half.","\"Shameless. To think that such a fraud who deceives the world for fame is actually a prince.\"","Whenever he thought that Prince Qi was just like Xiao Rongyan, Duke Zhenguo felt his spine weaken.","It would be better to choose a capable member of the imperial clan to adopt. If they were really allowed to become the emperor, our Dongzhao Kingdom would probably be eaten clean by the Beishuo Kingdom, not even leaving any crumbs.","Chu Liuyun rubbed his forehead in frustration. \"Prince Ying not only enjoys himself in the military camp, but he also buys people's hearts. He asks the cooks to make dozens of dishes every day, claiming it is for himself, but actually rewarding most of it to other generals. It is causing unrest among the men. We must drive him away as soon as possible.\"","Duke Zhenguo tossed the letter into the fire. \"After the snow stops in a few days, I will return to the capital, and I will take Prince Ying with me.\"","Chu Liuyun frowned. \"What if he refuses to leave?\"","Duke Zhenguo sneered. \"He probably wanted to leave a long time ago. Even if he doesn't lack food and drink, it cannot compare to the luxury and comfort of Prince Ying's mansion. Now that the Emperor already knows his good reputation for sympathizing with the soldiers, there is no point in enduring it any longer. With this stepping stone, he will definitely scram.\"","The thought that Xiao Rongyan would come again after the new year made Chu Liuyun feel annoyed all over.","...","Ou Shinian took the suggestions proposed by Song Jinzhao back to the Ministry of Works office and held a meeting for a full eight hours. Officials and craftsmen squeezed together, arguing up a storm. By the time the office doors opened again, the sky outside was already dark.","Unlike last time, everyone left with a smile on their face this time.","Ou Shinian collapsed into his chair. A wave of sleepiness hit him. Just as he closed his eyes, he saw a bottomless abyss beneath his feet, scaring him so much that he shuddered and almost fell off the chair.","Why the office again?","He touched his crooked hat. He couldn't sleep here; he had to go back. If he got burned again, he really wouldn't have any hair left!","A few days later, Xiao Chengjing summoned Ou Shinian to the Imperial Study and asked, \"How far along is the Ministry of Works with the construction of the ocean-going sailing ship?\"","Ou Shinian, who was well prepared, took out the design blueprints from his sleeve and presented them. \"To reply to Your Majesty, the framework design blueprints have basically been finalized.\"","Xiao Chengjing stared at the blueprints on the paper and asked suspiciously, \"Why does this ship look a bit different from the ones I have seen before?\"","Both the front and back were curved like a crescent moon. Wouldn't it capsize?","Ou Shinian completely copied Song Jinzhao's words, also adding many ideas that the Ministry of Works officials had discussed together over the past few days.","Xiao Chengjing nodded from time to time as he listened, very satisfied with these novel ideas.","\"Your Ministry of Works did a good job this time. You finally used your brains.\"","A heavy hammer seemed to smash into the top of Ou Shinian's head. He froze for two seconds and then silently lowered his head.","\"I dare not deceive Your Majesty. In truth, everyone in the Ministry of Works brainstormed for three days and three nights but couldn't figure out what kind of ship could sail in the deep sea and withstand fierce winds and giant waves. Later, having no other choice, I remembered Your Majesty saying that we could seek advice from County Princess Linghui, so I went to ask her.\"","The smile on Xiao Chengjing's face vanished. \"So your hair was also burned at that time?\"","Ou Shinian immediately lifted the hem of his robe and knelt down. \"I am guilty. I was too sleepy at the time and fell asleep in the office. As a result, I was too close to the charcoal brazier and almost caused a major fire. I beg Your Majesty for forgiveness.\"","Xiao Chengjing looked at the singed ends of his hair. \"Which ones did County Princess Linghui come up with?\"","\"...All of them.\"","\"...\"","Xiao Chengjing closed his eyes forcefully in exasperation and opened them again.","\"I think you might as well let County Princess Linghui be the Minister of Works.\"","Ou Shinian kept his head bowed to the ground, not daring to look up. \"I am truly ashamed. Compared to County Princess Linghui, I acknowledge my inferiority.\"","Xiao Chengjing pressed his lips tightly together and rolled his eyes at the ceiling speechlessly.","At least he had some self-awareness.","The fact that the entire Ministry of Works combined was no match for a seventeen-year-old girl made even Xiao Chengjing, the Emperor himself, feel a bit embarrassed.","Although he had given Ou Shinian permission to seek advice from Song Jinzhao, the word \"entire\" was simply too demoralizing."]},{"number":245,"title":"Chapter 245: New Year's Gift","paragraphs":["The heavy snow before the New Year fell continuously for seven days and seven nights before finally stopping. In unpopulated areas, the snow accumulated to a depth of nearly two meters.","In Anyang Prefecture, a thousand miles away, the blizzard was even worse. The roofs of families who did not clear the snow in time collapsed under the weight.","Blanketed in white snow, Song Village looked like an ink wash painting, exuding peace and tranquility everywhere.","The sound of carriage wheels rolling over the snow was exceptionally distinct.","Fushun stood on the carriage, gazing at the surrounding houses.","The Eldest Miss had said that the largest blue-brick house near the back mountain in the village was the newly built old house of the third branch of the Song family.","Thick black smoke drifted up into the sky from the chimney. His eyes lit up, and with a smile, he gripped the reins and drove the carriage further in.","Song Daniu and his wife, who lived at the entrance of the village, were just preparing to eat. Just as they were about to close their door, they saw a carriage pass by.","The couple stepped out of their courtyard to watch. \"It's not Master Zhao's carriage. It's heading towards the back mountain, so it must be Song Jinzhao.\"","Daniu's wife raised her brows in confusion. \"Didn't Old Man Song say that the third branch's family went to the capital and wouldn't be coming back for the New Year this year? Why are they back?\"","Song Daniu shook his head. \"The carriage is a bit small; it doesn't look like it can fit four people.\"","At the same time, the first and second branches of the Song family also saw the carriage.","Oldest Song looked at the back of the carriage and muttered, \"Could it be that Jinzhao and the others are back?\"","Elder Aunt Song, holding a child, nudged her husband's arm. \"Go over and take a look. If they're back, let me know so I can go help cook.\"","Oldest Song nodded.","Old Lady Song, who was cooking, heard a knock on the door and walked out with Old Man Song. \"Who is it?\"","The oldest and second sons never knocked when they came over, and on such a cold day, the villagers wouldn't even step out of their doors.","Fushun looked through the crack in the door and saw two elderly people approaching.","He smiled and called out inside, \"Old Master, Old Madam, I am Fushun, the Eldest Miss's steward in Anyang Prefecture. I have been ordered to deliver the New Year's gifts.\"","Old Man Song opened the door and looked at the beaming Fushun. \"Jinzhao sent you?\"","Fushun smiled and nodded, hurriedly bowing. \"This lowly one, Fushun, greets the Old Master and Old Madam.\"","\"Before the master left for the capital, she specifically instructed me to deliver the New Year's gifts during the twelfth lunar month. The snow has been too heavy these past few days, causing a delay on the road. I beg the Old Master and Old Madam's forgiveness.\"","Old Man Song and Old Lady Song, having never been bowed to before, subconsciously took a step back. They figured this must be a servant their eldest granddaughter bought in Anyang Prefecture.","\"Father, Mother,\" Oldest Song and Second Song with his wife called out at the same time.","The second branch lived closer than the first branch but saw the carriage later, so the two groups arrived almost simultaneously, one right after the other.","Fushun turned his head to look at the three approaching people, his eyes darting between them. Not knowing which was the first branch and which was the second, he first gave a slight bow to acknowledge them, then turned to Old Man Song, hoping to learn their identities through him.","Oldest Song glanced at Fushun and asked Old Man Song, \"Father, who is this?\"","Old Man Song replied, \"He is Jinzhao's steward in Anyang Prefecture, here to deliver some things.\"","\"This is my oldest son, and this is my second son and second daughter-in-law.\"","Fushun hurriedly smiled and bowed deeply again to Oldest Song and Second Song. \"Greetings, First Master. Greetings, Second Master. Greetings, Second Madam.\"","Oldest Song was bowed to and didn't quite know what to do, while Second Song and his wife looked Fushun up and down from head to toe.","Even a servant was dressed better than they were; one could only imagine how wealthy the third branch was now.","Seeing everyone standing at the door, Old Man Song opened both sides of the courtyard gates completely. \"It's cold outside, come in first.\"","Fushun nodded in agreement, turned around, and parked the carriage in the courtyard, tying it up. He lifted the carriage curtain, revealing a carriage full of New Year's gifts.","Seeing him carry things down from the carriage trip after trip, the Song family's eyes nearly popped out of their heads.","Were these all New Year's gifts? How much stuff was this!","After moving everything into the main hall, Fushun opened the chests and introduced them one by one.","\"These are two sets of new bedding the Eldest Miss prepared for you two elders; they are especially warm for the winter.\"","\"These are two sets of ready-made clothes, complete from inside to outside and top to bottom. These are fabrics, in case the Old Madam finds it convenient to make something herself.\"","\"These are new clothes the Second Miss prepared for her female cousins, along with hair flowers and handkerchiefs, all currently fashionable in Anyang Prefecture.\"","\"These are books, along with some brushes, ink, paper, and inkstones, that the Eldest Young Master prepared for his two younger male cousins who are studying.\"","After introducing the items in the chests, Fushun lifted the lids of the bamboo baskets. \"These are chickens and ducks raised on the estate's own farm, as well as pork and mutton, all properly cured. There is also wine and tea.\"","The dazzling array of items filled half the main hall, making everyone's eyes blur.","Second Aunt Song excitedly pinched Second Song's waist hard, wishing she could rake all the things into her own home.","The two elders looked at the things on the table and the floor, smiling so widely their eyes were almost squeezed shut.","\"She just sent someone to deliver things in September, why did she send so much again this time? Jinzhao must have spent a lot of silver.\"","Fushun smiled and bowed. \"The Eldest Miss is filial, so the Old Master and Old Madam should be happy.\"","With that, he turned sideways and pointed to two unopened chests on the floor, saying to Oldest Song and Second Song, \"These two chests are holiday gifts the Eldest Miss prepared separately for the first and second branches. She said since she isn't coming back this year, she still needs you two to take good care of the Old Master and Old Madam.\"","Before Oldest Song could reach out, Second Song stepped forward to pick first. However, Fushun pointed to the chest on the right and told him, \"This is for the second branch.\"","Second Song and his wife's eyes simultaneously fell on the remaining chest. \"Are the contents of the two chests the same?\"","Fushun feigned ignorance and shook his head. \"I do not know. These were all prepared by the Eldest Miss before she left.\"","He pointed out again, \"Second Master, your chest is this one.\"","Second Song and his wife looked unwillingly at the chest on the left, feeling that the things inside must be better.","A burning smell drifted in from outside. Old Lady Song, who was holding the new clothes and looking at them, suddenly widened her eyes upon smelling it and yelled at the top of her lungs, \"My pot!!!\"","She stumbled into the kitchen and lifted the pot lid. The water inside had completely boiled dry, and the bright orange pumpkin had been cooked black.","Old Lady Song hastily grabbed a spatula to scoop out the pumpkin. Seeing that a crust had formed at the bottom, she slapped her thigh in frustration.","\"Oh my goodness, my pumpkin! How are we supposed to eat this now?\"","Second Aunt Song, who had followed her over, said, \"With ready-made chicken and duck, who still wants to eat pumpkin? If it's burnt, it's burnt.\"","Old Man Song and Old Lady Song glared at Second Aunt Song at the same time, startling her so much that a chill ran down her spine, and she didn't dare make a sound.","Seeing Old Lady Song about to pour water to wash the pot, Fushun quickly stepped forward and took the water basin. \"Let me wash it.\"","Pushed aside, Old Lady Song looked at Old Man Song somewhat helplessly. They had never used servants before and were a bit unaccustomed to it.","Second Song grabbed Old Lady Song's arm. \"Mother, let's go over and tidy up the things first.\"","With so many things delivered, how could one chest be enough? No matter what, they had to get a share of the rest.","Elder Aunt Song, not seeing Oldest Song return after a long time, grew anxious.","She turned back to the room and handed the child to Song Qiaoniang. \"Take care of your younger brother. Mother is going to check on your grandfather's side.\"","Just before leaving, she gave a few instructions to Song Yongnian, who was reading in the other room."]},{"number":246,"title":"Chapter 246: The Silver Bracelet and Letter Given Solely to the Principal Wife","paragraphs":["Returning to the main room, Second Aunt Song opened her chest. Inside were simply ten bolts of cloth, not even worth as much as the single chest given to the old couple.","With a sweeping glance from her, Second Song decisively walked over to Oldest Song's side to open his chest.","With quick reflexes, Oldest Song firmly pressed his hand down on the chest. If the things Jinzhao gave their family were better than the second branch's, they would not only have to listen to a barrage of complaints, but the items might also be snatched away. This chest could not be opened.","Seeing his sneak attack fail, Second Song clamored, Brother, hurry and open the chest to see what's inside. We already opened ours.","Oldest Song used his leg to push the chest behind him. No need. I'll carry it back later and let your sister-in-law open it. It's probably just some cloth anyway.","Second Aunt Song came over smiling to back her husband up. Brother, open the chest and let me see. There are a few colors Jinzhao gave us that I don't really like. It just so happens that Sister-in-law likes purple, so I can trade this bolt with you.","Elder Aunt Song, who had just hurried over, happened to hear this and loudly declared without a second thought, I don't like purple. Sister-in-law, you should keep it to make clothes for yourself.","Stepping over the threshold and seeing so many things displayed in the room, she could hardly conceal the shock in her eyes.","Seeing her arrive, Oldest Song quickly smiled and pulled her over to the chest. Lihua, these are the New Year's gifts Jinzhao sent someone to deliver to us.","The second branch thought she would open the chest, but after nodding, Elder Aunt Song showed no further reaction.","Even though Jinzhao is far away in the capital, she still remembered to send us New Year's gifts. She really is a filial child.","Old Man Song looked at his eldest daughter-in-law with satisfaction. It was enough to appreciate the gesture in one's heart, unlike those two from the second branch whose eyes were practically falling out staring at the goods.","After washing the pots clean, Fushun came to the main room. Since the New Year's gifts have been delivered, if there are no further instructions, this lowly one will take his leave now.","Old Lady Song pointed at the gloomy sky and spoke up, It's getting late. You should leave tomorrow.","Fushun hesitated; he had originally planned to spend the night in the city.","Seeing this, Old Man Song said, The horse can barely walk anymore. At least let it rest too.","Seeing both elders speaking up to ask him to stay, Fushun had no choice but to smile, nod, and agree. Then this lowly one will go cook.","Old Lady Song was just about to reach out and stop him when she was blocked by Second Aunt Song. Mother-in-law, he is Jinzhao's steward, which means he's a servant. It's only right that he cooks. Let him do it.","Fushun was about to say that it was indeed his duty to cook, but Second Aunt Song beat him to it again.","She lifted a well-marinated and sun-dried braised duck and handed it to him. Chop this duck up and steam it.","Fushun looked toward Old Man Song.","Old Man Song's face darkened and his voice dropped. No need to steam it. There are vegetables in the kitchen, just casually make a couple of dishes. They aren't eating here, so just cook for the three of us.","Having lost face, Second Aunt Song bit her lip tightly.","Second Song said ingratiatingly, Father, let Brother and me stay and eat with you and Mother tonight.","Old Man Song showed no mercy. There's no need. Take the chest Jinzhao gave you and go back.","As for the things for the children, let them come and get them themselves tomorrow.","Second Song disappointedly scanned the items on the table and the floor. We can just take everything back together today.","Old Man Song raised his voice, his tone growing heavy. I said let them come and get it themselves.","Oldest Song picked up his chest and said, Father, Mother, then Lihua and I will leave first. We'll come to see you tomorrow.","Seeing the couple from the first branch leave, Second Aunt Song unwillingly signaled Second Song to leave as well.","Ever since the third branch became prosperous, their parents-in-law's tempers had grown worse and worse, and there was absolutely nothing they could do about it.","Upon returning to their old house, Elder Aunt Song could not wait to open the chest.","So it's just cloth too. I thought there would be something else. Oldest Song looked away, uninterested.","Elder Aunt Song took the cloth out. The colors are nicer than the second branch's. There are two bolts suitable for Qiaoniang to wear. When spring arrives, we can make spring shirts for her.","These two bolts of fabric are especially soft and have the character for fortune embroidered on them. They must be for Yongshi.","Oldest Song noticed the thickness of the cloth didn't look quite right and reached out to count the bolts. Twelve bolts. That's two more than the second branch got.","Hearing this, Elder Aunt Song happily stuffed the fabric back into the chest.","Clang, thud.","What was that sound?","Elder Aunt Song looked down at the ground but found nothing. However, the sound just now clearly indicated that something had dropped.","Song Qiaoniang came out of the room holding Song Yongshi, a silver bracelet in her hand.","Mother, is it this? It just rolled into the room and I saw it.","Elder Aunt Song took the bracelet with shining eyes. The delicate lotus patterns sparkled brightly, looking incredibly beautiful.","She looked at Oldest Song in pleasant surprise. Did Jinzhao give this to me?","Since it was a wide bracelet and a style suited for married women, it definitely wasn't for Qiaoniang.","Song Qiaoniang said with eyes full of envy, Mother, this bracelet is so pretty.","Elder Aunt Song put the bracelet on her wrist and carefully examined the patterns on it.","Not only is it pretty, but it's also valuable. Made of silver, it must be worth at least a few taels.","Song Yongnian walked out from the left room holding a book.","He bent down to pick up a letter that had fallen under the table and said, quite speechless, Not only is there a bracelet, but there's also a letter. They both dropped on the floor and you didn't even notice.","Elder Aunt Song glanced under the table. It was too far in, I didn't see it. Hurry and see what it says!","Song Yongnian opened the envelope. Inside was only a single sheet of paper with just a few words.","It's nothing much. Sister Jinzhao just says that Grandpa and Grandma are getting older, and asks you to take better care of them on a daily basis.","Oldest Song took the letter and looked at it from beginning to end. Even though he couldn't read a single word, he was just happy in his heart.","Jinzhao really is something. Taking care of our parents is our duty to begin with, yet she went out of her way to send a bracelet.","Elder Aunt Song reached out and took the bracelet off. She's giving me a hint. The bracelet was given to me, after all.","Seeing her take the bracelet off her wrist, Oldest Song hurriedly reached out to put it back on her.","It looks good on you, no need to take it off.","Elder Aunt Song dodged his hand, insisting on taking the bracelet off, and carefully cradled it in her hands.","It wouldn't be good to let the second branch see it. I don't need to wear a bracelet when I'm doing chores at home. I'll wear it when we return to my maiden home on the second day of the New Year.","Then she said to the siblings, Jinzhao bought things for you too. Grandpa said for you to go get them yourselves tomorrow. We should be eating dinner over there tomorrow night.","Oldest Song picked up the chest disapprovingly. Just now, the second brother wanted to eat there, but Father didn't let him. If we were going to eat together, we would have done it today. I reckon it won't be until the Little New Year.","Elder Aunt Song said, That's because there's an outsider in the house. He rushed over from a thousand miles away to deliver things, and then having to cook for a huge family, even if he is a servant, our parents wouldn't agree to that. We'll definitely wait until he leaves and eat tomorrow.","Oldest Song said, So that's how it is. I thought Father was upset.","Elder Aunt Song clicked her tongue. With Jinzhao sending so much, how could they possibly be upset? She was successful and filial; they would probably wake up laughing from their dreams."]},{"number":247,"title":"Chapter 247: There is Fifty Taels of Silver in the Sachet","paragraphs":["At night, Old Lady Song took the new bedding out of the chest and laid it out on the heated brick bed. As she unfolded it, a fragrant sachet fell out.","She picked it up and found that it was filled with silver ingots weighing one tael each, fifty of them in total.","\"Old man, come here quickly,\" Old Lady Song turned her head and shouted to Old Man Song, who was soaking his feet just outside the room.","\"Coming,\" Old Man Song replied while wiping his feet.","Unable to wait, Old Lady Song took the sachet to the main hall to show him, her eyes flashing with a pleasant surprise.","\"I just found this in the bedding. There are fifty taels of silver inside.\"","Old Man Song took the sachet and opened it. The gleaming white silver caught his eye, and he asked, \"Did Jinzhao give this?\"","Old Lady Song hesitated for a moment, \"Jinzhao must have put it there. It couldn't be anyone else.\"","Old Man Song handed the sachet back to Old Lady Song for safekeeping. He slipped on his cotton shoes and walked to the door, noticing that the room in the west wing was dark.","\"That steward must be asleep. I'll ask him tomorrow.\"","When Fushun woke up the next day, Old Lady Song was kneading dough in the kitchen.","Ever since the two of them moved out of the old house, the grain harvested this year combined with the rent from their fields meant the elderly couple enjoyed a much better standard of living than before.","Since the guest had come all this way in the bitter winter to deliver New Year's gifts and was leaving today, Old Man Song asked Old Lady Song to knead dough in the morning to make steamed buns, both plain and stuffed, so he could take some to eat on the road.","After washing up, Fushun tried to help out but was shooed out by Old Lady Song.","Seeing that he was awake, Old Man Song approached him with the sachet and asked, \"Did Jinzhao give this to us?\"","Fushun took a close look, broke into a wide smile, and said, \"The Eldest Miss gave it for you and the old madam to use. The Second Miss even made this sachet with her own hands.\"","Old Man Song's rough fingertips stroked the soaring crane embroidered on the sachet, his eyes filled with uncontrollable joy.","Having thought about it all night, Second Song and Second Aunt Song came over early in the morning, pushing Song Yaozu and the two sisters, Song Laidi and Song Pandi, to come and get things.","Thinking of the bedding, clothes, various meats, and now even the silver that Song Jinzhao had prepared, the more Old Man Song looked at Second Song, the more displeased he felt.","They always said to raise sons for support in old age, but in the end, a son was not as useful as a granddaughter.","\"We will wait until the two children from the first branch come over, then we will divide everything together. You two go back and leave the three children here.\"","Old Lady Song beckoned the Laidi sisters to sit down. She was growing more and more fond of her granddaughters.","People always said girls were useless, yet the girls in her family were the most promising.","\"Have you had breakfast? Grandma made some stuffed buns, come have a taste.\"","She picked up two meat buns from the plate and stuffed them into the hands of Song Laidi and Song Pandi, smiling lovingly as she said, \"They are fresh out of the pot, still piping hot.\"","The two sisters exchanged a glance. They had eaten breakfast, but it was just watery porridge, and their mother had rushed them so much that they hadn't eaten their fill at all.","Taking a bite of the meat bun, the savory aroma of meat filled their noses and mouths.","The filling was made by Old Lady Song, stir-fried with cured meat and bamboo shoots. It was savory and crisp with every bite.","The gluttonous Song Yaozu didn't wait for Old Lady Song to hand him one. He reached out, grabbed a meat bun himself, and took a huge bite. He looked completely satisfied, though his eyes remained fixed on the remaining buns on the plate.","Sitting on a small stool, Fushun observed silently. The Eldest Miss hadn't gone into detail with him about the first and second branches of the family, but judging by the New Year's gifts prepared, it was obvious that her relationship with the first branch was much better than with the second.","From yesterday to today, it now seemed there was good reason for that.","Just looking at the second branch's only male heir and the two young misses, the difference in their clothing and appearance was extraordinarily huge.","One looked like he lived a pampered life, while the other two had definitely suffered a lot. The calluses on their hands were even thicker than those of the kitchen maids in the manor.","Second Song and Second Aunt Song looked resentfully at the steamed buns on the table, their mouths watering. They wanted to eat too.","The sound of their swallowing was unusually loud, yet still, no one paid them any attention.","Not wanting to be scolded, the two had no choice but to leave dejectedly. Before leaving, they kept winking and signaling at Song Yaozu and the two sisters.","When it was time to divide the items, they absolutely had to fight for them and make sure they didn't get less than the first branch.","Song Qiaoniang had eaten a good breakfast and waited for Song Yongnian to finish reviewing his books before they came over together.","Seeing that all five children had arrived, Old Lady Song placed the items she had sorted out last night onto the table.","Song Jinzhao and the others had bought the gifts according to the number of people, so there was no need to agonize over it; it was clear which item was bought for whom.","Old Man Song called the five children to stand before him and handed the gifts to them one by one.","\"These are the gifts your cousin-sister and cousin-brother sent you. Yongnian, Yaozu, you two must study hard. Grandpa doesn't ask that you pass the provincial exams like Qiming; I'd be satisfied even if you just pass the county level.\"","Song Yongnian happily hugged his books and promised loudly, \"Don't worry, Grandpa, I will definitely pass next year.\"","Song Yaozu felt guilty and didn't dare look up. He kept his head down and mumbled softly, \"Grandpa, I will try my best.\"","Song Laidi and Song Pandi held a thick stack of new clothes, topped with hair flowers and handkerchiefs. They were all things they had never seen before, and they looked even better than the ones sent for last year's New Year.","Looking at his three granddaughters, Old Man Song thought of Song Jinzhao and Song Shixue, who were thousands of miles away. It would be wonderful if these three could also study.","Even if they couldn't take the imperial exams, just knowing how to read would be good enough. Their future lives would always be a bit better.","\"Yongnian, Yaozu, when you have free time, you two can try teaching your sisters to read. Knowing how to read is always better than being illiterate.\"","Song Yongnian and Song Yaozu looked at Old Man Song in astonishment, then turned their gazes to their respective sisters.","Teach them to read? Would that work?","Fushun, who was feeding the horse in the courtyard, silently made a mental note of all these matters, so he would have something to report if the Eldest Miss asked.","Seeing that Old Man Song had finished speaking, Old Lady Song stuffed a bowl of steamed buns into the hands of each family. \"Come over for dinner tonight, and tell your parents to come too.\"","Song Yongnian nodded, holding his books in one hand and the bowl in the other.","Song Laidi handed half the clothes she was holding to Song Pandi, freeing up one hand to take the bowl, and obediently nodded her chin. \"I know, Grandma.\"","After they had all left, Fushun finally walked in and said, \"Old Master, Old Madam, it's getting late, so this humble one will take his leave now.\"","Old Man Song nodded. \"The snowy roads are slippery, be careful on your way.\"","Old Lady Song turned around and brought out a cloth bundle, handing it to him. \"We don't have anything fancy at home, but take these buns to eat on the road.\"","\"Thank you very much, Old Madam,\" Fushun smiled as he took the bundle and placed it on the carriage.","The carriage traveled for about half an hour when Fushun heard the sound of gongs and drums in the distance. As he got closer, he realized it was people from the local government office, so he hurriedly pulled to the side to make way for them.","Gongs, drums, and suonas, and they were all wearing red flowers. What were they doing?","Even if it was a wedding procession, they shouldn't be wearing official uniforms, and the sedan chair didn't even have a single red silk ribbon tied to it.","After the procession left, Fushun didn't think much more about it and drove the carriage forward to continue his journey.","It wasn't until he entered Xining City to buy charcoal that he heard the shop owner chatting with a customer."]},{"number":248,"title":"Chapter 248: Learning That Song Jinzhao Has Become a County Princess","paragraphs":["As the woman watched the shop assistant load charcoal into her bamboo basket, she chatted with the shopkeeper, her face filled with envy and admiration.","\"Who would have thought a peasant girl could become a County Princess? I even bought cold noodles from her back when she was just running a street stall.\"","The shopkeeper jotted down a few words in his ledger while looking at his abacus.","\"Isn't that the truth? Everyone knows the Song family girl who ran the stall is highly skilled in martial arts and great at business. I used to go there all the time to buy cold noodles and iced plum rock sugar tea. I heard she was made a Lady of the County before, and now, not long after, she's become a County Princess. She's really made something of herself.\"","Standing behind the woman, Fushun's mind went blank. \"Shopkeeper, is the Song family girl you're talking about the one from Song Family Village? The one with three younger siblings?\"","The shopkeeper looked at the unfamiliar face of Fushun. \"You must be from out of town, right? It's the Song family girl who beat the Shuobei traitors to death, named Song Jinzhao.\"","The woman pointed out the door and said excitedly, \"Just a little while ago, the county magistrate took his men, beating gongs and drums, and hurried toward the Song family home. They brought a lot of things with them too. Didn't you see?\"","It felt as if a bolt of lightning had struck Fushun right on the head, leaving him numb all over as if he had been electrocuted.","His master had become a County Princess! Those yamen runners just now were heading to Song Family Village?","\"Ah—\" Fushun blinked furiously in disbelief, unable to suppress his emotions as he let out a loud shout, startling the shopkeeper, the assistant, and the customers buying charcoal.","\"What's wrong with this guy?\" The woman shrank back toward the shopkeeper in horror, thinking he had gone mad.","After his excited shout, Fushun immediately turned and ran outside. He had to hurry back to Anyang Prefecture to tell the others the news.","Just as he was about to drive his cart away, he suddenly remembered he hadn't bought the charcoal yet, so he quickly darted back. \"Shopkeeper, I need one hundred coins' worth of charcoal. Please pack it up for me quickly.\"","The three of them looked at the grin on his face, which looked as if he had just struck it rich, and felt somewhat baffled. Weren't they just talking about the Song family girl being titled County Princess? Why was he so happy?","The shopkeeper took the money from Fushun and told the assistant to pack the charcoal. \"Brother, do you know the Song family girl who was titled County Princess?\"","Otherwise, there was no way to explain why he was so thrilled.","Fushun's smile stretched from ear to ear as he proudly showed off, \"My master is the County Princess you're talking about.\"","The shopkeeper froze, carefully looking Fushun up and down. \"Brother, did you come from Anyang Prefecture?\"","Fushun nodded. \"My master accompanied the Young Master to the capital for the spring imperial examinations, and asked me to come here to deliver New Year gifts to Old Man Song and Old Lady Song living in their hometown.\"","At this moment, Old Man Song and Old Lady Song were completely bewildered by the sudden arrival of Zhang Yuanzong.","It had only been a few months, why was the county magistrate here again?","Zhang Yuanzong cupped his hands in greeting toward Old Man Song with a face full of smiles, scaring him so much that he froze in place, unable to move.","\"Congratulations, Master Song. The Linghui Lady of the County has been granted the title of County Princess by His Majesty.\"","Before the others could react, the village chief who had tagged along felt his mind explode.","His legs went weak, and he collapsed onto the ground, his soul seemingly having left his body.","Aren't County Princesses all imperial relatives? How did the Jinzhao girl get such a title?","Old Man Song looked at Song Mancang, who was sitting on the ground in a daze, and seemed to realize something. Was a County Princess much higher ranking than a Lady of the County?","Walking into the main hall, this time Zhang Yuanzong absolutely refused to sit in the seat of honor. He pushed Old Man Song into the main chair and then sat himself down in a lower seat.","After an unprecedented round of flattery, the Song family members standing in the room finally understood just how much weight Song Jinzhao's title of County Princess carried.","A title that only imperial relatives could receive had now been awarded to Jinzhao, a girl born of commoners.","The Emperor had even gifted her a County Princess Manor in the capital. How high must this position be? It reached the heavens!","The congratulatory gifts Zhang Yuanzong brought this time were double what he brought last time, and his mouth never stopped praising her, as if he wanted to use every good word in the world on Song Jinzhao.","This time, Zhang Yuanzong warmly greeted and checked on every single member of the Song family, staying for a full two hours before leaving.","No sooner had he left than the courtyard was packed with villagers.","They chattered endlessly, their voices noisier than a chicken coop.","The village chief, Song Mancang, excitedly grabbed Old Man Song's hands and shouted, \"Open the ancestral hall! We must open the ancestral hall! Open it immediately, and we need to erect a monument too!\"","Old Man Song was shaken until he felt dizzy, his whole being so immersed in excitement that he couldn't think straight.","Old Lady Song remembered Fushun who had just left and said in confusion, \"Jinzhao was made a County Princess, so why didn't that steward who just left tell us?\"","Song Mancang replied, \"I'm guessing the news hadn't reached Anyang Prefecture yet when he came over.\"","Old Lady Song nodded in understanding; that must be the case.","In fact, just as Song Mancang thought, Chunxing received the news on the fourth day after Fushun left Anyang Prefecture.","Delivered along with the news was a handwritten letter from Song Jinzhao, instructing them to harvest the potatoes from the greenhouse and send three thousand two hundred catties to the capital.","...","After the sun came out, Duke Zhenguo, who was preparing to return from the Western Suburbs Encampment, saw that Xiao Rongyan refused to take a carriage and insisted on riding a horse. Helpless, he stepped forward to dissuade him: \"Your Highness, the roads are slippery from the snow. It would be safer to take a carriage.\"","Although the Prince of Ying's riding skills were decent, he had never ridden on snowy roads. If he took a fall halfway, the unlucky ones would be the Duke and his son.","Xiao Rongyan refused, saying, \"If it's dangerous, just have someone clear the path ahead. This Prince will ride a horse back.\"","If he didn't show himself outside, how could anyone see him? He had to let the commoners in the capital see his majestic and imposing appearance.","Unable to persuade him, Duke Zhenguo personally led men to clear the path ahead, having the others ride alongside Xiao Rongyan to protect him.","The snowy sky and ground blended into one color, and there wasn't a single soul on the road.","The two-meter-thick snow had melted a bit but was still over a meter deep. Riding his horse, Duke Zhenguo slowed down to let the warhorses walk more steadily.","They had traveled this road thousands of times. Even if they couldn't see the path, they could tell where they were by the trees alongside it.","Chilled by the wind, Xiao Rongyan shrank his head into his cloak, wondering if his Imperial Father had missed him after not seeing him for so many days.","The vast, white fields stretched as far as the eye could see. As they passed a fir forest, Xiao Rongyan saw several antlers poking out of the snow. Looking closer, he discovered it was a herd of five elk.","He immediately pulled the reins to stop and ordered the guard walking next to him, \"Give me my bow and arrows.\"","The guard unhooked the bow and arrows from his horse and handed them to Xiao Rongyan. However, his first shot missed completely.","The startled herd of elk ran frantically into the distance, and Xiao Rongyan immediately spurred his horse to chase after them.","He had just been worrying about having nothing to give his Imperial Father, and now a gift had delivered itself right to his door.","Duke Zhenguo turned his head just in time to see Xiao Rongyan charging toward the fir forest on horseback, and he immediately shouted, \"Your Highness, don't ride off recklessly!\"","But how could Xiao Rongyan listen to Duke Zhenguo? He charged forward without even looking back.","Once he hunted a stag and gave it to his Imperial Father, his Imperial Father would surely be pleased.","Infuriated to the point of blowing his beard and glaring, Duke Zhenguo immediately turned his horse around to chase Xiao Rongyan back.","In the snow, the elk ran faster than the horses. Coupled with Xiao Rongyan's poor riding skills, not only did he fail to catch up, but the distance between them grew wider and wider.","Duke Zhenguo caught up with Xiao Rongyan and, furrowing his brows tightly, said to him, \"Your Highness, stop chasing them. There are steep slopes in the forest, it's very dangerous.\"","Just as Xiao Rongyan heard this and was about to stop, he saw the herd of elk ahead slowing down to turn a corner.","\"Let me take one more shot.\"","He dashed forward a few more steps, nocked an arrow, and drew the bowstring. He let the feathered arrow fly, but to his surprise, instead of hitting the most magnificent stag, it struck a young fawn."]},{"number":249,"title":"Chapter 249: The Unheeding Xiao Rongyan: Avalanche Startles Horses","paragraphs":["Xiao Rongyan threw his bow and arrow to the ground in frustration. Such a small catch could definitely not be presented to his imperial father.","A guard ran over to pick up the fawn that had been shot in the hind leg. The moment he turned around, an adult doe without antlers charged fiercely at his back.","Watch out. The calm expression on Duke Zhenguo's face instantly turned as cold as eternal ice. His longsword left its sheath, bringing with it a blinding flash of white light.","Just as the deer's head was about to crash into the guard's lower back, the sharp blade pierced its neck. Boiling hot blood spewed out, and the doe fell to the ground, twitching twice before losing its life.","Seeing Duke Zhenguo slay the doe with a single strike while it took him two arrows just to hit a fawn, Xiao Rongyan suddenly felt he had lost face.","He drew the sword hanging from his saddle and looked at the herd of elk watching from a distance, dark currents surging in his eyes. You wait here. I am going to kill a stag and bring it back.","Duke Zhenguo, who had just saved the guard, looked even more displeased. He rode his horse to block Xiao Rongyan's path.","Your Highness Prince Ying, if you want a stag, I will personally catch a live one for you another day. There are steep slopes near the fir forest, currently hidden by the snow. It is best not to ride around recklessly. The herd is too far away; they will run as soon as you approach, and you won't be able to hunt them.","Xiao Rongyan frowned in dissatisfaction, believing that Duke Zhenguo was looking down on him.","His frustrated gaze noticed the other soldiers who had followed them, making him feel even more humiliated.","He raised his chin and declared loudly to the crowd, Who says I cannot hunt one? During last year's spring hunt, let alone a stag, even a black bear was nothing to me.","Duke Zhenguo's thick black eyebrows twitched incessantly. Was it really you who hunted it?","The guards had completely surrounded the black bear, and you just went up and added an arrow. Not to mention that the black bear had three arrow wounds on its body, and it was only the third arrow that was fatal.","Watching Xiao Rongyan gallop toward the elk, Duke Zhenguo closed his eyes in exhaustion and waved his hand, signaling the other soldiers to follow.","It was truly eight lifetimes of bad luck to be stuck with such a prince, and to have him forcefully shoved into his military camp. Arrogant and unaware of his own limits, he was nothing but trouble everywhere he went.","Xiao Rongyan couldn't catch up to the startled herd at all. In the end, he broke out in a cold sweat, his sword-holding hand frozen stiff. He didn't even manage to touch an antler before the herd vanished without a trace.","Helpless, Xiao Rongyan had to turn his horse around and return. Looking at the already frozen doe on the ground and the fawn that was still bleating, he felt a surge of irritation and, as if venting his anger, raised his sword and chopped off the fawn's head.","The cries instantly ceased, and the fir forest fell into an eerie silence.","The others looked at Duke Zhenguo in dismay, only to see that Duke Zhenguo, whose boot had been splattered with blood, had a face as dark as ink.","Just as Xiao Rongyan's guard bent down to pick up the fawn's corpse from the ground, everyone gradually felt the ground begin to shake, the intensity growing stronger and stronger.","Duke Zhenguo abruptly looked up and ahead, only to see white waves churning on the distant mountainside, surging forward like a massive beast.","Run, it is an avalanche!","The anger on Xiao Rongyan's face vanished without a trace the moment he saw the avalanche. Under Duke Zhenguo's shouts, everyone turned their horses to flee.","A streak of orange and black suddenly appeared beside Xiao Rongyan. It snatched the fawn's corpse from the ground and ran off, its speed so fast that no one had time to react.","Neigh! The horse was startled, rearing its front hooves high into the air. Xiao Rongyan, riding on it, was caught off guard. His lower body was thrown into the air, and as the horse's hooves landed and it bolted in the opposite direction of the fleeing leopard, he fell heavily back onto the saddle.","He let out a muffled groan, a sharp pain in his ribs. He felt as if his internal organs had been shattered.","The sudden accident made Duke Zhenguo turn pale with fright. He immediately spurred his horse and chased after Xiao Rongyan.","Lean down, hug the horse's neck!","With the wind howling in his ears, the panicked Xiao Rongyan couldn't hear Duke Zhenguo's instructions at all. He pulled hard on the reins, trying to make the horse stop, but the more he did so, the faster the horse ran.","Seeing this, Duke Zhenguo had no choice but to whip his horse hard to catch up.","The cascading snow rushed into the fir forest like an unstoppable tsunami. Fortunately, there were enough trees in the forest to slightly divert and block it, slowing the avalanche's speed.","After catching up, the two horses ran side by side. Duke Zhenguo kicked hard with his legs and leaped into the air.","He landed on Xiao Rongyan's horse, snatched the reins from his hands, and pressed him down against the horse's back to lower their center of gravity. Meanwhile, he continuously pulled the reins hard to one side, trying to reduce their speed and bring the horse to a halt.","Under Duke Zhenguo's relentless efforts, the startled horse finally began to calm down. Just as the two of them were about to breathe a sigh of relief, their bodies suddenly hung in the air, and a strong sense of weightlessness washed over them.","The elderly Duke Zhenguo was so angry he wanted to curse. He had told him there were steep slopes, and now they had really fallen.","The horse let out a long, mournful neigh as its four hooves buckled, falling into the snowbank and rolling downward. In a matter of moments, it disappeared from sight.","Lord Duke! the soldiers who had caught up shouted in horror, their eyes bulging.","Xiao Rongyan's guard stood frozen in place, completely stunned.","His veins bulging, his arm bore the weight of two people. In a moment of desperation, Duke Zhenguo had grabbed the branch of a fir tree with his left hand, preventing them from rolling down with the horse.","His other hand was tightly gripped by Xiao Rongyan, nearly dislocating.","Stop yelling and hurry over to save us! Duke Zhenguo roared upwards.","Hearing his voice, the soldiers snapped back to reality, hastily dismounted, and rushed over.","The tremors caused their bodies to sway. Everyone turned to look to their right, only to see torrential waves of snow surging towards them, about to bury them alive.","The tree trunk swayed, and a crisp cracking sound rang out. Duke Zhenguo glanced down at Xiao Rongyan and used his right hand to forcefully pull him to his side.","Hurry up and climb up!","At this moment, not a trace of color could be seen on Xiao Rongyan's face. His mind was filled with only one thought: survive.","To Duke Zhenguo's surprise, he had thought Xiao Rongyan would grab the branch after climbing up, but instead, the prince actually stepped on his shoulder and kicked off hard, jumping up to hug the tree trunk.","The impact nearly snapped his left hand that was gripping the branch, and he almost lost his hold.","Just then, the snow rolling down from the mountainside crashed over them, burying everyone under the white snow.","The massive impact broke the already cracked branch. Duke Zhenguo's sturdy figure was swept down along with the snow, not even managing to cry out for help.","The rumbling sound roared past.","After a long while, hands began to reach out from the snow one after another. Then, the soldiers broke through the snow and climbed out.","At a glance, the snow around them was more than twice as thick as before, and the sound of the churning snow waves was gradually fading.","Xiao Rongyan climbed out of the snowbank, still hugging the tree trunk.","Seeing Xiao Rongyan but not Duke Zhenguo, a soldier immediately panicked and shouted for the Lord Duke towards the place where they had just fallen.","The voice echoed through the entire forest. Hearing this title, Xiao Rongyan's expression changed slightly, and he turned his head to look at the vast white snowfield behind him.","Thinking back to how his desperate kick had felt a sinking sensation, his already bloodless face could only be described as deathly pale. His heart pounded wildly, as if it were going to leap out of his chest, vibrating so hard that his ears began to ring."]},{"number":250,"title":"Chapter 250: The Duke Hanging by a Thread","paragraphs":["A fast horse galloped madly toward the western suburban camp. Seeing that the rider was dressed in the same uniform as them, the guards were just about to lift the barricade when they realized the rider had no intention of stopping. At breakneck speed, he leaped over the barricade and bolted toward the tent area.","The two guards stared in astonishment at his rapidly retreating back. Wasn't that one of the soldiers who had just left for the city with Duke Zhenguo and his men?","Why was he back? He looked frantic, as if something terrible had happened.","Inside the main tent, Chu Liuyun, who was in the middle of a military discussion, frowned at the sound of the approaching hooves. \"Who is riding a horse inside the camp?\"","Just as his lieutenant turned to go check, the soldier burst into the tent in a panic, as if chased by fierce beasts, and crashed right into him.","Glaring at the soldier who had fallen to the ground, the lieutenant scolded, \"Why are you barging in like your tail is on fire? Have you no sense of military discipline?\"","The soldier scrambled to his knees and crawled all the way to Chu Liuyun's feet, his face pale with absolute terror.","\"My Lord, disaster has struck! Duke Zhenguo encountered an avalanche on his way back to the city. He is missing and still hasn't been found!\"","The words struck like a thunderbolt. The generals in the tent stared at him in disbelief, their gazes as sharp and piercing as swords.","\"What did you say?\" Chu Liuyun's pupils contracted. He took a long stride forward, looming over the soldier, and demanded, \"The road back to the city doesn't pass near any snowy mountains! How could there be an avalanche?\"","The soldier looked as though he were about to cry. His voice stuttered in his panic. \"It was at Mount Xiaomao. Duke Zhenguo went missing in the fir forest.\"","\"Halfway through the journey, His Highness Prince Ying spotted a herd of elk and insisted on hunting them. After they were lured into the fir forest, an avalanche suddenly occurred. His Highness's horse was spooked, and to save Prince Ying, Duke Zhenguo fell down a steep slope near the forest. The snow is so thick that we still haven't found him.\"","Images of his own father falling off a cliff and freezing to death just to save Xiao Rongyan flashed through Chu Liuyun's mind. His tightly clenched fists trembled uncontrollably.","A cavalry of three hundred men charged out of the western suburban camp at top speed, leaving the guards at the gate staring at each other in utter bewilderment.","\"What's going on? Why is the Duke of Qing taking so many men out?\"","Having failed to find the missing man after so long, Xiao Rongyan stood with his legs buried in the snow, his clothes already soaked through. Looking out over the pale snowfield, his mind was already scheming about how to absolve himself of blame once he returned.","The massive cavalry charged over from the distance. When Chu Liuyun saw Xiao Rongyan standing motionless, safely surrounded by his guards, he could no longer suppress the raging fire in his mind.","He didn't say a single word as he dismounted and walked past, but his face was livid, and he shot him a vicious, venomous glare.","That single look made Xiao Rongyan feel a genuine murderous intent.","The three hundred-plus men quickly fanned out in the direction where Duke Zhenguo had fallen. They cleared the snow on the ground as fast as they could. When they encountered steep slopes, they lowered themselves with ropes and crawled down; when they met sheer cliffs, they detoured and kept searching.","As time ticked by, Chu Liuyun's heart grew increasingly frantic. If they didn't find him soon, he would freeze to death even if he hadn't been injured in the fall. The snow was so thick that if he couldn't climb out, he would suffocate.","The sun shifted from directly overhead to the west. Nearly two hours had passed since Duke Zhenguo went missing.","Suddenly, a sharp cry pierced the air. A soldier holding a shovel shouted toward Chu Liuyun, \"My Lord, we found him!\"","Everyone quickly gathered around, but upon seeing Duke Zhenguo's condition, they all froze in place, their blood running cold.","Sharp tree branches had pierced through Duke Zhenguo just above his collarbone and into his abdomen. His head had struck a rock and was split open. Had his eyelashes not been fluttering slightly, it would be entirely believable to say he was dead.","Chu Liuyun stared at his father, his face deathly pale. He dropped to one knee and reached out a trembling finger to place it under his father's nose. A faint breath brushed against his knuckle. Utterly drained of strength, he supported himself with both hands on the ground, panting heavily.","...","A large group of men and horses rushed into the city. The moment the stretcher was carried into the Duke Zhenguo's estate, the steward grabbed the official seal, mounted a horse, and galloped madly toward the imperial palace.","The physician who had been rushed over felt his heart skip a beat when he saw Duke Zhenguo lying on the bed with two tree branches protruding from his upper body.","Blood was still seeping from around the wounds, and the branches quivered with his faint breaths. It was obvious at a glance that they had pierced very deep.","The physician carefully reached out to take Duke Zhenguo's pulse.","The pulse was floating, large, soft, and empty. His breath was like a gossamer thread. He was losing blood and vital energy—a critical sign of impending exhaustion of qi and blood.","He feared this man could not be saved.","\"How is he?\" Upon seeing him pause, the voice of the over ninety-year-old Dowager Duchess Chu rang out, choked with sobs.","Looking at her, the physician didn't dare tell the truth.","Dowager Duchess Chu was nearly a hundred years old and already in poor health. She certainly wouldn't be able to handle such a devastating blow.","\"My medical skills are shallow. You must quickly invite the imperial physicians from the palace to treat him.\"","Hearing this, the hearts of everyone present stopped. They realized that Duke Zhenguo's life was hanging by a thread and that this physician could not save him.","Dowager Duchess Chu swayed unsteadily and collapsed backward. The maids and elder female servants hastily caught her, swarming around her with anxious cries.","The physician's expression changed drastically, and he quickly stepped forward to administer emergency aid.","An imperial physician in his forties was carried on horseback by the steward, galloping all the way to the Duke Zhenguo's estate. By the time they stopped, the physician had thrown up bile.","Upon entering the room and seeing Duke Zhenguo on the bed, the imperial physician conducted a thorough examination. He then looked nervously at Chu Liuyun. \"I am somewhat uncertain. It would be best to quickly invite Director Gu over.\"","The Chu family felt as if they had been struck by lightning. They were on the verge of total despair.","While the imperial physician struggled to stop the bleeding, more than half of the physicians from the Imperial Academy of Medicine were hauled over in carriages by the Duke Zhenguo's estate all at once.","The commotion was so massive that Xiao Chengjing, who was reviewing memorials in the imperial study, caught wind of the news.","He furrowed his brows and questioned, \"Wasn't Duke Zhenguo at the western suburban camp? How did he get injured?\"","The head eunuch lowered his head and replied, \"I heard that they encountered an avalanche on the way back. To save His Highness Prince Ying, Duke Zhenguo fell down a steep slope. Not only did he hit his head, but his body was also pierced by tree branches. His life is currently hanging by a thread.\"","Hearing this, Xiao Chengjing's eyes widened, and he stood up in concern.","\"Is Prince Ying injured? What do the imperial physicians say?\"","The head eunuch shook his head. \"His Highness Prince Ying is unharmed, but Duke Zhenguo's situation is not looking good.\"","\"Imperial Physician Xu, who went first, said he couldn't save him and requested that Director Gu be brought in. Now, more than half of the physicians from the Imperial Academy are at the Duke Zhenguo's estate, and the situation is still unknown.\"","Xiao Chengjing's anxious heart settled slightly, though he completely lost the mood to review his memorials. How could such a terrible thing happen out of nowhere?","He ordered loudly, \"Send someone to the Duke Zhenguo's estate immediately to keep an eye on things. Tell the imperial physicians to do everything in their power to save him. Take the remaining physicians from the Imperial Academy over there as well, and tell Prince Ying to come see me at once.\"","\"Yes, Your Majesty.\" The head eunuch bowed and hurried out, not daring to delay.","He dispatched someone to monitor the Duke Zhenguo's estate while sending another to summon the remaining doctors from the Imperial Academy of Medicine. Finally, he paused to catch his breath and ordered his apprentice to fetch the prince from Prince Ying's manor."]},{"number":251,"title":"Chapter 251: The Helpless Imperial Hospital: Have Them Prepare for the Funeral Arrangements","paragraphs":["News spread quickly in the palace. In no time at all, even the inner palace had heard about it.","Princess Yongjia wanted to leave the palace but was stopped by her maid.","\"Your Highness, the Duke Zhenguo's estate must be in chaos right now. It is best that you do not go.\"","Calming down, Xiao Yongjia stood rooted to the spot, her mind racing. \"You are right. My going there now would only add to the confusion. Leave the palace immediately and keep an eye on the Duke Zhenguo's estate. If anything happens, return and tell me at once.\"","The maid nodded vigorously. After helping Xiao Yongjia to sit on the couch, she immediately left the palace.","Gu Jupu stared fixedly at the branches that trembled with Duke Zhenguo's every breath. He clenched his jaw in distress, the fingers resting on the duke's wrist trembling slightly, his heart exceedingly heavy.","The branches were embedded deeply. Pulling them out would inevitably cause unstoppable bleeding.","The blood vessels inside were definitely injured. If the bleeding could not be stopped, they could only wait for death.","Behind him, over a dozen imperial physicians huddled together discussing the condition. Everyone's face was very solemn, and they would occasionally shake their heads and sigh.","The oppressive atmosphere made it even harder for the already devastated Chu family to accept.","Chu Liuyun's dark gaze fell straight upon the unconscious Duke Zhenguo. His rugged eye sockets, tempered by the flames of war, were now thoroughly red.","He originally thought that as long as he was alive, he could be saved, but he never expected it to be this difficult.","\"Director Gu?\"","The gray-haired Gu Jupu stood up to face Chu Liuyun, his dry lips pressed into a straight line.","He pointed to the two branches piercing Duke Zhenguo's body and said, \"This one above the collarbone is inserted over an inch deep; the bleeding is not too severe. However, the one in the abdomen has penetrated two inches into the body and trembles with his breathing, likely injuring the blood vessels of the internal organs. Once pulled out, he will inevitably bleed out and die on the spot.\"","\"This humble official truly does not know where to start. I must ask Madam Duke Zhenguo and Duke Qing to restrain your grief.\"","Director Gu's words had essentially sentenced Duke Zhenguo to death. In the next room, the Old Madam, unable to bear the shock, was still unconscious, and here her son was about to die.","Chu Liuyun asked with difficulty, a trace of pleading in his voice.","\"Is there really no other way to stop the bleeding?\"","Gu Jupu shook his head again. \"There is no way to stop the bleeding in this situation. It is already a blessing from the gods that Duke Zhenguo has held on until now. If we pull them out, he will die immediately.\"","Madam Duke Zhenguo covered her tear-filled eyes with a handkerchief and choked out, \"And if we don't pull them out?\"","Gu Jupu lowered his head. \"It will happen today. A cup of tea's time at the fastest, an hour at the slowest.\"","The eunuch standing behind the crowd turned pale. This meant he could not be saved and they needed to prepare for the funeral.","The moment the palace staff left, Madam Duke Zhenguo's long-suppressed emotions could no longer be controlled, and she wailed out loud. Disregarding the propriety between men and women, she cried and grabbed Gu Jupu's arm, about to kneel.","\"Director Gu, I beg you to think of another way. The Old Madam is advanced in years. If the Duke passes, I fear the old lady won't survive this ordeal. Please, look carefully again.\"","How could Gu Jupu accept such a grand gesture from a first-rank titled lady? He hastily crouched down to support Madam Duke Zhenguo.","\"Madam, this humble official truly cannot bear such a great courtesy. If he could be saved, I would do so even if it meant exhausting all my medical skills. But right now, there is truly nothing I can do.\"","Chu Liuyun stepped forward and embraced the devastated Madam Duke Zhenguo. His arms shook violently, unable to accept that his father, who was full of life just this morning, was now going to die.","Madam Duke Zhenguo lay in Chu Liuyun's arms, weeping bitterly.","Forcing herself to hold on, Old Madam Chu stumbled into the room. Seeing the continuous weeping, she unacceptably pushed everyone aside and threw herself at Duke Zhenguo's bedside.","Looking at her unconscious son, her wrinkle-filled eyes trembled violently.","She scolded loudly, roaring with a blood-laced voice, \"The man isn't dead yet, why are you mourning? Go and invite all the doctors in the capital. I don't believe no one can save my son!\"","Chu Liuyun, holding Madam Duke Zhenguo, suddenly widened his dead, pain-filled eyes, his cracked lips parting slightly.","He gently pushed Madam Duke Zhenguo aside and, as if grasping at a lifeline, said to Gu Jupu, \"Keep my father alive. I am going to find Song Jinzhao. She cured Ye Liangyu's leg; her medical skills are better than the imperial physicians'.\"","Watching Chu Liuyun rush out like the wind, shoving past all the imperial physicians, everyone in the room was first stunned, then dazed, and finally, a sliver of hope involuntarily sprouted in their hearts.","Gu Jupu looked blankly at his dozen or so subordinates. \"Was Duke Qing referring to County Princess Linghui?\"","Imperial Physician Xu nodded somewhat hesitantly. \"It should be.\"","Inside the Imperial Study, Xiao Rongyan stood before Xiao Chengjing, his lower half dripping wet. The mix of cold and heat made him shiver uncontrollably.","Seeing that although his face was pale, he didn't have a single injury on his body, the Emperor was finally completely relieved.","Thinking of Duke Zhenguo's severe injuries, and that the Prince of Ying was someone he himself had pushed into the military camp, if the man died, the Chu family might harbor resentment. He couldn't help but ask, \"What exactly happened? Was Duke Zhenguo injured trying to save you?\"","At this moment, Xiao Rongyan's mind was in utter chaos. Facing the Emperor's inquiry, he spoke the words he had prepared in advance.","\"On the way back, your son was attacked by a leopard, which spooked the horse. To save your son, Duke Zhenguo fell down a steep slope with me. In desperation, he pushed your son up first. Just as I hugged a tree trunk and tried to pull him up, the snow from the mountain rushed down and swept him away. By the time he was found, he was already terribly injured.\"","The Emperor frowned deeply. \"Duke Zhenguo's life is hanging by a thread because he saved you. By reason and emotion, you should immediately go to the Duke Zhenguo's estate to keep watch. Do not change out of these clothes.\"","Xiao Rongyan swallowed nervously. \"Your son will go at once.\"","\"Your Majesty, terrible news! Director Gu says he cannot be saved and has told the Duke Zhenguo's estate to prepare for the funeral.\" A eunuch ran in frantically, his inner garments soaked with sweat.","Xiao Rongyan's face turned pale. His feet felt glued to the floor, unsure for a moment whether he should still go.","The Imperial Study became incredibly quiet, with only the sound of the Emperor repeatedly tapping his fingers on the desk.","Inside Biluo Palace.","\"The imperial physicians have told them to prepare for the funeral, saying he won't last an hour. Old Madam Chu couldn't handle the shock and has fainted several times. Right now, the Duke Zhenguo's estate is in complete chaos.\"","Hearing the maid's report, Xiao Yongjia stood stiffly in place for a long time.","She asked, her voice floating, \"How is Brother Liuyun doing?\"","Maid: \"Duke Qing looks very devastated and is still begging the imperial physicians to continue treating him, but I'm afraid it is to no avail.\"","Inside the County Princess's estate, Song Jinzhao sat on the heated brick bed, instructing Lanxi to send someone to Daohua Manor tomorrow.","\"Have the stewards of Daohua Manor and Shiquan Manor come to the estate the day after tomorrow. I want to see them.\"","She did not plan to continue renting the fields to tenant farmers next year, and she needed to give the two stewards a heads-up regarding their arrangements in advance.","Lanxi nodded in agreement and then turned to report another matter.","\"The shop on Qipan Street was taken back this morning. The craftsmen responsible for renovating the shop have all been finalized. According to the blueprints you provided, County Princess, aside from the hot pot restaurant on Zhuque Street which requires a month, the other four shops can be finished before the new year.\"","Song Jinzhao: \"How is the training of the servants bought for the estate going?\"","Lanxi: \"The people to be assigned to the shops have basically all been decided. We are currently preparing for the second phase of professional training.\""]},{"number":252,"title":"Chapter 252: Storming into the County Princess's Mansion to Seek Song Jinzhao for Help","paragraphs":["Seeing that it was almost time for the shift change, the gatekeeper sitting behind the side door had already stood up, waiting for his replacement to arrive.","Bowl-sized iron hooves forcefully gripped the ground, splashing the snow and water on the ground four or five meters away.","With bloodshot eyes, Chu Liuyun tightly pulled the reins, the urgent horse's neigh sounding as if it had been strangled.","He stumbled off the horse, his figure more wretched than ever before.","\"Thump, thump, thump.\"","\"Thump, thump, thump.\"","The loud knocking on the door startled the gatekeeper like a clap of thunder.","He opened a crack in the door and looked to the left, only to see a man knocking on the door at the main entrance, his strength so great that it seemed he wanted to kick over the gate of the County Princess's manor.","\"Who is it?\" The gatekeeper rushed out, his face a little ugly.","No manners at all, is this how you knock on a door?","Hearing the voice, Chu Liuyun suddenly rushed towards the side door, loudly questioning as he rushed in, \"Is County Princess Linghui in the manor?\"","Seeing clearly that the visitor was the Duke of Qing, the gatekeeper put away the displeasure on his face and reached out to stop him while retreating, \"Answering the Duke of Qing, my County Princess is at home, please allow this servant to go and report.\"","No matter how high your official rank is, you can't force your way in. At any rate, my master is also a County Princess.","Chu Liuyun's strength was so great that the gatekeeper couldn't stop him at all, almost being dragged along.","After entering the door, the County Princess's manor was too big, and Chu Liuyun didn't know where to find Song Jinzhao.","He grabbed the gatekeeper's collar and roared, \"I have an urgent matter to find your County Princess, tell her to come out quickly.\"","Spit sprayed on the gatekeeper's face, and Chu Liuyun, glaring angrily like he wanted to eat someone, scared him silly, and he started to stutter when he spoke.","\"The County—the County Princess is in the backyard, please allow this lowly one to go and report.\"","The servants who saw the two pulling and tugging were shocked and turned to run towards the backyard. Why would the Duke of Qing suddenly attack the door out of nowhere?","\"County Princess~\" The servant hurried into the courtyard.","Before seeing the person, the voice was heard first. Song Jinzhao had just looked up when the servant rushed into the room, his whole body exuding panic.","\"County Princess, the Duke of Qing has forced his way into the manor, and his face looks very ugly.\"","Chu Liuyun? Song Jinzhao frowned and stood up, \"Where is he?\"","Servant: \"He grabbed the gatekeeper and is heading towards the backyard.\"","As soon as Song Jinzhao left the courtyard, she saw Chu Liuyun dragging the servant running over from the stone path.","Lanxi, who was following beside her, looked at Chu Liuyun dissatisfiedly. Even if his official rank was high, he couldn't force his way into the backyard of the County Princess's manor.","The moment he saw Song Jinzhao, Chu Liuyun decisively threw the gatekeeper away and rushed to her.","Just as Song Jinzhao was about to ask, she saw Chu Liuyun kneel on the ground without hesitation.","His knees hit the ground with a thump, startling everyone.","\"My father is severely injured and his life is hanging by a thread. I beg Miss Song to save my father's life.\"","A man's knees have gold underneath; he kneels to heaven, earth, and his parents.","Looking at Chu Liuyun's bloodshot eyes, tear-stained face, and the bulging veins on his neck, Song Jinzhao realized that Duke Zhenguo was probably going to die.","She asked in a deep voice, \"Where is he injured? Have any other doctors seen him?\"","Chu Liuyun spoke rapidly and urgently, wishing he could grab Song Jinzhao away immediately.","\"His forehead hit a rock, branches pierced above his collarbone and into his abdomen, and he was buried under the snow for two hours. The imperial physicians from the Imperial Hospital all came, saying that pulling them out would cause massive bleeding and he couldn't be saved.\"","A trace of disbelief flashed in Song Jinzhao's eyes, and she immediately turned and ran towards the courtyard.","\"I'm going to get something. Lanxi, prepare the carriage.\"","The medicine room was suddenly pushed open by Song Jinzhao, startling Song Shixue who was dispensing medicine inside.","Song Jinzhao ran to the corner, opened the box, and quickly checked the items inside.","\"What's wrong, Sister?\" The uninformed Song Shixue was a bit confused.","Song Jinzhao picked up the box and said to her, \"Duke Zhenguo is severely injured. Come with me to the Duke Zhenguo's manor immediately.\"","Song Shixue raised her eyebrows, quickly put down the medicine in her hand, put on her medicine box, and followed Song Jinzhao.","The door next to them was pushed open, and Song Anhao came out rubbing his eyes, \"Eldest Sister, Second Sister.\"","Song Jinzhao turned her head and stopped, \"Eldest Sister and Second Sister have to go out to handle some matters. Stay at home and be good.\"","\"Lanxi, watch over the Second Young Master.\"","Seeing Song Jinzhao holding a large box, Chu Liuyun reached out to take it, but Song Jinzhao dodged him.","\"I'll do it myself, you go drive the carriage.\" The things inside couldn't be dropped, and she wasn't relieved letting Chu Liuyun hold them.","After the two sisters got on the carriage, the driver who was about to get on was pulled down by Chu Liuyun, \"I'll do it.\"","He abandoned his own horse and drove the carriage of the County Princess's manor madly towards the Duke Zhenguo's manor.","The carriage bumped up and down. Song Jinzhao and Song Shixue propped their right hands against the wall of the carriage without saying a word.","Fortunately, the distance from Duke Zhenguo's manor to the County Princess's manor wasn't too far, and with Chu Liuyun driving like his life depended on it, Duke Zhenguo wasn't dead yet by the time they arrived.","The room full of imperial physicians looked at the seventeen-year-old Song Jinzhao, accompanied by the even younger Song Shixue, with even more suspicion in their eyes.","Even Director Gu said he couldn't be saved, and she could bring Duke Zhenguo back to life? She didn't look like it at all.","The Duke of Qing must have gone mad from desperation.","Seeing Chu Liuyun bring Song Jinzhao over, Gu Jupu decisively stepped aside.","Song Jinzhao scanned Duke Zhenguo from head to toe, squatted down, and carefully examined the two branches stuck in him.","\"How long has it been since the injury?\"","Chu Liuyun's voice was tense: \"It's been almost six hours.\"","Song Jinzhao looked up at Duke Zhenguo, whose eyelashes were trembling slightly and whose forehead was constantly sweating.","It was a miracle that he wasn't dead after so long.","The people of Duke Zhenguo's manor looked at the young Song Jinzhao and couldn't help but suspect that the Duke of Qing had found the wrong person.","Before Gu Jupu could speak, another imperial physician standing in the crowd couldn't wait to ask, \"What method does County Princess Linghui have to save Duke Zhenguo?\"","Song Jinzhao didn't even turn her head as she continued to examine him, saying indifferently, \"The person isn't dead yet, so where does the talk of saving him come from?\"","The imperial physician who was cut off was about to continue when Gu Jupu glared at him fiercely, \"Shut up, no one will think you're mute if you don't speak.\"","Song Jinzhao glanced at Gu Jupu, whose hair and beard were white, out of the corner of her eye. The other imperial physicians didn't dare to make a sound upon seeing this, and even the other people standing in the room didn't dare to speak, making the room exceptionally quiet.","\"Scissors.\"","Song Shixue quickly handed over the scissors.","Song Jinzhao carefully cut open the clothes around the wound.","Although the branches blocked the wound, so much time had passed, and a lot of blood had flowed out intermittently. If they weren't pulled out soon, he wouldn't be saved.","Without ultrasound or X-rays, it was impossible to accurately judge the injury. This surgery was extremely risky, and he might not survive the operating table.","Song Jinzhao stood up calmly and looked at Chu Liuyun, \"I'm going to cut him open and take out the branches now. The success rate is very low. Do you want to do it?\"","Chu Liuyun clenched his fists, his eyes trembling involuntarily, \"Is there hope?\"","Song Jinzhao: \"There is hope, but you must be prepared for the patient to die at any time.\""]},{"number":253,"title":"Chapter 253: Surgery Begins, Manual Hemostasis","paragraphs":["Madam Zhenguo looked up at Chu Liuyun; she could not make a decision.","Being supported, Dowager Duchess Chu nodded heavily without hesitation. \"Pull it out. As long as there is hope, pull it out.\"","Chu Liuyun stared intently at Song Jinzhao, his eyes filled with not only dry tears but also pleading. \"I leave it to you, County Princess.\"","Seeing that the Chu family had all agreed, an imperial physician standing to the side muttered softly, \"If you pull it out, won't he just die?\"","Song Jinzhao glanced at the imperial physician whose eyes were full of disapproval. \"It's better than dying doing nothing. There are too many people in the room; everyone get out.\"","\"Prepare boiling hot water, and close all the windows.\"","Gu Jupu took a step forward and bowed with cupped hands to Song Jinzhao. \"County Princess Linghui, could you allow this humble official to observe?\"","Song Jinzhao raised her eyes and swept a glance over them. \"Only two people can stay.\"","Dowager Duchess Chu grabbed the momo's hand and walked toward Song Jinzhao. \"Could you let this old woman stay here?\"","As she spoke, her tears burst out. \"I'm afraid I won't be able to see my son for the last time.\"","Song Jinzhao patiently said to Dowager Duchess Chu, \"The scene will be very bloody when I perform the surgery. I am afraid you won't be able to bear it, Dowager Duchess.\"","\"Family members are easily agitated when present. If his life hangs by a thread, I worry you will affect the surgery.\"","Chu Liuyun stepped forward to support Dowager Duchess Chu. He said to Song Jinzhao, \"Alright, we will go out. My father is in your hands, County Princess.\"","In the end, besides Song Jinzhao and Song Shixue, the only ones left in the room were Gu Jupu and Imperial Physician Xu, who stayed to observe and help hold down Duke Zhenguo.","The large chest they brought was opened. Song Shixue took out two protective suits and handed them to Gu Jupu and Imperial Physician Xu. \"Put these on.\"","All the tools in the chest were brought from Anyang Prefecture. They had not expected that the first time they would be used would be on the highly positioned and powerful Duke Zhenguo.","Imperial Physician Xu looked blankly at the cotton and linen garment in his hands. The outside was slippery, as if coated with a layer of oil wax.","The wound on Duke Zhenguo's head had already been treated by Imperial Physician Xu, who arrived first. After careful judgment, Song Jinzhao decided to extract the branch inserted above the collarbone first.","The sharp scalpel cut a cross-shaped incision above the collarbone, and fresh blood quickly dyed the gauze packed around it red.","Gu Jupu and Imperial Physician Xu, who stood to the side holding down Duke Zhenguo's limbs, stared unblinkingly at Song Jinzhao's hand movements. Both held their breath, their hearts beating wildly.","Compared to the branch inserted into the abdomen, extracting this one first was indeed much less risky. The difficult one was the one below.","As the wound was cut open, the rough head of the branch was exposed, and the flesh inside had already been slightly mangled.","Song Jinzhao said coldly, \"Silver needles.\"","Song Shixue, who had prepared them long ago, immediately handed the silver needles into her hand.","The acupoints around the collarbone, along with the shoulder blades and chest, were all sealed by Song Jinzhao with silver needles.","Gu Jupu and Imperial Physician Xu widened their eyes in shock; the bleeding around the wound had significantly decreased.","One must know that acupuncture is a very high-level and precise operation. Some acupoints cannot be easily touched, as it is extremely dangerous and can cost a person's life.","But in the hands of County Princess Linghui, how could the needle insertion be so decisive and rapid, and even stop the bleeding? They had never seen such a thing.","Song Jinzhao slowly pulled out the branch inserted above the collarbone. Grayish-black wood chips fell into the flesh, and the scalpel smoothly scooped away all the mangled, rotting flesh nearby.","Blood wandered around the wound like silk threads. When they saw Song Shixue take out a tray of threaded needles and hand it to Song Jinzhao, Gu Jupu and Imperial Physician Xu were completely astounded, their faces entirely blank.","Was she going to use thread to sew up the bleeding points? It was simply unbelievable, and this needle was not straight, but curved.","They saw Song Jinzhao pick up the curved needle with a clamp that looked like scissors.","As the silver needle, fine as a hair, passed through the bright red flesh, there was no pause, no hesitation. Song Jinzhao's movements were so fast they left an afterimage, and even breathing seemed to stop.","The bleeding points were completely covered by the rolled flesh. Song Jinzhao nimbly turned the needle head to tie a knot, and Song Shixue used scissors to cut the catgut.","Song Jinzhao put down the needle holder and turned to use tweezers to pick up gauze and absorb all the blood at the wound.","The silver needles sealing the acupoints were removed. Her gaze fell on the sutured area, and seeing that it was no longer bleeding, Song Jinzhao finally felt relieved.","Then she quickly picked up a new needle and thread to suture the outer layer of cut flesh. Crystal clear sweat beaded on her forehead. Upon seeing this, Song Shixue immediately used gauze to wipe her sweat.","In the room, apart from the sound of surgical tools being put down, Gu Jupu and Imperial Physician Xu did not even dare to breathe too loudly, afraid of affecting Song Jinzhao's hand movements.","The Chu family standing outside the room kept their eyes fixed on the door, not daring to look away. Their chests felt as if pressed by a large stone, not daring to relax, afraid that Duke Zhenguo would pass away in the next second.","Madam Zhenguo nervously clenched her hands into fists and placed them against her chest. \"Why is there no sound at all? I wonder how the situation is.\"","Chu Liuyun placed his hand on his mother's shoulder and comforted her in a hoarse voice, \"No sound is the best news.\"","Otherwise, they would have rushed out shouting that the person was dead.","Using the scalpel to cut open a slit in the abdominal wound, the exposed length made Song Jinzhao frown.","It pierced too deeply, and there were blood vessels all around. One slight misstep, and the person would be gone.","Duke Zhenguo had already lost too much blood. The speed had to be fast, and the bleeding had to be minimal, otherwise even if the branch was taken out, the person would probably have a hard time waking up.","Moreover, with such a severe injury, subsequent recovery would also be a major problem. If he couldn't survive it, everything done now would be in vain.","The depth to which the branch had pierced made Imperial Physician Xu gasp. The wounds they treated had never reached this depth.","Could he still live?","Song Shixue took out all the gauze from the chest and placed it close at hand, her heart already in her throat.","The wound was too deep; silver needles could no longer be effective for stopping the bleeding. The speed had to be fast.","The moment the branch was pulled out, fresh blood gushed forth. Gu Jupu and Imperial Physician Xu, standing to the side, subconsciously closed their eyes. Blood sprayed onto the white cotton and linen protective suits, making the scene extremely bloody.","In a split second, Song Jinzhao did not hesitate at all. She immediately put the clamp and the branch in her hands into the tray.","Her gloved right hand reached straight into the wound, her fingers quickly searching for the bleeding points inside the abdomen.","Her middle finger touched a spot where the bleeding decreased, and she immediately pressed down with a little force.","None of the four people present had a clean face, and Song Jinzhao's was especially the worst.","Blood sprayed onto her face and slid down her cheeks. Song Shixue, ignoring herself, hurriedly used gauze to wipe it.","Her thick, slightly curled eyelashes were stained with blood droplets. Song Jinzhao slightly closed her eyes to let Song Shixue wipe the blood away.","Her calm and sharp gaze fell on Duke Zhenguo; she could not let go now."]},{"number":254,"title":"Chapter 254: Pulling Someone Back from the Brink of Death","paragraphs":["Song Jinzhao took a deep breath and turned her head to look at Song Shixue.","\"Shixue, you do it. Use the smallest round needle to suture, and insert the needle right here.\"","Song Shixue swallowed nervously. Although she had practiced tens of thousands of times and had actually sutured over a hundred patients at the clinic, this was her first time suturing a blood vessel deep within an abdominal wound.","Seeing that she was a bit nervous, Song Jinzhao spoke up to comfort her, \"Just do as I say. You only need two stitches to temporarily stop the bleeding. You can do this.\"","Song Shixue took a deep breath and nodded vigorously to encourage herself.","\"Alright, I'll do the suturing.\"","Standing to the side, Imperial Physician Xu saw that the sweat on Song Jinzhao's face had already flowed down to her chin, and he thought of Song Shixue's actions just now.","He slowly picked up a piece of gauze and reached out to wipe the sweat from Song Jinzhao's face. Song Jinzhao glanced at him but did not refuse.","Gu Jupu stared at his subordinate's actions in astonishment. He learned so quickly, which made him feel like he was just standing there idle and redundant.","Song Shixue's movements were much slower. She inserted the needle with extreme caution, terrified of piercing the wrong spot.","\"Angle it upwards a bit more, and tighten the thread just a little bit.\"","Song Jinzhao's brows were tightly furrowed, her eyes slightly narrowed, her focus locked on the needle tip, not daring to shift even a fraction.","Song Shixue emptied her mind, focusing all her attention on her hands. The only thing she could hear was Song Jinzhao's commanding voice.","As the needle and thread wove through the blood vessel, after a few stitches, Song Shixue looked up uncertainly at Song Jinzhao. \"Sister, I'm done.\"","\"Stay still.\" Song Jinzhao slowly moved her fingers away. The massive spurting of blood did not resume.","She quickly withdrew her hands from the abdomen, picked up the prepared needle holder from the tray, clamped the smallest round needle, and reinforced the area where Song Shixue had just sutured.","From inserting the needle to finishing the stitch, it only took ten seconds. In the few blinks of an eye from Gu Jupu, Song Jinzhao was already done.","\"Knot, cut the thread, let go.\"","Receiving the order, Song Shixue immediately continued the finishing movements in her hands. It wasn't until she placed the needle holder back on the tray that she realized her entire back was soaked in sweat.","The chill seeped through her skin into her flesh, even making her bones feel cold.","Outside the Duke Zhenguo's mansion, a rather plain carriage stopped at the entrance. Xiao Rongyan, dressed in a white satin robe, stepped down from the carriage with complex feelings.","Deep down, he really didn't want to come, but he had no choice.","Duke Zhenguo had died saving him. If he didn't show up, the Chu family would surely harbor resentment. If Duke of Qing defected to Prince Qi because of this, it would be extremely disadvantageous to him.","Looking at the giant plaque hanging in the center of the Duke Zhenguo's mansion gates, Xiao Rongyan took a deep breath and stepped up the stairs.","The worry-filled gatekeeper looked up and saw Xiao Rongyan arriving, hastily kneeling to pay his respects. \"Greetings to His Highness Prince Ying.\"","Xiao Rongyan deliberately lowered his eyes, wearing a slightly sorrowful expression, his voice carrying a perfectly measured trace of hoarseness.","\"Has Duke Zhenguo passed away? I am here to offer my condolences.\"","The gatekeeper, who had retired from the military camp due to old age, looked up at Xiao Rongyan in shock. He gritted his back teeth, his cheeks trembling with anger.","The Duke wasn't dead yet, what condolences was he offering?","The returning soldiers had said that if Prince Ying hadn't insisted on going hunting, the Duke wouldn't have met with an accident at all. It was all his fault.","Now, coming to mourn before the person was even dead, was he hoping the Duke would die sooner?","Mindful of the other party's status, the gatekeeper clenched his hands hidden in his sleeves, his nails digging into his palms as he forcefully suppressed the anger in his chest.","He lowered his head and said through gritted teeth, \"To answer His Highness Prince Ying, my master is not dead yet.\"","The moisture in Xiao Rongyan's eyes instantly dried up. He stared in astonishment at the top of the gatekeeper's head. \"Didn't they say he wouldn't last an hour and that funeral arrangements were already being prepared?\"","The gatekeeper closed his eyes and suppressed his anger once more. \"The Young Duke went to the county princess's manor to invite County Princess Linghui over to save him. He is currently being treated.\"","Xiao Rongyan was stunned for quite a while, his tone rising in disbelief. \"Song Jinzhao?\"","The gatekeeper nodded.","Xiao Rongyan blinked, quickly bypassed the gatekeeper, and walked inside. When he was led into the courtyard where Duke Zhenguo was located, he found it packed with people.","Looking up at the room, the doors were tightly shut, and nothing could be seen.","Whether it was the Chu family or the imperial physicians, everyone's attention was entirely on the room at this moment. The first to notice Xiao Rongyan's entrance was actually a maid standing in the courtyard. Only after hearing the noise did the others turn around and see him.","Chu Liuyun's pitch-black pupils swept over the spotless white satin robe on his body, the coldness in his eyes deepening.","My father is lying in bed with his life hanging in the balance, yet you know how to enjoy yourself, even taking the time to change into a fresh set of clothes before coming over.","Standing in the snow for just a short while, you felt cold and got frozen, didn't you!","Xiao Rongyan drooped his brows and eyes, walking up to Chu Liuyun with a worried expression and asked, \"I heard that County Princess Linghui is currently treating Duke Zhenguo. How is the situation?\"","\"Still in surgery.\" Chu Liuyun turned indifferently to look at the room's door, dropping these words and ignoring him thereafter.","Seeing his cold attitude, Xiao Rongyan felt slighted, furrowing his brows in dissatisfaction.","Even if Duke Zhenguo was injured because he saved him, the thunder and the rain are all the grace of the sovereign. Trading a subject's life for a prince's life should make the Chu family feel honored. Harboring resentment—did they intend to disrespect the royal family?","\"Imperial Physician Long, you tell me.\"","The imperial physician standing in the crowd closed his eyes in agony and stepped forward. Why did he have to be the one called out? What terrible luck.","\"County Princess Linghui is going to cut open his abdomen to remove the tree branch lodged in Duke Zhenguo's body. Director Gu and Imperial Physician Xu are standing guard inside. No one else is allowed to enter, so this humble official does not know the current situation either.\"","Xiao Rongyan said displeased, \"Can Song Jinzhao's medical skills really surpass those of the imperial physicians from the Imperial Hospital? I think she has too high an opinion of herself and is treating Duke Zhenguo's life as a joke.\"","\"...\"","Everyone kept their mouths shut tight, not knowing how to respond. Even the imperial physicians who initially questioned Song Jinzhao's medical skills did not speak up to agree.","It was a fact that the imperial physicians couldn't cure Ye Liangyu's leg, but County Princess Linghui had cured it.","It was also a fact that the entire Imperial Hospital had issued a death notice for Duke Zhenguo, yet County Princess Linghui said there was hope to save him.","Regardless of what the final outcome would be, at least after so long, Duke Zhenguo was still alive. Being treated meant there was still hope, which was definitely better than not treating him and letting him die.","They were saving a life inside. Saying Song Jinzhao's medical skills were lacking now was already too late. They could only leave it to fate and pin all their hopes on her.","With no one answering, Xiao Rongyan grew even angrier. Did they even respect him as a prince at all? Even the imperial physicians were ignoring him.","Inside the room, Song Jinzhao sutured the finger-deep wound layer by layer. Gu Jupu asked uncertainly, \"County Princess, if the wounds inside the flesh are sewn up with thread, will we have to use a knife to cut open the outer flesh to remove the inner threads after the wound heals?\"","Song Jinzhao's hand movements did not stop as she calmly replied, \"No need. I am using catgut sutures made from sheep intestines. They can be absorbed naturally and do not need to be removed.\"","Gu Jupu let out a soft sound of sudden realization, though he blinked, still a bit confused.","Faced with this novel surgery today, there were many things he hadn't figured out. With a thousand questions in his mind, he didn't even know which one to ponder first.","Even when the outermost flesh was completely sutured, Song Jinzhao's expression did not show the slightest sign of relaxation.","This was only passing the first hurdle.","Next was whether the patient could wake up or not.","Would the wound become infected?","Would being unconscious from blood loss for so long leave any lasting complications?","These were all still unknowns, and it was too early to let my guard down."]},{"number":255,"title":"Chapter 255: The Next Two Days Are Critical","paragraphs":["Song Jinzhao had barely opened the door a crack when the Chu family swarmed around her.","Dowager Duchess Chu's hand trembled violently as she gripped Song Jinzhao's sleeve. County Princess, how is my son?","Pleading, trembling, tear-filled, and on the verge of shattering, numerous gazes focused on Song Jinzhao's face like magnets.","She opened the door halfway, stepped over the threshold, and closed it behind her.","The branches have been extracted, and the wounds are sutured. He has passed the first hurdle for now. It all depends on whether Duke Zhenguo can survive the next two days.","Hearing this, Dowager Duchess Chu relaxed and collapsed against her momo, while the Duchess of Zhenguo immediately moved to push the door open and go in.","It wasn't just her; the dozen or so imperial physicians standing behind them all wanted to go in as well.","Did County Princess Linghui really cure Duke Zhenguo?","How did she do it?","What was his current condition?","As medical practitioners, they were incredibly curious about all of this.","Song Jinzhao reached out to stop them, warning sternly, Don't let too many people in. Stand outside the curtain and don't get too close. Your bodies carry too many bacteria and haven't been disinfected.","Although they didn't understand what Song Jinzhao meant by bacteria and not being disinfected, the Chu family nodded vigorously in agreement.","We promise to only look from outside the curtain and absolutely will not go near.","Watching the family of three go in and close the door again, the people from the Imperial Academy of Medicine looked at each other in dismay. For a moment, no one dared to step forward and say they wanted to go in too.","Through the gap in the curtain, Chu Liuyun stared intently at Duke Zhenguo lying on the bed, his eyes slightly wet and his throat choked with emotion.","Even the strongest man could not bear the passing of his parents. For an entire afternoon, the usually resilient Chu Liuyun had been absolutely terrified.","Song Shixue washed all the tools clean in hot water and put them all into the box. This would have to do for now; they would need to be properly sterilized again once they returned.","In several trays lay pieces of bright red, excised flesh, along with clumps of blood-soaked gauze.","Xiao Rongyan furrowed his brows, staring fixedly at Song Jinzhao as he questioned her, County Princess Linghui, is Duke Zhenguo completely out of danger?","Song Jinzhao raised her eyebrows in surprise. Why was Prince Ying here?","Not at all. Successfully extracting the branches and suturing the wounds was merely the first hurdle.","Duke Zhenguo was too severely injured, and it dragged on for too long. His wounds are very deep, coupled with excessive blood loss. The next two days will be the most critical period, and the patient could fall into critical condition at any moment.","Seeing Gu Jupu and Imperial Physician Xu come out, the dozen or so imperial physicians standing in the courtyard immediately surrounded them, asking exactly how Song Jinzhao had treated him just now.","Chu Liuyun stepped out of the room and bowed to Song Jinzhao. Thank you, County Princess, for stepping in to save him. I will never forget this life-saving grace.","You just mentioned that my father will be in great danger over the next two days. I implore the County Princess to temporarily reside in our manor to prevent any unforeseen circumstances.","Song Jinzhao replied, It is only right. I hadn't planned on leaving either.","Having finally finished the surgery, she certainly couldn't leave before the patient woke up. Otherwise, if something happened, she wouldn't be able to make it back in time.","I need paper and a brush to write some prescriptions. There are also some items and medicinal herbs that my younger sister needs to fetch from our manor.","Chu Liuyun nodded hurriedly. I will immediately arrange for a driver to escort Second Miss Song back.","The Duchess of Zhenguo, tear tracks still on her cheeks, walked out clutching her handkerchief to thank Song Jinzhao. Thank you, County Princess, for saving his life.","She turned her head and instructed the momo beside her, Quickly, bring paper and a brush. Arrange for someone to tidy up the adjacent room for the County Princess to stay in temporarily. Use the best of everything.","Under the peach tree to the east, Imperial Physician Xu was speaking animatedly, gesturing wildly.","It was as if he had performed the surgery himself, and his words were filled with reverence for Song Jinzhao.","I have never seen anyone use a curved needle to suture wounds, let alone suture inside the abdomen.","Those blood vessels were so thin I couldn't even see them clearly, yet she was stitching them together with needle and thread. If I hadn't seen it with my own eyes, I wouldn't have believed it.","Seeing Imperial Physician Xu praise Song Jinzhao to the high heavens, the others didn't know whether to believe it or not for a moment.","Just as they were about to confirm with Gu Jupu, they saw him walk quickly to Song Jinzhao's side with a look of longing, following her into the next room.","When Song Jinzhao took up her brush, Gu Jupu watched from beside the table, his eyes constantly stealing glances.","Was this still the highly respected and highly skilled Director Gu of the Imperial Academy of Medicine?","Song Jinzhao knew Gu Jupu was peeking, but she didn't intend to hide it from him. She quickly wrote down several prescriptions on the paper and handed them to Song Shixue.","When you get back, gather the medicine according to the prescriptions and have the servants of Duke Zhenguo's manor bring them over. Older sister won't be going back today.","Song Shixue took the prescriptions and nodded. I will pack some clothes and have them brought over as well. With brother and me at home, you don't need to worry, older sister.","Chu Liuyun arranged for his personal guard to drive the carriage and take Song Shixue back.","He looked at the courtyard full of imperial physicians and breathed a sigh of relief. It is getting late. Thank you all for your trouble today.","The underlying message was that they could leave.","The crowd exchanged glances, somewhat reluctant to leave. They wanted to take a look at Duke Zhenguo but were afraid Chu Liuyun would not agree.","The tactful Gu Jupu cupped his hands toward Chu Liuyun. I still need to return to the palace to report to the Emperor, so I will take my leave first.","If there is any need later, the young duke can send someone to the Imperial Academy of Medicine at any time.","Chu Liuyun twitched the corners of his mouth in a forced smile. Thank you for your hard work today, Director Gu.","Completely ignored, Xiao Rongyan saw that Gu Jupu was returning to the palace to report. A dark glint flashed in his eyes as he greeted Chu Liuyun and left.","The crowded courtyard finally quieted down a bit.","Suddenly relaxing after an enormous drain on her energy, Dowager Duchess Chu felt dizzy, sleepy, and exhausted. Chu Liuyun had to persuade her for a long time before she agreed to rest in the adjacent room.","Before closing her eyes, Dowager Duchess Chu tightly grasped Chu Liuyun's hand and instructed him word by word, If anything happens to your father, you must wake me up immediately.","Chu Liuyun squeezed her hand, constantly reassuring her, Rest assured, Grandmother. With the County Princess here, Father will be fine.","Upon returning to the palace, Gu Jupu immediately requested an audience with the Emperor. Xiao Chengjing stared at the posthumous edict on the dragon desk, its ink not yet fully dry, and sighed softly.","Let him in.","Gu Jupu walked to the dragon desk and knelt.","Reporting to Your Majesty, County Princess Linghui has extracted the two branches pierced into Duke Zhenguo's body. Duke Zhenguo's life is temporarily preserved.","Xiao Chengjing blinked in stunned silence. Preserved? He had thought the man was already dead.","After recovering his wits, he confirmed, County Princess Linghui saved Duke Zhenguo?","Gu Jupu nodded. This humble minister is incompetent and was helpless regarding Duke Zhenguo's injuries. At the critical moment, Duke Qing went to the County Princess's estate and invited County Princess Linghui over. Only then was Duke Zhenguo's life saved.","However, the County Princess said that removing the branches was only the first step. If Duke Zhenguo fails to pull through the next few days, he may still lose his life.","The County Princess is keeping watch at Duke Zhenguo's manor. Seeing that this humble minister could be of no help, I had no choice but to return first.","Breathing a sigh of relief, Xiao Chengjing silently rolled up the imperial edict on the table. According to what you're saying, County Princess Linghui's medical skills are even better than yours, the Director of the Imperial Academy of Medicine?","Gu Jupu sighed helplessly and said with great shame, The County Princess possesses miraculous skills. Her medical expertise far surpasses that of this humble minister. I am truly ashamed of my inferiority."]},{"number":256,"title":"Chapter 256: Sowing Discord, Fever Strikes at Midnight","paragraphs":["Gu Jupu had barely stepped out of the imperial study when Prince Ying arrived.","\"Imperial Father, I have already visited the Duke Zhenguo's estate. Duke Zhenguo's life has been temporarily saved.\"","Xiao Chengjing gave a careless hum. \"I already know. I didn't expect County Princess Linghui's medical skills to truly surpass those of the imperial physicians. It is a great fortune that Duke Zhenguo could be saved.\"","Xiao Rongyan lowered his eyes to look at the carved dragon patterns on the imperial desk, his long, narrow eyelashes completely concealing the calculation in his eyes.","\"If it weren't for saving me, Duke Zhenguo wouldn't have been injured. Had I known an accident would occur, I never would have gone to the western suburban military camp in the first place.\"","Xiao Chengjing frowned in disapproval. \"As a prince, it is only right that he saves you when you encounter danger. It is Duke Zhenguo's duty as a subject.\"","\"Sending you to the western suburban camp was my arrangement. There are not many military generals in the court nowadays. In future times of war, if a prince can personally take the battlefield, it will surely boost military morale and defeat strong enemies in one fell swoop. You ought to learn well.\"","Xiao Rongyan nodded in agreement with a hint of worry in his expression. \"What Imperial Father says is correct. I also wish to expand the territories for you in the future, it's just...\"","Xiao Chengjing raised his eyes in confusion. \"Just what?\"","Xiao Rongyan lowered his head in feigned disappointment. \"When I went to visit the Duke Zhenguo's estate just now, the Duke of Qing's attitude was very cold. He must be displeased; after all, Duke Zhenguo was injured to save me.\"","\"But it doesn't matter. Over the next few days, I plan to visit daily. Once Duke Zhenguo's injuries heal, I will bring more gifts to thank them, and surely it will be fine.\"","Xiao Chengjing stared grimly at the closed posthumous edict on the table. After a long while, he said in a low voice, \"You may step down first.\"","Xiao Chengjing valued the fact that the Duke Zhenguo's estate favored neither Prince Qi nor Prince Ying, but he did not want them to despise imperial power and breed rebellious intentions.","In his view, even if Duke Zhenguo truly died to save Prince Ying, the Chu family must not show the slightest hint of dissatisfaction.","Sensing the dissatisfaction in the Emperor's tone, Xiao Rongyan, with his head still bowed, curled his lips into a smug smile. \"I will take my leave.\"","The news that Duke Zhenguo's life was hanging by a thread after saving Prince Ying, that the entire Imperial Hospital was helpless, and that County Princess Linghui was finally invited to treat him, quickly spread among the nobles and ministers.","Everyone's attention suddenly fell entirely on the Duke Zhenguo's estate.","What was Duke Zhenguo's condition? Was he alive or dead? Could he actually survive?","But it was already late, and it was no longer appropriate to visit.","They could only toss and turn all night with intense curiosity, until they were finally so exhausted that they were forced to fall asleep.","Prince Qi's Manor.","Upon hearing the news, Xiao Rongche gnashed his teeth and pounded his thigh. \"Why did Duke Zhenguo have to save Prince Ying? Even if he didn't die, being crippled would have been fine. What a pity!\"","Gu Qishan smiled calmly and said, \"Your Highness, this accident can be considered a good thing for us.\"","Xiao Rongche looked at Gu Qishan.","Gu Qishan continued, \"Little Mao Mountain, where the avalanche occurred, is very far from the official road. Logically, even if an avalanche happened, it wouldn't reach the official road. So, I went to ask the accompanying soldiers.\"","\"It turns out that on the way back to the city, Prince Ying insisted on hunting and rushed into the fir forest near the foot of Little Mao Mountain. The accompanying soldiers also said that Duke Zhenguo had tried to persuade Prince Ying several times not to go in, because there were steep slopes and cliffs near the fir forest, and the thick snow made it easy to step into nothingness. It was too dangerous, but Prince Ying stubbornly refused to listen.\"","\"In the end, the horses were spooked. To save Prince Ying, Duke Zhenguo fell down the steep slope with him. Now Prince Ying is completely fine, while Duke Zhenguo is severely injured and his life is still uncertain. The Duke of Qing must absolutely hate Prince Ying by now. This is definitely a tremendous boon for us.\"","Xiao Rongche's displeased brows suddenly relaxed, his eyes shining. \"If that's the case, wouldn't it be even more advantageous for us if Duke Zhenguo died?\"","\"...\"","Gu Qishan didn't know how to respond for a moment.","Even so, if he could avoid dying, it would be better not to die.","Duke Zhenguo had spent his life in the military, dedicating himself entirely to the court. It would truly be a pity if he died just to save Prince Ying.","When the guards who escorted Song Shixue home returned, they brought back another large chest.","Except for two sets of a change of clothes, the rest was entirely medicine.","Song Jinzhao called the maids guarding the door and handed them three packets of Chinese medicine, saying, \"Boil these three medicine packets separately and simmer them over low heat, so they can be drunk immediately when needed. The prescriptions are placed next to them; make sure not to mix them up.\"","The maids solemnly took the medicine packets and curtsied to Song Jinzhao. \"Yes, we will go brew them immediately.\"","Every half hour, Song Jinzhao would go next door to check on Duke Zhenguo's condition.","Perhaps because he hadn't woken up yet, the dinner at the Duke's estate tasted somewhat bitter.","Approaching the hour of Hai, a high fever developed, just as expected.","Song Jinzhao ordered the maid, \"Bring over the fever-reducing decoction.\"","The maid guarding the door widened her eyes and quickly turned to fetch the medicine.","Chu Liuyun, who had been standing outside the door and hadn't dared to sleep, looked anxiously at Duke Zhenguo lying on the bed. \"What's wrong? Has his condition worsened?\"","Song Jinzhao said, \"He has a fever, and his temperature is rising fast. We need to bring the fever down immediately.\"","Hearing the voices, Madam Duke Zhenguo ran out anxiously from the room on the right, staring fixedly at Song Jinzhao like a drowning person clutching a piece of driftwood.","\"How is he? Has the Duke woken up?\"","Song Jinzhao shook her head. \"He hasn't woken up. He has developed a fever.\"","It was as if a bolt of lightning struck right before Madam Duke Zhenguo's eyes, and she stumbled backward weakly.","A fever was definitely not a good sign.","The maid walked over quickly with a tray. Song Jinzhao took the medicine and tested the temperature of the bowl's surface.","There was a slight burning sensation on her fingertips; the temperature was just right.","After pouring the strong medicine down his throat, Song Jinzhao lifted the curtain and instructed the maid, \"Go prepare wet towels and ice.\"","Once the items were brought over, Madam Duke Zhenguo said to the maid, \"I'll do it.\"","She rolled up her sleeves and washed her hands repeatedly with hot water. The scorching heat she felt upon touching him made her eyes redden once again.","Taking a deep breath to hold back her tears, she carefully avoided the wound on Duke Zhenguo's forehead and wiped him with the towel wrapped around the ice.","Song Jinzhao sat quietly on a stool watching, feeling somewhat moved.","In this era, practicing monogamy was truly rare. The Chu family was no ordinary household, and yet, with only one heir, Chu Liuyun, they had not taken any concubines. The couple must be deeply in love.","After two hours, his temperature gradually began to drop, and everyone finally felt a sense of relief.","Song Jinzhao returned to the next room to rest, but Madam Duke Zhenguo could no longer sleep.","She and Chu Liuyun sat outside the curtain keeping watch, not daring to close their eyes as they guarded Duke Zhenguo.","This night felt longer than ever before. It wasn't until the sky began to lighten slightly that a wave of exhaustion washed over them, their bodies reaching the absolute limits of fatigue.","As long as Duke Zhenguo remained unconscious, the Chu family could not set their hearts at ease.","During the morning court assembly, many officials were distracted, wondering about Duke Zhenguo's current condition. There had been no news at all.","After discussing a few state affairs and seeing that no one else had memorials to present, the Emperor simply concluded the morning court.","On the way back to the Imperial Study, Xiao Chengjing instructed the chief eunuch, \"Have Gu Jupu go and keep watch at Duke Zhenguo's estate. If there is any news, report back to me immediately.\"","\"Yes, Your Majesty. This servant will see to it right away.\""]},{"number":257,"title":"Chapter 257: The Lump on the Back of the Head","paragraphs":["Looking at the Duke of Zhenguo, who lay on the bed and still had not woken up, the worry in Song Jinzhao's eyes grew deeper.","The Chu family's anxious gazes darted back and forth between her and the Duke of Zhenguo, their hearts filled with extreme unease.","Why had he not woken up yet? Could something have gone wrong?","Song Jinzhao leaned over and lifted the Duke of Zhenguo's eyelids, discovering a slight asymmetry in the size of his pupils. This had not been there an hour ago. Although the difference was subtle, it was already a dangerous signal.","She removed the gauze on his forehead. The wound was very shallow, and the surrounding skin was smooth; it shouldn't be affecting him.","After pondering for a few seconds, she turned her gaze to the Duke of Zhenguo's head. Reaching out, she parted his thick hair, her eyes sweeping over every inch of his scalp.","It wasn't until her hand touched the back of his head, which was supported by the pillow, that she felt a slightly bulging, elastic sensation with a hint of fluctuation.","The heart that Song Jinzhao had been keeping suspended finally settled down.","She crouched down and slightly lifted the Duke of Zhenguo's head. Bring me a candle.","Just as the maid was about to turn around, Chu Liuyun took two large strides over, lifted the lampshade on the table, and handed the candle right to Song Jinzhao's hand.","The scalp wasn't broken, but it was already swollen. Judging from the condition of his pupils, a blood clot must be blocking the blood vessels in his brain.","How is it? The crowd's gazes followed the angle of Song Jinzhao's line of sight.","Because the distance was too far and Song Jinzhao was blocking the way, they could not see the lump on the back of the Duke of Zhenguo's head. They could only guess from Song Jinzhao's expression that something might have gone wrong.","Song Jinzhao slowly lowered the Duke of Zhenguo's head and stood up with the candle in hand. He must have hit the back of his head when he fell down the steep slope. It looked fine yesterday, but now it has swollen up. Blood clots are blocking the blood vessels in his brain. The blood circulation is poor, so we must remove the stasis and stop the bleeding as soon as possible.","She lifted the curtain, walked to the next room, opened her medical box, and took out four or five pre-packaged herbal bundles to mix a new prescription.","The hearts of the Chu family rose and fell with trembling. In their eyes, besides worry, there was also the helplessness of not knowing what to do.","At this moment, the butler walked quickly to the door of the room. Seeing the three masters standing silently in place without moving, his expression immediately tightened.","Young Master, many people have come outside the gates wanting to visit the Duke. The Ministry of Personnel, the Ministry of War, the Ministry of Revenue, and even Prince Qi have sent people.","Chu Liuyun's cold gaze shot straight at the butler. His voice was not loud, but it was as sharp as a bladed tip.","Before my father wakes up, the manor's doors are closed to all guests. We will see no one.","The butler nodded heavily. Yes, this servant will go and send them away right now.","The officials from the Six Ministries, along with the butler from Prince Qi's estate, were persuaded to leave before they even entered the gates of the Duke of Zhenguo's estate.","Sitting in his carriage blowing his nose, Xiao Rongyan looked at the tightly closed doors of the Duke of Zhenguo's estate and ordered his guards to go knock.","His trusted guard spoke up hesitantly, Your Highness, the Duke of Zhenguo's estate has closed its doors to guests. Even the many officials from the Six Ministries couldn't get in. I'm afraid the Duke of Qing won't see you either.","Xiao Rongyan gathered his outer robe around himself. I don't care whether I can see him or not, as long as the Duke of Qing and my imperial father know that I have been here.","When the butler heard that Prince Ying had come, the anger in his heart flared even higher. Yesterday, the gatekeeper had already told him about Xiao Rongyan coming to mourn.","His own Duke had risked his life to save him, yet this man had come to mourn before even figuring out the situation. Such behavior was truly chilling; he had saved him for nothing.","We will not see him. The Young Master has spoken: our doors are closed to guests, and we are seeing no one.","The gatekeeper opened the side door just a crack and spoke coldly to the guard, The Duke has not awakened. My Young Master and Madam truly do not have the energy to entertain guests. Please ask His Highness Prince Ying to come back another day.","Having received the message, the guard immediately walked back to the carriage and told Xiao Rongyan.","Watching the carriage turn around and leave, the gatekeeper hatefully spat on the ground.","He didn't even get out of the carriage. You might as well just play dead.","Song Jinzhao personally kept an eye on the medicine pot. As soon as the medicine was brewed, she immediately brought it over and fed it to the Duke of Zhenguo.","Not long after, the butler came over with a dejected face to report, Young Master, Director Gu from the Imperial Academy of Medicine has arrived, saying he came under imperial orders to help.","Chu Liuyun closed his eyes in frustration and let out a deep breath. Let him in.","Gu Jupu also knew that he wouldn't be of much use coming here, so he simply took over the job of brewing the medicine.","Inside Biluo Palace, Princess Yongjia, who hadn't slept well all night, looked anxiously at the maid walking in. How is it? Has the Duke of Zhenguo woken up yet?","The maid shook her head. No. The Duke of Qing has ordered the doors closed to guests and is seeing no one. The situation is probably not very good.","Xiao Yongjia's slender shoulders slumped in disappointment. No, I need to go to Baohua Hall and burn some more Buddhist scriptures.","Yesterday they thought he was certain to die. Now that there was finally hope, nothing must go wrong.","At the County Princess's Manor, Song Anhao, who didn't have classes today, pouted unhappily and asked Song Shixue, Second Sister, when is Big Sister coming back?","Song Shixue, who was currently recording the process of yesterday's surgery, looked up. It might be another two days. The uncle who got hurt hasn't woken up yet.","Song Anhao disappointedly buried his head into Xuetuan's warm belly and rubbed against it.","Song Qiming, who had finally gotten a day off for his monthly break, hadn't gone out today either. Walking in and seeing his youngest brother wiggling on Xuetuan like a worm, he couldn't help but say, A gentleman should stand like a pine, sit like a bell, walk like the wind, and lie like a bow. What does it look like, twisting around like this? You should start practicing martial arts with us some other day.","Song Anhao lifted his head and said righteously, I am a child right now, not a gentleman. Brother, you are sounding more and more like Mr. Ye.","Having been retorted to, Song Qiming sat down helplessly and pulled Song Anhao onto his lap. It's not that I'm becoming more like my teacher; it's just how scholars are.","You'll know once you enter the academy to study in the future. If your back curves even a little, the teacher will hit you with a board, hitting you until you can't bend down anymore.","Song Anhao, who had never been beaten, stared at Song Qiming with wide eyes. After pondering with terrified eyes for a long time, he jumped off Song Qiming's lap and drilled into Song Shixue's embrace, saying muffledly, Then I just won't study.","Song Qiming smiled and played with the small round pom-pom on his hat. Not studying definitely won't do. The teacher even said that you could be the top scholar in the future.","Song Anhao awkwardly kicked his two legs, looking like a little turtle that couldn't climb onto a rock to sunbathe.","A servant walked into the room, bowed, and reported, Answering the Young Master, Young Master Dongfang is visiting outside the manor, saying he has come to look for you.","Song Qiming stood up in surprise and straightened his clothes. Didn't I already send someone to tell him that I wasn't going to the poetry club today? Why did he still come over?","Waiting in the main hall, Dongfang Yukun was drinking the milk tea brought up by the servants with a look of utter satisfaction. He had to admit that the tea drinks at the County Princess's Manor were truly unique and sweetly delicious.","After walking in, Song Qiming asked in confusion, Why are you here? Didn't you go to the poetry club?","Dongfang Yukun downed his cup in one gulp and signaled the maid to pour another. It's no fun going alone if you're not there.","Song Qiming was puzzled. Didn't Gao Li go?","Dongfang Yukun spread his hands and looked up at the ceiling. They don't have the skill to compete in poetry with me. The feeling of being invincible is just this lonely.","Song Qiming rolled his eyes at the ceiling speechlessly. Once Cui Zhengyang from Jiangnan enters the capital, you won't be this lonely anymore.","The corners of Dongfang Yukun's mouth froze. Upon hearing this name, he suddenly felt that the milk tea in his hand wasn't as sweet as it was a moment ago.","\"Ever since you found out about Cui Zhengyang, you have been constantly bringing him up. Don't forget, even if he shows up, he will still be nothing more than my defeated opponent.\"","Song Qiming picked up the pearl milk tea that the maid had just poured and took a sip.","\"If I didn't bring him up, your ego would soar to the heavens. Even as a defeated opponent, he is the kind that forces you to stay vigilant. If he surpasses you in this upcoming metropolitan examination, the throne for the most handsome man in the Dongzhao Kingdom will have to change owners.\"","Dongfang Yukun fiercely chewed the tapioca pearls in his mouth to a pulp. \"He can dream about surpassing me in his next life.\""]},{"number":258,"title":"Chapter 258: Finally Awake","paragraphs":["Dongfang Yukun changed the subject, his eyes shifting as he looked at Song Qiming. \"How is Duke Zhenguo? Rumor outside has it that he's dying.\"","Song Qiming shook his head. \"My elder sister hasn't returned yet. I heard from my younger sister that the surgery was a success, but because Duke Zhenguo was injured too severely, the next few days will be critical. If he makes it through, he'll be fine; if not, it's hard to say.\"","Dongfang Yukun asked in confusion, \"What is this surgery you speak of? I heard the entire Imperial Academy of Medicine was helpless, and in the end, your sister saved him.\"","Song Qiming furrowed his brows, looking a bit troubled. \"My elder sister taught all her medical skills to my younger sister, so I don't know much about it. It seems they use a knife to cut open the stomach, take out the branches that pierced inside, and then sew it up with a needle and thread.\"","Dongfang Yukun had never killed anyone and couldn't quite imagine the scene.","\"I heard before that Vice Censor-in-Chief Ye's legs were cured by County Princess Linghui. I didn't expect her to be this incredible.\"","\"The imperial physicians all said Duke Zhenguo could live for an hour at most. The fact that the County Princess has kept him alive until now is already amazing.\"","He chuckled playfully, \"If Duke Zhenguo truly recovers, the threshold of the County Princess's estate will probably be trampled flat by all the nobles in the capital.\"","Song Qiming replied, \"It's not like everyone gets rare and complicated diseases. There are so many doctors in the capital, and imperial physicians in the palace. People wouldn't seek my sister out for minor illnesses or pains. If everything were left to her alone, she wouldn't be able to handle it all.\"","Dongfang Yukun nodded slightly. \"You have a point. After all, given County Princess Linghui's status, ordinary people wouldn't be able to invite her anyway.\"","The main gates of Duke Zhenguo's estate remained closed throughout the entire day, and the maids and servants inside kept as quiet as winter cicadas.","Just as the sky grew dark and everyone in the estate began to have dinner, Duke Zhenguo, who was lying on the bed, slowly opened his eyes.","His wife, who had been guarding by his side, threw herself at the bedside in pleasant surprise and cried out, \"Husband, you're awake!\"","Chu Liuyun, who was standing in the outer room, quickly lifted the curtain and ran in. Their eyes met, and the heavy stone hanging in his heart was finally lifted.","Duke Zhenguo had just tried to turn his head when he realized his entire body ached.","The flesh on his neck and stomach felt a sharp, twisting pain as if pierced by knife tips. The agony contorted his features and made him almost bite through the roots of his teeth.","\"Don't move, be careful not to tear your wounds open,\" Song Jinzhao said as she walked in and pressed down on his shoulder.","\"The effects of the anesthesia have mostly worn off over the night. I can apply a little more to the surface wounds, but you'll just have to endure the pain deep inside your flesh.\"","Duke Zhenguo opened his eyes in pain. After seeing clearly that it was Song Jinzhao, he asked in confusion, \"Why is the County Princess here?\"","His wife carefully and gently placed her hand over the back of Duke Zhenguo's hand.","Choking back sobs, she explained, \"The County Princess saved you. Yesterday, many people from the Imperial Academy of Medicine came and said you couldn't be saved. Thank goodness Liuyun eventually invited County Princess Linghui over, which managed to save your life.\"","Duke Zhenguo hadn't expected Song Jinzhao to be the one who saved him. When he was delirious yesterday, he vaguely heard many people talking, but he couldn't open his eyes and didn't know exactly what was happening in his daze. Later, he had passed out completely.","\"Thank you, County Princess, for saving my life. My whole body is hurting terribly right now, what is going on?\"","Song Jinzhao reached out to check his pupils. \"I made two incisions, one in your supraclavicular fossa and one on your abdomen. The internal wounds haven't healed yet, so it will keep hurting and you'll have to bear with it.\"","\"Your forehead is cut, the back of your head was bleeding, the muscles in your left hand are severely strained, and your shoulder has a minor dislocation. Of course it hurts everywhere.\"","The more he listened, the dizzier Duke Zhenguo felt. Thinking of the kick he received from Prince Ying, and how the prince had ignored his warnings to hunt the stag, which ultimately led to this situation, he grew even angrier.","Seeing his breathing become rapid, Song Jinzhao reminded him, \"The next few days are crucial. You need to rest and recover properly now. Speak less and don't move around. If your wounds tear open and bleed, it will be disastrous.\"","Waking up meant that his bodily functions were operating normally. As for wound infections during the upcoming recovery period, they would have to be suppressed with medicine.","Before the sky turned completely dark, Gu Jupu rushed to the palace in a horse carriage.","\"Your Majesty, Duke Zhenguo has awakened.\" After entering the imperial study, he joyfully knelt down and bowed to the Emperor.","Xiao Chengjing straightened his back, not expecting that Song Jinzhao had actually managed to save Duke Zhenguo.","\"How is Duke Zhenguo's condition now?\"","Gu Jupu replied, \"The County Princess said the next few days are critical, but in my humble opinion, there is basically no major issue left. His life is definitely secure.\"","Xiao Chengjing nodded. \"You have worked hard these past two days. You may step down.\"","Gu Jupu had just left the imperial study when someone blocked his path.","With a face full of surprise, he bowed to the suddenly appearing Xiao Yongjia. \"It is getting late, why is Her Highness the Princess here?\"","Xiao Yongjia looked at Gu Jupu and said, \"I just wanted to ask you how Duke Zhenguo is doing now.\"","Duke Zhenguo's estate was closed to guests, so she couldn't get any news. Knowing that Gu Jupu was entering the palace, she immediately ran over from Baohua Hall to intercept him.","Gu Jupu let out a sigh of relief, a smile appearing on his face. \"Please rest assured, Your Highness. Duke Zhenguo has already awakened.\"","Xiao Yongjia let out a deep sigh of relief, the tension she had maintained all day finally relaxing.","\"It's good that he is awake. Buddha bless him, he is finally alright.\"","Early the next morning, when Song Jinzhao finally left Duke Zhenguo's estate, the news spread rapidly through the city as if it had grown wings.","However, Duke Zhenguo's estate still kept its doors closed to guests, with only the servants in charge of the kitchen going in and out through the back door.","Using his father's severe illness as a reason, Chu Liuyun requested a half-month leave from the Ministry of Personnel all at once. Combined with the New Year court recess, he wouldn't have to attend the morning court for over twenty days.","Just when everyone thought the matter would pass like this, news began to spread through the city that Prince Ying's stubborn insistence on hunting an elk had caused Duke Zhenguo to nearly lose his life while trying to save him.","Inside the imperial study, Xiao Chengjing smashed a memorial onto Prince Ying's head.","\"What did you tell me? Something about encountering a leopard that startled your horse and made you fall off! It's clear that you refused to listen to advice and insisted on shooting some elk. Go outside and listen to how the commoners in the capital are talking about you. You've completely disgraced me!\"","Kneeling on the ground, Xiao Rongyan struggled to explain, \"I just wanted to hunt a stag to present to Imperial Father to nourish your body. Who knew I would be so unlucky? If that leopard hadn't suddenly appeared, my horse wouldn't have been startled, and everything else wouldn't have happened.\"","Xiao Chengjing scolded him sternly, \"Shut up! It's obvious you wanted to eat it yourself. My health is perfectly fine, I don't need you to send me a deer.\"","\"Roll back and reflect on your mistakes behind closed doors. Don't attend court for the next two days.\""]},{"number":259,"title":"Chapter 259: Impeaching the King of England","paragraphs":["Xiao Rongyan returned to his manor feeling utterly stifled and aggrieved. Before his bottom even touched the seat, he smashed an entire tea set.","He was mad with rage. \"Who on earth did this?\"","\"Hahaha!\" Hearing that Prince Ying had been punished with confinement to reflect on his mistakes, Prince Qi leaped up from his chair in delight and laughed heartily.","\"This is what they call going for wool and coming home shorn. Not only was he reprimanded by Imperial Father, but he also offended the Chu family.\"","Sitting in his chair, Gu Qishan smiled and lightly stroked his beard. \"Your Highness is still the clever one, sending people to spread the news throughout the city. Otherwise, the Emperor wouldn't have taken it so seriously.\"","Prince Qi laughed until his whole body felt refreshed. He picked up his hot tea and took a large gulp. \"How could I not use a weakness delivered right to my doorstep? Xiao Rongyan has taken a massive tumble this time. Even if Imperial Father wants him to stay in the military camp, Chu Liuyun won't give him a good look.\"","Duke Zhenguo's Manor.","The bedroom windows were already open. Duke Zhenguo, who was lying in bed being fed medicine, turned his head slightly to ask Song Jinzhao.","\"County Princess, when will my injuries heal?\"","Song Jinzhao, who was packing up her medical box, looked up and met his eyes. \"You won't be able to get out of bed and walk slowly for another half a month. It takes time for wounds to heal. Moreover, since you had bleeding in your head, you cannot engage in any strenuous activities for at least half a year.\"","\"That long?\" Duke Zhenguo's eyes widened, finding it somewhat hard to accept.","Holding the soup spoon, the Duchess of Zhenguo's eyes grew slightly moist; her expression was a mix of anger and anxiety.","\"Husband, you almost died. Half a year is not long at all. You are already semi-retired anyway. If you ask me, you should just take this opportunity to officially resign from your post. With Liuyun holding up the family, there's no need for you to worry.\"","In his youth, Duke Zhenguo spent years on the battlefield. He married late and had children late.","He was over thirty when he had his son, Chu Liuyun. Now in his fifties, and being a military general with chronic hidden injuries, his health was long past its prime.","Had the Emperor not insisted on forcing Prince Ying upon them this time, he wouldn't have gone to the Western Suburbs Camp, as he was worried about leaving Chu Liuyun to deal with it alone.","Deep down, Duke Zhenguo was still somewhat reluctant, but seeing his wife's sorrowful appearance, he ultimately didn't voice any objections, figuring he would discuss it after his injuries healed.","Standing outside the door, Chu Liuyun heard the conversation inside crystal clear.","Thinking of Duke Zhenguo's torn muscles and slightly dislocated shoulder, while Prince Ying was merely punished with confinement, he couldn't suppress the fury in his heart.","Turning around and returning to his study, his personal guard walked in to report: \"To the Duke, according to your subordinate's investigation, Chancellor Gu sent people to question the accompanying soldiers, and the rumors were spread by Prince Qi.\"","With his back turned, Chu Liuyun stared coldly at the unsheathed sword resting on the rack.","\"Since that's the case, let's add fuel to the fire. Handle it personally and make it clean. Pin it on Prince Qi and don't let anyone trace it back to us.\"","The guard nodded vigorously. \"Yes, this subordinate will do it immediately.\"","Xiao Rongyan had only been confined for a day, yet the rumors, instead of dying down, grew increasingly rampant.","Unable to endure the bitter wind and snow, he lay in his carriage and tent all day enjoying himself; in just a few days, he burned through the winter charcoal allowance meant for the two Dukes of the Chu family for two months; he feasted extravagantly in the military camp, having the kitchens prepare hundreds of dishes for him daily; disgusted by the poor conditions of the camp, he sent people overnight to practically move the entire Prince Ying's Manor over—this series of behaviors began spreading among the commoners.","At first, many commoners felt that since Prince Ying was of royal birth, it was normal for someone of such delicate upbringing to be unable to endure hardship and to be a bit extravagant. That was until someone leaked the contents of the Ministry of War's memorial to the throne.","Supervising the army day and night, observing the military conditions, eating and living with the soldiers—he had even received the Emperor's praise for it.","When the two contrasting images were placed side by side, everyone was instantly rendered speechless.","You can be extravagant, and you can be unable to bear hardships, but you cannot resort to deceit and fish for unearned fame.","One must know that the current Emperor only had two princes; the throne would inevitably go to one of them. Flawed character was a massive taboo.","Thus, during the morning court assembly the next day, Prince Ying was impeached.","Ye Liangyu, a man who could not tolerate a single grain of sand in his eyes, stepped out from among the officials holding his jade tablet. He fell to both knees and bowed deeply toward the imperial steps.","\"This humble official, Ye Liangyu, wishes to impeach His Highness Prince Ying on three major crimes. I beseech Your Majesty to make a divine judgment!\"","The Hall of Supreme Harmony was so silent you could hear a pin drop. Everyone knew what Ye Liangyu was about to say; such scenes had occurred countless times before his legs were crippled.","However, in the past, he had only impeached officials. Even if Prince Qi and Prince Ying backed them, Ye Liangyu would impeach them without hesitation. Now, his target had directly become a prince.","Xiao Chengjing said in a deep voice, \"Speak.\"","Ye Liangyu kowtowed once more.","\"Firstly, the military maintains strict discipline, and everyone from the commander-in-chief down to the foot soldiers advocates frugality. Yet His Highness Prince Ying used luminous pearls worth a thousand pieces of gold as lamps and top-grade silk as carpets, bringing the extravagant ways of Prince Ying's Manor into the military camp. Such actions disrupt military morale and are truly intolerable in the army.\"","\"Secondly, Your Majesty ordered Prince Ying to learn how to become a commanding talent, yet Prince Ying was lazy and negligent, spending his days idling in his carriage and tent to stay warm. He cast Your Majesty's high hopes aside like worn-out shoes. Not only did he make zero contributions to the imperial court, but he also showed unfilial disrespect to Your Majesty.\"","\"Thirdly, Prince Ying practiced extravagance in the military camp but submitted a memorial claiming he attended to everything personally and lived and ate alongside the soldiers. This is blatant deceit and deceiving the sovereign.\"","Ye Liangyu kowtowed for the third time.","\"Your Majesty, he who wishes to pacify the world must first rectify its foundation. If the foundation is upright, the world will be secure; if the foundation is crooked, the world will be in peril. The rise and fall of the nation truly rests upon this.\"","\"The princes are the foundation of the realm. If the root is not straight, the branches will surely grow crooked. This humble official risks death to speak bluntly today, entirely for the sake of the state and our dynasty's eternal foundation! I beseech Your Majesty to investigate clearly and severely punish Prince Ying to set the record straight!\"","As soon as his voice fell, not only did the officials of the Censorate step forward one after another to echo his sentiments, but even many military generals knelt down to demand severe punishment for Prince Ying.","Standing at the very front of the officials, Prince Qi couldn't help but lower his head to stifle a laugh.","He had never found Ye Liangyu's words so pleasing to the ear.","The foundation of the nation, the cornerstone of eternal enterprise—this was essentially telling the Emperor point-blank that Prince Ying was unfit to be this foundation. If he were to become it, the Dongzhao Kingdom would be destroyed in his hands.","Facing Ye Liangyu's accusations, officials from Prince Ying's faction immediately stepped forward to explain: \"Your Majesty, Vice Censor-in-Chief Ye is truly exaggerating and making malicious accusations.\"","\"When the garrison rotation began, Prince Ying also rode on horseback, braving the wind and snow alongside the soldiers. Later, it was only because of his weak constitution that he was forced to stay in the carriage and tent for warmth. Despite this, His Highness still had his carriage travel alongside the soldiers, constantly monitoring the march.\"","Ye Liangyu stood up and furiously rebuked the speaker: \"Supervising the army from the sidelines while sitting in a carriage encrusted with gold, silver, and jewels? The soldiers were shivering in the freezing cold while His Highness drank tea and kept warm in his carriage. How do you expect the soldiers of the Western Suburbs Camp to feel about that? If this isn't disrupting military morale, what is?\"","The official's face turned beet red. \"Prince Ying is of noble status; how can he be compared to common foot soldiers?\"","Ye Liangyu stepped forward and spat angrily: \"Indeed, they cannot be compared. Yet His Highness falsely claimed that he toiled day and night, eating and living with the soldiers. If this isn't deceiving the sovereign, what is?\"","Watching the civil officials and censors bickering in a chaotic mess within the grand hall, Xiao Chengjing closed his eyes in sheer exhaustion. When he opened them again, his gaze swept over the silent Prince Qi, Gu Qishan, and the others, and suspicions began to rise in his heart.","For the rumors to spread so quickly, someone had to be pulling the strings behind the scenes.","Was it Duke of Qing taking malicious revenge, or Prince Qi kicking a man while he was down? This matter had to be investigated clearly."]},{"number":260,"title":"Chapter 260: The Minister of War Who Took the Blame Was Completely Outmaneuvered","paragraphs":["Facing Ye Liangyu's relentless verbal assault and written condemnation, the officials of Prince Ying's faction could initially offer a few words of rebuttal, but eventually, they could only stand there in anxious silence.","They pinned their hopes on the emperor sitting on the dragon throne. After all, this was his son, and the offense was not a grave one; surely he would offer some protection.","Xiao Chengjing looked at Xiao Rongche. \"Prince Qi, do you think I should severely punish Prince Ying?\"","Prince Qi stepped forward and cupped his hands. \"To reply to Imperial Father, although Second Brother is at fault, it is not a heinous crime. However, rumors are running rampant outside the palace. If left unchecked, I fear it will damage the imperial family's dignity.\"","You've said all the good and bad things, but you still just want me to punish him severely.","Looking at the military officials kneeling on the ground and recalling his own lavish praise for Prince Ying's performance in the military camp, Xiao Chengjing felt utterly humiliated.","\"Pass down my decree. Prince Ying has violated military discipline, engaged in extravagance within the military camp, and disturbed the army's morale. He is to be fined two years' salary. The penalized funds shall be entirely allocated to the army to rush the production of winter clothing to reward the soldiers.\"","\"As for the memorials he wrote, due to his youth and inappropriate wording, he is specially ordered to copy one thousand volumes of the Ministry of War's correspondence and memorials. He is forbidden from leaving his estate until the copying is complete.\"","\"The Minister of War, Pan Yong, has been negligent. He made arbitrary judgments on submitted memorials without even reading them properly, failing in his duty of oversight. He is demoted to the Provincial Administration Commissioner of Annan and must leave the capital immediately to take up his post.\"","Cowering among the officials of Prince Ying's faction, Pan Yong looked up at the emperor in disbelief. A myriad of thoughts tangled in his eyes before he finally fell to his knees with a thud.","\"This humble subject thanks Your Majesty for your leniency. Long live the Emperor, long live, long, long live.\"","Never mind. As long as Prince Ying was safe, taking the blame for him was fine. It wouldn't be too late to be transferred back once the prince ascended the throne in the future.","Ye Liangyu lowered his eyes and retreated to his original spot. He clearly knew that the emperor intended to handle the matter lightly.","If the charge of deceiving the sovereign were to fall on Prince Ying, it would essentially destroy half of his chances of ascending the throne in the future.","To prevent the balance of power in the court from tipping, Pan Yong had to be made the scapegoat.","However, Ye Liangyu was already quite satisfied with this outcome. With the position of Minister of War vacant, it was time to push a new person up.","After the morning assembly, Prince Qi immediately summoned Gu Qishan to his estate. \"The position of Minister of War is vacant; we must quickly push our own person into it.\"","Gu Qishan replied, \"Rest assured, Your Highness. This humble subject will contact the court officials to recommend the person we have planted in the Ministry of War. The position of Minister of War will definitely belong to Your Highness.\"","Xiao Rongyan, who was reflecting on his mistakes behind closed doors in his estate, exploded on the spot upon suddenly hearing this news.","\"What? Pan Yong was demoted to the Provincial Administration Commissioner of Annan and has left the capital!\"","After understanding the causes and consequences of the matter, he was mad with rage.","\"It's this Ye Liangyu again, opposing this prince at every turn! I should have learned from Prince Qi and killed him.\"","\"And who spread these rumors in the capital? Was it Prince Qi or the Duke of Qing? Send someone to investigate immediately, and report back to me as soon as you find out.\"","Enduring Prince Ying's fury, the servant knelt on the ground and nodded repeatedly. \"This lowly one will go investigate right away.\" With that, he ran off.","As the sky grew dark, Fan Guanshan, the commander of the Imperial Guards, appeared in the imperial study.","\"Reporting to Your Majesty, this humble subject has investigated clearly. The people spreading the rumors are from Prince Qi's estate.\"","Xiao Chengjing frowned. \"Did the Duke of Qing intervene?\"","Fan Guanshan shook his head and replied, \"Although Duke Zhenguo has awakened, Duke Zhenguo's estate remains closed to visitors. The Duke of Qing has not left his residence either. Only County Princess Linghui visits daily, staying until dusk before leaving.\"","\"The servants in the estate do not go out often. I also sent people to tail the few servants responsible for purchasing, and they have never spread any rumors.\"","Xiao Chengjing took a deep breath and slowly exhaled. Closing his eyes wearily, he said, \"You may step down first. This matter must not be leaked.\"","Meanwhile, under Chu Liuyun's deliberate guidance, Prince Ying's people also quickly traced the matter back to Prince Qi.","The desk full of memorials was overturned onto the ground. \"I knew it was him! Trying to push his own people into power? In his dreams!\"","Just as both factions were competing to recommend their candidates, the emperor suddenly issued a decree recalling the current Provincial Administration Commissioner of Annan back to the capital and appointing him to the position of Minister of War.","This news was a bolt from the blue for both Prince Qi and Prince Ying. There were so many people in the Ministry of War, and no shortage of officials in the capital capable of serving as the Minister of War. Why suddenly summon someone from the provinces?","Upon hearing the news, Ye Liangyu sat in place and pondered for a long time. Finally, he smiled and couldn't help but shake his head.","The emperor's calculations were truly excellent. He had probably planned this long ago, hadn't he?","It not only stabilized the court's situation, preventing the struggle between the two tigers from becoming too unbalanced, but also successfully weakened Prince Ying's power in the court.","Was it Prince Qi's turn next?","Every night, Song Jinzhao would learn a lot about what happened in the court from Song Qiming.","After seven days of treatment, Duke Zhenguo's wounds were healing well. Song Jinzhao no longer needed to stay and keep watch at Duke Zhenguo's estate every day; the check-ups were changed to a visit once every three days.","After the bloody storm in the court subsided, the main gates of Duke Zhenguo's estate finally opened."]},{"number":261,"title":"Chapter 261: Employment Contract","paragraphs":["The Imperial Study was so quiet it seemed empty, a hollow silence that made one's heart palpitate with unease.","Gu Jupu's hands, hanging by his sides, trembled slightly. His heart felt as though it might leap out of his throat, leaving him breathless when he tried to speak.","\"Your Majesty's dragon body is tied to the Mandate of Heaven. Although the County Princess of Linghui possesses extraordinary medical skills, she is ultimately but a mortal. A healer must observe, listen, question, and feel the pulse to understand a patient's condition and determine if it can be cured. This humble official dares not make any rash conclusions.\"","Xiao Chengjing's gaze fixed upon Gu Jupu like a malicious spirit crawling out of hell, tightly strangling his throat, terrifying him so much that he hardly dared to breathe.","\"You may leave.\"","After a long silence, a voice sounding like heavenly music rang in Gu Jupu's ears. He bowed slowly, pretending to be calm as he rose to leave. \"This humble official takes his leave.\"","His weak legs finally gave out after he turned the corner outside the Imperial Study, and he collapsed onto the freezing floor, breaking out in a cold sweat.","Just as he caught his breath, Gu Jupu felt as if someone was watching him from behind. He hurriedly pushed himself up from the ground and walked quickly toward the Imperial Hospital.","After three days, the bustling entrance of the County Princess's estate finally began to quiet down.","The day before the Preliminary Eve of the New Year, Lan Xi went to the estates to summon the managers of Daohua Estate and Shiquan Estate.","Chen Fu and Li Hou stood respectfully in the main hall, their hands curled into slight fists at their sides, waiting for Song Jinzhao's questioning.","Ever since the County Princess visited the estates to check on the tenant farmers, she hadn't asked about anything else. Being suddenly summoned this time left both men feeling somewhat apprehensive.","Draped in a fox fur cloak, Song Jinzhao entered the main hall. Her gaze swept over their uneasy faces. \"I called you here today to inform you that after the New Year, I do not intend to continue renting the two estates to the tenant farmers.\"","Chen Fu trembled all over, looking at Song Jinzhao in disbelief. Without land, what would those tenant farmers do?","Li Hou spoke up anxiously, trying to persuade Song Jinzhao to change her mind.","\"County Princess, the tenant farmers on the estates rely on farming to survive. If you take the land back, how will they live?\"","Chen Fu knelt and kowtowed, pleading, \"County Princess, if you feel that a thirty percent rent is too low, we can raise it by another ten percent. Please do not take the fields back.\"","Song Jinzhao looked at the panicked men and sighed wearily.","\"Even if I raised it to forty percent, I wouldn't collect much rent in a year. You both know the situation of the tenant farmers. The main laborers are women, and this kind of physical work simply isn't suitable for them. They work hard all year round but can't even fill their stomachs. They are poor, and I haven't made much money either.\"","Chen Fu and Li Hou looked troubled. They knew Song Jinzhao was right, but without the land, just surviving would be difficult.","If they left the estate to go outside, it would be troublesome if they caused any disasters.","Song Jinzhao continued, \"Therefore, I have decided to take back all the fields next year. Shiquan Estate will be converted into a farm to grow vegetables and raise chickens, ducks, and livestock. Daohua Estate will be turned into flower fields. The workers needed for the farm and the flower fields will be hired from among the tenant farmers, and they will be paid a monthly wage for their work.\"","Chen Fu and Li Hou were stunned, not expecting Song Jinzhao to have such a plan.","Growing crops depended on the heavens for food; ensuring a harvest during droughts and floods was highly unstable. Having a steady job would definitely be better than farming.","But they feared instability—making money when busy, but having not a single penny when idle.","Li Hou asked in confusion to confirm, \"County Princess, Shiquan Estate is not small. If it is all used to grow vegetables and raise poultry, it will be more than we can eat. Are you planning to sell them?\"","There were so many merchants buying and selling poultry in the capital; it would not be easy to get a piece of the pie.","Chen Fu also nodded and asked, \"The wealthy families in the capital all have gardens in their mansions. I wonder what plans the County Princess has for converting it into flower fields?\"","Song Jinzhao understood their concerns. Considering they were asking not for themselves but for the livelihood of the hundreds of people on the estates, she explained a little more.","\"I have bought a few shops in the capital to start a food business. Building the farm is so we can produce and sell our own goods. As for what to do with the flowers, you will find out later.\"","\"Go back and tell the tenant farmers on the estates that after the vegetables in the greenhouses are harvested, they don't need to worry about the spring plowing next year. Those who are willing can sign an employment contract. Lan Xi will discuss the wages and benefits with you.\"","Watching Song Jinzhao's retreating figure, Chen Fu and Li Hou turned their gazes to Lan Xi, who was waiting to the side.","Lan Xi pulled an employment contract template from her sleeve and handed it to Chen Fu. \"The County Princess drafted this contract herself. Take a look first, and feel free to ask me if there is anything you don't understand.\"","Chen Fu reached out and took the contract. Li Hou leaned his head closer, and the two stared at the contract, reading it silently in their hearts.","Those working in the flower fields would receive a monthly wage of two taels and five mace, while those working on the farm would receive two taels, which was five hundred cash less than the flower field workers.","There was a guaranteed minimum monthly wage of five hundred cash. The wages for the current month would be uniformly distributed on the first day of the following month.","They would have four days off in shifts each month. Working hours were from the beginning of the Chen hour in the morning to the beginning of the You hour in the afternoon, with a two-hour rest period at noon.","...","Li Hou spread his fingers and started calculating the money. Two taels of silver a month meant twenty-four taels a year. This was far more profitable than growing crops.","Chen Fu pointed to the words \"guaranteed minimum\" on the contract in confusion and asked Lan Xi, \"May I ask, Manager Lan, what does this guaranteed minimum of five hundred cash mean?\"","Lan Xi explained to him, \"It means that if there is no work to do on the estate, they can still receive five hundred cash every month.\"","\"But don't worry, you two. The County Princess won't give them a chance to be idle.\"","Chen Fu and Li Hou widened their eyes in surprise. They could still get paid without working?","If used frugally, five hundred cash was just enough to cover the monthly food expenses for a family of three, not to mention that three people combined would make one thousand five hundred cash.","After reading it, both of them felt that the conditions on the contract were excellent. For ordinary commoners, almost no one would refuse this; it was much better than being a tenant farmer.","Chen Fu tightly gripped the contract template and said to Lan Xi, \"Manager Lan, this news is a bit sudden. We need to go back and tell the tenant farmers to see what they think.\"","Lan Xi nodded. \"Handle it as you see fit. Anyway, the County Princess said that all the land must be cleared out before the first of March next year. Those who are willing to work can sign the contract, and those who aren't can figure out their own way.\"","Chen Fu and Li Hou exchanged a glance, almost certain that the tenant farmers would definitely sign.","\"Rest assured, Manager Lan. We will go back and ask, and we will definitely return with an answer for the County Princess within three days at the latest.\"","The two men rushed back to the estate without stopping. That very afternoon, they gathered all the tenant farmers together and explained the situation.","Chen Fu held up the contract and read it out loud to them, word by word. After he finished reading, he said, \"This is a rare opportunity of a lifetime. Twenty taels of silver a year—where else can you find such high wages?\"","Guan Nianshan used his one remaining eye to catch the words on the contract. It certainly looked better than farming.","He asked the manager, \"If the County Princess's business loses money and the estate can't keep running, does that mean our jobs will be gone?\"","Chen Fu explained to him, \"Didn't I just read it? If there is no work, you can still get a free wage of five hundred cash every month. It definitely won't let you starve.\"","\"Besides, the contract is signed once a year. If the County Princess doesn't make money next year and suffers a loss, she definitely won't continue the year after and will just rent the land out again.\"","Chen Fu's voice lowered. \"When that time comes, you can continue to rent, though the rent will probably have to go up a bit.\"","More than two hundred tenant families discussed the matter at the manor for a full two hours, only taking their leave when dusk began to fall."]},{"number":262,"title":"Chapter 262: Little New Year","paragraphs":["They didn't even wait until the third day; by the second day, Chen Fu and Li Hou had already returned with the contract templates, both of them beaming with joy.","\"County Princess, your servants have spoken to the tenant farmers. Once all the vegetables in the greenhouses are harvested, they will immediately clear the fields, no later than mid-February. Over two hundred tenant households are willing to be employed by you and can sign the employment contracts at any time.\"","Song Jinzhao looked at Lanxi, \"Give them the blank contracts. Those who can sign will sign, and those who can't can just leave their handprints or footprints. Bring them all over after the Lantern Festival.\"","\"According to the original plan, work was to start on the first of March. Shiquan Estate is going to be used to build a farm. If the fields can be completely cleared by mid-February, starting construction early means they can start working and earning wages earlier.\"","Chen Fu and Li Hou nodded happily. Starting half a month early meant earning an extra tael of silver; they definitely had to start early.","They hadn't built many greenhouses for growing vegetables in the first place. By February, whatever could be sold would be sold, and whatever could be eaten would be eaten. They would certainly be gone by then.","On the day of the Little New Year, Prince Ying was still in confinement. At the imperial family banquet, despite the multitude of concubines in the harem, Emperor Xiao Chengjing looked at the only two children beside him and just felt a sense of desolation.","His youngest son was absent, and seeing his eldest son chatting merrily with the clan members at the banquet made him feel even more irritated.","Inside the County Princess's manor, the four Song siblings were gathered around a table eating hot pot.","The split hot pot they had just picked up from the blacksmith's shop yesterday needed to be tested by themselves a couple of times first to see how the quality was.","Fresh meats and vegetables were laid out on the table, while snowflakes danced outside the window. The four snowmen standing in the courtyard had been built by the four siblings' own hands that morning.","Wearing red hats and red scarves, Song Jinzhao's snowman was pierced with the Lingyun Spear, Song Shixue's snowman held a bow, and Song Qiming's held a book made of ice blocks, which even had a New Year's greeting poem carved into it. The youngest, Song Anhao, had directly stuck a candied hawthorn stick on hers. Beside them crouched a chubby white tiger, which bore a seventy percent resemblance to Xuetuan.","Admiring the scenery after the meal, Song Shixue rested her head on Song Jinzhao's shoulder. The beautiful snowy landscape, combined with the outdoor chill against their bodies, actually created a remarkably poetic atmosphere.","In the courtyard, Song Anhao was standing on her tiptoes, getting ready to lick the candied hawthorn. In the next second, she was grabbed by the arm and lifted away by the suddenly appearing Song Qiming.","\"If you lick it, your tongue will get frozen to it. There are new ones inside the house; let your brother take you to get one.\"","Song Shixue smiled and rubbed her head against Song Jinzhao's shoulder. \"Sister, I hope we can spend every Little New Year together in the future, just like today.\"","A gentle smile curved the corners of Song Jinzhao's mouth. She reached out to loop an arm around Song Shixue's neck and affectionately pinched her cheek. \"Okay, we'll spend them together.\"","Qingshuang, who came over holding a hand warmer, smiled and gently shook her head. In a few more years, when the County Princess and the Second Miss were married off, such a scene would be very hard to see again.","Before the new year, the three shops located on Qipan Street were all completed on time. The barbecue shop in Wuyi Alley was only missing its tables and chairs, while the hot pot restaurant had not finished its renovations yet and would only be completed right before the Lantern Festival.","The shops on the street began closing on the twenty-eighth of the twelfth lunar month and would only gradually reopen starting from the third day of the new year.","The originally planned river snail rice noodle shop was put on hold because there were no winter bamboo shoots in the capital, and shipping them from the south was too expensive.","In addition, the river water froze in winter, and the river snails all burrowed into the sand, making them difficult to collect. Therefore, Song Jinzhao simply changed the shop meant for selling river snail rice noodles into one selling Crossing-the-Bridge rice noodles.","The opening time for the three shops on Qipan Street was set for the seventh day of the Lunar New Year. Both the barbecue shop and the hot pot restaurant were scheduled to open on the day of the Lantern Festival. The employees had all been trained, and once the new year passed, they would be incredibly busy."]},{"number":263,"title":"Chapter 263: Chinese New Year, Opening with Great Prosperity","paragraphs":["On New Year's Eve, the entire capital was brightly lit, especially the inner city. Lanterns hung at the doors of every household, making it as bright as day.","Although the shops on the streets were closed, Vermilion Bird Street was packed with vendors selling all sorts of goods. The yamen runners did not interfere on New Year's Eve, making the atmosphere exceptionally lively.","Song Jinzhao, Song Qiming, and their group walked from one end of the street to the other, making their already full stomachs even more stuffed.","Held in someone's arms, Song Anhao carried an orange and black tiger lantern, his round eyes peering everywhere.","On the streets, on the roof beams, and in the hands of the bustling passersby, lanterns of all weird and wonderful shapes shone brighter against the night sky than the gems he collected, so beautiful that one could not look away.","The Song family had no relatives in the capital; their only frequent contacts were Ye Liangyu and Song Gaoli.","After paying a New Year's visit to the Ye residence on the first day of the lunar year, they stayed home. On the third day, Song Gaoli came with gifts, the Duke of Zhenguo's estate also sent someone over with holiday presents, and Dongfang Yukun came knocking once to look for Song Qiming. Aside from them, there was no one else.","Three days before their shops opened, the advertising flyers designed by Song Jinzhao had already been distributed throughout the streets and alleys of the capital.","Considering that many commoners were illiterate, she specifically had the artists draw the items as realistically as possible.","Aside from the shop names and addresses, there was not a single word on the flyers. They relied entirely on lifelike illustrations and vibrant colors to catch people's eyes, making the food look incredibly appetizing.","The effect of such a novel promotional method was astonishing. Even before the shops opened, commoners were coming to find them with the flyers in hand.","Upon learning that there would be discounts when they opened on the seventh day, they patted their chests and promised they would definitely come.","Inside the study of Prince Ying's estate, Xiao Rongyan tossed the flyer depicting milk tea and braised food into the fire.","He said with disdain, She truly comes from a lowly background. She is already a County Princess, yet she still spends all day engaging in merchants' affairs. It is unpresentable. How much silver can she possibly earn by selling a bit of food?","Standing at the door, Li Qinyun's expression stiffened. Xiao Rongyan's voice was so loud that she could hear him clearly even with the door closed.","The Li family were merchants who owned quite a few restaurants; did His Highness also consider them unpresentable in his heart?","The mere thought of it made Li Qinyun uncontrollably sad.","Thinking of her current status and how her maiden family was waiting to soar to the heavens by following Prince Ying, Li Qinyun had to pretend she did not care. She curled her lips into a gentle smile and said to the guard at the door, I have come to deliver ginseng soup to the Prince.","The guard nodded, turned around, knocked on the door, and walked in.","Your Highness, the Side Consort has come to bring you ginseng soup.","Hearing that the visitor was Li Qinyun, Xiao Rongyan's expression grew even colder.","He had granted her the favor of returning in glory to celebrate Li Tianchong's birthday, giving her all the face she needed, yet she completely failed to accomplish what she was supposed to do.","Instead, she was played for a fool by Song Jinzhao, and now that she was in the capital, she was causing him trouble at every turn. She was truly useless.","I am busy with official duties and have no time to see her.","The guard bowed, exited the room, and said to Li Qinyun, Side Consort, His Highness is busy with official duties and has no time to see you. You may hand the ginseng soup over to this servant.","Li Qinyun smiled and signaled her maid to hand the ginseng soup to the guard.","In that case, I shall take my leave.","As she turned to leave, the gentle smile on Li Qinyun's face vanished without a trace.","Her personal maid, Lingque, who was following beside her, worriedly observed her master from the corner of her eye.","Ever since the Prince had reprimanded her master last month, Princess Ying had brought back two beautiful maids from her maiden home.","Within a few days, they became the Prince's concubines. Since then, the Prince had not stepped into her master's courtyard for over a month. Things could not go on like this.","After returning to her room, Li Qinyun looked at the flyer placed on the low table and lowered her eyes in distress, shedding tears.","Lingque, tell me, in the Prince's heart, is my status also considered lowly?","Her personal maid, Lingque, who had served Li Qinyun since childhood, immediately comforted her. How could that be? Our Li family has been in business for generations. Our wealth is immense, and our businesses spread far and wide across the lands. How can we be compared to ordinary merchants?","Furthermore, Your Ladyship is the Side Consort of Prince Ying, whose name is recorded in the royal genealogy. Your status is incredibly noble. The Prince simply finds County Princess Linghui an eyesore; it has nothing to do with Your Ladyship.","Li Qinyun slowly sat down, her expression not brightening at Lingque's words.","I only became Prince Ying's Side Consort because I married the Prince. Song Jinzhao is already a County Princess even before marriage. In terms of status, I might truly not compare to her.","Yunque picked up a blanket and covered Li Qinyun's legs.","Your Ladyship is overthinking. A County Princess is ultimately just a County Princess. When the Prince ascends the throne in the future, how could her status ever compare to yours?","Li Qinyun smiled bitterly and fell silent.","Nowadays, His Highness was being questioned by the Emperor, and the Prince of Qi was gaining momentum. Who could say for sure who would ascend the throne in the future?","She only hoped her father had not made the wrong choice, otherwise, all the Li family's efforts over the years, along with herself as a daughter, would be lost completely.","With three shops connected together and opening on the same day, Qipan Street was exceptionally bustling on the seventh day of the new year, with seventy percent of the people coming specifically for them.","For the first three days of opening, the winter beverages were buy-one-get-one-free, all braised items were thirty percent off, and there were special food tastings at the door.","The ancient people, who had never eaten rice noodles before, found it incredibly novel. The smooth texture with its rice aroma was chewier and more elastic than regular noodles.","The broth, simmered from pork bones and chicken carcasses, was full of umami. Paired with dozens of ingredients that could be blanched on the spot, it made for a fresh and stylish way of eating.","In just one day, the reputation of the three shops was thoroughly established.","On the second and third days, there were hundreds of people lining up at the door, all wanting to get a bite while the discounts lasted.","Fortunately, they had prepared enough stock and manpower in advance, otherwise, the braised food shop would have had to close by noon.","The owner of the noodle shop across the street stood under the eaves, holding a cup of caramel red date milk tea. His eyes were full of envy as he looked at the shops packed with people at the door.","I have never seen anyone do business with this many customers on this street.","The impact was not huge on the first day of opening, but on the second and third days, half of the customers at his noodle shop had been snatched away to eat crossing-the-bridge rice noodles.","The waiter, who was wiping the table with a rag, thought of the few bites of braised meat he had tasted and could not help but swallow his saliva.","That is because it is genuinely delicious. I have never seen a shop that can make pork offal taste so good, and the prices are not expensive either.","The boss pondered, Do you think if I opened a shop modeling theirs, business would be just as good?","The waiter looked troubled and said, Boss, I heard these three shops were opened by County Princess Linghui. Would there not be trouble if we did that?","Commoners should not fight with officials; if they offended the County Princess, their lives would probably be difficult.","The noodle shop owner kept tapping the ground with the tip of his foot, If I can successfully steal their recipe, I do not have to open on Qipan Street. At worst, I will go to the outer city or a neighboring city. The main thing is the taste; it has to be at least seventy percent similar.","How could there be no competitors in business? It was just a matter of time.","Many food vendors on the street shared the same thought as the noodle shop owner, though most felt they should wait and see a bit longer.","We will have to see if the business remains steady once the prices return to normal. After all, many people are just here for the novelty of trying a new dish."]},{"number":264,"title":"Chapter 264: One After Another Opening, Inquiring About Song Jinzhao","paragraphs":["Three days quickly passed. The queues outside had noticeably shortened, but the braised food shop still sold out and closed early every day. Business at the milk tea shop was non-stop from morning till night, and during meal times, there was never an empty table at the Crossing-the-Bridge Noodles restaurant.","Before the people on Qipan Street could even react, Song Jinzhao's barbecue restaurant in Wuyi Alley and her hotpot restaurant on Zhuque Street opened for business.","The identical promotional tactics immediately made the city's residents associate them with the other three newly opened shops.","With a mentality of giving it a try, they felt they simply had to go and taste the food.","The greenhouse vegetables grown at Daohua Manor and Shiquan Manor were carted away by the hotpot restaurant's staff in horse-drawn carriages before the two managers could even find buyers for them.","For a full ten days, Song Jinzhao shuttled back and forth among the five shops, adjusting the inventory based on their daily sales.","After the Lantern Festival, more and more scholars arrived in the capital to participate in the spring imperial examinations. The shops' business did not decline; instead, it reached another small peak.","Inside a classroom at the Imperial College, Dongfang Yukun held a new beverage from the tea shop and said to Song Qiming, \"You must come with me to the poetry and wine gathering tomorrow. You absolutely cannot be absent.\"","After pushing his essay to Song Gaoli, Song Qiming turned to look at him helplessly. \"Do you really care that much about Cui Zhengyang?\"","Taking the essay, Song Gaoli saw the two start talking, so he silently turned and returned to his seat at the very back to reflect on the suggestions Song Qiming had just given him regarding his writing.","Dongfang Yukun shook his head and quibbled, \"It's not that I care about him; it's that I don't want to lose.\"","\"You don't understand. Cui Zhengyang hasn't even arrived in the capital yet, but the scholars from Jiangnan are already swearing that he will definitely be the top scorer this time. I have to knock him down a peg, otherwise, people will think I'm afraid of him.\"","Song Qiming stared at Dongfang Yukun's face, a face that captivated thousands of young maidens. \"Whether it's age or talent, he can't compare to you. What you actually care about is his face.\"","He reached out his right hand, rested it on Dongfang Yukun's shoulder, and gave it a firm squeeze. \"Yukun, listen to me. The empty title of the most handsome man in the Dongzhao Kingdom isn't important at all. What you should care about is the spring examination. As long as you score first place, even if Cui Zhengyang is better looking than you, he will forever be beneath you.\"","Dongfang Yukun reached up and grasped Song Qiming's hand. His lips tightened, and his gaze carried a sense of earnest persistence.","\"Don't you want to see him too? This poetry and wine gathering might be the last banquet before the spring exams. If we don't go, we won't have another chance.\"","Song Qiming tilted his chin up, rolling his stiff neck. He withdrew his hand and said, \"Tomorrow I have to go to my teacher's house. I don't have time for the gathering.\"","Dongfang Yukun pressed Song Qiming's retreating hand onto the desk. \"The court doesn't have a day off tomorrow. By the time Lord Ye returns from the Censorate, it will already be afternoon. We can go in the morning and leave at noon. It won't delay you.\"","Thinking of his classmates' various evaluations of Cui Zhengyang, especially how deeply entangled the matter was with Dongfang Yukun, Song Qiming finally agreed. \"Fine, we'll go tomorrow. I'll ask Gaoli to come along.\"","Having achieved his goal, Dongfang Yukun immediately set the time. \"We'll meet tomorrow at the hour of Si. Don't go too early; we need to arrive a bit late.\"","After the Lantern Festival, several heavy snowfalls blanketed the capital again, dropping the temperature even lower than it was during the New Year.","Just past the second watch of the night, Xiao Chengjing, who was still reviewing memorials in the Imperial Study, placed the final document onto a mountain-like pile of memorials.","He wearily closed his eyes and leaned back against the dragon throne. After a while, he opened his eyes and asked, \"Is Fan Guanshan on night duty today?\"","The head eunuch lowered his head slightly and replied, \"Yes.\"","Xiao Chengjing sat up straight. \"Summon him here.\"","\"Yes, Your Majesty.\"","Half a quarter of an hour later, the Commander of the Imperial Guards, Fan Guanshan, walked into the Imperial Study wearing a full suit of armor and knelt. \"This humble official, Fan Guanshan, greets Your Majesty.\"","Xiao Chengjing looked at him and asked, \"What has County Princess Linghui been doing lately?\"","The head eunuch standing to the side instantly tensed his back. Is it finally coming?","Although Fan Guanshan didn't understand why the Emperor was asking about Song Jinzhao, he still relayed what he knew.","\"Recently, aside from visiting the Duke of Zhenguo's estate once every seven days, County Princess Linghui has spent the rest of her time busy with her shop businesses.\"","Xiao Chengjing asked in confusion, \"What businesses? Is the gold I rewarded her not enough to spend?\"","Fan Guanshan answered hesitantly, \"Perhaps it is to pass the time. County Princess Linghui has opened five shops in the capital, all selling food, and business is quite good.\"","Xiao Chengjing leaned back, pressing his spine against the dragon throne in thought.","\"I heard Song Jinzhao opened quite a few shops in Anyang Prefecture, so it isn't strange for her to acquire some properties now that she is in the capital. You may leave.\"","A completely bewildered Fan Guanshan bowed and turned to leave. He called me over specifically just to ask about this minor matter—what is the Emperor planning? Does it have something to do with County Princess Linghui?","Fan Guanshan kept a watchful eye for three days, but seeing that nothing happened, he gradually put the matter out of his mind.","On the day of the poetry and wine gathering, Dongfang Yukun, Song Qiming, and the others arrived at the banquet on time. Upon entering, they noticed that Cui Zhengyang had not yet arrived.","Dongfang Yukun regretfully pounded his fist into his palm. \"If I had known, we should have come even later.\"","Song Qiming gave him a side-eye. \"Any later, and we'd just be having lunch.\"","Most of the attendees for the poetry and wine gathering had already arrived, and the familiar faces were essentially all present.","After mingling and chatting with the crowd, Song Gaoli returned and said, \"They say Cui Zhengyang unfortunately caught a cold on the road from Jiangnan and won't be able to make it today.\"","The expression on Dongfang Yukun's face instantly vanished, turning serious. \"He had such a long journey from Jiangnan to the capital, and he still hasn't recovered?\"","Song Gaoli shook his head. \"I heard that after he entered the capital yesterday, the Cui residence immediately called for a doctor. They say he's been taking medicine for half a month with no sign of improvement.\"","\"Now they're all discussing that Cui Zhengyang might underperform in this spring examination.\""]},{"number":265,"title":"Chapter 265: Visiting the Patient: Cui Zhengyang, the Snow Lotus of Tianshan","paragraphs":["Hearing this, Dongfang Yukun's expression took a turn for the worse. His hand, resting on the table, remained motionless for a long time.","Not long after, he suddenly stood up and said to Song Qiming, \"Let's go, we're going to the Cui Manor to visit the sick.\"","\"Ah?\" Song Qiming stood up, looking stunned. Seeing the other moving so fast, he had no choice but to pull Song Gaoli along to keep up.","Is his competitive spirit really that strong? The man didn't even show up, so he has to track him down at Cui Zhengyang's own home?","Aside from constantly being compared to one another, could there be some grudge between these two?","The carriage passed through Wuyi Alley and arrived at the end of a quiet stone-paved road. The large trees by the road were stripped of their leaves, and in front of the gate was a man-made channel of flowing water, its surface currently covered in solid ice.","Looking at the two stone lions towering at the entrance, Song Qiming curiously asked Dongfang Yukun.","\"The Cui family is a prominent clan from Jiangnan. How could they have such a large mansion in the capital? And it looks quite old.\"","Dongfang Yukun looked up at the gate of the Cui Manor and explained, \"Five generations ago, the Cui family also had someone serving as an official in the imperial court, and he even reached the position of Prime Minister. By my reckoning, that should be Cui Zhengyang's great-great-grandfather. Later, when the Chili State fell and dynasties changed, the Cui family relocated their entire household to Jiangnan, leaving only this old mansion in the capital.\"","Song Qiming blinked in surprise. A Prime Minister of the previous dynasty?","\"As far as I know, after the founding emperor ascended the throne, he didn't expel the former officials of the previous dynasty. Did the Cui family have no successors at that time?\"","Dongfang Yukun shook his head and smiled. \"Not at all. The Cui family produced top scholars for three consecutive generations. Cui Zhengyang's great-grandfather once served as the Vice Minister of Works, and even his grandfather was the last top scholar before the fall of the Chili State. At that time, the Cui family had numerous disciples in the court, truly commanding universal response to a single call.\"","\"In recent years, the Cui Clan Academy has gained great fame in Jiangnan, cultivating many promising talents for the imperial court. Now that Cui Zhengyang is entering the court as an official, the Cui family is likely to rise again.\"","Hearing this, Song Qiming couldn't help but feel a sense of admiration. To be able to retreat bravely in such circumstances and choose to preserve the family's foundation, the head of the Cui family at that time must have been extremely wise.","Standing to the side, Song Gaoli listened to their conversation and only felt that this upcoming spring examination would truly be a fierce battle between dragons and tigers. He also grew increasingly curious about Cui Zhengyang.","The servant stepped forward and had just stopped knocking when someone opened the door from the inside.","Seeing three well-dressed young masters accompanied by servants, the gatekeeper politely asked, \"Who might you be? What business brings you to the Cui Manor?\"","Dongfang Yukun stepped forward and said, \"I'm looking for your young master. I heard Cui Zhengyang is ill, so we have come to visit him.\"","The gatekeeper carefully examined the faces of Song Qiming and the other two, confirming that he did not recognize them.","\"My young master has caught a chill and needs to rest. The madam has instructed that he is not to see outside guests. Please return, young masters.\"","Seeing that he was about to close the door, Dongfang Yukun quickly blocked it with his hand. \"Just tell your young master that Dongfang Yukun is here to see him. He will definitely see me.\"","The gatekeeper's hand paused, his surprised gaze fixing on Dongfang Yukun's face. No wonder he was so handsome; it turned out to be Young Master Dongfang, who was as famous as his own young master.","\"Please wait a moment, young masters. Allow this humble one to go in and report.\"","The gatekeeper closed the door, quickly turned, and ran through the front hall corridor toward the backyard. Stopping at the door of Cui Zhengyang's room, he said to the servant, \"There are three young masters at the door who want to see the young master. The one leading them is Dongfang Yukun, and he said the young master would definitely see him.\"","Mo Chen thought for a moment, and finally opened the door, walked to the bed, and woke Cui Zhengyang.","\"Young Master, Young Master Dongfang has come to visit you.\"","Cui Zhengyang, having just opened his eyes, was still a bit groggy. It was only when he heard the word \"Dongfang\" that his eyes cleared up slightly.","\"Is it Dongfang Yukun?\"","Mo Chen nodded. \"The gatekeeper said he also brought two other young masters, but didn't ask their names so he doesn't know who they are.\"","\"Bring them in.\"","Cui Zhengyang sat up somewhat weakly and ordered, \"Help me up and get me dressed.\"","The gatekeeper hurried back, smiling as he extended his hand toward Dongfang Yukun. \"Please come in, young masters. My young master has gotten up.\"","The three men's expressions changed slightly. It was nearing the end of the Si hour and Cui Zhengyang was just getting up; he must be quite ill.","Passing through pavilions and terraces over the water, although every brick and tile of the mansion looked a bit old, the scenery and furnishings exuded elegance everywhere.","Every wall was hung with paintings and calligraphy inscribed with poetry, and the rockery in the garden was not as complex and elaborate as those in wealthy households.","A mountain, a body of water, a plant, or a tree—the simple elegance possessed a unique sense of dynamic and profound tranquility, heavily steeped in a scholarly atmosphere.","Crossing the corridor, the door to the main room in the courtyard was open.","After entering the room, Song Qiming smelled a faint scent of medicine. His gaze fell upon the face of the man draped in a white fox fur coat on the couch, and his heart skipped a beat.","No wonder Dongfang Yukun cared so much; in terms of appearance, this man truly did not fall short.","The light from outside the window shone on the man's snow-white skin, giving it a jade-like quality. The stubbornness between his brows caused by his illness made him look like a precarious snow lotus on a snowy mountain, revealing a sense of resilience amidst his elegance.","Compared to Dongfang Yukun, although the two were only three years apart in age, Cui Zhengyang possessed a mature aura of having experienced a thousand sails, giving off a very reliable feeling.","\"How is your face so pale? What did the doctor say after seeing you? Can you be cured before the metropolitan examination?\"","Dongfang Yukun walked to the edge of the couch with dissatisfaction, his narrow, peach-blossom eyes already narrowing along with his slightly furrowed brows.","\"It dragged on for quite a while on the road, so I'm afraid it won't be easy to recover from.\"","Cui Zhengyang smiled at Dongfang Yukun, then his gaze fell on Song Qiming and Song Gaoli standing behind him. \"And these two are?\"","Song Qiming stepped forward and cupped his hands. \"I am Song Qiming, a student participating in this metropolitan examination. Hearing that Young Master Cui was unwell, please forgive our abrupt visit.\"","Song Gaoli: \"I am Song Gaoli, also a student participating in this examination. I have long heard that Young Master Cui possesses great talent and is known as the most handsome man in Jiangnan. Seeing you today, you truly live up to your reputation.\"","Song Qiming clenched his teeth, holding back a laugh, and winked at Song Gaoli.","Is that any way to speak? What kind of man wears his handsome appearance on his sleeve all day?","Song Gaoli opened his eyes wide in bewilderment.","Wasn't it said that he and Dongfang Yukun were competing for the title of the most handsome man in the Dongzhao Kingdom? He should be happy that I said that.","Song Qiming furrowed his brows. It was Dongfang Yukun who cared; this one never said anything about it.","Cui Zhengyang weakly curled the corners of his lips. \"I have long heard that Anyang Prefecture produced a thirteen-year-old top provincial scholar. Seeing Young Master Song today, you are indeed young.\"","His gaze turned to Dongfang Yukun. \"Brother Yukun, do you remember when we first met? You were the same age as Young Master Song.\"","Song Qiming and Song Gaoli exchanged glances, a hint of surprise in their eyes.","Brother Yukun?","How could Dongfang Yukun's attitude toward Cui Zhengyang be so different from the latter's attitude toward him? It didn't look like they were at odds at all."]},{"number":266,"title":"Chapter 266: Turning into Enemies More Like Tough Talk but Soft Heart","paragraphs":["Dongfang Yukun plopped heavily onto the cushioned round stool.","\"Don't call me that. You didn't even take the triennial metropolitan examination seriously. How could you catch a cold right at the last minute? Couldn't you have come to the capital earlier?\"","Mo Chen, who was waiting to the side, gestured for Song Qiming and Song Gaoli to take a seat, then picked up the teapot from the table to pour water for the three of them.","\"This is aged white tea brought all the way from Jiangnan. Please, have a taste, young masters.\"","Cui Zhengyang said, \"My grandfather is getting older by the day. I had to stay and help him celebrate his birthday before I could leave.\"","Dongfang Yukun crossed his arms and rolled his eyes. \"I think the scholars in Jiangnan just flattered you too much. You knew you couldn't beat me in the exam, so you made yourself sick on purpose just so my victory would feel unearned.\"","The corners of Cui Zhengyang's mouth curled up like melting snow in spring.","\"Brother Yukun, last March, Miss Huang gave birth to a son. What happened back then wasn't my fault. Why must you be so stubborn for so long? It's time to let it go.\"","Like a startled ragdoll cat, Dongfang Yukun instantly sprang up from his seat, his hair and the fine hairs on his body practically standing on end.","\"What do you mean it wasn't your fault? If you hadn't suddenly shown up and seduced her, why would she have rejected me!\"","Song Gaoli, who was sipping his tea, choked instantly, spitting out a mouthful of water and coughing non-stop.","Song Qiming, whose sleeve had been splashed by the tea, feigned composure as he placed his cup back down and reached out to pat Song Gaoli's back.","It all happened so suddenly. They had thought Dongfang Yukun and Cui Zhengyang were rivals in talent and looks, but they never expected them to be rivals in love.","Dongfang Yukun had just turned seventeen after the New Year. When he went to Jiangnan for his study tour, he must have been only twelve or thirteen. He already had a girl he liked back then?","Cui Zhengyang's tolerant gaze looked as though he were watching an unreasonable younger brother.","\"You were eleven at the time, and Miss Huang was even a year older than me. It wasn't that she looked down on you, nor did I seduce her. She simply thought you were too young and inappropriate.\"","Dongfang Yukun retorted angrily, \"So what if I was young? It was only a four-year difference.\"","\"She was already about to be moved by me, but then you suddenly appeared and drew her attention. Tell me, did she or did she not develop feelings for you after that?\"","Cui Zhengyang replied, \"It's not my fault she liked me. I only met her once. With looks like yours and mine, it would be strange if no one liked us. Anyway, I never liked her.\"","Dongfang Yukun let out three cold chuckles.","\"I spent days trying to win her over, but she fell for you after just one meeting, and in the end, you even turned your nose up at her. How do you expect me to feel about that?\"","Cui Zhengyang said patiently, \"If you had been the same age as me back then, Miss Huang definitely would have chosen you. She is married now and has a child, so why are you still brooding over this? There are so many women in the world; sooner or later, you will meet someone you like even more.\"","In Cui Zhengyang's eyes, Dongfang Yukun was only eleven at the time and didn't understand romantic love at all; it was merely a boy's innocent crush.","Dongfang Yukun stubbornly replied, \"I stopped caring about that a long time ago. What bothers me is that my talent and looks are clearly far superior to yours, yet people still compare the two of us.\"","\"I will definitely be the top scorer in this imperial examination. You had better recover from your illness quickly, lest you fail to even pass as a Jinshi. If that happens, three years of hard work will go down the drain, and you'll have to return to Jiangnan in disgrace to teach.\"","Song Qiming and Song Gaoli watched the two of them, enjoying the gossip.","One was proudly throwing out harsh words, while the other sat on the couch with a constant smile. There was an indescribable sense of harmonious intimacy between them, and even Cui Zhengyang's complexion looked much better than when they had first walked in.","They stayed at the Cui residence for nearly two hours, and Cui Zhengyang even invited them to stay for a meal.","Dongfang Yukun insisted on leaving, though he did tell Cui Zhengyang to rest and recover well before departing.","After stepping outside, Song Qiming couldn't help but ask curiously, \"Brother Dongfang, what is this about Miss Huang that you two were discussing?\"","Dongfang Yukun glared at him fiercely. \"That is all in the past. I have matters to attend to at home, so I'll be taking my leave.\"","Watching the carriage speed away, Song Gaoli excitedly clenched his fists.","Grinning from ear to ear, he gossiped, \"Now I really want to know how they turned into enemies back then.\"","Song Qiming raised his index finger and wagged it, clicking his tongue. \"Enemies? I doubt it.\"","\"I think he just has a sharp tongue but a soft heart. Cui Zhengyang didn't take Dongfang Yukun's little temper tantrum to heart at all; instead, it felt like an older brother looking at his younger sibling.\"","\"Just watch. If Young Master Cui's illness doesn't improve soon, Yukun will definitely be the first one to worry.\"","Song Gaoli noted, \"He was pretty anxious today.\"","As soon as he found out the other was sick, he rushed over. Before seeing them interact, he had assumed Yukun was coming to kick him while he was down.","...","The business of the five shops gradually got on track. All the vegetables for the hotpot restaurant were purchased from the farmstead. By late January, the greenhouse vegetables from both farmsteads had completely sold out.","The tenant farmers wanted to clear the land early to hand it over to Song Jinzhao so they could start working and earning wages sooner. Any remaining small crops that needed a couple more days were picked early, pushing the farmstead's schedule forward by an entire month.","Lanxi, who had spent time at the farmstead in Anyang Prefecture, was directly sent by Song Jinzhao to Shiquan Farmstead to supervise the work. Meanwhile, Song Jinzhao herself took Qingshuang around the capital every day to find reliable florists to pre-order flower seedlings and seeds for spring planting.","Some had to be transported from the south, so they needed to be ordered in advance to avoid delays.","On the third day after leaving the Cui residence, inside the Imperial Academy classroom, Song Qiming looked puzzledly at the empty desk next to him.","With the final sprint for the metropolitan examination approaching, Dongfang Yukun was actually skipping class at such a crucial time.","After classes ended at noon, Dongfang Yukun, who had been absent all morning, rushed into the dining hall and found Song Qiming eating. With a hint of pleading in his expression, he said, \"Cui Zhengyang has been taking medicine for three days without any improvement, and the Cui family cannot summon an imperial physician. Could I trouble you to ask County Princess Linghui to go take a look?\"","Song Qiming paused his chopsticks. \"So you went to the Cui residence this morning?\"","Dongfang Yukun nodded. \"I just wanted to know if his cold would get better. I don't want an unearned victory or to give people a reason to gossip.\"","Song Qiming pursed his lips and agreed, \"Alright, I'll tell my older sister when I go back tonight.\"","Dongfang Yukun grabbed Song Qiming's arm. \"Don't wait until tonight. We can head over right now during the noon break.\"","Song Qiming sat firmly without moving. \"Are you in that much of a hurry?\"","Dongfang Yukun tugged at his arm, trying to pull him up and drag him away. \"The metropolitan examination is in just over ten days. The sooner he gets treated, the sooner he recovers.\"","Song Qiming shook off his hand and picked up his chopsticks again. \"Wait for me to finish my food. It'll be quick.\"","After eating, the two took a carriage straight to the County Princess's estate. It was only when they walked into the courtyard that Song Shixue informed them Song Jinzhao wasn't home.","\"News came from the palace that the Empress suffered a headache attack last night and summoned my sister to the palace to treat her. She left less than fifteen minutes ago.\"","Song Qiming frowned. \"Aren't there imperial physicians in the palace?\"","Song Shixue guessed, \"They probably heard that my sister cured the Duke of Zhenguo, so they wanted her to take a look.\"","Song Qiming turned to Dongfang Yukun and said, \"My younger sister learned medicine from our eldest sister and has treated many patients in Anyang Prefecture. How about we let her go examine Young Master Cui?\"","Song Shixue asked, \"What illness?\"","Song Qiming explained, \"Yukun's friend, Young Master Cui Zhengyang, caught a chill on his way to the capital. He has seen several physicians to no avail, so he wanted to ask you, Sister, to go over and take a look, hoping you might be able to cure him before the imperial examination.\""]},{"number":267,"title":"Chapter 267: The Overly Anxious Empress is Taken to See the Emperor","paragraphs":["After the carriage entered the palace gates, it stopped at the entrance of the Qianqing Palace. The eunuch lifted the carriage curtain, respectfully bowed his head, and said to Song Jinzhao, \"County Princess, beyond the Qianqing Palace is the Inner Court. The carriage can only stop here.\"","After stepping down from the carriage, Song Jinzhao looked around. The last time she entered the palace was for the Emperor's birthday banquet, but her vision had been obscured by the night, and everything in the distance had been pitch black.","Looking at it now, the towering vermilion walls and the cold bluestone pavement felt empty and devoid of human warmth.","Setting aside the imperial majesty, it truly resembled a cage.","\"There are servants in the palace, so this momo does not need to enter. She can simply wait here.\"","Song Jinzhao looked at the eunuch in surprise. \"I can't even bring a single maid inside?\"","It wasn't a major occasion like a sacrifice or a grand celebration. According to the rules, she should be allowed to bring one or two maids when visiting the Empress in the inner palace.","The eunuch bowed and said, \"Her Majesty the Empress is feeling unwell and does not wish to see too many strangers. Please forgive us, County Princess.\"","Song Jinzhao lowered her eyes, feeling a bit strange. \"Since that is the case, Qingshuang, you stay here.\"","Qingshuang nodded and handed the medical box to Song Jinzhao.","\"This servant will wait here for you, Miss.\"","Walking to the entrance of the Kunning Palace, a palace maid immediately welcomed Song Jinzhao inside.","\"This servant greets County Princess Linghui. Her Majesty the Empress has been waiting for the County Princess for quite some time.\"","Upon entering the main hall of the Kunning Palace, a warm heat accompanied by a thick scent of sandalwood washed over her. The fragrance was so strong that it made Song Jinzhao feel uncomfortable.","\"Your subject Song Jinzhao pays her respects to Her Majesty the Empress. May the Empress be blessed with ten thousand fortunes and golden peace.\"","\"Rise, and be seated.\" The Empress wore a faint smile on her lips. Her voice, settled by time and authority, sounded like the low toll of a temple bell, giving off a feeling that was both gentle and inviolable.","Song Jinzhao stood up and raised her head.","The woman sitting upright on the phoenix chair possessed a luxurious aura. She wore a nine-tailed phoenix pearl-tassel hairpin on her head, and her dark blue kesi silk phoenix robe gave her a sense of stability and grace.","The current Empress of the Dongzhao Kingdom was Emperor Xiao Chengjing's first wife. Being only two years younger than him, she was considered relatively old in the flower-filled inner palace.","She had an excellent reputation outside, with her only flaw being her lack of children. Both princes were born to concubines. However, it was said that the imperial couple had a good relationship and treated each other with mutual respect.","The Empress looked at Song Jinzhao with a gentle expression and exchanged pleasantries. \"The last time I saw the County Princess was at the Emperor's birthday banquet. I had long wanted to summon you into the palace for a casual chat, but unfortunately, my health has been poor, and I haven't had much energy.\"","Song Jinzhao politely curved her lips. \"I heard that Your Majesty suffered from a severe headache last night and was in pain all night. Your complexion looks quite good now; presumably, the palace physicians have treated you well.\"","She was a County Princess with a different surname, not of imperial bloodline. She shouldn't have any family matters to chat about with the royal family.","The corners of the Empress's lips curled up, revealing a happy smile.","\"My headaches have been occurring for many years; it's an old ailment. When it flared up last night, the pain was unbearable. It was the Emperor who took pity on me. Knowing that the County Princess has superb medical skills, far surpassing the palace physicians, he mentioned it after court today, which is why you were brought into the palace to take a look.\"","Song Jinzhao lowered her eyes and smiled faintly.","So it was Xiao Chengjing's idea.","\"The Emperor's heart aches for Your Majesty. Since that is the case, your subject will now take Your Majesty's pulse.\"","Resting the pads of her fingers on the Empress's wrist, a strange look flashed through Song Jinzhao's eyes a moment later.","Excessive worry, internal stagnation, and a deficiency of qi and blood. It seemed this Empress was not living as well as she appeared on the surface.","\"Your Majesty's liver qi is stagnant, and your heart and spleen are both deficient, leading to a restless mind. Presumably, managing the affairs of the six palaces too diligently has caused your noble body to fall ill.\"","\"Your subject can use acupuncture to balance Your Majesty's qi, blood, yin, and yang, and to clear your meridians. This will be supplemented with herbal decoctions to nourish the body and consolidate qi. However, the headache is a chronic disease prone to relapses. Your Majesty must avoid excessive worry and maintain a joyful mood to reduce the frequency of recurrences, or even prevent them entirely.\"","The Empress gently stroked her temples and said slowly, \"As the Empress, I have to worry about everything in the six palaces. How can I not be anxious?\"","\"The imperial physicians have long advised me about these headaches. County Princess, just treat it as soon as possible.\"","Song Jinzhao stood up and took out her acupuncture tools from the medical box.","The Empress had been married for many years but had never been pregnant. Judging from the pulse just now, there were no issues with her fertility. Without contraceptive measures, it was impossible for her not to conceive. Perhaps the problem truly lay with Xiao Chengjing.","With the Empress childless, the Prince of Qi and the Prince of Ying had a higher chance of ascending the throne. She just didn't know who had taken action.","To dare to scheme against the Emperor, their courage was no ordinary thing.","Half an hour later, when Song Jinzhao removed the needles, the Empress, who was lying face down on the bed, had already fallen asleep.","Song Jinzhao handed the written prescription to the palace maid. \"Although sandalwood can calm the mind and soothe the spirit, using too much can cause dizziness and a constant feeling of mental fatigue and sleepiness. It is better to use less.\"","The Empress's personal maid curtsied and said, \"The imperial physicians said the same thing, but if we don't burn more, Her Majesty cannot fall asleep during her afternoon nap, and her energy will only be worse in the afternoon.\"","Song Jinzhao glanced at the Empress lying on the bed. She definitely suffered from depression, and it was not mild.","Walking out of the Kunning Palace, she saw the same eunuch who had led the way when she entered the palace. He seemingly hadn't entered the Kunning Palace earlier.","After walking for a distance, Song Jinzhao stopped in her tracks. \"Eunuch, this doesn't seem to be the way out of the palace.\"","At the intersection just now, they should have turned, but he had led her straight ahead.","The eunuch's body stiffened, his eyes showing a hint of nervousness. He hadn't expected Song Jinzhao to be so perceptive.","\"To reply to the County Princess, this servant is following Eunuch Zhao's orders to lead the way for you. The County Princess just needs to follow.\"","Song Jinzhao pursed her lips, and her hand gripping the medical box tightened slightly.","It seemed Xiao Chengjing's head eunuch was named Eunuch Zhao.","It was Xiao Chengjing who suggested she enter the palace to treat the Empress. Did he want to ask about the Empress's condition, or did he have other motives?","Seeing the plaque for the Funing Palace hanging above, Song Jinzhao was led to the side hall next to it.","The eunuch leading the way pushed open the door and stopped at the entrance. \"County Princess Linghui, please enter.\"","The moment Song Jinzhao stepped over the threshold, the large doors were shut behind her.","There were no palace maids or eunuchs inside the hall; only the flames on the candlestands flickered in the wind.","The sound of pages turning came from her left. Song Jinzhao took a deep breath and walked inward. When she saw Gu Jupu standing to the side, her footsteps paused imperceptibly.","\"Your subject Song Jinzhao kowtows to the Emperor. Long live the Emperor, long live, long long live.\"","Xiao Chengjing was sitting on the couch reading a book, with the head eunuch, Eunuch Zhao, waiting beside him. There were only the four of them in the room.","\"Rise.\" The majestic and solemn voice reached Song Jinzhao's ears from just a few yards away.","The moment Song Jinzhao stood up and raised her head, she met Xiao Chengjing's gaze.","It was like the eyes of a snake locking onto its prey, sending a chill down her spine. It felt completely different from the impression he gave at the birthday banquet last time.","\"How is the Empress's condition?\"","Song Jinzhao slowed her breathing and spoke slowly: \"Her Majesty's headache is a chronic disease that frequently relapses. Your subject has already administered acupuncture and prescribed medicine for Her Majesty. If she can constantly maintain a joyful mood, the frequency of relapses will be reduced.\"","Xiao Chengjing's gaze hadn't left Song Jinzhao since she appeared. \"Are you saying it cannot be completely cured?\""]},{"number":268,"title":"Chapter 268: Treating the Emperor","paragraphs":["Standing to the side, Gu Jupu's back shivered, and he dared not move a muscle.","Heaven bless, she must be careful with her words.","Song Jinzhao lowered her head. Chronic diseases can only be alleviated and are very difficult to cure completely. The frequency of headaches is closely related to one's mood. If treated properly, it is possible for them to not occur for a long period of time.","Xiao Chengjing said, State affairs have been heavy lately, and I am somewhat exhausted. Since you are already here, take a look at me as well.","Song Jinzhao took a deep breath, walked to the couch, and opened her medical box. This was his true purpose for bringing her into the palace; the Empress's headache was merely a smokescreen.","Allow this subject to take Your Majesty's pulse. The firm skin on his wrist looked better maintained than the Empress's. If he was capable of having children, being fifty years old was not an impossibility.","The side hall was dead silent, yet none of the four people present had a peaceful heart.","Especially Gu Jupu and Eunuch Zhao, whose hearts were pounding like drums, thumping endlessly, unable to calm down no matter how hard they tried.","Just as Song Jinzhao was taking his pulse, Xiao Chengjing suddenly spoke. The Empress and I have been deeply in love for many years, yet she has never been able to bear me a prince. Because of this, she has become depressed and developed these headaches. I am also deeply saddened by this.","Song Jinzhao's fingers resting on Xiao Chengjing's wrist paused slightly, and she did not immediately reply.","The pulse was deep and slow, thin and weak, especially evident in the chi position. It was the most common manifestation of kidney deficiency, but it was not innate.","It seemed to be permanent kidney damage caused by the long-term consumption of large amounts of bitter, cold, and heavy-sedating drugs.","May this subject be allowed to view Your Majesty's medical records from previous years?","Xiao Chengjing's gaze swept toward Gu Jupu standing nearby, scraping across his face as if lined with thorns.","Gu Jupu carefully took out three medical records from his sleeve and handed them to Song Jinzhao. These are the Emperor's medical records for the past year.","Song Jinzhao turned to look at him; he had come prepared.","The past year was of no use. Calculating from Princess Yongjia's age, it had to be at least over ten years.","I need the Emperor's medical records for the past twenty years.","Gu Jupu's shrinking neck gave a jolt, his gaze fixed on Song Jinzhao's face, momentarily at a loss for what to do.","Twenty years of medical records would fill several large boxes. Although the Imperial Hospital had them archived, moving them over would cause too much of a commotion and easily arouse suspicion.","He looked up at the Emperor, seeking his opinion.","The medical records over the years are all archived in the Imperial Hospital, but there are so many that I am afraid you will not be able to finish reading them in a short time.","Xiao Chengjing withdrew his hand and said unhurriedly, The Empress's medical records are also in the Imperial Hospital. The County Princess can go over and take a look.","Carrying the three medical records out of the side hall, Gu Jupu turned to look at Song Jinzhao walking beside him and asked with difficulty, Are you confident in this, County Princess?","Song Jinzhao followed leisurely with her medical box in hand. Is Director Gu referring to the Emperor or Her Majesty the Empress?","Gu Jupu choked on his words, almost making himself sick from holding it in.","What do you think, County Princess?","Song Jinzhao cast a complicated glance at him. I will not know who I am confident about until I have read the medical records.","Gu Jupu took a deep breath and helplessly led Song Jinzhao toward the Imperial Hospital.","Their shift had not yet ended, so when they entered, there were still many imperial physicians on duty in the Imperial Hospital.","Seeing Gu Jupu bring Song Jinzhao in, they immediately stopped their work and bowed deeply. This subordinate greets County Princess Linghui.","Director Gu said in a deep voice, The Empress's headache has flared up, so we specially invited County Princess Linghui into the palace for diagnosis and treatment. You all should reflect on why your medical skills have not improved for so long.","Seeing everyone lower their heads in silence, Gu Jupu secretly breathed a sigh of relief and led Song Jinzhao into the storeroom where the medical records were kept.","Hearing the door close, the people standing outside finally raised their heads to breathe.","Director Gu could not cure it himself, yet he was lecturing them.","The Empress was often in a bad mood, so there was simply no way to cure this headache completely. Each flare-up could only be mitigated by reducing the pain.","Thinking of how County Princess Linghui had saved Duke Zhenguo, many people in the Imperial Hospital began to worry again.","Because of the matter with Duke Zhenguo, the Emperor has already been disappointed with our Imperial Hospital once. If County Princess Linghui cures the Empress's headache, our days ahead will probably be even harder.","Imperial Physician Xu pulled a medical book from the shelf.","We cannot blame others for our own lack of medical skill. Besides, there are very few people in this world as exceptionally gifted as County Princess Linghui. We just need to do our own jobs well.","The imperial physicians sighed. Who could argue with that?","County Princess Linghui would only be eighteen after the New Year, while Director Gu was already seventy-four. There was simply no comparison."]},{"number":269,"title":"Chapter 269: Staying Overnight in the Palace, Gathering Information at the Ye Residence","paragraphs":["\"What? My County Princess is to stay in the palace today?\" Qingshuang looked at the young eunuch who had come to deliver the message, her face full of astonishment.","The young eunuch nodded. \"County Princess Linghui must stay behind to review Her Majesty the Empress's medical records. She asked that you return first.\"","Watching the eunuch turn and leave, Qingshuang's mind buzzed, descending into a chaotic mess.","Would reviewing medical records really take this long? Could something have happened?","After her panicked gaze darted around for a moment, Qingshuang quickly turned, scrambled onto the carriage, and hurried out of the palace. She had to get back and tell the Eldest Young Master right away.","Ever since Song Shixue returned from the Cui Manor that afternoon, she had been waiting for Song Jinzhao. Yet, no matter how long she waited, there was no sign of her.","Seeing that the sky was about to turn dark, the anxious Song Shixue simply walked to the main gate to wait. That way, she would see the carriage the moment it returned.","When Song Qiming returned from his studies at the Imperial Academy, he saw from afar that Song Shixue was craning her neck, peering down the road. Seeing a carriage approach, she immediately rushed down the steps, only to let her shoulders droop in disappointment upon realizing it was Song Qiming.","\"Shixue, what are you doing?\" Song Qiming asked as he jumped down from the carriage.","Song Shixue took a deep breath and replied uneasily, \"I'm waiting for our older sister.\"","Song Qiming's eyes widened, and he blurted out, \"Sister hasn't returned from the palace yet?\"","The sun had already set. How could she be delayed for so long?","Song Shixue nodded, her brows furrowed into a tight knot.","\"Sister entered the palace nearly four hours ago. The eunuch who brought the summons said Her Majesty was suffering from migraines; it shouldn't take this long.\"","As the two were talking, Lanxi, who had walked out following Song Anhao, sharply spotted a carriage appearing at the intersection. It was Song Jinzhao's carriage.","He pointed at it and shouted to Song Shixue, \"They're back! The County Princess and the others are back!\"","Hearing his voice, Song Qiming and Song Shixue immediately turned their heads to the right. Seeing Qingshuang driving the carriage, they instantly breathed a sigh of relief.","The moment the carriage stopped, the two hurried forward to meet it.","But before the carriage even came to a complete halt, Qingshuang threw down the reins, jumped off, and sprinted toward Song Qiming.","\"The palace eunuch said the County Princess must stay in the palace to review Her Majesty's medical records. She won't be coming back today!\"","The brother and sister skidded to a halt, freezing in place.","Song Qiming furrowed his brows. \"Is Her Majesty severely ill?\"","Qingshuang replied, \"This servant was stopped outside the inner court and couldn't enter the rear palace. I don't know the state of Her Majesty's illness.\"","Song Shixue muttered to herself in confusion, \"Does reviewing medical records really take that much time? She can't even come back for the night.\"","Song Qiming, on the other hand, stared at Qingshuang with a pensive look. His sister was a County Princess, and she was meeting the Empress; why wouldn't they allow her to bring her maid? It felt as though she was being targeted.","Seeing that both of them looked so upset, and with his own stomach growling from hunger, Song Anhao couldn't help but reach out and grab Song Shixue's sleeve.","\"Second Sister, is Eldest Sister still not back?\"","Song Shixue looked down at her young brother. She bent over to pick him up, and when the back of her hand brushed against his small hand resting on his waist, she turned her hand to hold it.","\"Sister went to the palace to treat Her Majesty. She will be back a bit later. Your hands are so cold, are you not wearing enough clothes?\"","Song Anhao slowly shook his head. \"I am. It's just a bit chilly from the wind.\"","Song Qiming said, \"It's getting late. You take Anhao inside to eat first. I'm going to find my teacher.\"","\"Qingshuang, you drive the carriage.\" He wanted to ask her more questions in detail.","Song Shixue nodded. At a time like this, seeking out Master Ye was their only option.","\"Brother, come back early.\"","On the way to the Ye Manor, Qingshuang recounted everything, from the palace eunuch arriving with the summons to the young eunuch telling her that the County Princess had to stay in the palace today.","She detailed everything meticulously, leaving out not a single word, even describing their facial expressions.","Aside from the fact that Qingshuang hadn't been allowed inside, Song Qiming couldn't find anything overtly wrong.","Yet he still couldn't put his mind at ease; something just felt off.","The palace was heavily guarded, and his sister was a female family member. Staying overnight was inappropriate to begin with. Even if it was to review medical records, was there a need to be in such a rush?","By the time Song Qiming arrived at the Ye Manor, the sky had turned completely dark, and lanterns had already been hung at the gates.","Seeing that it was Song Qiming, the servants let him in without even announcing his arrival.","When he reached the dining hall, Ye Liangyu was having his meal.","Every year, after the imperial court resumed its duties following the holidays, there was a large backlog of government affairs, petitions, and official documents from the past half-month. Furthermore, the Censorate had to audit the court's finances, taxes, and expenditures from the previous year, sometimes even dispatching officials to local provinces for inspections. As a result, during this period, Ye Liangyu always worked until dark before returning home.","Seeing Song Qiming approach, Ye Liangyu put down his chopsticks and asked, \"Why have you come at this hour? Did you encounter a difficult problem in your studies?\"","Song Qiming lowered his eyelids slightly, shook his head, and said, \"It's not about my studies. It's my older sister.\"","\"At noon today, a verbal decree came from the palace, summoning my sister to treat Her Majesty's migraines. However, her maid waited outside the inner court for over two hours, and finally, a eunuch relayed a message saying that my sister would stay overnight in the palace to review Her Majesty's medical records. I am somewhat worried. Are Her Majesty's migraines truly that severe?\"","The gentle expression on Ye Liangyu's face faded. \"She entered the palace at noon?\"","Song Qiming nodded vigorously. \"Yes, Qingshuang just returned from the palace with the message.\"","Ye Liangyu's hand, resting on the dining table, tightened slightly. He then stood up and paced back and forth in the dining hall for a few steps.","He did not know much about the affairs of the rear palace, but an overnight stay was indeed rather strange.","After pondering for a moment, Ye Liangyu looked up at Yunhe and instructed, \"Go to the Xu Manor immediately. See if Imperial Physician Xu has returned and find out if you can gather any news.\"","\"Yes, sir,\" Yunhe bowed with a solemn expression and exited the dining hall.","Seeing that Song Qiming's brows were still furrowed, Ye Liangyu offered words of comfort, \"Do not worry too much. Your sister is now a County Princess and the savior of the Duke of Zhenguo. Even if she cannot cure Her Majesty's illness, neither the Emperor nor the Empress will place too much blame on her.\"","Song Qiming took a deep breath and slowly exhaled. \"Imperial power is absolute. Your student just can't help but feel uneasy.\"","\"Grumble~~\" Just as he sat down, a sound came from his stomach.","Ye Liangyu looked up and asked, \"You haven't eaten yet?\"","Song Qiming rubbed his temple, looking a bit embarrassed. \"I came in a hurry, so I haven't eaten.\"","Ye Liangyu looked at the servants. \"Go fetch a bowl of rice.\"","He sat back down and said to Song Qiming, \"It will take time for Yunhe to go and return. Keep this old man company and eat a little.\"","About two hours later, Yunhe pushed open the door to the main hall and walked in.","\"Reporting to the Master, Imperial Physician Xu said that County Princess Linghui is indeed at the Imperial Academy of Medicine reviewing Her Majesty's medical records, accompanied by Director Gu. The two of them spent the entire afternoon in the archive room where the medical records are stored, and they still hadn't come out by the time the Imperial Academy of Medicine ended its shifts.\"","\"When this servant was on his way back, I passed by the Gu Manor and specifically asked their gatekeeper. Director Gu hasn't returned home either.\"","Hearing this, Song Qiming breathed a sigh of relief. As long as neither of them had returned, it was fine.","Ye Liangyu said to him, \"Since she is staying in the archive room, she must be looking for past medical records. It's normal that she wouldn't be able to finish reading them all in a short time. See, I told you there was nothing to worry about.\"","Song Qiming stood up, cupped his hands, and took his leave. \"I have troubled you today, Teacher. Shixue is probably still at home, unable to sleep. Your student will head back now.\"","Ye Liangyu waved his hand. \"Go on back. The snowy roads are slippery, so tell your driver to be careful.\"","Song Qiming smiled and nodded."]},{"number":270,"title":"Chapter 270: Excessive Indulgence","paragraphs":["The storeroom of the Imperial Hospital was as bright as day in the night. More than a dozen candles were lit on the desks, the walls, and the floor stands, making the lighting no darker than daytime.","The two imperial physicians on night duty outside were greatly shocked to see that it was Gu Jupu who brought in the dinner and midnight snacks.","\"I have never seen Director Gu so attentive.\"","Smacking his lips, the physician shook his head with a sigh, \"Who told you not to be County Princess Linghui? If it weren't for the fact that there are no female physicians in the palace, the position of the Director might have even changed hands.\"","In the Imperial Hospital, seniority was secondary; those with better medical skills were more likely to rise. Seeing that Director Gu would retire in a few years, no one could yet say they were capable of taking his place.","Song Jinzhao flipped through the records from the year before Princess Yongjia's birth to three years after, and then went back to read the emperor's medical pulse records before Prince Qi was born. She confirmed that the signs of kidney deficiency began in the year Princess Yongjia was born.","It wasn't obvious during each routine pulse check, but looking at half a year's worth of records together made it very clear.","Song Jinzhao raised her eyes and looked at Gu Jupu, \"Since Princess Yongjia's birth, the Emperor gradually showed signs of kidney deficiency. Did no one in the Imperial Hospital notice?\"","Gu Jupu looked troubled, his chapped lips parting as if he wanted to speak but stopped.","Seeing this, Song Jinzhao raised an eyebrow and asked, \"Does Director Gu have some unspeakable secret?\"","Since Xiao Chengjing allowed Gu Jupu to stay by his side when summoning her, it meant he knew about the Emperor's infertility.","Gu Jupu slightly opened his lips and mumbled, his voice quieter than a fly.","\"When the Emperor was young, he was overly indulgent in the bedroom. Furthermore, after Princess Yongjia was born, no other concubines became pregnant for a long time, so he became a bit too hasty in having them serve him.\"","Seeing his mouth moving but the sound gradually disappearing, Song Jinzhao leaned in closer to listen carefully. \"And then? Your voice is too low, I can't hear you.\"","Gu Jupu exhaled, leaned in, and whispered so softly it was barely a breath, \"The Emperor used some secret medicines.\"","Song Jinzhao straightened her back, her eyes slightly complex.","Looking at the medical records before Prince Qi was born, Xiao Chengjing's body didn't seem this weak.","Just how indulgent did he have to be to drain himself so quickly?","\"How many concubines are there in the Emperor's harem in total?\"","Gu Jupu held out his right hand.","Song Jinzhao asked, \"Fifty?\"","Gu Jupu shook his head.","Song Jinzhao widened her eyes, her tone rising at the end, \"Five hundred?\"","Gu Jupu nodded. \"These are just the ones with official ranks registered in the books. The number of palace maids who have received the Emperor's grace is countless. Every year, a batch of them is granted special permission to leave the palace, so the exact number is impossible to count.\"","Song Jinzhao stared blankly with her mouth open, feeling nothing but astonishment.","What did he mean by impossible to count?","Had all the palace maids in the palace been favored by the Emperor?","Favouring them without giving them a title and then sending them out of the palace—could Xiao Chengjing not afford to keep them? He was already the Emperor, yet he still didn't want to take responsibility!","Did those palace maids who had been favored have anywhere else to go after leaving the palace?","Ordinary men wouldn't dare to marry them. If they hid the truth, they would be exposed on their wedding night, and their fate could easily be imagined.","No wonder the Empress was overly anxious and depressed. With a husband like this, it would be a miracle if she didn't suffer from depression.","However, despite all this, the imperial physicians had never mentioned this in previous medical records, which meant Xiao Chengjing's health must have been quite good in the past.","Seeing Song Jinzhao's unacceptable expression, Gu Jupu quickly tried to save face for the Emperor. \"Most of the current concubines in the palace are older. After Princess Yongjia was born, the Emperor frequently used medicine and worked hard for three years. After that, no more palace maids were favored.\"","Song Jinzhao looked away with an indescribable expression and stared at the air. It was probably a case of the spirit being willing but the flesh being weak.","It wasn't that he didn't want to show favor; he just couldn't get it up anymore.","With bedroom affairs so frequent they bordered on indulgence, coupled with the use of secret medicines, Song Jinzhao began to doubt her previous speculations.","Perhaps no one had poisoned Xiao Chengjing; he had ruined his own body.","Even if someone had poisoned him, that person might have already left the palace.","Ruining the innocence of so many palace maids without giving them a title, it wouldn't be strange if someone harbored hatred and poisoned him. Some might have even been forced.","Being stuck with such an irresponsible emperor, it was perfectly normal to be unwilling.","\"Besides the biological mothers of Prince Qi, Prince Ying, and Princess Yongjia, did no other women in the palace ever get pregnant?\"","Favouring so many people, as long as there was no contraception, there should have been quite a few pregnancies.","Gu Jupu replied, \"There were quite a few concubines who got pregnant, but the infighting in the harem was extremely fierce at that time. Many suffered miscarriages, and several babies died before they were even a month old.\"","\"Afterwards, the Emperor cleaned up the harem once, and then Princess Yongjia was born. But since then, no concubine has ever become pregnant again.\""]},{"number":271,"title":"Chapter 271: I Am Ninety Percent Certain","paragraphs":["As her voice faded, the hall fell so utterly silent that one could hear a single strand of hair scraping against the dust and floor tiles if it dropped.","Still kneeling on the floor, Song Jinzhao bowed low, touching her forehead to the ground.","She spoke with utmost solemnity, \"Your Majesty suffers from kidney deficiency and fatigue, and your vital essence is cold, which makes it difficult to produce heirs. The toll taken on your body over the years has been too severe. Coupled with advancing age, this is not something human effort can completely reverse.\"","Xiao Chengjing pursed his lips. His face darkened, and his voice carried a hint of simmering anger.","\"You have greatly disappointed We, County Princess.\"","Song Jinzhao kept her forehead against the floor. Only upon hearing Xiao Chengjing speak did she slowly straighten her upper body, a trace of hesitation flickering in her eyes.","\"Please forgive my inadequate medical skills, Your Majesty. However, if Your Majesty merely wishes for a few more heirs, I do have a method that might be worth a try.\"","Xiao Chengjing's tightly knitted brows relaxed slightly. \"Speak.\"","Taking a deep breath, Song Jinzhao said, \"I drafted a prescription last night that can grant Your Majesty immense vigor for a short period of time.\"","\"However, this method only treats the symptoms, not the root cause. It essentially concentrates Your Majesty's remaining kidney vitality to be expended within a specific timeframe. Once it is exhausted, your body will revert to its original state, and it will be exceedingly difficult to ever achieve such vigor again.\"","Xiao Chengjing narrowed his eyes. Standing nearby, Eunuch Zhao did not even dare to breathe too loudly.","\"How can you guarantee that the concubines I favor during this time will conceive?\"","Meeting Xiao Chengjing's gaze, Song Jinzhao replied, \"As long as Your Majesty follows my instructions, I am ninety percent certain.\"","Xiao Chengjing leaned back. \"Explain it to me in detail.\"","Song Jinzhao began, \"First, Your Majesty's body will require a month of conditioning, during which you must abstain from all intimate relations.\"","\"Simultaneously, I will need to select several concubines from the inner palace between the ages of twenty-six and thirty-five, and condition their bodies to an optimal state for conception.\"","Xiao Chengjing questioned this, \"Why between twenty-six and thirty-five? Shouldn't they be as young as possible?\"","Song Jinzhao met Xiao Chengjing's gaze levelly, not shrinking back in the slightest, projecting an air of absolute confidence.","\"Women between the ages of twenty-six and thirty-five have robust constitutions. They are well-suited for childbearing and are less prone to miscarriages.\"","Keep dreaming. There was no way she would let him ruin the younger girls.","Once his time was up, were they supposed to live as young widows for the rest of their lives?","Seeing Xiao Chengjing remain silent in apparent agreement, Song Jinzhao continued, \"After a month, Your Majesty will begin taking the medication. I will track the selected concubines' monthly cycles to determine their most fertile days. If Your Majesty shares a bed with them on those specific days, it will drastically increase the chances of conception.\"","Hearing this, Xiao Chengjing began tapping his fingers rhythmically against his thigh.","Given the circumstances, having a chance was better than having none at all.","Thinking of the constant scheming and sheer incompetence of Prince Qi and Prince Ying in the royal court, he realized that if he could just produce other sons, everything would become much easier to manage.","After a long moment of consideration, Xiao Chengjing spoke in a deep voice, \"We will do as you suggest. This matter must not be discovered by anyone.\"","Song Jinzhao curtsied gracefully. \"I will strictly obey Your Majesty's command.\"","\"Director Gu, you are to assist County Princess Linghui in selecting the concubines. This must be done with the utmost discretion; even the women themselves must not suspect a thing.\"","Gu Jupu knelt. \"This subject obeys the decree.\"","With the arrangements settled, Xiao Chengjing straightened his posture and addressed Song Jinzhao, \"Her Majesty the Empress is feeling unwell. County Princess Linghui, you are required to enter the palace every seven days to check on her pulse and ensure her well-being. Zhao Yande, you will make the necessary arrangements.\"","Standing to the side, Eunuch Zhao immediately bowed his head. \"This servant obeys the decree.\"","After exiting the side hall, Song Jinzhao left the palace alongside Gu Jupu.","As soon as she stepped out of the palace gates, she spotted a familiar carriage parked in the distance.","The moment she saw Song Jinzhao appear, Song Shixue, who had arrived early and waited for an hour, quickly emerged from the carriage cabin.","\"Sister!\" she called out, waving excitedly at Song Jinzhao.","Song Jinzhao smiled and turned to Gu Jupu. \"Since my family is here, I won't be needing a ride back in Director Gu's carriage.\"","Gu Jupu respectfully cupped his hands toward Song Jinzhao. \"This lower official bids the County Princess farewell.\"","Once seated inside the carriage, Song Shixue immediately asked Song Jinzhao what had happened in the palace the previous day.","She asked with a hint of uncertainty, \"Sister, are the Empress's headaches really that severe? Were you able to cure her?\"","Song Jinzhao shook her head. \"The Empress's headaches are a chronic ailment. It will take some time to cure her; it cannot be rushed.\"","\"From now on, I will have to enter the palace once every seven days. This treatment may need to continue for two or three months.\"","Song Jinzhao's tense shoulders relaxed. \"As long as she can be cured, that's fine. I was just afraid that if she wasn't, the Empress would blame you.\"","\"You didn't come home all night yesterday. If our brother hadn't gone to Lord Ye's residence to ask around and confirmed you were safe, I wouldn't have dared to close my eyes.\"","Song Jinzhao noticed the dark circles under her sister's eyes and gently ruffled Song Shixue's hair.","\"What is there to be afraid of? Even if I couldn't cure her, the Emperor wouldn't kill me. At most, he would scold me a few times to vent his anger.\"","Upon returning to the County Princess's estate, Song Shixue instructed the servants to go to the Imperial College and inform Song Qiming, just so he wouldn't be distracted with worry during his classes.","Having barely slept the entire night, Song Jinzhao ate her breakfast, crawled into bed, and slept soundly until the sun went down.","On the official road ten miles outside the city, Fushun gripped the reins. He was bundled up so tightly from head to toe that only his eyes were visible, leading a convoy of five carriages behind him.","After two long months of travel, they were finally arriving at the capital.","Resting on a warm couch heated by a fire kang, Song Jinzhao was reviewing the profiles of the thirty-four concubines that Gu Jupu had handed over to her.","The oldest was thirty-five, and the youngest was thirty. When the youngest had been favored by the Emperor back in the day, she had only been thirteen years old—a completely innocent child who knew nothing of the world.","Gu Jupu had outlined the past medical histories of all thirty-four women.","The records clearly detailed what illnesses they had suffered from and how long their recoveries took. Most importantly, it included precise notes on their monthly cycles, which was the detail Song Jinzhao cared about the most.","Song Jinzhao's gaze swept over the documents, and she eventually selected the fourteen best candidates.","Since this was his very last chance, she might as well let Xiao Chengjing produce a few more heirs.","With a larger number of children, they could always pick out a capable one.","It was better than only having one or two; if they were to unfortunately pass away prematurely, he truly would have no chances left.","Xuetuan strolled in through the door with a wobbly gait, carrying Song Anhao on its back.","\"Big Sister, Second Sister asked me to give this to you.\"","Song Anhao clung to Song Jinzhao's leg and held the object in his hands high up in the air.","Song Jinzhao closed the record book. When she saw clearly what it was, her gaze paused for a moment.","She reached out, taking the wooden object from Song Anhao's hands to examine it closely.","Eighteen square wooden pillars interlocked flawlessly to form an incredibly tight cube. It was indeed an Eighteen Arhats puzzle lock.","How did it end up here?","Walking in a few steps behind, Song Anhao saw Song Jinzhao staring at the Eighteen Arhats lock with great interest. A happy grin spread across her face as she said, \"I knew Big Sister would like it.\"","Song Jinzhao looked up and asked, \"Where did you get this?\"","Song Shixue scooped up Song Anhao, and they both climbed onto the warm kang. \"Young Master Cui gave it to me.\"","\"Yesterday at noon, our brother and Young Master Dongfang returned from the Imperial College. They mentioned that Young Master Dongfang's friend, Cui Zhengyang, had caught a cold that simply wouldn't go away. With the metropolitan examination fast approaching, they wanted to invite you over to treat him. When they found out you weren't home, they asked me to go take a look instead.\"","\"I spotted this puzzle lock on a shelf in his room. I thought it was quite novel and figured you would like it, so I took a few extra glances at it. Seeing that I was interested, Young Master Cui gave it to me as a gift.\""]},{"number":272,"title":"Chapter 272: The Lock of the Eighteen Arhats, The Second Batch of Potatoes Arrives in Beijing","paragraphs":["Song Jinzhao pulled at each wooden pillar, trying to find the loosest one.","\"Did Young Master Cui make this puzzle lock himself, or did someone give it to him?\"","Song Shixue answered, \"He said he made it himself, and no one has ever been able to take it apart. It's incredibly difficult.\"","Song Jinzhao's lips curled into a faint smile.","Back in college, she had a roommate who was obsessed with Lu Ban locks.","Her desk was covered in all kinds of burr puzzles. Not to mention the Eighteen Arhats lock, she even had the more difficult twenty-four prism and the ball-in-a-cage puzzles.","Whenever she had free time, she would tinker with them and often taught the rest of them how to play.","Song Jinzhao had seen the exact one Cui Zhengyang had given them; apart from the color of the wood, it was identical.","Her fingers slowly tugged at each wooden pillar, patiently feeling the resistance to find the loosest one to start with.","As Song Jinzhao pulled out the first pillar, the siblings' eyes widened simultaneously.","They had played with it for a long time last night while waiting for news, and no matter which piece they moved, it would get stuck. Yet their older sister had managed to pull one out so quickly!","One large and one small head bumped together as they stared at the Eighteen Arhats lock in Song Jinzhao's hands. They thought that after the first piece was removed, the rest would be quick, but it turned out that Song Jinzhao took even longer to remove the second piece than the first.","By the time it was completely dismantled, an hour had passed.","Song Shixue looked at the eighteen wooden pillars on the table. \"No wonder Young Master Cui said it was difficult. Even you took this long, Sister.\"","Song Jinzhao smiled gently and said, \"Taking this apart is indeed very difficult.\"","The first time she played with it, she had jammed it after just a few random moves. The second time, she tried for two days and still couldn't take it apart. In the end, she helplessly compromised and asked her roommate to teach her, even recording a video of it.","Song Jinzhao placed all the pillars onto a tray. \"Taking it apart isn't the hardest part; putting it back together is. I'll show you tomorrow.\"","Song Shixue said with joyful excitement, \"When I go to check on Young Master Cui tomorrow, I must tell him that you solved his lock in just an hour.\"","Song Anhao grabbed Song Jinzhao's fingers, swaying his round head as he acted spoiled. \"Sister, will you teach me?\"","As the three were talking, Qingshuang walked briskly in through the door.","\"Princess, Fushun has arrived. He is at the door with over three thousand catties of potatoes.\"","Song Jinzhao withdrew the hand that was rubbing Song Anhao's cheek, lifted the blanket, and got down from the heated brick bed.","\"How many people came? Have the kitchen prepare hot food and soup, and let them rest after they have eaten their fill.\"","Qingshuang said as they walked, \"This servant has already arranged it. There are six carts and twenty people in total. Seven of them are escorts Fushun hired in Anyang Prefecture.\"","When they reached the front hall, Fushun was talking to Lanxi.","\"When we set off, I specifically had people pad the bottom of the baskets with dried straw and spread another layer on top. Finally, when loading them onto the carriages, we covered them with two thick straw mats. Whenever it snowed on the road, we burned charcoal in the carriages. I guarantee not a single potato was frostbitten.\"","\"It is just that the cost was a bit high. If the Princess had not specially instructed it in her letter, I would have been reluctant to spend so much.\"","Lanxi pulled aside the straw on top of the bamboo baskets. The golden potatoes looked appetizing. \"There is no helping it for goods that are to be handed over to the imperial court.\"","\"Was the journey smooth?\" Song Jinzhao's voice sounded behind the two of them.","Fushun hurriedly turned around and immediately knelt upon seeing Song Jinzhao. \"This lowly one greets the Princess.\"","Song Jinzhao said, \"Rise.\"","After standing up, the smile on Fushun's face was as bright as a flower. \"Replying to the Princess, it was fairly smooth. We encountered a few highwaymen, but they were all dealt with by the escorts. Fortunately, they were just small-time thugs.\"","Seeing the servants unloading the bamboo baskets from the carriages, Song Jinzhao bent down and picked up a potato. Potatoes grown in winter greenhouses were a size smaller than those grown outdoors and harvested in autumn."]},{"number":273,"title":"Chapter 273: The Shocked Cui Zhengyang and the Secretly Active Gu Jupu","paragraphs":["\"What? County Princess Linghui solved my Eighteen Arhats puzzle in just an hour?\" Cui Zhengyang, who was sitting on the kang bed drinking his medicine, looked at Song Shixue in astonishment.","Song Shixue placed the pulse pillow back into her medical box. \"Yes, it only took her an hour. My older sister also said she would reassemble it today, mentioning that putting it back together is harder than taking it apart.\"","Cui Zhengyang sat there in a daze, unable to believe it. To think someone could actually solve the Eighteen Arhats puzzle he had made, and in merely an hour at that.","After staring blankly for a long while, Cui Zhengyang got down from the bed.","He slipped on his shoes, walked over to the bookshelf, and took out a twenty-four-pillar puzzle lock from the bottom drawer, handing it to Song Shixue.","\"This is a twenty-four-pillar puzzle lock I made. It's a bit more complex than the Eighteen Arhats one. Could I trouble Second Miss Song to pass this on to the County Princess?\"","Song Shixue took the twenty-four-pillar lock and examined it from all angles. This thing definitely wouldn't stump her sister.","\"Young Master Cui, my sister knows how to build hydraulic waterwheels and even wheelchairs, which are no simpler than this creation of yours. I really don't think this will be difficult for her.\"","Cui Zhengyang felt a bit dealt a blow by Song Shixue's blunt words. This was something he had spent several years figuring out.","\"Second Miss Song, just take it back with you. If the County Princess solves it, I will figure out an even harder one.\"","Song Shixue placed the twenty-four-pillar lock into her medical box.","\"Your priority right now is to recover. The metropolitan examination begins in just ten days, and I promised my brother and Young Master Dongfang that I would cure you.\"","Cui Zhengyang returned to the bed and covered his lower half with a blanket. \"Second Miss Song's medical skills are exquisite. My body already feels much better than yesterday.\"","Song Shixue said, \"You let your cold drag on for too long, and it has already damaged your lungs. Over the next two days, your body's reactions will be quite pronounced.\"","\"A sore throat, fever, full-body aches, and fatigue are all normal symptoms. Make sure to rest plenty and maintain a light diet. I will come back in two days.\"","Cui Zhengyang nodded. \"Thank you very much, Second Miss Song.\"","\"Mo Chen, see Second Miss Song out.\"","In the Imperial Academy of Medicine, Gu Jupu sat in his room, pondering how to send away the imperial physician responsible for conducting the routine health checkups for those fourteen concubines.","There were numerous concubines in the palace but few imperial physicians. With routine checkups required every half a month, each physician had to take charge of dozens of concubines.","Especially those of the lowest ranks, they were often assigned to the most junior physicians. These fourteen individuals were all handled by the same physician.","After a while, Gu Jupu stood up and headed to the Imperial Dispensary.","Seeing Gu Jupu enter, the Apothecary Official immediately stood up and walked out to welcome him.","\"Why has Director Gu come in person? If you need any medicine, just send someone to let us know, and I would personally deliver it.\"","Gu Jupu clasped his hands behind his back and said sternly, \"I am not here to fetch medicine. Where is your Director Sha? I have official business with him.\"","The Apothecary Official brought out a chair for Gu Jupu to sit. \"Director Gu, please wait a moment. I will go call for him right away.\"","Before long, the head of the Imperial Dispensary hurried over.","After the two sat down in the room, Gu Jupu spoke to him, \"Has the matter of the Imperial Dispensary sending personnel out of the palace to procure supplies this year been finalized? When will they depart?\"","The head of the Imperial Dispensary fixed his gaze on Gu Jupu, wondering why he would ask this. In the past, the Imperial Academy of Medicine never interfered in such matters.","Nevertheless, he answered truthfully, \"It has been settled. The head eunuch in charge of procurement will leave the palace tomorrow. Does Your Excellency wish to purchase some medicinal herbs?\"","Gu Jupu lightly stroked his beard and nodded.","\"The Empress in the palace is unwell. I need a batch of top-quality thousand-year-old ginseng to use in her medicine. I fear the procurement officers might buy inferior goods, so for this trip, I wish to dispatch an imperial physician to accompany them.\"","The head of the Imperial Dispensary furrowed his brows.","The ginseng typically purchased for the palace ranged from thirty to two hundred years old. A batch of thousand-year-old ginseng was far too high a demand.","According to custom, procuring expensive medicinal materials with special requirements indeed necessitated the accompaniment of someone from the Imperial Academy of Medicine; otherwise, a mistaken purchase could cause disastrous delays.","\"May I ask which imperial physician Your Excellency intends to send?\"","Gu Jupu replied, \"Imperial Physician Jiao Siqiao.\"","The head of the Imperial Dispensary nodded. \"In that case, let Imperial Physician Jiao set out tomorrow alongside the head eunuch in charge of procurement. However, the journey is long, and this trip will likely be very exhausting.\"","Gu Jupu said, \"Imperial Physician Jiao is still young and a rising star in the Imperial Academy of Medicine. It is only right that he gains some experience. Enduring a little hardship is nothing.\"","After returning to the Imperial Academy of Medicine, Gu Jupu reached out and tapped twice on Jiao Siqiao's desk. \"Follow me inside.\"","Completely baffled, Jiao Siqiao put down what he was holding and followed Gu Jupu into the room.","Gu Jupu instructed, \"Close the door.\"","Jiao Siqiao's heart began to drum. What matter required closing the door to speak with him alone?","Standing in front of the desk, Jiao Siqiao felt a numb tingling all over from being stared at so intently.","\"Tomorrow, the people from the Imperial Dispensary will leave the palace to procure medicinal herbs. This time, you will go with them.\"","Jiao Siqiao pointed at himself in disbelief. \"Me? Leave the palace to buy medicine?\"","Gu Jupu nodded. \"I need a batch of premium thousand-year-old ginseng. The eyes of those in the Imperial Dispensary are not discerning enough. Only if you go will I feel at ease.\"","Jiao Siqiao's heart instantly bloomed with joy. He hadn't expected Director Gu to trust him so much.","\"Rest assured, Director. I will definitely handle this matter flawlessly.\"","On second thought, he looked a bit troubled. \"Director, this month's routine pulse checkups have not yet been completed. Since I will be away from the palace for a long time, do the tasks on my hands need to be handed over to another imperial physician?\"","Gu Jupu said nonchalantly, \"Write down the tasks that need to be done and hand the paper to me. I will arrange the rest. Just focus on your departure.\"","A bit agitated with excitement, Jiao Siqiao cupped his hands and bowed to Gu Jupu. \"Thank you, Director. On this trip, I will certainly not disappoint your expectations.\"","In the evening, before leaving the palace, Jiao Siqiao organized the tasks on his hands and handed them over to Gu Jupu.","Looking at the thick stack in his hands, Gu Jupu frowned in dismay.","Flipping through it casually, there was a massive pile of matters. Just the concubines he was responsible for numbered thirty, and all the ones with the lowest statuses were assigned to him.","The next day, after Jiao Siqiao had set off, Gu Jupu called Imperial Physician Xu before him.","\"Imperial Physician Jiao has left the palace to procure medicinal herbs and will not return in the short term. A portion of the concubines under his care will be temporarily entrusted to you.\"","Gu Jupu gave him fifteen, keeping the remaining fifteen to handle personally. Among those, fourteen were the exact individuals Song Jinzhao had specifically named.","In the afternoon, faced with Gu Jupu personally taking their pulses, these fifteen concubines were all astounded. Given their status, how could they be worthy of having the Director of the Imperial Academy of Medicine treat them?","Only upon asking did they learn that it was because Imperial Physician Jiao was not in the palace, so Gu Jupu was temporarily stepping in to help.","When the other imperial physicians found out, they all praised Gu Jupu for being considerate of his subordinates, taking the burden upon himself instead of delegating it to others.","Some even ran up to Gu Jupu to volunteer their services, but he rejected them all.","Sitting in his chair, Imperial Physician Xu was deeply puzzled. Why had he given none to anyone else, yet specifically handed fifteen over to him?","He quietly asked another imperial physician sitting next to him, \"Did I somehow offend the Director?\"","His colleague patted his shoulder encouragingly and said, \"How could that be? The Director entrusting this task solely to you shows that he values you. Others couldn't get it even if they wanted to.\"","Imperial Physician Xu thought about it and felt that made sense; otherwise, why didn't he seek out someone else?","Last time at the Duke of Zhenguo's estate, only he and Director Gu had witnessed the entire surgical procedure with their own eyes.","Ever since then, he really did start talking to her more often, and his demeanor became much gentler than before. This must mean he truly valued her."]},{"number":274,"title":"Chapter 274: End-of-Month Report from Five Shopkeepers","paragraphs":["After leaving the palace in the evening, Gu Jupu went straight to the County Princess's estate to deliver the results of the day's routine pulse diagnosis.","Song Jinzhao looked at the first sheet and found no issues. \"I will write down the warming and nourishing prescription tonight. Please come and pick it up tomorrow morning, Director Gu.\"","Gu Jupu breathed a sigh of relief. \"No problem, I will come over tomorrow morning.\"","As the metropolitan examination approached, both Prince Qi and Prince Ying focused all their attention on the imperial exams, paying no mind to matters of the inner palace.","As for the imperial concubines, the ones involved were merely low-ranking women who had been out of favor for years. To put it harshly, they were little better than palace maids, so the higher-ranking consorts paid them no heed.","Instead, it was Xiao Chengjing's high regard for the Empress that sparked their jealousy, leading them to make many sour remarks behind her back.","...","After classes ended at the Imperial College, Dongfang Yukun grabbed Song Qiming's arm and said, \"I went to the Cui residence last night to see Cui Zhengyang. His complexion looked much better than it did two days ago. Many thanks to your sister.\"","Song Qiming closed his book. \"Shixue said that although Cui Zhengyang's illness will be cured before the metropolitan examination, his physical strength definitely won't fully recover in such a short time.\"","\"The exam lasts for nine consecutive days, and candidates are not allowed to leave during each session. The conditions in the examination hall are relatively poor. I'm just worried his body won't be able to handle it, which might affect his performance.\"","Dongfang Yukun's eyes drooped, his expression turning somewhat dejected.","\"We have done all we can. When the time comes, we can only let him leave it to fate.\"","Song Qiming joked, \"Aren't you afraid that people will say you won an unfair victory?\"","Dongfang Yukun replied, \"People can say whatever they want. I can't stop them.\"","Song Qiming smiled and shook his head.","Rather than proving to outsiders that he was more talented than Cui Zhengyang, Dongfang Yukun was more worried that Cui Zhengyang wouldn't achieve a good rank due to his illness.","To put it plainly, he genuinely cared about Cui Zhengyang as a person, rather than finding a doctor for him out of mere competitiveness.","On the last day of the first lunar month, the managers of the five shops brought their account books and profits to the County Princess's estate to report their recent business operations to Song Jinzhao.","The tea shop manager reported, \"Since the tea shop opened, the foot traffic for the first three days was between eight hundred and a thousand. After the promotions ended, the number of customers started to drop. Now it has stabilized at around four hundred and fifty to five hundred and fifty a day. In the twenty-three days since opening, we have made a total profit of two hundred and thirty-six taels.\"","The braised food shop manager said, \"Our daily braised food is never enough to meet the demand. We have already increased our staff twice. Excluding costs, our daily profit is now around sixteen taels of silver. This month, we have earned a total of three hundred and twelve taels.\"","\"However, a few days ago, I saw a newly opened braised food shop in the outer city. They sell exactly the same things we do, but the taste is much inferior.\"","The barbecue shop manager stepped forward. \"I also discovered a barbecue shop in the outer city that opened by copying us. If this continues, someone will definitely open a shop in the inner city, which will surely affect our business.\"","...","The five of them talked one after another, spit flying as they spoke in front of Song Jinzhao.","Every single one of them was worried that the emergence of competitors would affect their shops' business.","The incessant chatter made Song Jinzhao's ears ache.","\"Enough,\" she said. \"It is impossible to run a business without competitors ever appearing. You just need to protect your recipes and make sure they don't leak out.\"","\"In the short term, no matter how well they copy us, their taste cannot surpass ours. Since the business in the shops is good, what you should be thinking about is opening branch stores as soon as possible to gather all the customers in the capital.\"","\"I want to see new stores open within a month. You will decide everything yourselves, from selecting locations to hiring staff. The profit of the first month after opening will be your evaluation standard. Show this County Princess your capabilities, and absolutely do not disappoint me.\"","The five men straightened their backs, their nerves instantly tensing.","During their training, it was mentioned that there was a grading system among the managers. This affected their monthly salaries and year-end dividends. If they performed poorly, they would be trampled by the others, so they could not afford to take it lightly.","A few days later, Song Jinzhao entered the palace. First, she went to diagnose the Empress, and then she was taken to the Funing Hall to examine Xiao Chengjing.","\"Please rest assured, Your Majesty. The tonic has already taken effect, and everything is proceeding according to plan.\"","Xiao Chengjing gently raised his eyebrows and smiled calmly. \"I naturally trust the medical skills of County Princess Linghui.\"","\"The metropolitan examination is in a few days. How is your younger brother preparing?\"","Song Jinzhao calmly curled her lips and replied, \"My younger brother has been studying at the Imperial College these past few days. The chancellor and instructors responsible for teaching are not only highly knowledgeable but also diligent and responsible. I haven't had to worry much.\"","In a good mood, Xiao Chengjing did not hold back his praise. \"I heard that your brother gets along quite well with Dongfang Yukun. I suppose talented people find it easier to appreciate one another.\"","\"The officials in the court are all advancing in age. It is time for some fresh blood. The vitality of youth is much more pleasing to my eyes.\"","After leaving Funing Hall, Song Jinzhao sat in a sedan chair and was carried toward the palace exit. This was arranged by Eunuch Zhao when she entered the palace today.","It was said that the distance from the inner court to Kunning Palace was a bit far, so the Emperor specially rewarded Song Jinzhao with a sedan chair for transportation.","Walking out of the inner court gates, Song Jinzhao was just about to board her carriage when Princess Yongjia chased after her from behind.","\"Song Jinzhao!\"","Song Jinzhao pulled back the leg she had lifted to step up, turned around, and curtsied to Xiao Yongjia, who was running toward her.","\"Your subject Song Jinzhao pays her respects to Princess Yongjia.\"","Panting heavily, Xiao Yongjia asked, \"Where did you go? The guards said you hadn't left the palace, and I've been looking for you for ages.\"","Song Jinzhao replied, \"The Emperor was concerned about Her Majesty the Empress's condition, so he sent someone to bring me to Funing Hall to inquire about it.\"","\"Is there something Your Highness needs from me?\"","Her breathing calming down, Xiao Yongjia's chest wasn't heaving as much anymore. She asked, \"Have you been to the estate of Duke Zhenguo recently?\"","Song Jinzhao answered, \"I went there four days ago for a follow-up consultation with Duke Zhenguo.\"","Duke Zhenguo's injuries were recovering very well. In another half month, she wouldn't need to go there anymore.","A trace of worry colored Xiao Yongjia's eyes. \"Not long ago, the Duke Zhenguo estate went to the Imperial Academy of Medicine to request an imperial physician, saying that the Dowager Duchess is not doing well.\"","Her hand grabbed, Song Jinzhao asked, \"Has the imperial physician gone?\"","Xiao Yongjia pulled Song Jinzhao onto the carriage. \"The imperial physician has already gone, but aren't your medical skills even better than theirs? Hurry up and come take a look with me.\"","Xiao Yongjia's carriage was both spacious and fast. It didn't take long for them to arrive at the gates of the Duke Zhenguo estate.","Seeing that the arrivals were Princess Yongjia and Song Jinzhao, the gate guards hastily knelt to pay their respects.","\"Greetings to Princess Yongjia.\"","\"Greetings to County Princess Linghui.\""]},{"number":275,"title":"Chapter 275: Lady Chu's Passing, the Imperial Examination Begins","paragraphs":["Xiao Yongjia completely ignored them, leading Song Jinzhao directly to the courtyard where Dowager Duchess Chu resided.","A familiar scene unfolded once again, identical to the time when the Duke of Zhenguo had his accident.","The servants in the courtyard kept their heads bowed, not daring to make a sound, while the Chu family members crowded the main room inside.","\"Princess Yongjia and County Princess Linghui have arrived!\"","At the guide's loud announcement, everyone turned their heads simultaneously. Upon recognizing the arrivals, they successively knelt to pay their respects.","\"Greetings to Princess Yongjia.\"","Upon seeing Song Jinzhao, the Duke of Zhenguo, whose injuries had yet to fully heal, rushed out of the room. \"County Princess, I beg of you, please save my mother.\"","Stepping into the inner chamber, Imperial Physician Xu, who was standing by the bed, made way and silently gave Song Jinzhao a meaningful look.","If it were an illness, he believed Song Jinzhao could cure it. However, Dowager Duchess Chu was simply of advanced age; her body and spirit had reached their natural limits. She was naturally passing away, and there was no medical cure for that.","Lying on the bed, Dowager Duchess Chu's eyes were mere slits. Her hair was white, and the hand exposed outside the quilt was so pale it was almost transparent. A clear jade bracelet hung loosely on her shriveled wrist, making it look even thinner. The veins bulged beneath her skin, resembling withered, desiccated wood.","Her vital energy was dissipating, and the balance of yin and yang was on the verge of collapsing.","It was the pulse of a lamp running out of oil; her life was slowly fading away.","Song Jinzhao stood up and looked at the Duke and Duchess of Zhenguo, as well as Chu Liuyun. Stepping out of the inner chamber, she shook her head and said, \"The Dowager Duchess is of advanced age. Having experienced such profound grief, she has reached the end of her life. It will likely happen today or tomorrow. Please prepare yourselves for the loss.\"","The Duke of Zhenguo's pupils dilated in shock. Unable to accept it, he froze in place, his hands hanging by his sides unconsciously clenching into fists.","After a wave of sorrow, the Chu family members entered the inner chamber to kneel by the bed and accompany her, while outsiders retreated from the room to wait in the courtyard.","Through the window, Xiao Yongjia saw a tear slip down Chu Liuyun's cheek. She looked at Song Jinzhao with heartache.","\"Is there truly no way at all? When I came over during the Lantern Festival, the Dowager Duchess still looked perfectly fine.\"","Song Jinzhao said with a calm expression, \"Birth, aging, illness, and death are the normal course of human life; no one can avoid them. I am not a deity, and I possess no elixir of immortality.\"","That evening, paper money was hung before the gates of the Zhenguo Duke's estate. The news of Dowager Duchess Chu's passing spread rapidly in a very short amount of time.","The next day, before the morning court session even began, the Duke of Zhenguo's memorial requesting a leave of absence for mourning was presented to the Emperor by the Ministry of Personnel.","Xiao Chengjing stared at the heart-wrenching words of absolute grief on the memorial, the blurred strokes faintly smudged by tears.","He set the memorial down and gazed out at the empty space ahead.","\"Draft a decree.\"","Everyone in the room instantly dropped to their knees.","\"I have heard of Dowager Duchess Chu's passing and feel profound sorrow. I posthumously bestow upon her the title of Dowager Madame Zhuangjing. The Ministry of Rites is to immediately draft the official edict.\"","\"Dispatch the Minister of Personnel, Dongfang Shaoting, and the Director of Ceremonial, Eunuch Zhuo Yan, to go to the Zhenguo Duke's estate to offer sacrifices on My behalf.\"","By the time the imperial decree arrived at the Zhenguo Duke's estate, the interior was already awash in white mourning garb.","Kneeling on the ground, Chu Liuyun was clad in coarse hemp mourning clothes.","The Duke of Zhenguo, his injuries still unhealed, knelt at the very front of the mourning hall with a hunched back. His lifeless eyes stared at the spirit tablet placed in the hall, his eye sockets swollen like spheres.","Dongfang Shaoting unrolled the imperial decree and began to read, his tone heavy and his voice drawn out.","After the reading was finished, the Duke of Zhenguo raised his hands above his head and, face devoid of expression, knocked his forehead heavily against the ground.","\"This subject thanks His Majesty for his immense grace.\"","Looking at the Duke of Zhenguo, who seemed to have aged significantly all at once, Dongfang Shaoting could not help but offer words of comfort. \"The Dowager Duchess has passed. I pray the Duke restrains his grief.\"","With the Duke of Zhenguo losing his mother and the Emperor personally bestowing a posthumous title, mourners came in an endless stream throughout the entire day.","From minor ninth-rank officials of the capital to the first-rank Grand Secretaries of the Cabinet, they all brought their families to offer their condolences.","Following behind Song Jinzhao, Song Qiming bowed and offered incense to the mourning hall. His gaze swept over the coffin resting in the room, and he could not help but think of his parents buried in their hometown.","He missed them a little.","\"His Highness, the Prince of Qi, has arrived.\"","\"His Highness, the Prince of Ying, has arrived.\"","The crowd turned and bowed. \"Greetings to His Highness, the Prince of Qi. Greetings to His Highness, the Prince of Ying.\"","A pair of black satin boots embroidered with gold trim stopped before the Duke of Zhenguo.","Xiao Rongyan supported the Duke's arm and comforted him earnestly, \"Please, Duke of Zhenguo, restrain your grief.\"","From the corner of his eye, Chu Liuyun caught the deliberately feigned sorrow on Xiao Rongyan's face. He could not help but clench his jaw, a dark gleam flashing in his eyes.","If it were not for him causing his father to be severely injured, his grandmother would not have suffered such a tragic bout of grief.","The instigator coming here now to put on a hypocritical act was simply disgusting.","Seeing that many courtiers crowded around to flatter the two princes after they finished their sacrifices, Song Jinzhao silently took Song Qiming and turned to leave.","Nowadays, the eyes of the court officials were entirely fixed on the two princes. It was unknown how things would change once the new prince was born.","Before the funeral arrangements at the Zhenguo Duke's estate were even finished, the metropolitan examination arrived.","The day before the examination, Ye Liangyu specifically called Song Qiming to his residence for a solemn word of advice.","\"Relax, and do not be nervous. You are still young, so do not put too much pressure on yourself.\"","He reached out and gently patted Song Qiming's shoulder. \"Do your best. I believe you will definitely rank among the top.\"","Song Qiming bowed with his hands clasped, brimming with confidence. \"Rest assured, Teacher. Your student will certainly pass.\"","In the mock metropolitan examinations at the Imperial College, Song Qiming's scores had consistently ranked in the top three. He had the confidence to pass.","At three quarters past the hour of Mao, the sky was still dark, but the entrance to the examination compound was already packed with a massive crowd.","With several thousand candidates, along with the pageboys and relatives who came to see them off, the hard stone pavement had literally been trampled into forming several cracks.","A ring of massive lanterns hung around the entrance of the examination compound, their combined length spanning hundreds of zhang.","The candlelight illuminated face after face filled with a thirst for success, intertwining calmness and urgency, painting a picture of candidates rushing to the winter examination compound.","Song Qiming gathered his thick cotton coat tighter around himself. Facing the expectant gazes of his older and younger sisters, he smiled and said, \"Don't worry, Sister. The metropolitan examination won't stump me.\"","Song Jinzhao glanced at the examination compound gates that were currently being opened and gave Song Qiming a gentle nod.","\"Your sister has faith in you.\"","Gifted, capable of enduring hardship, and possessing strong self-discipline—ever since Song Qiming entered the private academy to study, his academic progress had never given Song Jinzhao cause for worry.","As the examination compound gates were fully opened, armored guards holding weapons stood in formation at the entrance.","An elderly man dressed in a scarlet official robe stepped out from within the gates, his sharp gaze sweeping over the thousands of candidates present.","\"By imperial decree, the Dragon Gate is opened. Students, heed your orders: First, verify your identities; Second, undergo a full body search; Third, collect your examination papers; Fourth, proceed to your respective examination cells.\"","\"Anyone found smuggling hidden materials, making loud noises, or colluding will be stripped of their scholarly honors at best, or imprisoned and exiled at worst. I expect you all to conduct yourselves accordingly.\"","As the elderly man stepped back, an armored guard wielding a weapon raised his voice to the sky and shouted, \"Body searches commence! Form a line!\"","The tightly packed line, chest-to-back, began to slowly inch forward. Song Qiming turned his head and waved to Song Jinzhao.","Waiting until his figure had completely disappeared, Song Jinzhao reached out to brush the dewdrops from Song Shixue's hair. \"Let's return home. We will come back in three days.\"","The metropolitan examination was divided into three sessions. Each session required staying inside for three days, and one could only come out once the session concluded.","Song Shixue nodded obediently and followed Song Jinzhao onto the carriage."]},{"number":276,"title":"Chapter 276: Activate Backup Exam Questions","paragraphs":["Sitting on the stool in his examination cell, Song Qiming heard nothing but the sounds of footsteps and the grinding of ink around him. It sounded like mice gnawing on wood, making him uncontrollably tense and panicked.","As the exam was about to begin, just as the outer curtain official was about to open the sealed exam questions, a dark blue figure hurriedly lifted the door curtain and walked in.","Flicking his whisk high and resting it on his elbow, Zhao Yande took an imperial edict from his sleeve and unfolded it.","\"The Emperor decrees: the first session of the metropolitan examination shall use the backup exam questions.\"","The room was quiet at first, and then instantly erupted into an uproar.","\"The exam is about to start, why would the Emperor suddenly change the questions?\"","\"What backup questions? Were backup questions even prepared for this metropolitan exam?\"","The outer curtain official holding the sealed bag took the imperial edict, somewhat at a loss, and asked Zhao Yande in confusion.","\"Eunuch Zhao, where are these backup exam questions?\"","He had not received any news about this at all.","Since when did the metropolitan exam have backup questions? Wasn't there always only one set?","Zhao Yande raised his chin and said righteously, \"They will be delivered immediately.\"","As soon as he finished speaking, an armored soldier walked in holding a sealed bag, exactly the same as the one in the outer curtain official's hand.","Everyone was astonished. There really were backup questions? Had the Emperor prepared these long ago?","The thousands of candidates sitting in their cells were completely unaware of what had happened in the room. Everyone was anxiously waiting for the exam questions to be distributed.","Once the questions were announced, Song Qiming thought for a moment before he started writing on his draft paper.","In contrast, the candidate sitting opposite Song Qiming was filled with confusion when he saw the questions.","Why was it different from what was agreed upon? It was completely poles apart.","There were many candidates in the examination hall who had the same reaction, sitting on their stools unable to figure it out.","It was impossible that they were deceived, but what was going on now? Could they have been discovered?","The more they thought about it, the more panicked they became. Their minds turned to mush, and they couldn't remember anything.","Song Qiming strictly managed his time for eating, sleeping, and waking up. His body, accustomed to practicing martial arts year-round, allowed him to easily cope with the cold and damp environment of the examination cell.","On the other side, Cui Zhengyang, who had just recovered from a severe illness, was wrapped in a thick fox fur coat, not daring to let any draft in.","The edge of the fox fur coat had been cut open by the inspecting official with a knife for checking. Cold wind sneaked in through the opening, so Cui Zhengyang used his buttocks and thighs to press down on the torn spot.","The full three days of exam time were agonizingly long for everyone.","As the drumbeat signaling the submission of papers rang out, some sighed in relief, some pulled their hair, and some even wiped away tears over their answer sheets.","Song Qiming slowly organized his exam papers. It wasn't until he handed them over to the collecting official that the first heavy stone hanging in his heart was finally lifted.","At a quarter to four in the afternoon, the main gates of the examination compound slowly opened, and a massive crowd of people flowed out, accompanied by chattering voices.","The sharp-eyed Song Jinzhao spotted Song Qiming in the crowd at a glance and immediately led her people to greet him.","Song Qiming, who was being squeezed like a twisted dough stick in the crowd, suddenly felt his sleeve being grabbed. He turned his head, and a smile blossomed on his face.","\"Sister.\"","Song Jinzhao and Song Shixue each pulled one of his sleeves, dragging Song Qiming out of the flow of people, while Lanxi and the others were responsible for holding back the surging crowd.","It wasn't until they climbed into the carriage that everyone breathed a sigh of relief.","Suddenly relaxing, Song Qiming now felt a deep sense of drowsiness and could not help but yawn.","Song Jinzhao didn't ask him how he performed but instead said, \"Dinner is already prepared at the manor. You can eat as soon as we get back.\"","There was no real break between the three exam sessions; they could only hurry to wash up, eat, and sleep, lest they fail to wake up with enough energy the next day.","Upon returning home, Song Qiming first had a hearty meal, then quickly took a bath and went straight to meet the Duke of Zhou in his dreams.","Unlike the majority of people who hurried to rest, a small group of people rushed home and immediately started complaining.","\"Father, the exam questions were completely different from what you told me!\"","\"How could that be? Are you sure they were different?\" Teng Fei, the Vice Director of the Ministry of War, frowned and stood up, his face looking extremely stern.","Teng Shaoqin stomped his foot hard. \"I took the exam myself, how could I not know? They were completely unrelated, without the slightest similarity.\"","\"What you told me was 'He who uses virtue to practice benevolence is a true king,' but what was written on it was 'He who uses force while pretending to be benevolent is a hegemon.'\"","\"And then there was 'When a gentleman takes office, he carries out his righteousness,' versus 'When the Way prevails in the world, show yourself; when it does not, hide yourself.' One is about entering society and the other is about withdrawing from it. They are in completely opposite directions...\"","With every sentence Teng Shaoqin spoke, the frown on the face of Teng Fei, the Vice Director of the Ministry of War, deepened.","The exam questions were told to him by His Highness the Prince of Qi. How could there be a mistake?","Teng Shaoqin sat down with a look of utter defeat. \"I definitely won't pass to become a tribute student this time.\"","\"Father, who exactly told you these exam questions?\"","The same situation was happening simultaneously in the manors of several court ministers. Not long after, these people split into two factions and hurriedly rushed towards the Prince of Qi's Manor and the Prince of Ying's Manor.","Xiao Rongche, who was drinking wine and listening to music in his manor, suddenly heard this news and found it unbelievable.","\"How can this be? Are you certain that the questions for this metropolitan exam were different from what I said?\"","The official whose son had participated in the exam nodded vigorously. \"My son told me about it the moment he returned.\"","He asked uncertainly, \"Your Highness, was the previous information incorrect, or were the exam questions changed at the last minute? Could our scheme have been discovered?\"","At this moment, the expression on Xiao Rongche's face had turned extremely ugly.","He turned and instructed his trusted aide, \"Go to the examination compound immediately and find Yun Simiao. See what exactly is going on.\"","The subordinate responded heavily, \"Yes, your subordinate will do it right away.\"","On the other side, the situation at the Prince of Ying's Manor was exactly the same.","Teng Fei looked at Xiao Rongyan, whose brows were tightly furrowed, and his heart sank deeper and deeper.","The two groups of people dispatched arrived almost simultaneously at the courtyard where the examiners were staying within the examination compound.","Upon seeing the armored soldiers standing guard at the gate, they walked a lap around the courtyard and discovered that the entire area was completely surrounded by the armored military.","Realizing something was wrong, both sides swiftly turned around and ran back to report the news.","\"Your Highness, the courtyard where the examiners are staying is completely surrounded by armored soldiers. They are armed with spears and bows. Let alone finding someone to pass a message, not even a bird could fly in.\"","The personal bodyguard knelt before the Prince of Ying, his back breaking out in a cold sweat from anxiety.","Teng Fei's legs went weak, and he fell to his knees on the ground, his trembling voice filled with terror.","\"We are doomed now. The Emperor has surely found out.\"","Bribing examiners and leaking exam questions—once discovered, meant beheading.","Xiao Rongyan sharply reprimanded, \"With me here, what are you panicking for!\"","\"Imperial Father has not summoned us; perhaps there is another reason for this.\"","\"You go back and wait for news first. Once I have investigated the course of events clearly, I will send someone to inform you. Let your son participate in tomorrow's exam as usual. Pretend that nothing has happened. Whatever you do, do not lose your composure and expose yourself.\"","When Teng Fei left the Prince of Ying's Manor, his footsteps were unsteady.","While descending the steps, he was not paying attention, twisted his ankle, and rolled down. His forehead hit the axle of the carriage, and a large lump swelled up on the spot."]},{"number":277,"title":"Chapter 277: Exam Over, Song Gaoli Under Immense Pressure","paragraphs":["The next two exams, just like the first one, had their questions swapped for backup ones right before the test began.","The completely unaware candidates racked their brains in their examination cells, writing furiously.","The external officials responsible for invigilation were already overwhelmed with swirling thoughts, their minds buzzing like a beehive poked with a stick.","Not daring to ask around, they could only bottle up their anxieties and wait for the exams to end.","Once all three exams were over, the candidates walking out of the examination compound felt as if a heavy burden had been lifted. Aside from relief, their bodies felt nothing but sheer exhaustion.","Moving forward with the surging crowd, Song Gaoli looked around at his peers, feeling an ever-growing heaviness in his heart.","When he came to the capital last year, his mindset was just to give it a try, thinking it wouldn't matter if he failed. But now, the pressure weighing on him was unprecedentedly immense.","Although he felt more confident about his performance this time, he still lacked absolute certainty, experiencing a panicky sensation of floating in the air without being able to land.","Inside Chongde Pavilion, fifty-two bronze lotus lamps encircled the room, and a separate desk lamp sat on each person's desk, illuminating the space so brightly that even a speck of dust on the wooden floor could be seen clearly.","Stacks of shuffled answer sheets were placed on the desks. Yun Simiao looked at the top paper, his back that had been sweating cold sweat for nine days now feeling as freezing as a block of ice.","Xiao Chengjing's sudden move to change the exam questions had caught him completely off guard. For nine whole days, Yun Simiao's heart had not known a moment of peace.","He had wanted to pass a message to Prince Ying, but upon stepping out, he found that the guards outside Chongde Pavilion had been replaced by the Ironclad Army at some unknown point.","There were many of them, standing guard from morning till night, and there was not a single other soul in sight outside.","After suffering through nine whole days of torment, his emotions transitioning from anxiety to numbness, Yun Simiao's mind was now left with only one thought: leave it to fate.","Beneath the plaque that read Selecting Talent for the Nation, the chief examiner of this metropolitan examination, Left Vice Minister of Revenue Jing Yunli, swept his deep, dark gaze over everyone present.","With a heavy slap of his palm against the table, the grading for this metropolitan examination officially began.","Twenty-five pairs of hands moved simultaneously. One by one, the answer sheets were marked with circles, ticks, dots, and lines by the grading examiners brushes.","Among them, very few received circles. When encountering an exceptionally outstanding paper, an examiner might even write the word Recommend at the top of the scroll.","Candles as thick as an arm burned down one after another, and the only sound left in the room was the rustling of turning pages.","The entire grading and evaluation process for the metropolitan examination would last for over twenty days.","During this period, none of the examiners responsible for grading could step out of Chongde Pavilion. They graded from morning until night every day, only able to sleep late in the evening.","In contrast, the candidates who had finished the exam were much more relaxed.","Their first day out of the compound was spent sleeping soundly. After waking up naturally, they would shave, wash their hair, and bathe, then change into clean clothes and go out for a massive feast, wishing they could make up for all the hardships of the past nine days in one go.","Once their bodies recovered, many began gathering in the various guild halls around the capital to discuss the exam questions and their respective essays.","From the nuances of the classics and histories to the preferences of the various examiners, and even some baseless inside rumors, they could discuss these topics for days on end.","On the afternoon of the second day after the exam ended, Song Qiming brought Song Gaoli to the Ye residence.","After reading Song Qiming's recreated exam paper from memory, Ye Liangyu revealed a satisfied smile.","He praised with great confidence, No problem at all. It will definitely rank in the upper-middle tier.","Hearing that Song Qiming had done well, Song Gaoli, who was holding his own paper, felt even more nervous.","Seeing Song Gaoli's hand trembling as he handed over his paper, Ye Liangyu couldn't help but sigh inwardly.","He had helped as much as he could, and he was well aware of Song Gaoli's performance at the Imperial Academy.","It could be said that he forgot to eat and sleep, working tirelessly day and night, and his attitude in class was also extremely proactive.","Compared to the three months he received his guidance before the provincial qualifying exam back then, his level of effort was unimaginably higher.","But ultimately, his foundation was a bit weak, and his time at the Imperial Academy had been too short. Looking at his current state, it seemed he still lacked confidence.","Taking a deep breath, Ye Liangyu lowered his head and began to read the paper carefully.","Song Gaoli clenched his hands tightly, staring intently at Ye Liangyu without blinking.","Any micro-expression on Ye Liangyu's face would make Song Gaoli's heart race, pounding in his chest as if it were about to leap out.","When he saw Song Gaoli's unique interpretation of he who uses force while pretending to be benevolent is a hegemon in the classics section, the hand Ye Liangyu used to hold the paper twitched.","His tightly furrowed brows relaxed slightly, and a flash of surprise crossed his eyes.","The expected situation of empty words and armchair theorizing did not occur; instead, the thesis was demonstrated with small but dense real-world examples.","The further he read, the more Ye Liangyu's brows relaxed. A smile of appreciation gradually filled his eyes, and the corners of his mouth unconsciously curled into a faint arc.","Ye Liangyu spent more time on Song Gaoli's paper than on Song Qiming's. The former was impeccable, while the latter required finding bright spots amidst plain and unadorned sentences.","Ye Liangyu would frown when he saw weak points, and his brows would relax when he spotted highlights.","After finishing the recreated papers for all three exams, Ye Liangyu's mood was somewhat complex.","Under the intense pressure of cramming, Song Gaoli's progress was very obvious.","If he had been given a little more time, perhaps he would have performed much better than he did now.","Seeing that Ye Liangyu was taking a long time to speak, Song Gaoli couldn't help but ask softly, Lord Ye, how did I do?","Ye Liangyu looked up at him, his fingers continuously tapping on the table, his mind wavering.","Finally, he squeezed out a sentence: You barely met the standard but have shortcomings. There is a chance, but it is very risky. It will depend on luck.","The light in Song Gaoli's pupils instantly dimmed, and a deep sense of disappointment showed between his brows.","Was it still not enough after all?","Gaoli has always had good luck, there is definitely a chance.","A crisp and clear voice rang out in his ears. Song Qiming slapped Song Gaoli on the shoulder, his face full of confidence.","Song Gaoli's heavy heart was not comforted by this. He forced a stiff smile, I hope so.","Ye Liangyu stood up and said to the two of them, Until the results are out, anything is possible. You have worked hard during this time. Rest well and just wait for the results to be posted.","The two nodded.","As soon as Song Gaoli returned to the Duan residence, he was cornered by Duan Yanhua.","With eyes full of expectation, he asked, What did Vice Censor-in-Chief Ye say?","Song Gaoli gave a helpless, bitter smile, Teacher, haven't you already read it? Lord Ye said pretty much the same thing as you did.","Duan Yanhua said dissatisfiedly, You went over there just to have him review your paper?","Song Gaoli raised his eyebrows in confusion, What else could I do? The exams are already over.","Duan Yanhua slumped his shoulders in frustration at his lack of ambition and said angrily, For someone like you who just needs a little push to pass, Vice Censor-in-Chief Ye could easily put in a good word with the chief examiner. I sent you there to do that, what the hell is the use of a review!","Song Gaoli's eyes widened, How could we do that! Cheating will result in being stripped of one's scholarly honors.","Besides, the examiners are all locked up in the examination compound and can't come out. The papers are recopied and the names are covered up, so how would they even know which paper is mine? Teacher, please don't say such things in the future, lest someone hears and it brings trouble."]},{"number":278,"title":"Chapter 278: Angry Duan Yanhua, The Erotic Picture Painted by Song Jinzhao Herself","paragraphs":["Duan Yanhua's chest heaved with anger as he repeatedly poked Song Gaoli's temple with his finger.","\"Why are you so inflexible? This small matter is just a lift of a finger for Ye Liangyu to handle.\"","\"Your relationship with the Song family is meant to be used at a time like this. Go find Song Qiming tomorrow and ask him to put in a good word for you. Ye Liangyu will definitely agree.\"","Song Gaoli clenched his jaw, lowered his head, and his voice was muffled.","\"Teacher, doing this is forcing him into a difficult position. Besides, I might not necessarily fail the exam. I might just pass.\"","Duan Yanhua glared, wishing he could rip out all of his hair.","\"By the time the results are announced, it'll be too late! I've already seen the exam papers of your senior fellow students; they have no hope at all. If you also fail, all my years of hard work will be in vain.\"","Song Gaoli hesitated and mumbled, \"I want to try on my own. If I don't pass, I can take it again in three years. But if I'm caught cheating, it's all over.\"","\"Timid and cowardly! What kind of future can you possibly have acting like this? I was truly blind to have chosen you.\"","Watching Duan Yanhua storm off with a flick of his sleeve, Song Gaoli let out a deep breath, his breathing slightly trembling.","He wanted to become a Jinshi, but not through such despicable means.","If he really spoke to Song Qiming, he couldn't even imagine how the other party would look at him, and the knot in his own heart would never disappear.","At worst, he would just wait another three years. Maybe he would even perform better then.","During the wait for the exam results, Xiao Chengjing made no moves, as if the last-minute change of exam questions had never happened.","Xiao Rongche and Xiao Rongyan's anxious hearts gradually calmed down. Perhaps it was just a sudden whim of their imperial father; otherwise, how could there have been backup questions prepared from the start?","If their actions had been discovered at the last minute, the questions would have been thought up on the spot, not prepared well in advance.","Inside the Hall of Supreme Harmony, Xiao Chengjing sat on the dragon throne, his gaze sweeping over the heads of the civil and military officials, finally landing on the Prince of Qi and the Prince of Ying standing at the very front.","Every metropolitan exam, he was aware of the little tricks played in secret; it was just that the matters were usually too small to bother with.","Water that is too clear has no fish; sometimes one shouldn't be too strict.","This time, using the backup exam papers was firstly to give certain people a warning, letting them know who the real emperor was; secondly, it was to select more scholars from humble backgrounds, compressing the power of the Prince of Qi and the Prince of Ying in the court.","As for digging out the cheaters, Xiao Chengjing had no such intention for the time being.","Before any other princes were born, he only had the Prince of Qi and the Prince of Ying as his sons; they could not bear a tainted reputation.","In the chill of early spring, the mountain peach blossoms in the garden of the County Princess's estate quietly bloomed.","These days, Song Jinzhao was either busy with business or entering the palace to treat the Emperor and Empress.","Although her true purpose was to help Xiao Chengjing's concubines get pregnant, the Empress's migraines were a useful cover that she also had to attend to.","Fortunately, the bodies of Xiao Chengjing and the fourteen concubines had been adequately conditioned. Song Jinzhao called for Gu Jupu and handed him a calendar with circled dates.","\"On these days circled in red, intercourse is most likely to result in pregnancy. Have the Emperor take his medicine and go to these concubines' palaces on those exact days.\"","\"These are the best intercourse positions for conception, and I've also written down what the concubines need to do afterwards. They must follow my instructions exactly.\"","Gu Jupu stared dumbfounded at the erotic illustrations Song Jinzhao handed him.","The bizarre and varied poses of the naked, intertwined men and women on the paper made it hard to imagine that the intelligent County Princess Linghui had drawn them herself.","One must know that Song Jinzhao was eighteen this year. Let alone being a married woman, she didn't even have a marriage arrangement. How did she come up with all this?","Despite his confusion, Gu Jupu tucked the papers into his robe and obediently followed Song Jinzhao's orders to inform the Emperor.","Upon hearing that he could resume sexual relations, Xiao Chengjing, who had been holding back his desires for twenty days, immediately began summoning the concubines marked on the calendar for the night.","After downing a potent bowl of medicine, his body indeed felt much better than before.","The concubines in the inner palace were full of astonishment when they heard the news.","\"The Emperor hasn't entered the inner palace for twenty days, why would he suddenly summon Low-Rank Concubine Yan?\"","There were many concubines in the inner palace, and those of low rank were practically like palace maids. They had never been summoned by the Emperor in all these years.","For this to happen so suddenly left many quite surprised.","A higher-ranking concubine curled her lip in disdain, \"What else could it be? Low-Rank Concubine Yan must have pretended to bump into the Emperor and seduced him. Otherwise, how could he possibly remember her?\"","With over five hundred concubines and having not seen her for over a decade, he probably didn't even remember her name or face.","To everyone's surprise, Xiao Chengjing summoned Low-Rank Concubine Yan for three consecutive days.","Just as the jealousy of the previously favored concubines reached its peak, Xiao Chengjing switched his favor to someone else.","Thus, the usually tranquil inner palace began to see frequent scrambles for favor, with concubines constantly running to Xiao Chengjing to offer pastries and soups.","Unfortunately, despite the gifts, Xiao Chengjing ignored them all. Instead, the low-ranking concubines were repeatedly summoned to serve him at night.","Unable to figure it out, the other concubines had to attribute the reason to age, as the ones summoned were all the youngest in the palace.","Before the metropolitan exam results were even posted, Songjing Village, thousands of miles away, had already received good news.","Old Man Song gripped Song Yongnian's shoulders tightly, repeatedly saying \"Good,\" his face wrinkling with a massive smile.","Following Song Qiming passing the provincial exam, Song Yongnian from the first branch had finally passed the county exam this year.","In the courtyard, Second Song looked at the smile on his eldest brother's face and felt incredibly stifled.","Yongnian passed, but his own son failed.","Among the first, second, and third branches, now only their second branch was left behind.","Feeling humiliated, Second Song turned and walked away. A step behind, Second Aunt Song looked at Old Man Song's high regard for Song Yongnian and felt a bitter taste in her mouth.","Nowadays, the third branch sent so many things to the old couple every year, and probably silver too.","Now that Yongnian had passed the county exam and the third branch wasn't around, wouldn't the old man prioritize the first branch for everything in the future? What were they to do!","Returning home, Second Song felt angry just looking at Song Yaozu and pointed at his nose to scold him.","\"You go to school together every day, how come Yongnian passes and you don't?\"","\"Did you not study properly at the private school? How did I give birth to such a useless, stupid son?\"","Eleven-year-old Song Yaozu stood there without a word.","Seeing him silent like a sealed gourd, Second Song waved his hand in anger.","\"Since you can't even pass the TongSheng exam, don't go to the private school anymore. Stay home and farm, at least you can harvest some grain.\"","Second Aunt Song, who had half a foot through the doorway, immediately became anxious.","\"No, he must keep studying.\"","\"It's just two failures. Didn't the village chief's Song Gaoli take the exam many times before? And what happened later? He soared to the sky.\"","\"Yaozu is just young, his mind hasn't opened up yet.\""]},{"number":279,"title":"Chapter 279: Release of the Metropolitan Examination Results","paragraphs":["Second Song clapped his hands in anger toward her, revealing his empty palms.","\"Father only promised to subsidize us for three years. Now that the time is up, where are we supposed to get the other half of the tuition?\"","Second Aunt Song's throat tightened, and she unconsciously lowered her voice.","\"Father and Mother are not short of money now. Let alone half the tuition, they could easily afford to pay the whole amount.\"","\"Jinzhao is so wealthy; just a little slipping through her fingers would be enough for us.\"","Second Song closed his eyes in exhaustion. \"Who doesn't know the Third Branch has money? But it only matters if Jinzhao is willing to give it.\"","\"She sends gifts during the holidays, but not a single penny of silver. I'm afraid Father will lose his temper if I ask him for it.\"","Second Aunt Song walked over to Second Song and hugged his arm. \"Jinzhao is now a noble County Princess. Could she really let her cousin go without an education? What would people say if word got out?\"","\"As long as you explain the pros and cons to Father, and considering Yaozu is his own grandson, this will definitely work out.\"","\"Do you want our only son to be a peasant toiling in the fields? Let alone the Third Branch, your older brother will definitely look down on you in the future, and how will the villagers laugh at you? We cannot give up on his studies.\"","Second Song plopped down on the heated brick bed, scratching his hair into a messy bird's nest.","On the other side, after the initial joy, Old Man Song began to worry.","\"The village chief said the metropolitan examination is around this time. I wonder how Qiming did? The capital is so far away, and we haven't received any news at all.\"","In a good mood, Oldest Song blurted out, \"Father, don't worry. Qiming is so smart, he will definitely pass and become a Jinshi.\"","Old Man Song continued asking, \"Taking the prefectural examination requires going to Anyang Prefecture. When do you plan to take Yongnian there?\"","Oldest Song replied, \"Many children from the private school are going. We'll set off in mid-March. Yongnian said he can go with Scholar Zheng and the others; it's safer with more people.\"","Speaking of going to Anyang Prefecture, Oldest Song hesitated for a few seconds before asking Old Man Song.","\"Father, when I take Yongnian to Anyang Prefecture, should we stay at an inn or at Jinzhao's place? Don't they have a residence in Anyang Prefecture?\"","Old Man Song didn't hesitate. He turned to go into the room and brought out a slip of paper, handing it to Oldest Song.","\"This is the address of the Third Branch's residence in Anyang Prefecture. Jinzhao mentioned it when that steward came last time.\"","\"If Yongnian and Yaozu go to the prefectural capital for their exams, they can just stay in the residence. Although they aren't home, there are still servants in the estate, so food and lodging will be convenient.\"","Oldest Song took the slip of paper. He couldn't read the words on it, but his mind was already at ease.","He smiled and praised, \"I didn't expect Jinzhao to have given instructions so early. This child is truly reliable in everything she does.\"","Old Man Song grinned, his eyes full of gratification.","\"Jinzhao has always had great foresight; otherwise, she wouldn't have insisted on sending Qiming to the private school to study.\"","\"But you must know, those servants were bought by Jinzhao to work, and they are very busy. After moving in, don't be too picky about everything; making do is good enough.\"","Oldest Song replied, \"Rest assured, Father. Your son knows what to do.\"","Old Man Song nodded. \"It's good that you know the boundaries.\"","Listening to the villagers' flattery toward the First Branch, Second Song, who had endured it for a few days, finally couldn't overcome the hurdle in his heart.","He found Old Man Song and pondered aloud, \"Father, Yaozu didn't pass this time, but he is still young and will have opportunities in the future. I want him to continue studying.\"","Old Man Song, who was leaning on a lounge chair basking in the sun, opened his eyes and turned to look at him.","\"If he wants to study, then let him study. Am I going to stop you from sending your son to school?\"","Second Song licked his dry lips, a look of longing in his eyes. \"Then what about the tuition?\"","Old Man Song took a deep breath and sighed. \"Just like before, I will subsidize half of the tuition.\"","Second Song stared at Old Man Song in a daze, not expecting him to agree so readily this time.","After he left, Old Lady Song walked out of the house. \"You just agreed like that?\"","Old Man Song shifted his bottom back and straightened his upper body.","\"Yongnian has already passed the county exam. Whether he passes the prefectural exam or not, he will continue studying. The expenses will only grow larger in the future, so we have to subsidize them somewhat.\"","\"Yaozu is two years younger than Yongnian, so letting him study for another two years is fine. We have to treat everyone fairly.\"","Old Lady Song shook her head in disagreement.","\"I don't think this child is cut out for studying. He's playful and a bit lazy, just like his parents. What if he keeps failing the exams? We can't just throw shining silver away without even hearing a splash.\"","Old Man Song said, \"Let's observe for another two years. If it really doesn't work out, at least he'll be literate and can do something else later.\"","Seeing Old Man Song's persistence, Old Lady Song could only agree.","Fortunately, they had enough money now; they could afford six taels of silver for two years.","As time passed day by day, the day for the release of the metropolitan examination results drew closer.","On this day, the entrance to the examination hall was a sea of people, a vast expanse of heads as far as the eye could see.","The candidates who arrived early waited from dark until dawn. The cold wind made their noses run, but their eyes remained fixed on the examination hall gates, waiting for them to open.","In a carriage outside the crowd, the four members of the Song family were also waiting.","After the hour of Mao, the crowd suddenly became restless.","Song Qiming lifted the carriage curtain and stood on the frame to look ahead. He saw the gates of the examination hall slowly opening, and countless people were desperately pushing forward.","He jumped off the carriage and shouted toward the cabin, \"Sister, they are releasing the results.\"","Song Shixue jumped down from the carriage first. Seeing that there were too many people, Song Jinzhao decided not to bring Anhao along to squeeze through the crowd.","\"You two go look, Lanxi, you follow them.\"","The three nodded and swiftly rushed into the crowd, pushing their way forward.","After the main gates opened wide, over a dozen yamen runners rushed out from inside to push the crowd back until a large empty space was cleared in front of the entrance.","Several officials from the Ministry of Rites walked out of the examination hall. Their calm gazes swept over the thousands of scholars present, and then, with a faint smile, they walked to the high wall at the entrance of the examination hall.","Long strips of yellow paper were unrolled inch by inch from left to right. Everyone's eyes moved along with them, like scanners, not missing a single name.","The rankings on the metropolitan examination board were arranged from right to left. The higher the rank, the further to the right it was, meaning those with lower ranks on the board would actually see their names first.","Song Gaoli, his face red from the cold, stood in the front row of the crowd. His eyes stared blankly at the second-to-last column on the list, his whole body turning into a statue.","The noisy sounds around him completely vanished at this moment. His mind buzzed, leaving only a blank void.","After a long time, his lips parted slightly, and his voice was quieter than a mosquito's hum.","\"I passed?\"","As soon as the words fell, wild ecstasy followed. His eyes were instantly wet with tears. He threw his hands in the air, jumping up and down on the spot, and screamed excitedly at the top of his lungs, \"Ah, I passed, I passed, I passed!\"","Standing on the carriage in the distance, Song Jinzhao spotted him at a glance.","Seeing Song Gaoli so happy he looked like a madman, almost shouting himself hoarse, Song Jinzhao couldn't help but smile, her eyes curving into crescents.","Hearing the shouts, Song Anhao tugged at Song Jinzhao's hand and looked up at her.","\"Eldest Sister, that's Brother Gaoli's voice.\"","Song Jinzhao lowered her eyes, her lips curling into a smile as she nodded. \"Yes, he passed.\""]},{"number":280,"title":"Chapter 280: Third Place, A Chance Encounter with Cui Zhengyang","paragraphs":["Squeezed on the other side of the crowd, Song Qiming heard the shout and stood on his tiptoes to see where the person was. However, there were too many people, and the taller ones completely blocked his view.","Just then, Dongfang Yukun squeezed out from behind him. Was that Song Gaoli shouting just now? It sounded a bit like him.","Song Qiming smiled and nodded. It is him. He must have passed.","Dongfang Yukun glanced in the direction of the voice, but seeing nothing, he withdrew his gaze. He pursed his lips and sighed, It really has not been easy for him either.","Song Qiming replied, It was actually quite smooth. At least he passed every time.","Four hundred names were too many for a single sheet of yellow paper. When the final sheet was unfolded and posted, Dongfang Yukun looked at the three names on the far right and smugly lifted his chin at Song Qiming.","I told you, Cui Zhengyang could never beat me.","On the far right of the yellow paper, three names were prominently displayed from right to left.","First place, Dongfang Yukun; second place, Cui Zhengyang; third place, Song Qiming.","Song Qiming broke into a wry smile. He looked around but did not see any sign of Cui Zhengyang.","Where is Brother Cui? Why do I not see him?","Dongfang Yukun curled his lip and said, He has not left his house since the exam ended. His body is too weak, so he has been resting at home. I figure he will arrive a bit late.","At that moment, Song Shixue, who had been standing nearby, dashed outward, and Lanxi quickly followed.","Big Sister, Brother passed! He got third place! Her voice reached them before she even got close.","Song Jinzhao's eyes widened in pleasant surprise. She immediately handed Song Anhao over to Song Shixue to look after.","You watch him. I am going to take a look.","She still needed to see it with her own eyes; otherwise, she would feel a bit regretful.","Song Jinzhao's agile body quickly wove through the crowd, and in no time, she had squeezed her way to the very front.","After finishing looking at the results, Song Qiming came out and noticed Song Jinzhao was missing. He asked in confusion, Where is Big Sister?","Song Shixue pointed ahead. She went to look at the list. She will be right back.","Having finally found Song Qiming, Song Gaoli rushed over.","He excitedly threw his arms around Song Qiming's neck, nearly strangling him to death.","After letting go, he held up two fingers and gestured at him repeatedly, the smile on his face never fading for a second.","I passed! Three hundred and ninety-ninth place!","Watching his uncontrollably excited demeanor, Song Qiming could not help but smile, his eyes growing slightly moist.","I know. I heard you the moment you let out your first shout.","Having shared his joy, Song Gaoli gripped Song Qiming's shoulders and laughed heartily at the sky again.","I never expected to actually pass this time, ahhh!","Song Qiming was shaken back and forth. A joyful atmosphere permeated the air around them, and everyone who walked by cast a glance their way.","After shouting for a long time, Song Gaoli pushed him away, his eyes shining like diamonds.","I saw your name too! Third place! My jaw nearly dropped.","Song Jinzhao, who had squeezed her way to the list, saw Song Qiming's name written in the third column with her own eyes. After reading his personal information on the examination list word for word, she lingered in place for a short while. At this moment, she felt like she was back in school looking at the school rankings.","Arriving a step late, Cui Zhengyang looked at Song Jinzhao in confusion.","She seemed to be looking at the top few names. She had no maid or elder accompanying her, yet her extraordinary attire made her look like a lady from a prominent family.","What drew Cui Zhengyang's attention was that he found Song Jinzhao somewhat familiar, but he could not recall where he had seen her before.","A heavy shove from behind struck Cui Zhengyang's back, sending him pitching forward. He was just about to crash into the wall.","In a flash, Song Jinzhao grabbed the back collar of his clothes and pulled him back.","After steadying himself, Cui Zhengyang looked at Song Jinzhao with lingering fear. Just a moment ago, he felt as if he had been sent flying.","The servant standing nearby was also startled. He grabbed his master's arm and scanned him up and down repeatedly, only daring to relax once he confirmed there was no problem.","Recovering his wits, Cui Zhengyang cupped his hands and thanked Song Jinzhao. Thank you for your help, Miss.","Seeing Cui Zhengyang's face, Song Jinzhao froze for a moment, somewhat stunned by his looks.","It is nothing. He was quite handsome, able to evenly match Dongfang Yukun in looks.","Perhaps because he was a bit older, Song Jinzhao found him even more attractive than Dongfang Yukun. It was the kind of feeling where she wanted to take a bite out of him at first sight.","It was just that his physique was a bit weak, and his stance was not steady at all. A light bump was enough to knock him over; he was too frail.","Cui Zhengyang was long accustomed to the admiration in Song Jinzhao's eyes. He broke the ice, saying, Whose name is Miss looking for? Did a brother in your family participate in the metropolitan examination?","Song Jinzhao nodded and pointed at Song Qiming's name on the list. I have already found it.","Cui Zhengyang followed the direction she pointed; it seemed to be Song Qiming's name.","He blinked, staring at Song Jinzhao's facial features again and again, and finally remembered where he had seen her.","Setting aside her aura and expression, the shape of her brows and eyes was somewhat similar to Song Shixue's.","Song Shixue seemed to only have one older sister.","Cui Zhengyang asked uncertainly, Are you County Princess Linghui?","Song Jinzhao looked at him in surprise. You are?","Cui Zhengyang took a small step back and respectfully bowed to Song Jinzhao with cupped hands. Student Cui Zhengyang pays his respects to the County Princess.","Song Jinzhao suddenly realized. So you are Cui Zhengyang. Did you make the Eighteen Arhats Lock?","Cui Zhengyang lifted his head and nodded vigorously in pleasant surprise. That is right, I made it.","I originally planned to visit the County Princess's manor after the metropolitan examination. First, to thank Second Miss Song for treating me, and second, to visit the County Princess and discuss mechanism locks. However, due to my poor health, I have not left the house. I never expected to run into the County Princess here today. What a coincidence.","At this moment, Song Jinzhao's gaze had shifted from admiring his appearance to marveling at his talent.","His name seemed to be right next to Qiming's. She cast a sidelong glance.","Indeed, it was second place.","He knew how to make Luban locks and was second place in the metropolitan examination. This person might be useful in the future.","Returning to the carriage, Song Qiming looked in confusion at Cui Zhengyang, who was following a step behind Song Jinzhao.","Brother Cui, why are you walking with my older sister?","They should not know each other.","Cui Zhengyang explained, I just happened to run into County Princess Linghui in front of the list. Knowing you were here, I came over to say hello.","Seeing Song Gaoli but not Dongfang Yukun, he could not help but ask, Did Yukun not come with you?","Song Qiming curled his lips, finding it a bit funny. At this time, he has probably already gone to the Cui Manor to look for you.","Cui Zhengyang chuckled softly, helplessly shaking his head.","I understand. My mother is still waiting at the restaurant, so I will come to visit another day.","On the way back, Song Gaoli got off the carriage when it passed an intersection.","He said to Song Qiming, I will head back first to tell my teacher the news. I will come find you tomorrow.","Even though Duan Yanhua had been lukewarm towards him ever since losing his temper last time, he still needed to inform him now that the results were out.","Losing his temper was one thing, but their master-disciple relationship had not been severed, and he was still living in the Duan Manor. Even if they had different ideas, he had to hold it in.","It was not that Song Gaoli had not thought about moving out; it was just that after living there for so long, moving out right after the exam would be inappropriate.","Unless Duan Yanhua had kicked him out at the time, and Song Gaoli compensated him for room and board, only then would their relationship truly be considered over.","But now, everything is different."]},{"number":281,"title":"Chapter 281: The Scheming Duan Yanhua and the Visit from Cui Zhengyang","paragraphs":["Song Gaoli walked into the Duan Manor with his head slightly bowed. Duan Yanhua, who had been waiting for a long time, immediately rushed up to him.","Smiling broadly, he patted Song Gaoli on the shoulder.","\"I knew you would definitely pass. My careful teaching over the past few months wasn't in vain. You've finally become a Tribute Student, and next is the Palace Examination.\"","Song Gaoli's gaze swept over his senior fellow apprentices standing under the eaves.","Duan Yanhua had been so certain he wouldn't pass that he hadn't even gone to check the results; it must have been them who told the teacher.","He touched his head and said modestly, \"I was just lucky to pass. Ranking three hundred and ninety-ninth is really not high. I estimate I'll only make the third tier in the Palace Examination.\"","Duan Yanhua withdrew his hand. \"I heard Song Qiming took third place?\"","Song Gaoli nodded.","Clasping his hands behind his back, Duan Yanhua sighed, \"With Ye Liangyu and County Princess Linghui backing him, regardless of whether Song Qiming places in the first or second tier in the Palace Examination, he will definitely stay in the capital. He'll most likely enter the Hanlin Academy.\"","\"Gaoli, do you want to stay in the capital as an official?\"","Song Gaoli lowered his eyes. \"It would naturally be good to stay in the capital, but I am lacking in talent and knowledge. I fear I have the desire but not the ability.\"","Duan Yanhua looked around. Seeing people behind them, he led Song Gaoli to the study.","\"Your ranking in the Metropolitan Examination wasn't high, and you don't have much of a reputation. It is almost impossible for you to jump to the second tier in the Palace Examination. Your only chance is the Court Examination that follows it, which is the crucial test that determines where candidates like you will be placed.\"","\"The Court Examination is jointly managed by the Hanlin Academy and the Ministry of Personnel. Unfortunately, my rank is too low to access the test questions, but Lord Fei definitely knows. He has a close relationship with Ye Liangyu. After the Palace Examination, you should go to Ye Liangyu, pour out your grievances, and have him help you get the questions. Aim for a good rank so you at least won't have to leave the capital.\"","Song Gaoli's Adam's apple bobbed, his heart fluttering with panic.","He felt that everything Duan Yanhua did was like walking on the edge of a cliff. It was a sheer miracle that he had managed to stay safely in the Hanlin Academy for so many years.","In truth, Duan Yanhua had spent plenty of effort on his own official career.","It was just that he was already thirty-seven when he became a Tribute Student, and his rank was low. If he hadn't had a good father-in-law, he wouldn't have been able to stay in the capital at all.","He exhausted all his efforts to enter the Hanlin Academy, only to achieve nothing in his first few years. His rank was low, and his direct superiors were all tough nuts to crack, leaving him with nowhere to use his crooked methods.","Later, few of the students he took in managed to pass the exams. The rare one or two who did only made the third tier. Lacking the ability to promote them, they had no choice but to be sent out as local officials.","He had taken Song Gaoli as his student precisely because he valued his relationship with Song Qiming, which could help him connect with Ye Liangyu.","He figured he could get others to do what he couldn't, and then he could just sit back and enjoy the results.","Seeing Duan Yanhua staring fixedly at him with an expression that demanded absolute obedience, Song Gaoli decided to stall.","His expression flickered, and he said tactfully, \"I want to try my best to get into the second tier. If I perform a bit better in the Court Examination, I will have more confidence when I go asking for help.\"","Seeing that he was at least open to the idea of asking for help, Duan Yanhua felt a bit more confident, despite his disappointment.","Their relationship had grown a bit stiff recently, so he couldn't push too hard right now.","\"As long as you know what you're doing. The Ministry of Personnel is in charge of official appointments. Don't you have dealings with Dongfang Yukun? When the time comes, you can ask him for help and have his father arrange a better position for you.\"","Song Gaoli stiffly curled the corners of his mouth. If he performed well, calling in a favor would be fine.","But having someone leak the exam questions to him—he absolutely could not do such a thing. He was afraid of death, and he didn't have the face to ask.","With half a month left before the Palace Examination, many candidates who had become Tribute Students began to actively socialize in the capital.","Bringing their poems and essays, they visited high-ranking officials from their hometowns in the capital, trying to pave the way for the Court Examination and official appointments that would follow.","Literary societies and teahouses were teeming with candidates who spent time every day inquiring about the latest court affairs, trying to guess the essay questions for the Palace Examination.","Not wanting to stay in the Duan Manor any longer than necessary, Song Gaoli simply left early and returned late, spending his days at the Princess's estate.","While Song Qiming focused entirely on preparing for the Palace Examination, Song Gaoli had no expectations of skyrocketing to success in it. Instead, he spent seventy percent of his energy on memorials, official documents, and poetry. The Court Examination questions in previous years usually selected two out of these three topics.","The Court Examination took place just three days after the Palace Examination. Waiting until the Palace Examination was over to prepare would be far too late.","He wanted to pull ahead of the others and overtake them on the curve, striving for a higher rank in the Court Examination.","The March temperatures had only been warm for a few days before a late spring cold snap hit, and the charcoal fires inside the rooms were lit once again.","Song Jinzhao, who had just returned from the palace, was reviewing the account books.","Following her instructions, the five managers had already opened the new shops.","Over the past half month, a significant amount of silver had been spent on everything from buying the storefronts to renovating them.","When the shops ran short on funds, they would draw from the estate, making the estate's expenses quite heavy this month.","During this time, Song Jinzhao had been constantly spending money, and her only income came from thank-you gifts sent by others, most notably from the Duke of Zhenguo's estate.","Standing in the middle of the main hall, Lanxi reported, \"The farmstead at Shiquan Manor is fully completed, and the flower fields at Daohua Manor have all been plowed. The poultry and livestock ordered from the merchants will all arrive in three days. The braised food shop's demand for chickens and ducks is even greater than originally anticipated. I believe we can increase the number of animals raised at the farmstead by another thirty percent.\"","Song Jinzhao raised her eyes and asked, \"Is there enough manpower at the manor?\"","Lanxi nodded in reply, \"The tenant farmers originally at the manor are diligent, responsible, and hardworking. Right now, there isn't too much to do, so they have free time. Increasing it by thirty percent won't be a problem.\"","\"Then increase it by thirty percent.\" Song Jinzhao looked toward Qingshuang. \"How are things with the flower seedlings?\"","Qingshuang said, \"According to the rose and jasmine seedlings the County Princess previously confirmed with the flower merchants, they have already been loaded onto ships from Jiangnan. They will travel by water first and then by land, arriving in the capital by early April. The lavender seeds will also be shipped over together, so it won't delay the spring planting.\"","Song Jinzhao tapped her fingers on the small table on the couch. \"Fushun has already arrived in the capital. Hand over the housekeeping duties to him; I have other matters for you to attend to.\"","Qingshuang nodded. \"This servant will complete the handover within three days.\"","A maid stopped at the door, curtsied, and reported, \"To the County Princess, Young Master Cui has come to request an audience.\"","Song Jinzhao looked up. \"Have you informed the Eldest Young Master?\"","The maid replied, \"The Eldest Young Master has already gone over, but Young Master Cui said he came specifically to see you.\"","The empty front hall was a bit chilly without a charcoal basin. Cui Zhengyang's eyes darted everywhere, trying to find evidence that Song Jinzhao was a mechanism enthusiast like himself.","However, after looking around, there wasn't a single decoration that resembled a puzzle lock.","Even the vases were ordinary, and the calligraphy and paintings hanging on the walls all bore Song Qiming's seal.","Seeing him pause in front of his calligraphy, Song Qiming couldn't help but stand up and speak.","\"The handwriting is clumsy; I've made a fool of myself before Brother Cui.\"","Cui Zhengyang shook his head and smiled. \"How could the handwriting of the third-place winner in the Metropolitan Examination be clumsy? It's just that most people hang their own calligraphy and paintings in their study or inner chambers. It's quite rare to see them hung in the front hall like in your esteemed residence.\""]},{"number":282,"title":"Chapter 282: Considering Song Jinzhao as a Confidant, the Palace Examination Begins","paragraphs":["Song Qiming: \"This residence is the County Princess Estate bestowed upon Ah Jie by the Emperor. We have few people in our family, so we haven't bought many furnishings since moving in.\"","\"We can't display the precious artifacts rewarded by the Emperor for fear of breaking them, and it wouldn't be appropriate to display the gifts sent by other estates. Therefore, most of the calligraphy and paintings hung in the estate are my own work. Ah Jie and Shixue also wrote a few pieces, but they are all displayed in the inner courtyard, not here.\"","As the two were talking, Song Jinzhao stepped over the threshold and strolled in.","Seeing Song Jinzhao, Cui Zhengyang turned and bowed to her. \"Greetings to the County Princess.\"","Song Jinzhao walked over to a chair and sat down. \"Young Master Cui, no need for formalities. May I know what brings you to me today?\"","Cui Zhengyang immediately perked up and gestured for Mochen to bring the chest over.","Two people carried a large chest in. Upon opening the lid, a chest full of oddly shaped Luban locks appeared before Song Jinzhao.","\"The mechanical locks I previously asked the Second Miss Song to give to the County Princess have all been dismantled by you. These are the ones I've made over the past few years. Does the County Princess see any she likes?\"","Song Qiming looked at the chest of wood and hesitated to speak. This gift was quite unique.","He was already so busy with his studies, yet he still had the mind to play with wood.","Song Jinzhao stood up and crouched beside the chest to rummage through it. They ranged from simple to difficult, and some Luban locks were even carved with exquisite patterns.","It seemed Cui Zhengyang was truly interested in these things. He was willing to delve into them and had talent. If he developed in the field of mechanical arts, his achievements might not be small.","Song Jinzhao pulled out a large, seemingly new pineapple-shaped spherical lock.","Cui Zhengyang's eyes lit up. \"I made this at home after finishing the metropolitan examination. Would the County Princess like to try unlocking it?\"","After examining it, Song Jinzhao's fingers moved rapidly, and in less than a quarter of an hour, she had dismantled it into pieces.","\"You could try making it a bit more complex, adding a few more layers on the outside. This one has too few parts.\"","Seeing that the item he had spent twenty days working on was dismantled so effortlessly by Song Jinzhao, Cui Zhengyang felt discouraged, but at the same time, the thought of needing to increase the difficulty sprouted within him.","He looked up at Song Jinzhao expectantly. \"Since the County Princess is so skilled in this, I wonder if you have made any novelties to let me feast my eyes upon?\"","Song Jinzhao pieced the scattered parts back together. \"I've been quite busy lately, so I haven't tinkered with these.\"","\"After Young Master Cui enters the court as an official, you can go take a look at the Ministry of Works. They are currently building ocean-going sailing ships. You should be interested.\"","Cui Zhengyang possessed extremely strong spatial imagination and systematic thinking. He would certainly be adept at engineering and manufacturing tasks.","Following that, Cui Zhengyang pulled Song Jinzhao into a conversation for over half an hour.","They chatted from why he thought of making these, to the difficulties he encountered and the inspiration he sparked over the years of making Luban locks. It only ended when Song Qiming forcefully dragged him away.","\"Gaoli and I have been preparing for the palace examination and the court examination these past few days. Since Brother Cui is here, you must give us some good guidance.\"","Watching Cui Zhengyang being dragged away, Song Jinzhao wearily rubbed the center of her brows. Talking to him really consumed too many brain cells; if she wasn't careful, she couldn't keep up with his rhythm.","Under the anxious and nervous wait of the four hundred tribute students, the palace examination finally arrived.","On this day, Song Qiming wore the official uniform issued by the Ministry of Rites and headed to the Hall of Supreme Harmony to participate in the palace examination.","As the bell chimed, the first ray of morning light shone on the roof of the Hall of Supreme Harmony. The glazed tiles refracted a flowing golden light, appearing both dazzling and sacred.","When the time came, the main doors of the Hall of Supreme Harmony slowly opened.","\"Summon all tribute students to enter the hall—\" The drawn-out voice echoed within the imperial palace.","The uniform procession began to walk up the white jade steps row by row, quiet and orderly.","Inside the hall, hundreds of desks were laid out all the way to the eaves outside the Hall of Supreme Harmony. Sitting on the golden dragon throne, Xiao Chengjing looked down at the young talents slowly walking in, his gaze sweeping over the leading Dongfang Yukun, Cui Zhengyang, and Song Qiming.","The four hundred people were divided into ten columns, and Song Qiming was the first in the third column.","At this moment, although there were hundreds of people in the Hall of Supreme Harmony, no one dared to make a sound. Even the air felt stagnant.","Everyone kept their heads down, not daring to look up. Their awe of imperial power was fully manifested at this moment.","After taking their positions, as if suddenly receiving some signal, the four hundred people simultaneously knelt, kowtowed, and shouted loudly, \"Long live the Emperor, long live, long long live!\"","The level of synchronization was comparable to being connected via Bluetooth; their brainwaves were on the same frequency at this moment.","\"Rise—\" The voice of the Master of Ceremonies eunuch pierced from front to back, echoing in the hall.","It wasn't until they stood up that the crowd dared to slightly raise their heads and steal a glance at the monarch sitting on the dragon throne.","The intimidating gaze scared them into immediately lowering their heads after just one look.","The aura of an emperor, the power of life and death, inspired awe but also struck fear into their hearts.","\"Sit—\"","After everyone sat down, the eunuchs began carrying wooden chests over to distribute the examination papers. There was only one sheet of questions, and there were only two policy essay topics.","The first question: Asked how the imperial court should handle the rise of foreign tribes in the southwest.","The second question: Asked how the national treasury's tax revenue could achieve rapid growth, requiring specific strategies to be pointed out.","Song Qiming stared at the two lines of words on the question paper, grinding his ink block while thinking about how to write his response.","After pondering for a moment, he picked up his brush and began to write on the draft paper: \"The sovereign rules the four seas, and the world pledges its allegiance. However, the foreign tribes in the southwest have been amassing troops for years...\"","For a time, the only sounds left in the grand hall were the rustling of sleeves and paper. The scent of ink lingered at the tip of Xiao Chengjing's nose, making him a bit drowsy as time went on.","Footsteps gradually approached, and the hairs on the bodies of the examinees sitting in the first row instantly stood on end.","Xiao Chengjing's intense, scrutinizing gaze first paused beside Dongfang Yukun for a while, and then he walked sequentially from left to right.","The hem of the robe embroidered with dragon patterns stopped in front of Song Qiming. The tip of his brush paused for a fraction of a second before he continued writing, but his tense back still betrayed his inner apprehension.","Although there were only two questions, the examination lasted from dawn until dusk.","As the last bit of incense burned out in the censer in front of the hall, a dull metallic clanging sound rang out. A eunuch holding a gong shouted loudly, \"Stop writing! Collect the papers!\"","In an instant, regardless of whether they had a brush in their hands or not, all four hundred people simultaneously lowered their hands from the desks.","Only after all the examinees' answer sheets were collected and boxed up were Song Qiming and the others allowed to leave.","After walking out of the grand hall, the crowd stood on the steps and gazed at the distant palaces. They only felt that the imperial palace under the setting sun appeared exceptionally quiet, even somewhat lonely.","Lining up to exit the imperial palace, those with carriages had them waiting outside the palace gates early on.","After greeting Song Gaoli and the others, Song Qiming boarded his carriage. It wasn't until he heard the lively shouting of vendors on both sides of the main street that his mind finally began to relax.","From a child student to a presented scholar, the final step was finally over.","Upon returning to the County Princess Estate, Song Jinzhao and the others had already been waiting for a long time. Even Xuetuan rushed up to paw at his clothes.","\"Ah Jie, I've finished the exam. It should be pretty good.\"","Song Jinzhao curled her lips into a smile and said with gratification, \"Ah Jie is already very satisfied that you could make it this far. You must be hungry, right? Let's eat.\"","Piping hot food was served on the table, and the broth in the pot was bubbling away.","Having only eaten a single sugar cake at noon, Song Qiming immediately picked up his chopsticks and dug in, his appetite thoroughly whetted."]},{"number":283,"title":"Chapter 283: Review of Palace Examination Papers","paragraphs":["On the second day of the Palace Examination, the Grand Secretaries of the Hanlin Academy, the cabinet ministers of the Six Ministries, and other important officials all stayed in the Wenhua Hall to grade exam papers overnight.","Since Dongfang Yukun was among the candidates this time and was the Huiyuan, the top scorer in the metropolitan exam, to avoid suspicion, Secretariat Director Dongfang Yuanbin and Minister of Personnel Dongfang Shaoting did not participate in the grading.","Song Qiming was Ye Liangyu's only student. At Gu Qishan's strong insistence, he was also excluded from the grading panel.","Inside the quiet Wenhua Hall, the burning candles made a crackling sound.","Gu Qishan picked up an exam paper, and a familiar handwriting caught his eye.","After reading the two essays, his calm eyes turned dark. He was almost certain that this paper belonged to Song Qiming.","After pondering for two seconds, Gu Qishan decisively took his brush and drew a sharp symbol indicating a sub-standard grade in the upper right corner.","When the paper fell into the hands of the Minister of Rites, he finished reading it and noticed the sharp symbol in the upper right corner. He silently raised his eyes to look at Gu Qishan.","Their eyes met. After a moment of deliberation, the Minister of Rites also used his brush to draw a sharp symbol below Gu Qishan's.","In the grading process, an examiner's circle represented an excellent grade, a sharp mark meant sub-standard, a dot meant poor, and a line meant failing.","A paper marked with a sharp symbol would basically never make it to the Emperor's desk. The final result would most likely be placement in the second tier.","When the Minister of Works, Ou Shinian, received the paper in turn, his eyes were initially full of appreciation, but he frowned after noticing the two sharp symbols.","He rubbed his fingers against the edge of the paper in thought, and finally picked up his brush to draw a circle.","The Minister of Revenue struggled for a long time but couldn't make up his mind, so he directly pushed the paper to the newly appointed Minister of War.","Lord Wu, I still need to deliberate over this paper. You go first.","The former Provincial Administration Commissioner of Annan and the newly appointed Minister of War, Wu Jianzheng, had just arrived in the capital seven days ago. He was originally not on the grading panel; the Emperor had forcefully squeezed him in.","Wu Jianzheng didn't think much of it, assuming the Minister of Revenue truly hadn't made up his mind, and took the paper to read.","Upon seeing Song Qiming's views and strategies regarding the foreign tribes in the southwest, Wu Jianzheng's thick eyebrows shot up, and he excitedly slapped his thigh.","Exceptionally well written! This person must have a very detailed understanding of southwestern affairs. These strategies can be implemented with just a little refinement.","Noticing the symbols in the upper right corner, he immediately frowned in confusion and said, How can such a good essay only be considered sub-standard? Who marked this? It must be excellent!","After reading so many papers, this is the only one that catches my eye.","Annan bordered the southwest. When it came to understanding the local situation, none of the dozen or so people present could compare to Wu Jianzheng.","The Minister of Revenue sitting next to him kept his mouth shut tight, lowering his head to hold back a laugh.","Wu Jianzheng had just been transferred back from Annan and did not yet understand the political situation in the capital. He certainly couldn't recognize Song Qiming's handwriting and writing style. Now there was a good show to watch.","Gu Qishan, pretending to pass by with his hands behind his back, saw Wu Jianzheng draw a large red circle next to the familiar sharp symbols. His face instantly turned as black as the bottom of a pot.","It really was this paper. How could he be so oblivious? Didn't he see that there were already two sub-standard marks?","When Fei Yanzhang saw this paper, he quietly glanced at Gu Qishan, a faint hint of mockery appearing at the corner of his mouth.","When the Minister of Revenue saw that there were five excellent marks and four sub-standard marks on it, he secretly used his sleeve to cover the paper and quickly drew a circle on it.","Two papers, both receiving six excellent marks and four sub-standard marks, were placed in front of everyone. Gu Qishan's expression could no longer be described as merely ugly.","Jing Yunli picked up the two papers and said meaningfully to the crowd, My lords, which of these two should be selected for the top ten?","Wu Jianzheng slammed his right hand heavily on the table and pointed to Song Qiming's paper, saying, Definitely this one. Out of four hundred papers, I haven't seen a better answer to the first policy question than his.","The four sharp sub-standard marks only seemed like an eyesore to Wu Jianzheng.","Gu Qishan said in a deep voice, Although this essay has a clear train of thought, it is too slick and lacks edge. I believe we should choose this other person.","Wu Jianzheng looked at the hand pressing on the other paper. He hadn't expected that one of the four sub-standard grades came from Gu Qishan.","He had just returned to the capital, so it was better not to contradict the reigning Prime Minister.","Catching sight of Wu Jianzheng silently withdrawing his hand, Fei Yanzhang fearlessly met Gu Qishan's cold, piercing gaze.","Since the scores of these two papers are the same, let's present them both to the Emperor for judgment. If the Emperor asks who gave the four sub-standard marks, I hope Prime Minister Gu will be able to repeat those same words then.","Gu Qishan's jaw tightened, and he stared at Fei Yanzhang with a sinister gaze.","The Minister of Rites and the others suddenly raised their heads. They couldn't let the Emperor judge this. Regardless of who was superior or inferior, they would be the ones to suffer the consequences.","The displeasure on Gu Qishan's face suddenly turned into a smile, and he cast a light glance at Wu Jianzheng.","Since Lord Wu appreciates this person so much, let us present this paper. After all, there isn't much difference between the two.","Wu Jianzheng, hearing his name called, was a little at a loss. He felt a chill down his back. His influence shouldn't be this great, right?","Before midnight, the group submitted the selected top ten exam papers to the Emperor's desk.","Gu Qishan bowed his head and said, The best candidates from this Palace Examination have been selected. We invite Your Majesty to make the final decision.","Xiao Chengjing looked through them in order, starting from the first one. When he saw the last paper, his gaze paused slightly.","Is there a problem with my eyesight, or is there a problem with the eyesight of the ten grading officials I selected? How could such an essay be ranked tenth?","He instructed the head eunuch waiting beside him, Zhao Yande, remove the paper seals covering the names.","Yes, Your Majesty. Zhao Yande immediately stepped forward, removed the paper fasteners on the right side of the exam papers, and unfolded the folded sections. The candidates' names and hometowns were written there.","The first place recommended was undoubtedly Dongfang Yukun, and the second place was Cui Zhengyang. But as for this third place...","Xiao Chengjing placed Song Qiming's paper to the side. Comparing the two, he let out a playful chuckle.","Alright, you may all return.","We take our leave. Fei Yanzhang bowed deeply with his hands clasped, then turned and walked out with his head held high.","Gu Qishan took one last unwilling look at the paper on the desk, and finally left the imperial study, holding in his frustration.","He did not return directly to his manor, but instead went to the residence of Prince Qi.","Xiao Rongche, who hadn't gone to sleep yet, asked with an expectant look, How did it go? Who are the top three?","Gu Qishan took a deep breath. Barring any surprises, Dongfang Yukun and Cui Zhengyang will definitely be in the first tier. As for the remaining spot, I cannot be certain. It might very well be Song Qiming.","Xiao Rongche's brow immediately furrowed. Didn't I tell you to kick him out of the top ten?","Gu Qishan replied, Although Ye Liangyu was not on the grading panel, Fei Yanzhang was. There was also the newly appointed Minister of War, Wu Jianzheng, who was loud and completely oblivious to the situation.","Song Qiming performed exceptionally well. Six grading officials gave him an excellent mark. I couldn't suppress his score.","Xiao Rongche's brow twisted into a tight knot. Did Prince Ying's faction have no reaction? Who were the other four?","Gu Qishan wearily closed his eyes and opened them again. The Minister of Works, Ou Shinian. As for the other three, I am not certain, but they are likely three of those who have been wavering."]},{"number":284,"title":"Chapter 284: Announced as the Third Highest Scorer in the Imperial Palace Examination","paragraphs":["Just like the situation at Prince Qi's manor, Xiao Rongyan was extremely displeased when he heard the news.","Seeing Xiao Rongyan slamming the table in anger, Minister of Justice Sui Zhuangling said, \"Dongfang Yukun and Cui Zhengyang's literary talents are a cut above the rest. It can be said that there is only one spot left in the First Class. Song Qiming is only fourteen, too young and unsteady. I presume the Emperor will not choose him.\"","Xiao Rongyan's face darkened. \"It better be so. If Song Qiming ranks in the First Class, Ye Liangyu will become unbearably arrogant.\"","Sui Zhuangling thought to himself: Actually, even if he makes the First Class, it doesn't matter. At most, he'll be a seventh-rank compiler in the Hanlin Academy, which won't affect the grand scheme of things.","However, seeing how much Xiao Rongyan cared, he kept his thoughts to himself.","On the day of the Honglu Ceremony, the Meridian Gate, located five hundred meters in a straight line from the Hall of Supreme Harmony, was crowded with neatly dressed tribute students.","Bathed in the sunlight, a slightly warm breeze lifted the corners of their robes, yet they could not suppress the turmoil in their hearts.","Inside the Hall of Supreme Harmony, the civil and military officials stood in formation; not a single person was absent.","As a whip was struck forcefully against the white jade steps outside the Hall of Supreme Harmony, the sharp cracks echoed three times throughout the imperial palace.","The officials in the hall and the four hundred tribute students outside the Meridian Gate knelt and kowtowed.","Accompanied by the loud chants of \"Long live the Emperor, long live, long long live,\" Xiao Chengjing, clad in a dragon robe, appeared in the Golden Throne Room.","After taking his seat, his intimidating gaze swept over the crowd. The most crucial part of the Honglu Ceremony had arrived.","The current Prime Minister, Gu Qishan, and the Grand Secretary of the Hanlin Academy, Fei Yanzhang, slowly stepped out from the crowd. The two stopped on the white jade steps, one on the left and one on the right, and slowly unrolled the Golden Scroll.","Upon seeing the names written on it, Gu Qishan's brows instantly knitted together tightly.","Fei Yanzhang noticed the tension on the other side increase. Turning his head, he saw the veins popping out on the back of Gu Qishan's hands.","He curled his lips into a satisfied smile, took a deep breath, and sang out with a resonant voice toward the front: \"First Class, First Place: Dongfang Yukun of Chang'an County, Jingzhao Prefecture.\"","The voice reached the bottom of the steps, and the officials of the Court of State Ceremonial shouted: \"First Class, First Place: Dongfang Yukun of Chang'an County, Jingzhao Prefecture.\"","The voice reached the Meridian Gate, and the Imperial Guards shouted once more: \"First Class, First Place: Dongfang Yukun of Chang'an County, Jingzhao Prefecture.\"","Standing at the very front of the ranks, Dongfang Yukun stepped forward confidently and performed the grand ceremony of three kneelings and nine kowtows toward the Hall of Supreme Harmony.","He appeared exceedingly calm and steady, as if he had long anticipated this result.","Suppressing the surging displeasure in his heart, Gu Qishan shouted loudly, \"First Class, Second Place: Cui Zhengyang of Yuhang County, Jiangnan Prefecture.\"","\"First Class, Second Place: Cui Zhengyang of Yuhang County, Jiangnan Prefecture.\"","\"First Class, Second Place: Cui Zhengyang of Yuhang County, Jiangnan Prefecture.\"","He was equally calm and steady, whereas the other tribute students standing in the front row were restless, holding their breath in slight frustration.","When Fei Yanzhang called out the third place, he had a smile on his face, and even his voice sounded exceptionally pleasant and joyful.","\"First Class, Third Place: Song Qiming of Xining County, Anyang Prefecture.\"","Court of State Ceremonial officials: \"First Class, Third Place: Song Qiming of Xining County, Anyang Prefecture.\"","Imperial Guards at the Meridian Gate: \"First Class, Third Place: Song Qiming of Xining County, Anyang Prefecture.\"","Standing third in the first row, Song Qiming shuddered when he heard the guards call his name.","Trying his best to suppress the joy bursting from his chest, he took a step forward on slightly weak legs and knelt to pay his respects.","Among the four hundred people present, Song Qiming was the youngest. Standing next to Dongfang Yukun and Cui Zhengyang, his short stature made him look rather slight and small.","A fourteen-year-old Tanhua had never appeared in the centuries-long history of the Dongzhao Kingdom.","It was said that if Dongfang Yukun had participated in the metropolitan examination at the age of eleven, he could have also placed in the First Class, but after all, he hadn't participated.","Song Qiming's achievement as a fourteen-year-old First Class Tanhua, however, was firmly grasped in his hands.","After the top ten names of the Second Class were called, Dongfang Yukun, Cui Zhengyang, and Song Qiming were led all the way into the Hall of Supreme Harmony by the officials of the Court of State Ceremonial.","The three stopped before the throne, closest to the Emperor. They knelt on both knees and kowtowed three times before waiting for Xiao Chengjing to speak.","On the elevated throne, Xiao Chengjing's gaze swept over their faces, a satisfied smile appearing on his lips.","The Dongfang family did not take sides and only supported him.","The Cui family had been in Jiangnan for so many years and had absolutely nothing to do with Prince Qi or Prince Ying.","As for the remaining one, a true scholar from a humble background, as long as he learned even thirty percent of Ye Liangyu's temperament, he would basically be uninvolved in partisan disputes in the court.","Not to mention that before even entering the court, he had already offended two of his own sons and was targeted to the point where he almost didn't make the top ten. He was truly a bit pitiful.","A voice carrying a hint of oppression reached the ears of the three from above.","\"Since you three are the First Class, you ought to be the role models for thousands of scholars in the world. I hope that from now on you will strictly fulfill your duties, become braver in the face of difficulties, and live up to what you have learned and to my expectations.\"","Dongfang Yukun, Cui Zhengyang, and Song Qiming bowed and kowtowed for the third time.","\"We thank Your Majesty for your immense grace. We will dedicate ourselves entirely to your service until our dying days, and we will not disappoint Your Majesty's divine trust.\"","As the three walked out of the Hall of Supreme Harmony, the officials of the Court of State Ceremonial carried the Golden Scroll out of the imperial palace, and all the new Jinshi lined up and followed.","Only when they saw their own names appearing on the Golden Scroll did the immense sense of glory in their hearts completely surge onto their faces.","Song Gaoli stared at the fifth-to-last name in the Third Class and finally breathed a sigh of relief. Next would be the court examination.","The day of the triennial Honglu Ceremony could be said to be the busiest day for the runners of the Ministry of Rites.","After the roll call ended, dozens of people began running through the streets of the capital to announce the good news, a process that usually lasted an entire day.","The sound of gongs and drums approached from afar, appearing at the corner of the street. Passing commoners stopped to watch the excitement, and the residents living along the street also came out to look around upon hearing the noise.","\"Which family's young master has passed the imperial examination and become a Jinshi?\" the onlookers asked around.","A literate commoner pointed at the golden characters on the vermilion cloud-headed placard and said excitedly, \"It's the Third Place of the First Class! This is the Tanhua.\"","Four Ministry of Rites runners dressed in dark red ceremonial robes walked down the middle of the street in two rows. Two held the placard high, and two continuously beat copper gongs. Upon seeing them, the commoners quickly retreated to the sides of the street to make way.","The sound grew closer and closer.","At the entrance of the County Princess's manor, the porter who had been waiting for a long time hurriedly ran down the steps to look. Upon seeing the procession announcing the good news, he immediately shouted into the gates.","\"They're here, they're here! The officials announcing the good news are here!\"","Song Qiming passing the examination and becoming a Jinshi was an absolute certainty. Early in the morning, Qingshuang had already informed the porter that runners would come to announce the good news today, telling him to keep a close watch and report back immediately."]},{"number":285,"title":"Chapter 285: The Imperial Banquet and the Procession on Horseback","paragraphs":["When the procession bearing the good news arrived at the gates of the County Princess's estate, the two runners beating the bronze gongs moved their hands so fast they became a blur, as if playing a joyous celebratory tune.","The commoners who had followed along to watch the spectacle saw the procession stop at the estate's entrance, and they all pointed at the main gates, chattering animatedly.","\"This is the residence of County Princess Linghui. The one who placed third in the imperial examination is her younger brother, Eldest Young Master Song.\"","\"The Song family's ancestors must be blessing them from the grave! County Princess Linghui was just conferred her title last year, and barely half a year later, Young Master Song scores third overall. His future is boundless!\"","\"I heard Young Master Song is only fourteen this year. To become a Jinshi at fourteen, he is simply the reincarnation of the God of Literature.\"","\"...\"","The clamor at the gate continued unabated, filled entirely with praise and envy for the Song siblings.","As the rapid beating of the gongs came to an end, the runners from the Ministry of Rites shouted loudly toward the estate gates.","\"Tidings of victory! Congratulations to Song Qiming of the County Princess's estate! Lord Song has achieved third place in the first class, earning the title of Tanhua!\"","The voices carried into the manor. Neatly dressed, Song Jinzhao led Song Shixue and Song Anhao out the main doors to greet them.","The two sisters wore expressions of irrepressible joy. The young Song Anhao was still a bit bewildered; he didn't quite understand just what a massive cause for celebration placing third was.","The Ministry of Rites runner respectfully presented the congratulatory notice to Song Jinzhao with both hands.","\"Congratulations, County Princess. For Eldest Young Master Song to earn the title of Tanhua at such a young age makes him truly the first in our Dongzhao Nation. The County Princess has indeed taught him well.\"","Looking at the gold-traced notice in her hands, the corners of Song Jinzhao's mouth turned up, and even her brows were filled with smiles.","\"Thank you all for your hard work. Fushun, give them their reward money.\"","Behind her, Fushun immediately took out four coin purses and pressed them into the hands of the four runners. Qingshuang also handed each of them a bamboo cup of milk tea.","\"After walking for so long, you runners must be thirsty. Take this homemade tea to drink on your way.\"","The heavy coin purses made the four beam with joy. Smiling broadly, they bowed to Song Jinzhao. \"Thank you for the generous reward, County Princess. We wish Lord Tanhua a bright future and a prosperous official career.\"","After the ceremony at the Honglu Hall concluded, the four hundred new Jinshi scholars did not return to their lodgings. Instead, they all gathered at the Ministry of Rites to await the start of the Qionglin Banquet.","A quarter of an hour before noon, accompanied by the loud calls of the Ministry of Rites officials, everyone was guided to their respective seats by the runners according to their rankings in the palace examination.","Dongfang Yukun, Cui Zhengyang, and Song Qiming were led to the same table, their seats arranged close together.","Meanwhile, the second-class and third-class Jinshi were seated at other tables. After sitting down, everyone communicated through glances; no one dared to whisper to each other.","The food and wine on the tables had long been set out. The enticing aromas drifted into their noses, and many scholars who hadn't eaten breakfast found their stomachs rumbling. Yet, unable to touch their chopsticks, they could only swallow their saliva and wait.","After waiting for about half an hour, high-ranking court officials dressed in crimson and purple official robes appeared at the entrance of the Ministry of Rites office.","In the courtyard, the four hundred scholars stood up in unison to respectfully await them.","Secretariat Director Dongfang Yuanbin, Chancellor Gu Qishan, Grand Secretary of the Hanlin Academy Fei Yanzhang, and two other important court ministers strode forward.","The eldest, Dongfang Yuanbin, walked straight to the incense altar without looking sideways. He turned around, and his deep, resonant voice reached everyone's ears.","\"His Majesty's Imperial Edict.\"","Instantly, all the officials, scholars, and runners present knelt to receive the decree.","\"By the grace of Heaven, the Emperor decrees: We hold the imperial examinations to select scholars, hoping to obtain the virtuous and capable. You students have honorably inscribed your names on the golden roll. We hope that from now on, you will be diligent in the affairs of the state and serve the court. We specially bestow this banquet at Qionglin, and hope you all enjoy yourselves to the fullest.\"","\"We thank His Majesty for his heavenly grace. Long live the Emperor, long live, long long live,\" the scholars shouted as they kowtowed.","Having spoken, Dongfang Yuanbin gave a slight nod to the Ministry of Rites officials.","Upon receiving the signal, the Ministry of Rites official immediately tilted his head back and shouted at the sky, \"Bestow the imperial wine!\"","Dozens of runners approached carrying trays, the cups on them already filled with imperial wine.","After the cup was downed, the official continued to shout, \"Pin the flowers!\"","Dongfang Yuanbin individually pinned the imperially bestowed gold-leaf palace flowers on the right brim of the hats of Dongfang Yukun, Cui Zhengyang, and Song Qiming.","The second and third-class scholars, however, took velvet flowers from the trays themselves and pinned them on their own hat brims.","Accompanied by the call to commence the banquet, the five high ministers took their seats at the table where Song Qiming and the other two were seated.","The gazes of all the new scholars were either cautious or filled with envy and jealousy. One by one, they kept their heads slightly lowered, stealing glances from the corners of their eyes at those sitting at the first table.","Dongfang Yukun, who had been holding back his laughter this whole time, finally managed to curl the corners of his lips and shoot a look at his grandfather, as if asking for praise.","See? I told you the title of Zhuangyuan would be mine.","Dongfang Yuanbin gratifyingly raised his eyebrows, which were as white as frost. He was about to retire, and having a successor for the family was his greatest wish.","Now that Dongfang Yukun had scored first as Zhuangyuan, he could finally set his heart completely at ease.","To Song Qiming, the gazes of Gu Qishan and Sui Zhuangling felt like thorns in his back. He deliberately pretended not to notice, silently eating his food and occasionally drinking and exchanging a few words with Cui Zhengyang.","After a while, Dongfang Yukun stood up to toast Gu Qishan and the others. Seeing this, Cui Zhengyang and Song Qiming sequentially stood up to follow suit.","In front of the crowd, no matter how displeased Gu Qishan felt in his heart, he could only drink the wine offered by Song Qiming.","After the top three had finished their toasts, the new scholars from the other tables also began to come over with their wine cups to offer their greetings.","When the Qionglin Banquet ended, the Zhuangyuan, Bangyan, and Tanhua were led by the Ministry of Rites runners into an inner chamber to change into their celebratory robes.","The most bustling event of the afternoon, the horseback parade through the streets, began.","The three rode on horses, followed by numerous runners holding up placards. Behind them, gongs and drums were beaten, and the sound of the suona echoed through the skies.","Both sides of Vermilion Bird Street were packed with commoners watching the spectacle. There were unmarried young women carrying flower baskets, throwing floral branches at the three men.","From the second floors of the adjacent shops, sheltered ladies ceaselessly tossed down handkerchiefs, scented sachets, palm leaf fans, and accessories.","On the second-floor balcony of a hotpot shop, Song Shixue playfully scratched her head. \"There are so few people giving flowers to brother.\"","The ceremonial robes of Dongfang Yukun and Cui Zhengyang were already adorned with colorful petals. Song Qiming, however, didn't have a single petal on him; he looked as clean as an attendant.","Song Anhao, gripping the railing with both hands, blurted out, \"The ones throwing things are all girls, and Big Brother isn't as good-looking as they are.\"","Song Jinzhao rubbed her forehead with a wry smile, grabbing her youngest brother's shoulder to keep him from leaning too close to the railing.","\"Don't speak such blunt truths. Your brother just hasn't fully grown into his looks yet.\"","In truth, Song Qiming was not ugly, but Dongfang Yukun and Cui Zhengyang were exceptionally handsome. By comparison, Song Qiming looked a bit too ordinary.","Moreover, he was still young. Compared to Dongfang Yukun and Cui Zhengyang, who were of prime marriageable age, he naturally wasn't as popular with the young ladies.","As the parade passed below the hotpot shop, Song Shixue grabbed the bamboo basket from Lanxi's hands and threw pink peach blossoms at Song Qiming as if her life depended on it.","\"Brother, over here!\"","Hearing the familiar voice, Song Qiming turned his head, and a branch of peach blossoms perfectly lodged itself right in the middle of his ceremonial hat.","Seeing Song Jinzhao and the other two standing on the balcony, Song Qiming smiled and raised his hand to wave at them.","The spectating crowd followed his gaze, only to see that the ones greeting him were two young ladies.","A woman carrying a vegetable basket turned her head and saw Song Qiming take down the peach branch from his hat to sniff it. She said in surprise, \"What is the relationship between those two girls and Lord Tanhua? Did he get engaged at such a young age?\"","The man squeezed next to her looked at her with astonishment, \"What nonsense are you talking about? That is County Princess Linghui and her younger sister. The Tanhua is County Princess Linghui's biological younger brother.\"","The woman looked at the man, her face full of shock.","\"Lord Tanhua is the younger brother of the Divine Doctor County Princess?\"","The man's eyes held joy, and he nodded vigorously, \"I was there when the good news procession went to the County Princess's estate this morning. The estate even handed out lucky money. The Tanhua is named Song Qiming.\"","The day after the street parade, led by the officials of the Ministry of Rites, four hundred newly minted jinshi scholars went to the Confucius Temple to perform a grand kneeling and bowing ceremony.","Inside the Imperial Study, Xiao Chengjing stared at the half-written imperial edict on the desk with a tight frown.","Eunuch Zhao, who already held two imperial edicts in his hands, glanced at the Emperor with some confusion when he saw him stop writing halfway.","Could it be that the Emperor did not want to confer the title of Hanlin Academy Compiler, a rank seven official, upon Song Qiming?","The top three of the first tier did not need to participate in the court examination but were directly appointed by the Emperor. Usually, they would first enter the Hanlin Academy to work their way up from the bottom.","Xiao Chengjing put down the wolf-hair brush, sat on the dragon throne, and asked, \"Since Song Qiming passed the jinshi examination, does he need to return to his hometown to honor his ancestors?\"","Zhao Yande was stunned for a moment, then bowed and answered, \"According to customary etiquette, he should return.\"","After scoring high, most people would return to their hometowns to honor their ancestors and visit their families.","Therefore, whether it was the Emperor or the Ministry of Personnel, they would grant a special leave of absence, allowing them to take up their posts later.","The leave usually lasted three to six months, and for those far away, a year was not uncommon.","Song Qiming's ancestral home was not in the capital. Factoring in the travel and the time for ancestor worship, he should rightfully have a six-month leave.","Xiao Chengjing thought for a moment and ordered, \"Bring two new blank edicts. The court is in urgent need of people, so urgent matters must be handled urgently. The top three of the first tier must enter the Hanlin Academy to serve as soon as possible. There is no need for them to return to their hometowns to honor their ancestors in the meantime.\"","Anyang Prefecture was thousands of miles away from the capital. A round trip would take four months, plus the days spent in their hometown; they wouldn't be back for at least five months.","If Song Qiming went back to honor his ancestors, Song Jinzhao would definitely go back too, and she could not leave the capital right now.","The next day, three imperial edicts were delivered by the imperial eunuchs to the Dongfang estate, the Cui estate, and the County Princess's estate respectively.","Dongfang Yukun was appointed as a Hanlin Academy Senior Compiler, a secondary sixth-rank official, while Cui Zhengyang and Song Qiming were appointed as Hanlin Academy Compilers, primary seventh-rank officials, sitting as equals with Duan Yanhua.","The starting point of these three was arguably the highest among all the new jinshi. The rest had to participate in the court examination jointly held by the Ministry of Personnel and the Hanlin Academy today, and official posts would be selected based on their ranking in the examination.","In the front hall of the County Princess's estate.","Having just seen off the imperial eunuch, Song Qiming looked at the edict in his hand with a slight frown.","\"Only a half-month leave. That's not enough for a trip back to the village.\"","The original plan was for Song Jinzhao and the others to return to Song Family Village after the palace examination.","Now that the Emperor had issued an order, Song Qiming had to take up his post at the Hanlin Academy in half a month, leaving absolutely no time to go back and honor their ancestors.","Song Shixue, sitting on a stool, looked a bit disappointed, \"Does that mean we can't go back?\" Half a month wasn't even enough to reach Anyang Prefecture.","Song Qiming paced around for a moment, then faced Song Jinzhao and hesitated, \"Sister, how about you take Shixue and Anhao back for a trip?\"","Although they had already enshrined their parents' memorial tablets in the County Princess's estate, their bodies were still buried in the village.","Secondly, it had been over a year since they went back to see their grandfather and grandmother.","Song Jinzhao rubbed her finger along the rim of her cup.","\"The Empress's health is unsettled in the palace, and I have to enter the palace once every seven days. I'm afraid I won't be able to leave in the short term.\"","Before the concubines in the inner harem became pregnant, Xiao Chengjing would definitely not let her leave the capital.","Thinking of this, Song Jinzhao suddenly looked at the edict in Song Qiming's hand.","Could it be that the Emperor deliberately shortened the time so much?","Song Shixue looked at Song Jinzhao with a face full of confusion, \"Sister, hasn't the Empress's headache been cured yet?\"","With her sister's medical skills, it shouldn't take this long.","Song Jinzhao silently calculated the time and replied, \"It will take about another month.\"","It takes a month of pregnancy to detect the signs, and to be one hundred percent certain, it takes at least a month and a half to two months.","Calculating the time the fourteen concubines served the Emperor, the earliest was only twenty-some days ago.","Song Qiming put the edict into the brocade box and closed the lid, \"Then we'll wait a bit longer. Let's write a letter back first to let Grandfather know. After the court examination, Gaoli should be going back, and we can go together then.\"","Song Shixue looked worriedly at Song Jinzhao, \"If we all go back, will you be okay at home alone, brother?\"","Song Qiming smiled and reached out to tug his sister's little braid, \"There are so many servants in the estate, and my teacher is also in the capital. I'll be fine by myself.\"","Song Jinzhao looked at the increasingly mature Song Qiming and rested her chin on her hand in deep thought.","Song Family Village was more than two months' journey from the capital, and a round trip would take nearly half a year.","The imperial court only granted a few days of leave every year, so Qiming would have no time to go back in the future.","She herself had many businesses in the capital and rarely went back.","This time, when they go back, they must arrange the lives of the two elders well.","The second branch was unreliable, and the first branch could take care of them but not comprehensively.","Although their two sons were still around, there were some things that a grandson had no place meddling in.","However, Old Man Song and Old Lady Song had treated the third branch well. Now that the third branch was rising, they had to let them enjoy their twilight years in peace and comfort, and worry less.","In the evening, Song Gaoli rushed straight to the County Princess's estate from the Ministry of Personnel after finishing his examination.","With a happy face, he said to Song Qiming, \"I think I did well this time. I should be in the upper-middle tier.\"","Song Qiming curled his lips into a smile and asked, \"So confident?\"","Song Gaoli nodded vigorously, \"This exam was different from before. I wrote very smoothly.\"","As they walked into the study, Song Gaoli recounted the examination questions and how he answered them to Song Qiming in detail.","Half an hour later, Song Qiming stroked his chin and pondered, \"I think it's pretty good. It just depends on the examiners and how the others performed.\"","The day before the court examination rankings were released, Song Qiming learned Song Gaoli's results in advance from Ye Liangyu.","\"One hundred and thirty-sixth place. Under normal circumstances, this rank would not allow him to stay in the capital.\"","Song Qiming heard the tone in Ye Liangyu's voice and quietly waited for him to continue.","Ye Liangyu picked up his teacup and took a sip.","\"He can forget about becoming a Shujishi. If he wants to stay in the capital, he has to wait a few months, first enter the Six Ministries to observe and study for a period of time, and then figure out a way to stay.\"","\"If he doesn't consider staying in the capital, he can be assigned to a local post as a county magistrate, and then slowly transfer back later.\"","Song Qiming asked, \"If he stays, which of the Six Ministries should he enter?\"","Ye Liangyu replied, \"The Ministry of Justice is the sphere of influence of the Prince of Ying, and the Ministry of Rites is the sphere of influence of the Prince of Qi. The Minister of Revenue sways from side to side and flatters both parties; anyone could be pushed out as a scapegoat. He definitely cannot go to these three.\""]},{"number":286,"title":"Chapter 286: Song Gaoli's Whereabouts, Possibly Pregnant","paragraphs":["\"Wu Jianzheng, the Minister of War, has just taken office and urgently needs to place his own people in the Ministry.\"","\"Dongfang Yuanbin has already submitted his retirement petition to the Emperor. It won't be long before Dongfang Shaoting is promoted to Secretariat Director. The new Minister of Personnel is his man. Since you have a good relationship with Dongfang Yukun, entering the Ministry of Personnel would be a steady choice.\"","Song Qiming spoke up, \"Ou Shinian, the Minister of Works, has a good relationship with Ah Jie. He doesn't take sides.\"","Ye Liangyu nodded. \"The Ministries of War, Personnel, and Works—these three are quite suitable. But I think entering the Ministry of War is the best.\"","\"Wu Jianzheng was personally transferred back from Annan by the Emperor. Most of the officials remaining in the Ministry of War belong to the Prince of Ying's faction. A new official always brings sweeping changes; he will definitely clear out some people. If Gao Li can gain Wu Jianzheng's favor and trust, he will rise very quickly in the Ministry of War.\"","\"On the other hand, the Ministries of Personnel and Works are relatively stable. Every position is fixed. Without outstanding achievements, and given Gao Li's low starting point, he would only be able to slowly wait out his years of service if he goes there. The fastest he could become an expectant Vice Director is six years, and that's only if someone is guiding him.\"","Song Qiming rolled his slightly stiff neck. \"In that case, the Ministry of War is indeed the most suitable destination. Gao Li is ambitious but lacks a powerful background, so Wu Jianzheng should feel at ease using him.\"","Ye Liangyu nodded. \"After the imperial examination rankings are announced tomorrow, he will probably come looking for you. If he wants to stay in the capital, explain the pros and cons to him and let him choose for himself.\"","\"If he chooses the Ministry of Personnel, have Dongfang Yukun introduce him to the Dongfang family. If he chooses the Ministry of Works, your Ah Jie can handle it. If he chooses the Ministry of War, I will arrange it.\"","Song Qiming stood up and gave Ye Liangyu a deep, formal bow. \"Thank you, Teacher, for taking the trouble to plan for Gao Li.\"","Ye Liangyu waved his hand. \"These are just minor matters.\"","\"After all, I taught him for a while, and you have a close relationship with him. Even if his official rank is small, you never know when he might be of use; he is also a connection for you.\"","He continued speaking to Song Qiming, \"This time, the Emperor has decreed that you will enter the Hanlin Academy in half a month. Perform well once you're there, and don't let Lord Fei make a joke out of your teacher.\"","If there was anyone he didn't have to worry about, it was his own student. Aside from putting some effort into daily teaching, he never had to worry about his examination rankings.","The goal was the Second Class, but he directly scored in the First Class. Entering the Hanlin Academy was perfectly justified and didn't require any worrying on his part.","Song Qiming smiled, lowered his eyes, and then looked up. \"Rest assured, Teacher, your student will definitely not embarrass you.\"","After the rankings were announced the next day, Song Gao Li first went to the Ministry of Personnel to inquire about his possible placements.","Caressing the wolf-hair brush in his sleeve, the Ministry of Personnel director advised lazily, \"If there are any high-ranking officials in the capital from your hometown, bring some gifts and pay them a visit. Try to get a posting as a county magistrate in a place with beautiful scenery. If you perform well, you can be promoted in three years.\"","After leaving the Ministry of Personnel, Song Gao Li found Song Qiming and told him about the situation.","\"They said that the imperial treasury hasn't been abundant in recent years, so everyone is fighting for county magistrate positions in good locations.\"","\"Although my examination ranking is decent, I only placed in the Third Class in the palace examination. It wouldn't be a problem to serve in a remote county, but if I don't want to go that far, I'll most likely end up as a prefectural school instructor or a deputy to a local prefect.\"","Song Qiming didn't immediately reveal the path Ye Liangyu had planned for him. Instead, he asked, \"What are your thoughts right now?\"","On the way to the Princess's estate, Song Gao Li had been thinking the whole time, the worry between his brows never fading.","He pursed his lips, his heart completely torn.","\"It wasn't easy getting to the capital, and I want to stay. The appointment and dismissal of officials are handled by the Ministry of Personnel. I want to ask Dongfang Yukun for help. Even if I can't stay, being sent out to the Jiangnan region as a county magistrate would be fine too.\"","Seeing him say this, Song Qiming finally spoke.","\"Yesterday, Teacher called me over and told me your examination ranking. If you want to stay in the capital, you can first enter the Six Ministries to learn government affairs.\"","Then, Song Qiming recounted everything Ye Liangyu had told him the day before in great detail, finally asking, \"The Ministries of Personnel, War, and Works—how do you want to choose?\"","At this moment, the expression on Song Gao Li's face could no longer be described merely as pleasant surprise. Excitement crashed against his brain and heart like ocean waves. He sat frozen in place, blinking wildly in disbelief.","He hadn't even gone looking for help yet, and a position was already arranged?","Unable to suppress his emotions or think straight, Song Gao Li simply stood up and began pacing rapidly around the table.","After a long brainstorming session in his head, he spoke to Song Qiming with absolute certainty: \"I want to go to the Ministry of War.\"","The corners of Song Qiming's mouth curled up slightly. \"Are you sure? The Ministry of War is quite chaotic right now.\"","Song Gao Li nodded vigorously, his mind already drifting to the grand ambitions he would realize in the Ministry of War.","\"I'm sure. The risks are high, but so are the opportunities. I want to take a gamble.\"","Song Qiming had guessed he would make this choice. He stood up with a smile and patted Song Gao Li on the arm.","\"Alright, I'll take you to see Teacher.\"","No sooner had the two men stepped out of the estate than Gu Jupu, who was supposed to be on duty at the Imperial Academy of Medicine, came rushing into the Princess's estate.","Standing excitedly in front of Song Jinzhao, he gestured wildly as he spoke: \"Princess, Low-Rank Concubine Yan in the palace has had her monthly cycle delayed by seven days, and Attendant Hai is also three days late. Their pulses feel like slippery pulses, but because the time is so short, I am a little unsure.\"","Song Jinzhao took the ledger Gu Jupu handed her, which recorded the bed-attending times, ovulation periods, and menstrual cycles of fourteen concubines.","\"Calculating the time, it should be about right. Have you told them?\"","Gu Jupu shook his head. \"I wasn't certain, so I didn't say anything, lest a misdiagnosis disappoint the Emperor.\"","Imperial heirs were a major matter, and the Emperor valued them so highly. If he made a mistake and gave the Emperor false hope, it wasn't impossible that heads would roll.","Song Jinzhao continued flipping through the pages. Over the past month or so, the fourteen concubines had all been favored three or four times.","The potent prescription she had given Xiao Chengjing could only be maintained for another half a month at most. Only two concubines being pregnant was still too few.","\"Then wait a few more days. We will speak of it once the pregnancies are confirmed. You must also pay attention to the other concubines; they might already be pregnant, but it just can't be diagnosed yet.\"","Gu Jupu nodded heavily. \"Rest assured, Princess. I am personally caring for these fourteen concubines, and I will instruct them to be careful with their diets and all other aspects.\"","When Song Gao Li returned to the Duan residence that evening, Duan Yanhua called him into the study to question him.","\"I already know your examination ranking. You were away from home all day—did you go look for Song Qiming, or Dongfang Yukun?\"","At this moment, Song Gao Li was still feeling a bit excited. He restrained his expression and gave a slight nod.","\"The Ministry of Personnel said I would be sent out of the capital. With no other options, I had to go find Qiming. He promised to try his best to put in a good word for me with Lord Ye, but whether it works or not remains to be seen.\"","Duan Yanhua's eyes lit up, and he happily grabbed Song Gao Li's shoulders.","\"Well done. If you can stay in the capital, we, master and disciple, can look out for each other.\"","\"I have been in officialdom for so many years; I can offer you some guidance so that a newcomer like you doesn't take too many detours.\"","Song Gao Li's mouth twitched. Given your style of doing things, I'm afraid I wouldn't have a way forward for twenty or thirty years. I'd better not borrow from that experience."]},{"number":287,"title":"Chapter 287: Imperial Harem Consorts Announce Pregnancies in Succession","paragraphs":["A few days later, Gu Jupu's fingers, resting on the wrist of Low-Rank Concubine Yan, trembled involuntarily.","His heart raced, and even his breathing became slightly labored.","The drowsy Low-Rank Concubine Yan looked in confusion at Gu Jupu, who remained motionless and silent on the floor.","\"Director Gu, what is wrong? Have I contracted some illness?\"","With Imperial Physician Jiao's sudden departure from the capital, the head of the Imperial Hospital had taken over the care of these low-ranking concubines. Low-Rank Concubine Yan was overwhelmed by this favor, and his earnest, responsible, and hands-on attitude had won their praise and trust.","Resting his left hand on his medical box, Gu Jupu slowly stood up. \"Congratulations, My Lady. You are with child.\"","A teacup filled to the brim crashed onto the floor. Low-Rank Concubine Yan blinked, failing to process the words for a moment.","\"What did you say?\"","Gu Jupu repeated, \"To answer you, My Lady, you are already a month and a half pregnant.\"","The only palace maid in the room looked at Low-Rank Concubine Yan in absolute shock. It had been over a decade since any concubine in the palace had become pregnant, and now her lady was expecting?","Coming to her senses, Low-Rank Concubine Yan immediately looked down and placed her hands over her stomach. \"I am pregnant... I am pregnant!\"","Weeping tears of joy, she covered her mouth and hurriedly instructed the maid.","\"Caixia, go quickly and tell the Emperor. Tell him I am with child.\"","The maid named Caixia nodded hastily and ran outside, almost tripping over the threshold in her carelessness.","Soon, Xiao Chengjing arrived, clad in his dragon robes.","His intense gaze fixed on Low-Rank Concubine Yan's stomach, his eyes brimming with pleasant surprise.","\"Gu Jupu, I am entrusting Low-Rank Concubine Yan's pregnancy to your care. You must ensure she safely delivers a prince.\"","Gu Jupu nearly choked on his own saliva. What if she gave birth to a princess?","\"This humble official obeys Your Majesty's decree.\"","It did not take long for the news of Low-Rank Concubine Yan's pregnancy to spread to every concubine in the inner palace.","For a time, hundreds of people simply could not accept it.","No one in the inner palace had been pregnant for over ten years. They had assumed it was because the Emperor was getting older and his endurance was lacking, which was why they could not conceive.","But now, Low-Rank Concubine Yan had become pregnant after only two months of his favor. Could it be that the Emperor was not the problem after all?","Upon learning of Low-Rank Concubine Yan's pregnancy, the Empress immediately rushed over to offer endless advice and arranged for over a dozen palace maids and eunuchs to wait on her.","If the other concubines were merely jealous of Low-Rank Concubine Yan, the birth mothers of the Prince of Qi and the Prince of Ying were downright terrified.","If a prince was born, wouldn't that mean another rival competing with their sons for the throne!","The Prince of Ying's birth mother, Noble Consort Rong, slumped onto her couch, muttering to herself in disbelief.","\"How could she be pregnant? Hasn't the Emperor already...\" She shut her mouth tightly just before the words slipped out, her brows locked in a deep frown.","The Emperor had already lost his ability to sire children, so how could he get a woman pregnant?","When the Prince of Qi, Xiao Rongche, first heard the news, he thought it was a mere rumor.","\"Who is this Low-Rank Concubine Yan? Why have I never heard of her?\"","The steward responsible for relaying palace news replied, \"Recently, the Emperor has bestowed his favor upon quite a few young, low-ranking concubines who were previously out of favor. Low-Rank Concubine Yan is one of them. Director Gu stated that she is already a month and a half pregnant.\"","Xiao Rongche placed his hands on either side of his forehead, massaging his temples with his palms.","\"Imperial Father is already at such an age. How can a prince still be born? This child truly should not have come.\"","The steward reminded him softly, \"Your Highness, perhaps it will be a princess.\"","Xiao Rongche opened his eyes, a dark glint flashing in their depths.","It had better be a princess. If it was a prince, there was no guarantee he would grow up safely.","Upon learning of Low-Rank Concubine Yan's pregnancy, Xiao Rongyan rushed straight to the palace to question Noble Consort Rong.","All the servants in the Palace of Eternal Harmony were dismissed from the room.","\"Mother, how could Low-Rank Concubine Yan be expecting? Didn't you say that Imperial Father could no longer impregnate women?\"","Noble Consort Rong sat on her chaise longue, her face filled with worry.","\"I do not know what is going on either. That palace maid definitely drugged your imperial father back then; otherwise, the inner palace would not have gone so many years without a pregnancy.\"","Xiao Rongyan slowly walked over and crouched before Noble Consort Rong. \"Could it be that the child in Low-Rank Concubine Yan's belly does not belong to Imperial Father?\"","Noble Consort Rong's eyes widened abruptly, glaring larger than a bull's, and she drew in a sharp breath.","\"Are you saying Low-Rank Concubine Yan committed adultery?\"","Xiao Rongyan nodded. \"Besides Imperial Father, there are guards in the palace. It is entirely possible that Low-Rank Concubine Yan could not bear the loneliness. Otherwise, there is no way to explain why she alone is expecting.\"","After pondering for a moment, Noble Consort Rong felt her son's words made sense.","Since the Emperor could not get a woman pregnant, the child in Low-Rank Concubine Yan's womb had to belong to someone else.","\"I will investigate this matter. As long as they are still in contact, I will definitely root him out.\"","Shifting her gaze, Noble Consort Rong stared at Xiao Rongyan and urged him to have children. \"Yan'er, both you and the Prince of Qi only have daughters and no sons. Whoever manages to produce your imperial father's first imperial grandson will surely bring him great joy.\"","\"A while ago, I had your maternal grandfather search the civilian populace for a few women who are well-suited for childbearing. I will have them sent to your manor today.\"","Xiao Rongyan replied, \"Thank you for your concern, Mother. I will work hard.\"","Both of them thought they would soon uncover Low-Rank Concubine Yan's secret lover, but who could have known that just a few days later, another concubine in the palace would become pregnant.","Inside a humble palace chamber, Noble Consort Rong watched as rewards were carried in endlessly like flowing water, her expression turning as dark as coal.","How could this be!","Surely Attendant Hai had not committed adultery as well!","With two pieces of good news in succession, Xiao Chengjing was smiling even while reviewing memorials upon returning to the Imperial Study.","After going through two memorials, he suddenly thought of something and turned his head to instruct Zhao Yande.","\"Summon County Princess Linghui into the palace for an audience, and bring Gu Jupu to me as well.\"","Song Jinzhao, who had been packing her things, was called into the palace before she could even change her clothes.","Just as she walked into the Imperial Study and prepared to kneel in greeting, the Emperor stopped her.","\"Dispense with the formalities. I have summoned the two of you here today to assign you an important task.\"","Hearing Xiao Chengjing say there was an important task, an ominous feeling welled up in Song Jinzhao's heart. She had a strong sense that this would not be a good thing.","She glanced at Gu Jupu standing beside her, and he returned a look telling her to stay calm.","Xiao Chengjing said sternly, \"Two concubines in the palace are pregnant at the same time. It is inevitable that Director Gu will be stretched too thin trying to care for them alone.\"","\"I have already witnessed County Princess Linghui's medical skills. To protect the imperial heirs, starting today, you will reside in the palace. You no longer need to attend to the Empress. I am entrusting Attendant Hai's pregnancy to your care. You must ensure she safely delivers a prince.\"","Song Jinzhao fluttered her eyelashes in astonishment.","Were all those imperial physicians in the Imperial Hospital just fed for nothing? They couldn't even protect a pregnancy, and now she was being forced to live in the palace on call twenty-four hours a day.","This wasn't a matter of a day or two. The pregnancy was only a month along, which meant there were eight months left until the delivery. She absolutely could not agree to such a long commitment."]},{"number":288,"title":"Chapter 288: All Fourteen Imperial Concubines Are Expecting","paragraphs":["Forcing a stiff smile, she said to Xiao Chengjing, \"In reply to Your Majesty, when summoned to the palace, this subject was packing her luggage at home. I am to take my younger brother and sister back to our hometown to pay respects to our ancestors in a few days. Many imperial physicians in the palace specialize in women's and children's ailments. They are surely more skilled in stabilizing a pregnancy than this subject. It would be more appropriate to entrust the care of Attendant Hai's imperial fetus to the Imperial Academy of Medicine.\"","Xiao Chengjing's lips turned downward, and he frowned in dissatisfaction.","\"In a few days, your brother will take up his post at the Hanlin Academy. As the third-ranking scholar of the imperial examination, how could he not return to pay respects to his ancestors? Once Attendant Hai gives birth to the imperial child, I will grant Song Qiming four months of leave. You can all return together then.\"","Song Jinzhao looked troubled. \"In that case, this subject thanks Your Majesty for your profound grace. However, my youngest brother is truly young and lacks an elder's care. If I were to reside in the palace constantly, I would be deeply worried. Why not let the imperial physicians care for Attendant Hai's imperial fetus? I can enter the palace every few days to check her pulse and ensure the fetus is safe. This would also prevent outsiders from thinking that the imperial physicians are nothing but useless fools, with medical skills so poor they cannot even stabilize a pregnancy, which is why Your Majesty does not trust them.\"","Hearing this, Gu Jupu, the head of the Imperial Academy of Medicine, had no choice but to step forward and speak. Otherwise, the imperial physicians would truly become the useless fools Song Jinzhao described. How could they show their faces in the future?","\"Your Majesty, many physicians in the Imperial Academy of Medicine excel in gynecology. Imperial Physician Hong and Imperial Physician Cheng have practiced medicine for many years. They were the ones who cared for Noble Consort Jin and Noble Consort Rong when they safely gave birth to the two princes. If they are entrusted with the care of Attendant Hai's imperial fetus, the pregnancy will undoubtedly be secure.\"","Xiao Chengjing rhythmically tapped his hand on the dragon desk. After a long moment, he spoke, \"Since that is the case, Imperial Physician Hong will be responsible for Attendant Hai's imperial fetus. County Princess Linghui will only need to enter the palace daily to check the pulses of the two pregnant concubines, just to ensure nothing goes wrong.\"","Sitting in the carriage leaving the palace, Song Jinzhao looked at the dragon-shaped jade tablet in her hand, engraved with the words 'Unrestricted Palace Access,' and felt nothing but exhaustion.","Upon returning to the County Princess's estate and seeing that Song Shixue had already packed their trunks, Song Jinzhao sighed helplessly and sat down.","Noticing her elder sister's gloomy expression, Song Shixue could not help but ask, \"Sister, what is wrong? Has the Empress's headache flared up again?\"","Just as Song Jinzhao was about to speak, Song Qiming and Song Gaoli walked in, looking travel-worn and carrying quite a few things in their arms.","Seeing them packing, Song Qiming said, \"Sister, today my teacher introduced Gaoli to the Minister of War. Lord Wu said that many new scholars are fighting for the only vacant official position in the Ministry of War. If he wants it, he has to take up the post as soon as possible. He cannot go back.\"","Song Gaoli handed a prepared letter to Song Jinzhao.","\"Sister Jinzhao, could you help me take this letter back, along with these things?\"","Song Jinzhao pressed her lips into a thin line, helplessly took the letter, and placed it on the table.","\"Shixue and I cannot go back either. There are pregnant concubines in the palace, and the Emperor has ordered me to enter the palace daily until they safely give birth. For the next eight months, I cannot leave the capital. I will have someone take the letter and the things back to the village.\"","Song Qiming was stunned at first, then lowered his eyes with a complex expression.","Song Shixue unhappily slumped her shoulders and complained.","\"Are there not imperial physicians in the palace? You just cured the Empress's headache, and now there are other concubines. The Emperor is too demanding.\"","Song Qiming furrowed his brows, looked up, and said in a hoarse voice, \"Shixue, watch your words. Some things cannot be spoken aloud.\"","Song Shixue closed her mouth, feeling wronged.","Song Qiming turned his head to Song Gaoli and said, \"You head back first. I will not accompany you to look for a house this afternoon.\"","After having someone escort Song Gaoli out of the courtyard, Song Qiming closed the door, walked up to Song Jinzhao, and asked in a deep voice, \"Sister, who exactly were you treating when you went to the palace before?\"","Seeing his deliberate action of closing the door, Song Jinzhao knew he already had suspicions, so she simply stopped hiding it.","\"It was the Emperor. He wants another prince.\"","His guess confirmed, Song Qiming sat down, resting his forehead in his hand. \"No wonder my teacher said that. It turns out to be true.\"","Song Jinzhao raised her eyebrows. \"Lord Ye already knew?\"","Song Qiming nodded. \"When news of the pregnant concubines came out of the palace a few days ago, my teacher suspected it. He asked me in passing, saying that no one in the palace had been pregnant for so many years, and since you had been entering the palace frequently recently, whether it had something to do with you. I did not pay attention to it at the time, but I did not expect it to be true.\"","Hearing this, Song Shixue suddenly understood.","\"I was wondering why Sister took so long to treat Her Majesty the Empress's headache. It turns out she was not treating her at all.\"","Song Jinzhao lowered her voice and explained to them, \"The Emperor did not want anyone to know about his impotence, so he used the Empress's headache as a cover. Although concubines in the inner palace are now pregnant, you two must keep this a secret. You cannot reveal a single word.\"","Song Qiming and Song Shixue nodded heavily in agreement.","When Prince Qi and Prince Ying learned that there was another pregnant concubine in the palace, they remained speechless for a long time.","Not only that, but the subsequent development of events far exceeded their imaginations. Even the civil and military officials found it unbelievable when they heard the news.","The concubines whom Xiao Chengjing had favored over the past two months were successively diagnosed as pregnant. The number of pregnant concubines in the palace went from two to fourteen.","With so many people, Gu Jupu and Song Jinzhao simply could not take care of them all. The Emperor stopped being picky about which imperial physicians to use and simply issued an edict ordering Gu Jupu, as the Head of the Imperial Academy of Medicine, to assign personnel. If anything went wrong, the Imperial Academy of Medicine would be held accountable.","Song Jinzhao still had to enter the palace daily to act as a gatekeeper and oversee things.","The concubines in the inner palace went from being jealous of Low-Rank Concubine Yan's pregnancy at the very beginning, to becoming almost numb as news of pregnancies was announced every few days.","The clever ones ran to the Emperor to show their attentiveness, hoping to serve him in bed, but Xiao Chengjing completely ignored them.","In the Palace of Eternal Harmony, Noble Consort Rong had given up investigating who Low-Rank Concubine Yan's secret lover was.","It was impossible for so many concubines to be having affairs at the same time. The only explanation was that the Emperor was capable of getting women pregnant again.","Prince Ying sat on a soft cushion with a gloomy face, his hands resting on his knees tightly clenched into fists.","\"It must be Song Jinzhao. She must have cured Imperial Father.\"","\"Treating the Empress was a cover, and Gu Jupu caring for the low-ranking concubines was also premeditated. Imperial Father is hiding this from us.\"","Noble Consort Rong anxiously clutched her silk handkerchief. \"By doing this, is the Emperor dissatisfied with you and Prince Qi? If a prince is truly born, the position of the Crown Prince might be in jeopardy.\"","Xiao Rongyan raised his fist and slammed it hard on the table, splashing all the water out of the teacup.","\"It is all because of this Song Jinzhao. Ever since she entered the capital, nothing has gone right for me. If I do not eliminate her, it will be hard to relieve the hatred in my heart.\"","In the Palace of Eternal Longevity, Prince Qi, Xiao Rongche, said to Noble Consort Jin, \"Mother, someone among these fourteen concubines will definitely give birth to a prince. Can we get rid of the children in their bellies first?\"","Noble Consort Jin's gaze suddenly darkened, and she refused without hesitation.","\"No. One or two miscarriages could be called an accident, but if all fourteen miscarry, the Emperor will definitely order a thorough investigation. When that brings disaster upon us, neither you nor I will be able to save ourselves.\""]},{"number":289,"title":"Chapter 289: Imperial Concubine Jin Extends an Invitation","paragraphs":["Inside the Imperial Academy of Medicine, Gu Jupu swept a stern gaze over the fourteen imperial physicians standing in the room.","\"Physician Xu, you will be responsible for Low-Rank Concubine Yan; Physician Hong, you are in charge of caring for Attendant Hai's dragon fetus; Physician Cheng, you take Female Attendant Wu...\"","After assigning all fourteen men, Gu Jupu addressed them loudly, \"Everyone must pay a hundred and twenty percent attention. If anything happens to the concubines you are responsible for, even I won't be able to protect you when His Majesty's blame comes down.\"","\"If you encounter any tricky problems, you must immediately inform me and County Princess Linghui. Do not be negligent or let your guard down.\"","Physician Xu looked up, his eyes shining.","\"So County Princess Linghui will be coming to the Imperial Academy of Medicine? Aside from matters regarding the pregnant concubines, can we consult her on other difficult medical problems?\"","The other thirteen nodded in agreement. They also wanted to ask this question; it would be wonderful if they could learn County Princess Linghui's skill of cutting open stomachs.","Gu Jupu's face darkened. \"You should put all your energy into the dragon fetuses. The County Princess is very busy and doesn't have that much time to answer your questions and clear your doubts.\"","Physician Cheng said, \"Of course we value the dragon fetuses, but we can't just stay in the young mistresses' palaces all day without leaving.\"","Physician Hong added, \"It is precisely because our medical skills are lacking that we must learn from County Princess Linghui. How can we let such a good opportunity slip by?\"","Looking at the two physicians whose status was second only to his own, Gu Jupu pursed his lips and said, \"The County Princess will enter the palace every morning to check the pulses of the young mistresses. Afterward, she might sit in the Imperial Academy of Medicine for a short while.\"","\"Whether you can get the County Princess's guidance will depend on your own abilities.\"","At a temporarily cleared desk in the Imperial Academy of Medicine, Song Jinzhao was leaning back in a chair, reading medical books collected by the palace.","On her right side were tea and pastries.","\"Head Physician Gu, may I take these medical books back to my manor to read?\"","Gu Jupu stopped recording the pulse cases, looked up, and glanced at the stack of medical books on the desk.","\"The County Princess may take any medical books from the Academy. Just remember to return them when you are done.\"","On a chair by the bookshelf, Physician Hong's fingers had almost rubbed the skin off his pen.","Hearing their conversation, he immediately took out a medical book preserved for hundreds of years from a drawer under the cabinet.","\"This is a rare copy of a medical book my grandfather found early on. If the County Princess doesn't mind, you can take it back to read.\"","Looking at the old cover handed to the desk, Song Jinzhao reached out, took it, and casually flipped through a few pages.","The book recorded many diseases of various body parts and included real cases and treatment processes, like a summary of a doctor's many years of practice.","Judging from the years of the cases, this book was written over two hundred years ago.","\"Thank you, Physician Hong. Some of the conditions in here are quite useful for reference.\"","Receiving a response, Physician Hong immediately pulled over a chair, sat next to Song Jinzhao, and started chatting with her.","\"To be honest with the County Princess, I have studied some of the conditions in there for years but have never fully understood them.\"","Saying this, he reached out and quickly flipped through the book.","Sitting opposite, Physician Xu curled his lips and rolled his eyes at Physician Hong.","How did he let him get ahead? He intentionally brought a medical book from home; what a good scheme.","Returning from the palace, Song Jinzhao said, \"Didn't you say you were bored staying at home? These are all rare copies collected by the Imperial Academy of Medicine. Study them well.\"","Song Shixue, who was holding her young brother's hand teaching him to write, had her eyes light up. She put down the pen and came over.","Opening any book at random, she found they were all ones she had never read.","She excitedly hugged the books and said to Song Jinzhao, \"Sister, you are amazing! Can we copy these?\"","Song Jinzhao shook her head and vetoed, \"No, but you can summarize them yourself after reading. Just don't copy them word for word.\"","Song Shixue understood instantly.","She nodded vigorously, then carefully hugged the books and placed them neatly on the bookshelf behind the desk.","As Song Jinzhao went to the palace every day to hold the fort, it wasn't just Prince Qi and Prince Ying who caught on; the civil and military officials also started to form their own speculations.","A beaming Ye Liangyu held up a wine cup to toast Song Jinzhao.","\"The County Princess is indeed formidable. Now, Lao Fei and I won't have to set our sights on the imperial clan's descendants anymore.\"","Even if only half of the fourteen concubines were carrying male fetuses, that would still mean seven princes.","Currently, the Emperor was in good health. Living until they were in their teens would be absolutely no problem, and by then, there would be many more choices.","After staying in the Imperial Academy of Medicine for seven consecutive days, the imperial physicians in the palace had all become familiar with Song Jinzhao.","The collision between modern medical ideology and ancient medical thinking often sparked considerable inspiration.","The imperial physicians broadened their horizons, and Song Jinzhao also gained a lot in return.","\"This servant pays respects to County Princess Linghui. My lady is feeling unwell and her stomach suddenly hurts terribly. I beseech the County Princess to quickly go and take a look.\"","Song Jinzhao looked at the unfamiliar palace maid; she hadn't seen her in the palaces of the pregnant concubines.","\"Who is your lady?\"","The palace maid raised her chin. \"My lady is Noble Consort Jin.\"","Song Jinzhao looked her up and down, thought for a second, and then turned her head to shout into the inner room.","\"Head Physician Gu, Noble Consort Jin is unwell and requests your consultation.\"","The palace maid widened her eyes, frowned in dissatisfaction, and said to Song Jinzhao, \"County Princess, Her Ladyship asked you to treat her, not Imperial Physician Gu.\"","Song Jinzhao asked in return, \"Is Noble Consort Jin pregnant?\"","The palace maid shook her head.","Song Jinzhao said, \"The Emperor only ordered me to care for the dragon fetuses of the fourteen pregnant concubines. Noble Consort Jin is not pregnant, so she is not within my scope of duties.\"","Raising her voice, the palace maid retorted incredulously and angrily, \"My lady is a Noble Consort! Is she not worthy of having the County Princess treat her?\"","Song Jinzhao stood up and gathered her things, preparing to leave the palace.","\"When people in the palace fall ill, they must seek an imperial physician, but I am not an imperial physician.\"","Watching Song Jinzhao's carefree departing figure, the palace maid felt as uncomfortable as if she had swallowed a fly.","She stomped her feet in a huff and walked out.","Leaving a room full of imperial physicians looking at each other in dismay—so, should they send an imperial physician over to look or not?","Didn't she say Noble Consort Jin's stomach hurt?","Called out, Gu Jupu stood at the door in a dilemma. Going or not going right now were both bad options; he was bound to get a scolding either way.","In the end, he still went to the Palace of Eternal Longevity.","He really couldn't diagnose any illness, so he finally had to say she had caught a chill in the evening that affected her stomach. He threw out a few perfunctory words of advice and left.","She was clearly faking an illness. What was Noble Consort Jin trying to do?","After finishing his shift in the evening, Gu Jupu stopped by the County Princess's manor on his way.","Song Jinzhao was looking at account books.","\"I went to the Palace of Eternal Longevity to check. Noble Consort Jin's health is perfectly fine.\"","Song Jinzhao replied, \"Whether she is fine or not has nothing to do with me. There are dozens of imperial physicians in the palace; can't she find one to treat her?\"","Trying to fleece her specifically, treating her as if she were easy to bully.","Gu Jupu looked troubled.","\"Noble Consort Jin is, after all, the birth mother of His Highness Prince Qi and is deeply favored by the Emperor. If she whispers in the Emperor's ear, I fear His Majesty might blame the County Princess.\"","Song Jinzhao raised an eyebrow slightly. \"A mother's honor depends on her son, and a mother's lowliness is due to her son. Tell me, in the Emperor's heart, who is more important: the dragon fetuses or Noble Consort Jin?\"","Gu Jupu: \"...\""]},{"number":290,"title":"Chapter 290: Failing in Accusation and Getting Reprimanded Instead","paragraphs":["Inside Yongshou Palace.","Noble Consort Jin had sent people to invite him three times before Xiao Chengjing finally came to her palace for dinner.","\"Your Majesty, this is the peach blossom mandarin fish soup I specially ordered them to simmer for you. Please have a taste.\"","Her pale fingers appeared exceptionally slender against the golden nail guards, and even the way she held the bowl seemed meticulously practiced.","Xiao Chengjing nodded, signaling Noble Consort Jin to place the soup bowl in front of him, then picked up the spoon, scooped a mouthful, and tasted it.","The fresh fish flavor, infused with the scent of peach blossoms, danced on his tongue, and his furrowed brows gradually relaxed.","\"This soup is quite good. The culinary skills of your palace's small kitchen are getting better and better.\"","A maidservant waiting on them smiled and chimed in.","\"No matter how good the small kitchen's skills are, they cannot compare to Her Ladyship's devotion.\"","\"Her Ladyship personally went to the peach orchard to pick these peach blossoms, and even the dew used to boil the soup was collected by Her Ladyship early this morning.\"","Hearing how much effort Noble Consort Jin had put in for him, Xiao Chengjing's heart could not help but soften.","His large hand, wearing a jade thumb ring, covered the woman's soft hand.","\"In the future, you can leave these things to the servants. Your hands are so cold, it pains my heart.\"","Noble Consort Jin turned her hand to clasp Xiao Chengjing's, intertwining their fingers, and said with a bashful look, \"For Your Majesty, I am willing to do anything.\"","\"Cough, cough, cough.\" Her expression changed slightly, and she hurriedly withdrew her hand, covering her mouth and nose with a silk handkerchief as she coughed several times in a row.","Seeing this, Xiao Chengjing quickly showed his concern: \"Why are you suddenly coughing? Did you catch a chill?\"","Noble Consort Jin frowned slightly. \"My stomach hurt a little this afternoon. I must have caught a chill from waking up early. It is nothing serious.\"","Xiao Chengjing: \"Did you summon an imperial physician to take a look?\"","The maidservant immediately complained to Xiao Chengjing with a meaningful tone, \"To reply to Your Majesty, this morning Her Ladyship asked this servant to go to the Imperial Hospital to invite County Princess Linghui over to take a look.\"","Her voice lowered, becoming increasingly aggrieved.","\"But the County Princess said she only treats pregnant concubines. She left without even coming here. Her Ladyship was quite saddened for a good while after she found out.\"","Xiao Chengjing's right hand, resting on the table, paused slightly, and the concern on his face slowly faded away.","He straightened his upper body and said, \"If you are unwell, you can summon an imperial physician. Song Jinzhao is not an imperial physician; she is a County Princess personally titled by me.\"","The maidservant's face turned pale, and she looked at her master in panic.","The hand Noble Consort Jin used to lightly wipe the corners of her mouth stiffened for a moment, but she immediately put on a pitiful expression.","\"I heard that County Princess Linghui has superb medical skills, and even Director Gu cannot compare to her, which is why I sent my maid to invite her.\"","Xiao Chengjing picked up the spoon and took a few more sips.","It was the exact same soup, but in just the span of a few sentences, it no longer tasted as good as before, and the aroma had faded.","\"Minor ailments and pains can be treated by the imperial physicians in the palace. County Princess Linghui already works very hard checking the pulses of fourteen pregnant concubines every day. Do not bother her next time.\"","Noble Consort Jin's face became increasingly stiff.","She awkwardly raised the corners of her mouth and obediently nodded at Xiao Chengjing.","\"Your Majesty's reprimand is right; it was my lack of consideration.\"","Looking at her pretentious expression, Xiao Chengjing suddenly felt that she had aged; wrinkles were even showing on her face.","Compared to the young concubines who had served him in bed recently, her appearance was lacking by more than just a little.","He picked up the handkerchief on the table, wiped his mouth, stood up, and said, \"I am done eating. There are still memorials to review in the Imperial Study. Rest well.\"","Noble Consort Jin's expression changed drastically. Gritting her teeth, she curtsied.","\"I respectfully see Your Majesty off.\"","Watching Xiao Chengjing's heartless departing back, Noble Consort Jin waited until he was gone before standing up with a cold face.","\"I really suffered a double loss. I didn't expect the Emperor to value Song Jinzhao this much. If I had known, I wouldn't have said anything.\"","The maidservant who had spoken earlier bowed her upper body to minimize her presence, terrified that Noble Consort Jin would blame her.","A few days later, Imperial Physician Hong walked into the Imperial Hospital with a frown.","He walked up to Song Jinzhao and said, \"County Princess, Attendant Hai says her stomach hurts. I couldn't find any problem during my examination, so I request you to go take a look.\"","Song Jinzhao raised her eyes, a hint of confusion in her gaze.","\"Wasn't she just fine a moment ago?\"","Imperial Physician Hong: \"It was right after you checked her pulse and left that she said her stomach felt a bit uncomfortable. When I went to see her just now, she said it hurts more than before.\"","Song Jinzhao picked up her medical box and walked out, with Imperial Physician Hong quickly following behind.","When they arrived at Xianyue Pavilion, Attendant Hai was lying in bed with a look of discomfort.","She looked at Song Jinzhao as if she had seen a lifesaver. \"County Princess, please quickly take a look at me. My stomach has been feeling bloated and uncomfortable since just now, and occasionally it hurts a little.\"","Song Jinzhao sat down on the round stool by the bed, opened her medical box, and took out a pulse pillow, placing it under the other woman's wrist.","After a moment, Song Jinzhao asked her uncertainly.","\"Are you sure your stomach hurts?\"","Attendant Hai nodded, staring into Song Jinzhao's eyes, and said, \"It hurt several times just now.\"","Song Jinzhao checked her pulse once more.","The pulse was smooth, even, calm, and gentle.","The fetal pulse was very stable; there was no problem at all.","\"What kind of pain is it?\"","Attendant Hai answered while touching her stomach, \"It comes in waves, like something is pressing on it, like a needle prick.\"","Song Jinzhao withdrew the hand she used to check the pulse. \"How often does it hurt? Is it bloated or painful right now?\"","\"Did you eat a lot this morning?\"","Attendant Hai: \"I just ate two pieces of osmanthus cake earlier. It doesn't hurt right now, just a bit bloated.\"","Song Jinzhao turned her head and glanced at the osmanthus cakes on the table.","They were the size of a thumb; two pieces were not a lot.","\"The fetal pulse is very stable, and there are no major issues. Are you perhaps too nervous?\"","Small strands of hair stuck to the woman's neck; she was sweating quite a bit.","Attendant Hai grabbed Song Jinzhao's hand and pleaded, \"County Princess, I'm so scared. Could you sit here for a while? Please wait until I'm no longer in pain before you leave.\"","Imperial Physician Hong shot Song Jinzhao a pleading look. \"County Princess, how about you sit for a little longer?\"","If something went wrong with the dragon fetus, his old life wouldn't be enough to pay for it.","Seeing one person terrified and the other pleading, Song Jinzhao had no choice but to nod and agree.","Afterwards, every so often, Attendant Hai would frown and say her stomach was uncomfortable, especially whenever Song Jinzhao was about to leave.","After being examined, she would say it felt a little better.","After this happened several times, Song Jinzhao gradually realized something was wrong.","Leaning her back against the chair, she stared fixedly at Attendant Hai.","The stomachache was fake; she simply didn't want her to leave.","What was she trying to do?","Seeing that the sky was about to turn dark, the complexion of Imperial Physician Hong, who had been sitting by their side the entire time, grew increasingly poor.","What on earth was Attendant Hai trying to do? Making things difficult for no reason. If they dragged this out any longer, the palace gates would close.","\"My lady, it is getting late. I see that your stomach is fine, and there are still many official duties to handle at the Imperial Hospital. County Princess Linghui and I will take our leave first.\"","Attendant Hai's eyes flickered. After stammering for a long while, she hurriedly waved at her maid.","\"Since Imperial Physician Hong has official duties to handle, you may return to the Imperial Hospital first. It is fine as long as the County Princess is here.\"","\"Someone, quickly serve the meal. Tell the Imperial Kitchen to send over more dishes. The County Princess will dine in my palace today.\"","Imperial Physician Hong furrowed his brows and looked at Song Jinzhao. Seeing her tacit consent, he then picked up his medical box and left.","\"I shall take my leave.\""]},{"number":291,"title":"Chapter 291: Cut Open Your Belly and Let Commander Fan Escort You","paragraphs":["Song Jinzhao's gaze swept lightly across Attendant Hai's face, her index finger tapping a steady rhythm on the back of her hand.","There was no bad blood between them; it was highly likely that someone had instructed her to do this.","Were they trying to keep her in the palace? And who was the mastermind behind this?","During their meal, Song Jinzhao teased with a smile, \"For someone with an upset stomach, you certainly have a good appetite. Are you still not full after downing two bowls of rice?\"","Attendant Hai stopped her chopsticks awkwardly. \"I'm just afraid of starving the royal fetus.\"","Song Jinzhao picked up the last boiled shrimp from the plate with her chopsticks.","\"Pregnant women shouldn't eat too much, lest the child grows too large to be delivered. If the Emperor orders to save the child at the expense of the mother, I will have no choice but to cut open your stomach and take the child out.\"","Her heart skipping a beat, Attendant Hai looked at Song Jinzhao in disbelief.","\"Cut open my stomach?\"","Song Jinzhao nodded, using her chopsticks to gesture at the other woman's belly. \"Just like gutting a fish, scooping out all the innards and roe.\"","\"But don't worry, my blade is very fast. It will only hurt for a moment. Once you're dead, you won't feel any pain.\"","\"Gulp.\" Attendant Hai swallowed nervously in terror, as if she could already picture herself being sliced open during childbirth.","Taking in the pale face and trembling hands, Song Jinzhao curled her lips in a cold sneer.","To dare scheme against someone with such little courage—the mastermind had certainly chosen a dull blade for the job.","After dinner, the sky outside had grown so dark that one couldn't see their own fingers in front of them.","Having entirely lost her appetite, Attendant Hai spoke to Song Jinzhao with a dry voice, \"It is getting late. You should leave the palace soon.\"","It seemed she didn't want to keep her in the palace overnight; dragging it out this late was simply to wait for nightfall.","Song Jinzhao replied, \"The palace gates are already closed at this hour. I shall stay overnight in your quarters today, just in case your stomach starts hurting again.\"","Attendant Hai quickly waved her hands in refusal. \"It doesn't hurt at all anymore. Perhaps, as you said, I was just a little nervous because it's my first pregnancy.\"","\"You see, there is only one room in my quarters, and the adjacent ones are for the servants. I truly have nowhere to host you.\"","\"Didn't the Emperor grant you a token that allows you to enter and exit the palace freely? With that token, you can leave even if the gates are closed.\"","Seeing her insist on making her leave the palace, Song Jinzhao became even more certain that danger awaited her outside.","Noble Consort Jin from a few days ago likely had the exact same goal.","She was the biological mother of the Prince of Qi.","Could the mastermind be Xiao Rongche?","The imperial guards, having already changed shifts, saw someone trying to leave the palace and immediately stepped forward to stop the carriage.","He said sternly, \"The palace gates are closed for the night. Everyone must halt. Who is sitting in the carriage?\"","Song Jinzhao lifted the carriage curtain.","Upon seeing her, the guard who spoke immediately took a step back and lowered his head.","\"So it is County Princess Linghui. Why are you out so late today?\"","A few days ago, when he was on the day shift, County Princess Linghui had left the palace in the morning.","Song Jinzhao replied, \"Attendant Hai was feeling unwell, so I stayed a bit later.\"","The guard said, \"I see. Please wait a moment, I will have someone open the gates immediately.\"","Two men forcefully pushed the locked bolt to the right.","The creaking sound was exceptionally piercing in the silent, nocturnal palace.","Fan Guanshan, the commander of the imperial guards who was patrolling the palace walls, heard the noise and walked down the stone steps.","\"Who is opening the palace gates?\"","Normally, if someone needed to enter or exit the palace at night due to special circumstances, servants and imperial physicians would use the side doors.","Why was the side gate being opened now?","The guard opening the gate immediately stopped what he was doing, turned around, and explained, \"Reporting to the Commander, it is County Princess Linghui who wishes to leave the palace.\"","Song Jinzhao stared at the approaching Fan Guanshan, a faint, dark glint flashing in her eyes.","Perfect timing.","\"Commander Fan was here when I entered the palace this morning. Why haven't you finished your shift at such a late hour?\"","Seeing that it was Song Jinzhao, Fan Guanshan dropped his guard.","\"I was planning to do one more patrol before leaving. Why are you heading back so late today?\"","Song Jinzhao feigned a troubled expression and said, \"Attendant Hai had an upset stomach and kept holding onto me, refusing to let me leave. I had no choice but to stay this late.\"","\"It is so dark, and it is only my maid and me. It is truly a bit frightening. Since Commander Fan is also leaving the palace, could you escort me back to my estate along the way?\"","Fan Guanshan paused for a moment.","Didn't County Princess Linghui know martial arts?","Would someone who had killed people be afraid of walking at night?","Surely she couldn't be afraid of ghosts.","Song Jinzhao pressed, \"Commander Fan?\"","Fan Guanshan replied, \"Please wait a moment. I will go get my horse.\"","Song Jinzhao stepped out of the carriage, extended her hand, and gestured, \"The night winds and dew are heavy. Riding a horse in the wind might give you facial paralysis. It would be better for Commander Fan to ride in the carriage.\"","Just as Fan Guanshan was about to refuse, Song Jinzhao spoke again.","\"If Lord Fan were to fall ill because of this, it would be my fault. Please hurry and get in.\"","Seeing Song Jinzhao slip back into the carriage after she finished speaking, Fan Guanshan had no choice but to follow her inside.","The carriage drove out of the palace gates, and the side gate closed again behind them.","Inside the carriage, Fan Guanshan sat as stiffly as a statue.","Remembering that Song Jinzhao was only eighteen, he spoke up, \"Given your noble status now, you should bring a few more servants when you go out in the future. One maid is not enough; you should have at least one male servant.\"","Song Jinzhao curled her lips into a faint smile and said, \"I am not used to bringing many people with me when I go out, and I didn't expect it to get this late today. Thank you for the trouble, Commander Fan.\"","Fan Guanshan shook his head. \"It is a trivial matter, no trouble at all.\"","On the streets after the second watch, not a single soul could be seen.","The moon was veiled in a gray layer of dark clouds. The lantern hanging on the carriage was the only source of light on the street, while everything beyond three meters was pitch black.","After struggling internally for a while, Fan Guanshan couldn't hold back his doubts.","\"I heard that in Xining City, you not only killed spies from the Shuobei Kingdom but also helped the county office slay quite a few bandits and robbers. How could you be afraid of traveling at night now?\"","\"From what I can tell, the maid driving the carriage outside also seems to know martial arts.\"","There were calluses on the webbing and palms of her hands from years of gripping a sword, which were especially obvious when she pulled the reins just now.","Song Jinzhao looked at him with an expression of deep sentiment.","\"It is precisely because I have killed so many people that my heart is uneasy. I am not afraid of people, but of ghosts—especially evil spirits.\"","\"Women have heavy yin energy and attract these things the most. Unlike Lord Fan, who, as a man, possesses flourishing yang energy that even ghosts and spirits must avoid.\""]},{"number":292,"title":"Chapter 292: Two Groups of Assassins","paragraphs":["Fan Guanshan, who was over forty, laughed along. \"I didn't expect the County Princess to believe in ghosts and gods.\"","Folk legends say that female ghosts suck the life force of men. He now felt a chill all over his body.","Especially his back, as if a female ghost outside the carriage was staring at him, her mouth full of sharp teeth dripping with blood.","Song Jinzhao crossed her arms over her chest. \"People believe there are gods in heaven, so why can't they believe there are ghosts and monsters below?\"","She lowered her voice, her tone becoming light and airy.","\"But sometimes, people are more terrifying than ghosts.\"","Fan Guanshan closed his mouth, not wanting to say another word. He felt an eerie atmosphere all around him.","In a dark alley by the street, a masked man in night clothes stared intently at the slowly approaching carriage.","Just as the horse's head was about to pass the alley, he swung his sword down fiercely and ordered in a hoarse voice, \"Do it.\"","The sound of something piercing the air from a distance rang in Song Jinzhao's ears. She lowered her eyes and glanced outside the carriage.","There really was an ambush, and the distance was closing in.","Hearing the footsteps, Fan Guanshan frowned, panic rising in his chest.","Were ghosts really coming?","The next second, doubt crept in. Don't ghosts float when they walk? Why would there be footsteps?","Then he realized people were rushing out of the alley.","Dressed in black and masked, holding weapons in their hands, their eyes gleamed with a cold, murderous intent.","Qingshuang immediately sped up and shouted, \"County Princess, there are assassins!\"","Fan Guanshan's pupils shrank. He quickly glanced at Song Jinzhao. It wasn't ghosts; it was assassins.","After surrounding the carriage, the assassins launched a fierce attack.","The unarmed Qingshuang dodged an incoming longsword, grabbed the attacker's wrist backhandedly, twisted it hard, caught the dropping sword, and ruthlessly thrust it into his heart.","Two narrow swords pierced into the carriage. As she tilted her head, the reflective blades passed right by Song Jinzhao's neck, heading straight for Fan Guanshan's eyes.","Fan Guanshan grabbed the scimitar beside his hand and chopped off the incoming sword tips with a single strike.","Seeing Song Jinzhao's calm and unbothered demeanor, sudden realization dawned on him.","Afraid of the dark and ghosts? Nonsense, it was all a lie.","She knew all along there would be an assassination attempt, which was why she dragged him along.","For such a young girl, she was quite scheming.","With more and more assassins appearing, Fan Guanshan had no time to dwell on being fooled by Song Jinzhao. He gripped his scimitar and rushed out.","Leaping onto the roof of the carriage, he wielded his scimitar with masterful skill. Every strike drew blood, and no swing was wasted.","Upon seeing the man's face clearly, the lead assassin's eyes widened in shock. Why was Fan Guanshan in the carriage?","Wasn't County Princess Linghui supposed to be sitting inside?","As screams rang out continuously, Song Jinzhao twirled the silver needles she held in her hand.","The assassins ambushing on the eaves looked down in confusion at the people already fighting below.","Why were there other assassins?","Were there really this many people who wanted to kill County Princess Linghui!","They hadn't even made their move yet!","\"Boss, Commander Fan is here. Are we still going to do it?\"","The lead assassin clenched his fists and gritted his teeth.","\"The Prince ordered that he must hear the news of County Princess Linghui's death tonight.\"","\"Now that they have Fan Guanshan tied up, it's the perfect time for us to strike at Song Jinzhao.\"","Taking advantage of the moment Fan Guanshan jumped off the carriage to fight the others, the assassin leader gave the order, and over a dozen men flew down from the roof simultaneously.","Looking at the sudden appearance of another group of people, Qingshuang shouted back in panic.","\"County Princess, there are a dozen more assassins!\"","Song Jinzhao lifted the torn carriage curtain, ruthlessly smashing a thick wooden board down onto a man's head.","The wooden bench that had been nailed inside the carriage behind her was now gone.","Splinters flew. Splattered brains and bulging eyeballs spun a full three hundred and sixty degrees along with the board.","In the blink of an eye, the severed head fell to the ground.","With a dark gleam in her eyes, Song Jinzhao flicked her index finger.","Several flashes of silver pierced the dark night sky, accurately embedding themselves into the assassins' eyes.","Agonizing screams tore through the air. The commoners living along the street were jolted awake from their dreams, breaking out in a cold sweat upon hearing the shrieks.","The entangled Fan Guanshan looked up and saw Song Jinzhao pull out a longsword stuck in the carriage, slitting the throats of five men with a single stroke. His mouth dropped open in astonishment.","A cold light flashed past his eyes; as he ducked his head, a lock of his flying hair was sliced off.","\"You're courting death!\" he cursed fiercely, kicking the assassin away. He backhandedly snatched a short sword from another person and threw it, piercing the man's stomach.","Miserable screams echoed repeatedly. The awakened commoners hugged their quilts, trembling in fear, not daring to make a sound.","The bricks on the ground were stained dark red with blood. Song Jinzhao pressed her right foot down heavily on a man's stomach, the bloody blade resting across his neck.","\"Who sent you to kill me?\"","The assassin, determined to die, stared at Song Jinzhao. His lips twitched slightly as he bit down on the poison hidden between his teeth, bleeding from his seven orifices and dying instantly.","\"County Princess, here is another one alive.\" Qingshuang dragged over a gagged assassin and threw him in front of Song Jinzhao.","\"These people are death soldiers. If the assassination fails, they immediately commit suicide. They all have poison hidden in their mouths.\"","With disheveled hair, Fan Guanshan grabbed two assassins by their necks and threw them to the ground. Their mouths were dripping with blood, their teeth completely shattered.","Song Jinzhao leaned over and pried open the assassin's mouth.","The sharp blade was inserted and twisted in a circle. When she pulled it out, not a single tooth remained, yet she hadn't harmed his tongue in the slightest.","\"Speak, who ordered you to kill me?\"","The assassin, having a layer of bone scraped off his upper and lower jaws, convulsed in agony. His brain buzzed; he felt that dying would be far more merciful.","But Song Jinzhao deliberately refused to let him die.","The sharp blade sliced across the man's face like carving meat, curling up a slice of cheek flesh.","Heart-wrenching screams echoed from one end of the street to the other.","As clothes were sliced open, Fan Guanshan squinted, unable to bear looking.","It wasn't that he had never seen the punishment of death by a thousand cuts, but the one wielding the knife right now was an eighteen-year-old girl, the emperor's personally titled County Princess Linghui. It truly startled him.","The yamen runners from the Jingzhao Prefecture, who had rushed over upon hearing the noise, went weak in the knees upon seeing the scene before them.","At this moment, in their eyes, Song Jinzhao looked like a vicious ghost crawling out of hell—absolutely terrifying.","\"Commander Fan, County Princess Linghui, what happened here?\"","The head runner looked at the dozens of corpses lying on the ground and swallowed hard in lingering fear.","Judging by their attire, these people should be assassins. Who were they here to kill?","Qingshuang looked at the head runner and said, \"Someone tried to assassinate our County Princess. Fortunately, Commander Fan was escorting us, otherwise the consequences would be unimaginable.\"","Fan Guanshan looked at the assassin who had been tortured beyond recognition, the corner of his mouth twitching three times uncontrollably.","Even without him, the consequences wouldn't have been unimaginable.","With County Princess Linghui's ruthlessness, it really wasn't certain who would be killing whom.","Fan Guanshan said, \"County Princess, since the people from Jingzhao Prefecture have arrived, it's better to hand these assassins over to them for interrogation, lest you dirty your hands.\"","If this continued, the man would probably be tortured to death before spilling the truth.","Hearing Fan Guanshan's words, the head runner nodded hastily.","\"I have already sent someone to notify the Prefectural Magistrate. He must have arrived at the yamen by now. We will interrogate them overnight and definitely give the County Princess an explanation.\"","At the foot of the Son of Heaven, in the vital capital region.","To think that an assassination attempt on a County Princess would happen here. These people were truly too audacious.","Song Jinzhao looked at Fan Guanshan. \"Since Commander Fan says these men are death-sworn assassins, I imagine they will be extremely tight-lipped.\"","\"As this concerns my safety, I intend to personally join the interrogation. Would Commander Fan be willing to accompany me?\"","The Governor of the Jingzhao Prefecture held too low a rank; she needed someone present who could hold the floor and whose words would carry enough weight when it mattered.","Seeing the unwavering resolve in Song Jinzhao's eyes, Fan Guanshan knew he wouldn't be able to get out of this.","Anyone capable of cultivating so many elite assassins was undoubtedly someone of formidable standing.","This was not going to be a trivial matter.","Harboring a sliver of curiosity, Fan Guanshan sheathed his scimitar and said, \"If that is the case, then this humble official shall accompany the County Princess.\""]},{"number":293,"title":"Chapter 293: Interrogated Through the Night, It Was Directed by the King of Qi","paragraphs":["Jiang Dongsheng, the Governor of Jingzhao Prefecture, was woken up in the middle of the night. When he saw the two people who had been brought in, his face drastically changed color.","\"Greetings to County Princess Linghui. This humble official pays his respects to Commander Fan.\"","Song Jinzhao said, \"I was ambushed by so many assassins right after leaving the palace. I am afraid I cannot be at peace.\"","Cold sweat poured down Jiang Dongsheng's face.","\"It is this humble official's dereliction of duty. I beg the County Princess for forgiveness.\"","\"Men, lock these three survivors in the cells immediately. I will interrogate them overnight and root out the mastermind.\"","Inside the gloomy prison, the sleeping inmates were awakened by a sudden commotion.","The heavy main door slammed open, crashing against the wall and shaking the room.","Watching the yamen runners drag in three men, one of whom had an upper body that was mangled beyond recognition, two prisoners near the corridor felt sick to their stomachs and threw up on the spot.","\"There is a woman too.\"","\"Are you stupid? With that kind of attire, she is obviously not a prisoner.\"","Looking at Song Jinzhao as she walked in, many people huddled together and whispered.","She wore a yellow dress with narrowed cuffs and a hem that did not drag on the floor. The style was simple, but the embroidered patterns on it were exquisite.","Especially the center of the flowers, which were adorned with thumb-sized pearls.","Her brows carried an aloofness that looked down upon the world. Her fleeting glance swept over them, making them shudder with fear and subconsciously lower their heads, not daring to look again.","Even though Song Jinzhao had just killed more than a dozen people, not a single drop of blood stained her body. Even the tops of her embroidered shoes were perfectly clean.","The three men were tied to wooden crosses.","A basin of cold water was splashed onto them. The assassin who had endured the slicing torture woke up. The glaring firelight forced him to open his eyes and then squeeze them shut again.","On two smooth mahogany chairs, Song Jinzhao and Fan Guanshan sat with calm expressions, watching the Governor conduct the interrogation.","Scorching flames, agonizing screams, the increasingly heavy stench of blood hitting their noses, and fingernails falling to the ground one after another.","Fan Guanshan turned his head to look at Song Jinzhao. \"Is the County Princess not going to handle this personally?\"","Song Jinzhao crossed her legs and smiled faintly.","\"I have already sent my maid back to the manor to fetch my interrogation tools. Let the Governor loosen their bones and muscles first.\"","He had not spoken even after being tortured like that just now. The mouths of these death-sworn soldiers were indeed very tight; they needed some different methods.","Fan Guanshan scanned the hundreds of torture tools in the prison cell. Were these still not enough?","The three men fainted and woke up, woke up and fainted again, but their mouths remained shut tight like mutes, not saying a single word.","At his wits' end, Jiang Dongsheng looked at Song Jinzhao.","\"County Princess, should we take a break? If this continues, they will die.\"","Song Jinzhao said, \"Dragging this out until tomorrow brings too many variables. Who knows if someone might try to break them out of prison? We must get the answers tonight.\"","\"Sister.\" A yamen runner pushed the door open, and Song Qiming walked in holding a box.","His gaze swept over the three men tied to the wooden frames, and he frowned slightly.","\"This humble official pays respects to Commander Fan and Lord Jiang.\"","Jiang Dongsheng hurriedly said, \"Lord Song, there is no need for such formalities.\"","Fan Guanshan gave him a slight nod.","Song Qiming placed the wooden box on the table, then pulled a porcelain bottle from his sleeve and handed it to Song Jinzhao.","\"Qingshuang has already gone to the slaughterhouse. It is not open in the middle of the night, so she will come over a bit later.\"","Song Jinzhao unplugged the porcelain bottle and poured out three black pills.","\"That is fine. Let us start with a little appetizer. Perhaps we will not even need her.\"","After forcing the three pills down their throats, Song Jinzhao opened the lid of the wooden box. Using a pair of tweezers, she placed three centipedes on the foreheads of the three men.","As the two-finger-long centipedes crawled into the assassins' mouths, the yamen runner holding the branding iron could not hold it back and ran outside to vomit on the spot.","Governor Jiang Dongsheng pressed his lips tightly together, forcing himself to endure it.","Fan Guanshan's fingers, which were resting on the chair, subconsciously curled up. His thick eyebrows knitted into a deep frown.","\"The County Princess's interrogation methods are truly unique.\"","Song Jinzhao looked appreciatively at the three men's disgusted, terrified, and agonizing struggles.","\"I have used this method before. Those thug enforcers who tried to kill my brother spilled everything in half the time it takes to drink a cup of tea. I just wonder how long these death-sworn soldiers can hold out.\"","Fan Guanshan thought of how Song Jinzhao had pretended to be afraid to get him to escort her, and he could not help but swallow hard.","Fortunately, not all women in the world were like this, otherwise he really would be a little terrified.","The saying that a woman's heart is the most poisonous was indeed true. She was incredibly fickle.","He cast a glance at Song Qiming, who stood to the side without changing his expression. To be this accustomed to it at fourteen years old, he had probably experienced quite a lot.","In the future, he absolutely could not afford to provoke this County Princess Linghui in the slightest.","The itching in their throats, the pain in their chests, the tightening of their intestines, immense terror hovered over the heads of the three men.","They screamed until their voices went hoarse. Finally, two of the assassins could not bear it anymore and burst into tears.","\"I will talk! I will talk! Please let me go, please take it out!\"","Song Jinzhao used the tip of a knife to slowly trace across one of the men's stomachs.","\"Speak. Who is the mastermind?\"","The centipede gnawing inside his stomach seemed to jump and bite along with the movement, terrifying him into full-body convulsions. It felt as if his soul was floating out of his body.","\"It is Prince Qi. Prince Qi sent us to kill you.\" Tears mixed with blood and saliva flowed down his face, his features contorted in sheer agony.","In the prison cell, Jiang Dongsheng's expression drastically changed, and he looked at the assassin in horror.","Fan Guanshan's frown deepened even further.","It was actually Prince Qi. Why would he want to kill County Princess Linghui?","Song Qiming's hands, hanging by his sides, clenched into tight fists. The veins on the back of his hands bulged, and his eyes revealed a surge of murderous intent.","His teacher was right indeed; neither of the two princes in the court was any good.","Since Prince Qi dared to send people to assassinate his eldest sister, he absolutely could not be allowed to ascend the throne. Moreover, he had to die.","Song Jinzhao continued to ask, \"Why did he want to kill me?\"","The assassin stared in terror at a centipede crawling out of his nostril, his entire body drained of strength.","\"The one responsible for passing the orders was Cen Yue, who is by the Prince's side. He told us to lie in ambush in the alley at the second watch, but he did not say anything else.\""]},{"number":294,"title":"Chapter 294: Resorting to Coercion, Unable to Withstand Torture, Reveals the Mastermind Behind the Scenes","paragraphs":["Looking at the other silent assassin, the torn flesh on his face was still bleeding.","\"Still not going to talk?\"","The assassin stared at Song Jinzhao with an indifferent expression, but the hatred in his eyes seemed as if he wanted to slice her into a thousand pieces.","Seeing this, Song Jinzhao sneered, \"I'd like to see just how stubborn you can be!\"","The clerk sitting on the stool, holding a brush, couldn't stop his hand from trembling when he wrote the words \"Prince of Qi\".","Going against a prince would cost one's life. Even if he really sent someone to assassinate County Princess Linghui, would the Emperor actually kill his own son?","This matter was too big; small fries like them simply couldn't bear the consequences.","Looking at the signed and fingerprinted confession, Fan Guanshan looked at Song Jinzhao with complex eyes.","\"What does the County Princess plan to do next?\"","Song Jinzhao pinched the confession and threw it onto the table.","\"Finish interrogating this remaining person, and then take their confessions into the palace to file an imperial complaint.\"","She didn't have the right to trespass into a prince's estate, so naturally, she had to find someone who did.","This matter wouldn't end easily; she had to make them pay the price.","Fan Guanshan took a deep, nervous breath.","A storm was brewing, and he couldn't imagine how the Emperor would handle this.","Whether he would punish the Prince of Qi or try to smooth things over, tomorrow's morning court was likely to be turned upside down.","After another two quarters of an hour, the yamen runner pushed open the door and walked in with Qingshuang.","\"Woof, woof, woof.\" The sound of a dog barking approached from a distance.","\"County Princess, your maid has arrived.\"","The yamen runner pushed the door open, and Qingshuang walked in leading a dirty black dog.","\"County Princess, as per your request, this servant found one at the butcher's shop.\"","Everyone in the cell looked in confusion at the dog being led in. What was this for?","Was she going to let this dog eat a person?","Song Jinzhao tilted her head and looked at its robust appendage. \"Feed it the medicine. I want to see if he can withstand it.\"","Qingshuang pried open the dog's mouth and poured in a packet of white powder.","The iron chains binding the assassin's hands were untied, and with a thud, the man fell to his knees on the ground.","Iron chains bound his feet, so he couldn't move. He could only endure the physical pain and the torture of the centipedes while panting heavily.","Song Jinzhao stepped on his back with her right foot, leaned down, and whispered a few words into the assassin's ear.","The man looked up in disbelief, his eyes full of shock, as if he were looking at a demon.","\"Everyone step out. Qingshuang, take off his pants.\"","From taking the medicine to its effects kicking in, less than half a quarter of an hour had passed.","Everyone stared dumbfounded into the cell, as if struck by a thunderbolt, completely unable to accept the scene.","\"This... this...\"","The following five hundred words are omitted...","Song Jinzhao leaned leisurely against the wooden railing. Having been a doctor for a long time, she had seen too much; this was just a drizzle.","\"No! I'll talk! I'll talk! I'll talk!\" A sobbing, stammering voice rang out in less than a quarter of an hour, so loud it almost blew the roof off the cell.","The other two assassins tied to the wooden frames felt completely cold, as if they had fallen into an ice hole.","Fortunately, they had confessed quickly just now; otherwise, the consequences would be unimaginable.","When everyone returned to the cell, their entire bodies were weak.","Their worldviews had been shattered and rebuilt, their minds filled with unspeakable images.","After a bowl of water-dissolved antidote was poured down its throat, Qingshuang tied the dog to the table leg. The continuously dripping drool frightened the assassin so much that he soiled himself.","Song Jinzhao slowly sat back in her chair and tapped her finger forcefully on the table.","\"Speak.\"","The man curled up into a ball in terror, his face covered in snot and tears.","\"It's the Prince of Ying. We are the Prince of Ying's men.\"","Boom!","A clap of thunder seemed to strike the heads of Jiang Dongsheng and the others. How did the Prince of Ying get dragged into this too?","Now they were truly doomed.","After the confession was written and fingerprinted, the sky outside had already begun to brighten slightly.","At this time, morning court hadn't started yet.","Song Jinzhao stood up holding the confessions, \"This County Princess is now going to the palace to file an imperial complaint. Are Commander Fan and Lord Jiang going to come along?\"","Jiang Dongsheng shook his head like a rattle drum.","\"This humble official is feeling a bit unwell. Please go ahead, County Princess.\"","At the very least, he had to wait for the Emperor's summons. He absolutely could not enter the palace with County Princess Linghui right now.","Fan Guanshan said, \"It's about time for this commander to enter the palace to guard the imperial city, which happens to be on the same way as the County Princess.\"","This time, Song Jinzhao rode in the carriage that Song Qiming had driven over from the County Princess's estate, while Fan Guanshan led a horse out from the Jingzhao Prefecture to ride.","Right before getting into the carriage, Song Jinzhao beckoned Song Qiming over and whispered a few instructions.","Song Qiming nodded slightly and agreed, \"Don't worry, sister, I will go do it immediately.\"","Seeing the carriage and Fan Guanshan heading toward the palace city, the two groups of people ordered to keep watch opposite the Jingzhao Prefecture changed their expressions drastically, instantly turning into rockets and rushing off in different directions.","\"Your Highness, this is bad! County Princess Linghui and Commander Fan are on their way to the palace.\"","\"Your Highness, this is bad! County Princess Linghui and Commander Fan have entered the palace together.\"","Xiao Rongche, who had been awake all night, sat silently in his chair.","Cen Yue said in a panic, \"It's been a whole night; the captured death warriors must have spilled everything.\"","Xiao Rongche glared at him with icy eyes, and in the next second, his right hand forcefully strangled his neck.","\"They are all useless trash who cling to life and fear death! I told you to train death warriors, and this is how you train them for this prince?\"","Unable to breathe, Cen Yue rolled his eyes in agony, on the verge of suffocation.","On the other side, Xiao Rongyan looked in dissatisfaction at his panicked subordinate.","\"What are you afraid of? As long as this prince doesn't admit it, even if Song Jinzhao has a confession, it won't be of any use.\"","The subordinate said fearfully, \"But Mo Liu has seen this humble servant. When he came to the estate, many people saw him.\"","Xiao Rongyan swept a cold glance over him.","Zhao Yande walked nervously into the Funing Palace. Xiao Chengjing, who had just gotten up not long ago, was having his morning meal.","\"Your Majesty, County Princess Linghui is currently kneeling outside the Baohe Hall requesting an audience with Your Majesty, saying she wants to file an imperial complaint.\"","Though the voice was quiet, it shocked everyone in the hall.","Xiao Chengjing furrowed his brows deeply, \"File what imperial complaint?\"","After hesitating for a long time, Zhao Yande lowered his head even further.","\"Last night, County Princess Linghui was assassinated on her way back to her estate. After a night of interrogation at the Jingzhao Prefecture, the assassins said the ones who ordered them were His Highness the Prince of Qi and His Highness the Prince of Ying.\"","The exquisite porcelain bowl fell to the ground with a clatter, and Xiao Chengjing's face sank like water.","\"Bring her to the Imperial Study, and summon the Governor of the Jingzhao Prefecture, the Prince of Qi, and the Prince of Ying into the palace.\"","Outside the Baohe Hall, the officials who had arrived early looked at Song Jinzhao kneeling on the steps and discussed animatedly among themselves.","Ye Liangyu, who arrived a step late, looked gloomily at Song Jinzhao's back. Today's battle was destined to be very difficult to fight.","Fei Yanzhang, a Grand Secretary of the Hanlin Academy, saw his friend approach and immediately pulled him aside, asking sternly, \"Just now, County Princess Linghui said that the Prince of Qi and the Prince of Ying sent assassins to kill her last night. Did you know about this?\"","Ye Liangyu said, \"I also just found out. Right before I left the house, Qiming rushed over to tell me. The assassins are currently locked up in the Jingzhao Prefecture prison.\"","Fei Yanzhang's eyes widened, \"They've already finished the interrogation and gotten the confessions?\"","Ye Liangyu nodded, \"Both groups have confessed, otherwise the County Princess wouldn't have entered the palace.\"","Fei Yanzhang grabbed his friend's arm, feeling a bit unsteady on his feet.","After a long while, he spat out a sentence, \"I'm afraid this crime won't stick.\"","Ye Liangyu's expression slightly withdrew, his gaze sinking.","\"Even if it's hard to sue, we still have to sue. Even if the crime doesn't stick, we have to make them shed a layer of skin.\"","Upon hearing the urgent summons from the palace, Jiang Dongsheng, who had been sitting on a cold bench for over half an hour, let out a trembling sigh.","\"I couldn't escape it after all. Why am I so unlucky!\"","The civil and military officials watched helplessly as Song Jinzhao was led away by Eunuch Zhao.","Shortly after, Fan Guanshan, Commander of the Imperial Guards, walked toward the Imperial Study with a heavy expression.","A little while later, Jiang Dongsheng, the Governor of Jingzhao Prefecture, along with the Prince of Qi and the Prince of Ying, also arrived.","The crowd looked up at the morning glow rising in the east. It was time for the morning court assembly.","However, the bells and drums had not sounded, and the palace doors remained closed. It was clear that the assembly would not be held today.","The ministers aligned with the Prince of Qi and the Prince of Ying saw Ye Liangyu pull seven imperial censors aside to whisper to them, and their expressions instantly turned grim.","Inside the Imperial Study, Xiao Rongche and Xiao Rongyan were met with their father's furious glare the moment they stepped through the door.","Despite their inner nervousness, the two knelt down, feigning ignorance. \"Your sons pay their respects to Imperial Father.\"","Xiao Chengjing suppressed his anger and interrogated them.","\"Last night, County Princess Linghui and Commander Fan were attacked outside the palace. The assassins claimed they were acting under your orders. What do you have to say for yourselves?\""]},{"number":295,"title":"Chapter 295: Accusing the Emperor Before the Court and Confrontation in the Imperial Hall","paragraphs":["Xiao Rongche's entire body tensed. His eyes, like frightened moths, quickly darted away after colliding with Xiao Chengjing's gaze.","\"I only just learned about the County Princess being assassinated, so how could I have sent people to kill her? I am wrongfully accused.\"","Xiao Rongyan looked indignantly at the Emperor sitting on the dragon throne, his tone carrying a trace of grievance from being falsely accused.","\"Imperial Father, I have no enmity with County Princess Linghui, so why would I send assassins after her? This matter is absolutely a frame-up.\"","Song Jinzhao turned her head to look at the two of them. \"Your Highnesses keep claiming innocence, but why didn't the assassins frame anyone else? Why only frame you?\"","\"You must know that framing a prince is a capital offense.\"","After speaking, she knelt towards Xiao Chengjing on the dragon throne.","\"Your Majesty, according to the confessions of the three assassins, it was the Prince of Qi who ordered his personal guard Cen Yue to give the death-sworn assassins the mission to kill me. Mo Liu, the death-sworn assassin who confessed against the Prince of Ying, even gave the name of Zhao Zhihe, a commanding general of the Prince of Ying's estate. I implore Your Majesty to immediately issue an edict to arrest these two men and bring them to justice. When the time comes, the truth will naturally be revealed.\"","Xiao Chengjing narrowed his eyes and ordered, \"Fan Guanshan, heed my command. Immediately take the Imperial Guards to the Prince of Qi's estate and the Prince of Ying's estate to arrest these two men and bring them to justice.\"","Fan Guanshan knelt to receive the edict. \"This humble official obeys.\"","Seeing Xiao Rongche and Xiao Rongyan kneeling silently on the ground, a flash of speculation crossed Song Jinzhao's eyes.","Not long after, Fan Guanshan hurried into the imperial study and knelt.","\"Answering Your Majesty, this humble official led men to search the estates of the Prince of Qi and the Prince of Ying thoroughly, but did not find Cen Yue and Zhao Zhihe. The stewards of both estates said they hadn't seen them since early morning. They must have fled in fear of punishment.\"","Xiao Rongche immediately knelt and begged for mercy. \"Imperial Father, I am completely unaware of this. Someone must have bribed Cen Yue to plant evidence and frame me.\"","Xiao Rongyan spoke with a resonant and forceful tone, \"Imperial Father, General Zhao would absolutely never assassinate the County Princess. Someone must have kidnapped General Zhao in order to deal with me.\"","\"I beg Imperial Father to immediately order the lockdown of the city. We must find General Zhao to return my innocence.\"","Song Jinzhao said sarcastically, \"I am afraid Cen Yue and Zhao Zhihe have already been silenced by Your Highnesses. In my opinion, what we should be looking for is not people, but corpses.\"","Xiao Rongyan angrily rebuked Song Jinzhao.","\"Watch your words, County Princess. General Zhao is responsible for the safety of the entire Prince of Ying's estate. I would even entrust my own life to him, so how could I kill him?\"","\"I know the County Princess is extremely furious at this moment, but you cannot make arbitrary judgments and play into the hands of the real mastermind.\"","The corners of Song Jinzhao's mouth curled into a cold sneer.","\"Then His Highness the Prince of Ying should tell us, who exactly is this real mastermind behind the scenes?\"","\"Who has formed such a massive grudge with the two princes that they would not hesitate to assassinate me just to frame you?\"","\"And who in the entire capital could cultivate so many death-sworn assassins?\"","The imperial study was dead silent. The eyes of Xiao Chengjing, who sat on the dragon throne, were dark and unreadable.","Unless the two of them were framing each other, who else would dare to frame the current princes?","Seeing that none of them spoke, Song Jinzhao faced Xiao Chengjing and spoke again.","\"Answering Your Majesty, I still have another doubt in my heart.\"","\"Yesterday, Imperial Physician Hong and I took Attendant Hai's pulse. The fetal pulse was clearly very stable, yet the young mistress complained of stomach pains and kept me there until evening before letting me leave.\"","\"I usually leave the palace before noon. Yet yesterday, the assassins seemed to know well in advance that I would leave the palace at that later time, and set up an ambush ahead of time. I have reason to suspect that Attendant Hai was faking her illness. I beseech Your Majesty to summon Attendant Hai here for a confrontation.\"","Xiao Chengjing frowned and instructed Zhao Yande, \"Have someone bring Attendant Hai over.\"","Kneeling on the ground, Xiao Rongche nervously clenched his fists, his heart pounding incessantly.","Xiao Rongyan, kneeling on the right side, glanced at the Prince of Qi.","He himself had not instructed Attendant Hai; the one who instructed her must definitely be his good older brother.","Since he did not sweep his tail clean, he might as well let him take the fall for all the crimes.","Outside the Hall of Preserving Harmony, the civil and military officials who had come to attend the morning assembly had already been standing for two hours.","An impatient official could not help but say to Gu Qishan, \"Prime Minister Gu, it is already late morning. Will this morning assembly still be held?\"","\"How about you go and ask the Emperor?\"","Gu Qishan remained expressionless. \"The Emperor has issued no edict, so we simply wait.\"","Helpless, the crowd stood back in their original places.","So much time had already passed, and no one knew what the situation was inside the imperial study right now.","Was the assassination case really done by the Prince of Qi and the Prince of Ying?","It was worrying them to death.","Just as everyone thought Attendant Hai was about to arrive, the little eunuch who had gone to deliver the message came running in, stumbling and crawling.","\"Your Majesty, terrible news! Attendant Hai fell into the lotus pond in the Imperial Garden. The imperial physicians rushed over and said she might not make it.\""]},{"number":296,"title":"Chapter 296: A Female Naval Officer Drowned, the Case Can Only Be Treated as a Lesser Crime","paragraphs":["Upon the throne, Xiao Chengjing's already ugly expression turned completely black, the veins on his forehead and neck throbbing violently.","He stood up abruptly, sweeping everything on the desk onto the floor.","\"Insolent.\"","Everyone instantly fell to their knees. \"Your Majesty, please calm your anger.\"","Song Jinzhao was surprised at first, then a faint smile rippled at the corners of her mouth.","They were truly foolish to the extreme.","They were forcing Xiao Chengjing to take action. Now she didn't even need to waste her breath.","\"County Princess Linghui, the royal fetus must not be lost. Come with me to save her immediately.\"","Unfortunately, halfway there, they ran into a eunuch coming to report the news.","\"To Your Majesty, Attendant Hai could not be saved. She has already passed away.\"","Arriving at the palace where Attendant Hai lived, the Empress and many concubines had already arrived.","Gu Jupu and Imperial Physician Hong knelt in the hall, feeling as if the sky had fallen.","Encountering such a terrible matter early in the morning, the fourteen pregnant concubines were suddenly short by one. Who knew how angry the Emperor would be.","Song Jinzhao walked to the bed to examine the body. Although the wound from the head impact was large, there was white and pale pink mushroom-like foam at the mouth and nose, which is one of the most important characteristics of death by drowning.","\"When Attendant Hai fell into the lotus pond, did you not go down to save her immediately? How could you let her drown?\"","This single sentence completely ignited Xiao Chengjing's fury.","He glared angrily at the maids and eunuchs standing in the room. \"How exactly did your mistress fall into the lotus pond? Why didn't you save her at the first moment?\"","The three maids and two eunuchs in the room immediately knelt down.","The head maid, who had only been transferred here a few days ago, was covered in tears.","\"To Your Majesty, after our mistress woke up this morning, she said it was stuffy in the room and wanted to stroll in the Imperial Garden. She asked Qiuyue and Lanxin to accompany her. Who knew that an accident would happen not long after she went out.\"","\"This servant hurriedly sent someone to fetch the imperial physician, but who knew it was still a step too late.\"","Xiao Chengjing questioned, \"Who are Qiuyue and Lanxin?\"","A maid with two small braids trembled as she knocked her forehead heavily against the ground.","Qiuyue: \"This servant is Qiuyue. When we reached the Imperial Garden, our mistress said she was cold and asked this servant to come back and get some clothes. By the time I returned, she was already unconscious.\"","Lanxin closed her eyes in deep sorrow, as if knowing she could not escape this.","\"Our mistress fell into the lotus pond because her foot slipped. This servant does not know how to swim, so I could only call for people to come and save her. Who knew it was still a step too late. I beg Your Majesty to spare my life.\"","Song Jinzhao said with a doubtful expression, \"She died right when people were about to be summoned. This is far too coincidental.\"","\"In this subject's view, there might be something fishy about Attendant Hai's death. They did not even spare the fetus; the mastermind behind this is truly vicious.\"","Thinking of his lost child, Xiao Chengjing kicked the maid to the ground.","\"Full of nonsense! With so many maids and eunuchs in the Imperial Garden, you couldn't find a single one who knows how to swim?\"","\"Her foot slipped and she fell into the lotus pond? Are you dead? Didn't you know to support her?\"","\"Men, lock all the maids and eunuchs of Cuiming Pavilion into the Department of Penalties and torture them severely. You must extract the truth.\"","The other four kneeling on the ground raised their heads in terror. \"Your Majesty, we are wronged. We servants are innocent.\"","\"Your Majesty, spare our lives...\"","Returning to the Imperial Study, Xiao Chengjing looked at his two sons kneeling on the ground, the anger in his chest blazing even hotter.","Acting recklessly, deceiving superiors and hiding things from subordinates.","They even dared to lay hands on a concubine carrying a royal fetus. They were simply lawless, not putting him, the Emperor, in their eyes at all.","He immediately ordered, \"Order the Three Judicial Offices to jointly try the case of the assassination attempt on County Princess Linghui. Until the case is thoroughly investigated, the involved princes are confined to their mansions and are forbidden to meddle in outside affairs. Violators will be killed without pardon.\"","Not long after, Eunuch Zhao walked outside the Hall of Preserving Harmony with the imperial decree and proclaimed it publicly.","Minister of Justice Sui Zhuangling and Chief Minister of the Court of Judicature and Revision Zhou Min, who were kneeling on the ground, immediately frowned. Even Ye Liangyu suddenly felt immense pressure.","One must know that Minister of Justice Sui Zhuangling was Prince Ying's man, and Chief Minister Zhou Min was Prince Qi's man.","Being stuck in the middle, no matter who he convicted, he would encounter obstruction from the other party. This case would be very difficult to handle.","When Song Jinzhao returned to the County Princess's Mansion, the news in the capital about Prince Qi and Prince Ying sending people to assassinate her had already spread like wildfire.","The news of the joint trial by the Three Judicial Offices further detonated all the restaurants and teahouses in the capital.","\"Why do you think two perfectly fine princes would send people to assassinate County Princess Linghui?\"","A man holding a wine cup at the next table leaned over, \"I heard that the pregnancies of so many consorts in the palace are related to County Princess Linghui. If more princes are born, there will be more people fighting for the throne, so Prince Qi and Prince Ying retaliated against County Princess Linghui.\"","A man wearing a hat rushed in from outside.","\"Latest news, a pregnant consort drowned in the palace. I heard it's also related to the assassination case of the County Princess.\"","The commoner who asked the question earlier was instantly shocked, \"So there's one less already?\"","The man holding the wine cup shook his head and sighed, \"The fight for the throne has always been cruel. Who knows how many of the fourteen will be left in the end.\"","Another person said, \"If you ask me, the most innocent one is still County Princess Linghui. Just treating illnesses properly could bring about fatal disaster. Fortunately, Commander Fan was there yesterday, otherwise County Princess Linghui's corpse would be cold by now.\"","As soon as the imperial decree was issued, Minister of Justice Sui Zhuangling and Chief Minister Zhou Min immediately sent people to the Jingzhao Prefecture to receive the prisoners and related evidence.","Staring at the three assassins locked in the cell, Zhou Min looked at Governor Jiang Dongsheng in surprise.","\"I didn't expect the Jingzhao Prefecture's interrogation methods to be even more formidable than the Ministry of Justice's. There isn't a single piece of good flesh on their bodies.\"","Jiang Dongsheng awkwardly put his hands behind his back.","\"This subordinate is truly ashamed. These death-sworn assassins have very tight lips. This subordinate interrogated them for four hours without prying their mouths open. In the end, it was County Princess Linghui who took action personally.\"","Sui Zhuangling frowned, pointing at the assassins' exposed, curled-up flesh.","\"Are you saying these injuries were caused by County Princess Linghui?\"","How could a teenage girl be so ruthless? It's too brutal!","After last night's interrogation, Jiang Dongsheng actually admired Song Jinzhao a little in his heart.","He had never seen such a woman. When she became ruthless, even men couldn't compare.","\"The County Princess applied torture right on the street. When he was brought back, he was already like this.\"","I'm too embarrassed to mention the more formidable things. Compared to these physical injuries, the psychological trauma is even harder to accept.","After handing over the assassins and their confessions, the two also took away the corpses of forty-three assassins.","After locking the prisoners in the Ministry of Justice's prison, Zhou Min spoke to Sui Zhuangling with righteous indignation, \"Minister Sui, these three people are both prisoners and witnesses. This case involves a wide range of matters. They must be strictly guarded and absolutely nothing can happen to them.\"","Sui Zhuangling patted his chest and guaranteed, \"Lord Zhou, rest assured. This official has already mobilized dozens of jailers to surround the Ministry of Justice like an iron barrel. Whether someone wants to go out or come in, they won't be able to escape even if they had wings.\"","The two sat in the main hall of the Ministry of Justice for almost an hour before Ye Liangyu arrived belatedly.","\"Lord Ye, the Emperor kept you behind alone. Did he specifically instruct you on something?\" Sui Zhuangling stared at him and asked.","Ye Liangyu sat down expressionlessly, in a terrible mood.","\"It has nothing to do with the County Princess's case. It's about matters in the southwest.\"","Seeing that Ye Liangyu was unwilling to say more, Sui Zhuangling and Zhou Min didn't continue to ask.","After discussing it, the three decided to interrogate the suspects again while simultaneously sending people to track down the whereabouts of Cen Yue and Zhao Zhihe.","At dusk, Ye Liangyu arrived at the County Princess's estate, exhausted. Song Jinzhao and Song Qiming had been waiting for a long time.","\"Teacher, have you found Cen Yue and Zhao Zhihe?\"","Ye Liangyu shook his head. \"We've searched the entire capital and plastered their portraits all over the streets and alleys, but there's still no news. I fear the worst.\"","Song Qiming paced back and forth anxiously. \"If we can't find them, the Prince of Qi and the Prince of Ying will definitely refuse to confess.\"","Seeing Song Jinzhao remain silent, Ye Liangyu hesitated for a long time before finally speaking up.","\"Actually, after the Emperor issued the edict for the Three Judicial Offices to hold a joint trial today, he kept me behind to say a few words in private.\"","Song Qiming turned to look at his teacher. \"What did he say?\"","Song Jinzhao raised her eyes.","Ye Liangyu took a deep breath, finding the words hard to say.","\"No matter how the investigation turns out, the royal dignity must not be compromised.\"","\"In truth, the Emperor already believes that the Prince of Qi and the Prince of Ying are the masterminds behind this, but the impact of this case must be limited to the court. The two princes can only be lightly punished for their heavy crimes.\"","Song Qiming's eyes widened, his lips trembling with anger.","\"What does that mean? The Emperor is going to shield his sons!\"","\"The laws of the court state: a prince who breaks the law is guilty of the same crime as a commoner. How can the Emperor knowingly violate this? Where does this leave the common people of the world!\"","Unlike Song Qiming's righteous indignation, Song Jinzhao's expression was much calmer.","\"I guessed this would be the outcome long ago. If it weren't for the drowning of Attendant Hai angering the Emperor, he might not have even let the Three Judicial Offices try this case.\"","\"No one's life is worth more than his sons' lives. Unless it's treason or patricide, even if the Prince of Qi and the Prince of Ying commit the greatest of crimes, the Emperor will not kill them.\"","Ye Liangyu's mouth moved for a long time, not knowing how to respond to Song Jinzhao's words.","Because it was the truth.","Song Qiming said unwillingly, \"Are we just supposed to let this go? If we don't make them pay the price, what if they send someone to assassinate you again, Sister?\""]},{"number":297,"title":"Chapter 297: A witness emerges, leading to the demotion from princely title to commandery prince.","paragraphs":["Ye Liangyu stood up and paced back and forth.","\"Not killing him doesn't mean he won't be severely punished. The Emperor is only protecting him now because there are only two princes in the court, and he has no other choice. As soon as another prince is born in the inner palace, this advantage will vanish. It will be much easier to strike then.\"","Inside the imperial palace, Xiao Chengjing, who had been sulking all day, was lying on the dragon throne, resting with his eyes closed.","Zhao Yande walked in carefully, carrying a late-night snack.","\"Your Majesty, you have hardly eaten anything all day. The imperial kitchen has prepared some longan and silver ear mushroom soup. Please have a little, or it will harm your stomach.\"","Xiao Chengjing sat up and opened his eyes, which were completely bloodshot.","\"Zhao Yande, do you think they assassinated Song Jinzhao because they were dissatisfied with the concubines in the palace getting pregnant?\"","Eunuch Zhao, who had served the Emperor for most of his life, did not dare to utter a word.","He slowly placed the longan and silver ear mushroom soup on the table, tightened his throat, and spoke in a low voice.","\"Perhaps County Princess Linghui somehow offended the two princes. Besides, the case hasn't been fully investigated yet.\"","Xiao Chengjing gave a stiff twitch of his lips.","\"Cen Yue and Zhao Zhihe are their men. There is no need to investigate this case; I am just deceiving myself.\"","A young eunuch walked in, bowing deeply. \"Your Majesty, Wang Duorui, the Head of the Internal Affairs Department, requests an audience.\"","It must be that the case of Attendant Hai falling into the water had a result. \"Let him in.\"","\"To reply to Your Majesty, the eunuchs and maids of Cuiming Pavilion have undergone severe torture and keep crying out their innocence.\"","\"However, this servant found out that Attendant Hai fell in because she stepped on some moss next to the lotus pond. This servant went to look personally. That piece of moss was deliberately placed there, and it should have been placed last night.\"","\"The maid Lanxin said there was no one near the lotus pond. This servant sent people to inquire and found out that Concubine Yi of Qiushui Palace had called everyone away. She said that when she went to pay respects at the Empress's palace early in the morning, she found the luan-phoenix jade pendant she carried with her was missing, which is why she had everyone go to the west side of the imperial garden to look for it.\"","Xiao Chengjing frowned. \"Is it the luan-phoenix jade pendant left to her by the Empress Dowager?\"","Wang Duorui nodded. \"That is the one.\"","Xiao Chengjing closed his eyes in frustration. How did she get dragged into this too?","\"Who in the palace has been to Cuiming Pavilion in the last few days?\"","Wang Duorui lowered his head and answered, \"Both the Empress and Noble Consort Jin sent people to deliver things to Cuiming Pavilion the day before yesterday. However, this morning, Noble Consort Jin sent a maid to deliver a bowl of blood bird's nest soup to Attendant Hai to nourish her body. It was only after this that Attendant Hai went to the imperial garden.\"","As expected, it was related to her.","\"Take the maid who delivered the items to the Department of Punishment and torture her severely. I want to know the truth.\"","Wang Duorui kowtowed. \"This servant obeys.\"","The confessions of the three assassins remained unchanged. Just as the Ministry of Justice and the Court of Judicature and Revision continued searching for the whereabouts of Cen Yue and Zhao Zhihe, news spread from the palace.","Noble Consort Jin was demoted to Concubine Jin for attempting to murder an imperial heir. She was confined to Yongshou Palace to reflect on her mistakes and was forbidden from leaving the palace gates without an imperial edict.","With Cen Yue and Zhao Zhihe still nowhere to be found, and the capital's citizens gradually losing interest in the assassination case, just as Ye Liangyu thought the Emperor was preparing to smooth things over and hastily close the case, an old retired soldier who had returned to his hometown years ago came to the Court of Judicature and Revision.","Holding a notice torn from the bulletin board, the old man spoke to the bailiff at the entrance of the Court of Judicature and Revision, \"Sir, I have seen the man on this poster.\"","He pointed to the last line on the wanted poster. \"It says here that a reward of fifty taels of silver will be given for providing clues. Is this true?\"","Seeing that he was pointing at the portrait of Zhao Zhihe, the bailiff's expression drastically changed.","\"Where did you see him?\"","The old man nodded vigorously.","\"Right in the bamboo forest on the mountain behind my house. Ten days ago, I saw two men burying a corpse there. If I hadn't come into town to buy things today, I wouldn't have known that the corpse they were burying was a wanted criminal.\"","Soon, Zhou Min, the Chief Minister of the Court of Judicature and Revision, led his men to Yunlong Mountain where the old man lived, and dug up Zhao Zhihe's corpse in the bamboo forest.","After examining the body, the coroner reported, \"Killed with a single strike. Based on the size of the maggots, he has been dead for about ten days.\"","In other words, he died the very day he went missing. Prince Ying was truly decisive and merciless in his actions.","Zhou Min turned around, went back to the hall, and asked the old man, \"Did you see the faces of the two men who buried the corpse?\"","\"I saw them.\" The old man nodded and reached out his hands to gesture.","\"They were wearing gray clothes. One of them stood tall and straight, looking like a trained martial artist. He was a head taller than me. When they were burying the body, I also saw a scar on the back of his hand.\"","\"The other man was about the same height as me. His eyes were so small that they disappeared when he squinted, and he had a mole on his face.\"","There were so many people in the capital; searching based on this criteria would be exceedingly difficult.","Zhou Min ordered his subordinate, \"Go to the Capital Mayor's Office immediately and find a clerk who knows how to draw portraits.\"","The subordinate widened his eyes in confusion. \"My Lord, shouldn't we go to the Ministry of Justice? The portrait artists there are definitely better than those at the Capital Mayor's Office.\"","Zhou Min kicked him in the leg. \"Just go when I tell you to. Why ask so many questions?\"","Looking at the drawn portraits, Zhou Min proudly straightened his back and flicked the paper, making a rustling sound.","\"It really took no effort at all.\"","Zhou Min had seen the men in the portraits before; they were the servants who frequently followed Prince Ying.","Sui Zhuangling and Ye Liangyu were completely baffled when they received the news. By the time they rushed to the imperial palace, Fan Guanshan had already taken men to Prince Ying's manor and arrested the two men in the portraits.","After leaving the imperial study, Sui Zhuangling glared gloomily and lashed out at Zhou Min.","\"Lord Zhou, the Emperor ordered a joint trial by the three judicial offices. When there was a clue in the case, why didn't you inform Lord Ye and me first, but instead came to see the Emperor alone? This is no way to hog the credit.\"","Seeing him extremely furious, Zhou Min felt even happier inside.","\"I was just afraid that the news would leak out and the murderers would escape again. As long as the case can be solved, what difference does it make who reports it?\"","If I had told you in advance, and you passed the news to Prince Ying, these two murderers would probably have ended up with the same fate as Zhao Zhihe.","\"What do you mean? Are you suggesting that Lord Ye and I would cover up for the murderers?\" Sui Zhuangling, like a cat whose tail had been stepped on, pointed a finger at Zhou Min in a towering rage.","Zhou Min straightened his sleeves. \"I meant no such thing. Lord Wu, please do not let your imagination run wild.\"","Seeing the two of them arguing fiercely, Ye Liangyu silently stepped aside to watch the show.","This sudden witness would increase the Emperor's punishment for Prince Ying.","With Noble Consort Jin demoted to a concubine, Prince Ying must be feeling quite proud of himself. This explosive news came at just the right time.","Inside Prince Ying's manor, Xiao Rongyan watched helplessly as his personal servant and guard were taken away by the Imperial Guards, feeling both furious and anxious.","These two had served him since childhood, which was why he had entrusted them with something as important as silencing a witness.","In the desolate wilderness, with so many days having passed, how could the corpse have been dug up?","When the two men were brought to the Ministry of Justice, Zhou Min brought the old man who had reported the case over to identify them.","\"My Lord, it's them. I saw them burying the corpse with my own eyes.\"","The servant and the guard, brought to the hall with their hands tied, looked at the old man in disbelief.","Impossible. There was absolutely no one around when they buried the corpse. Where did he come from?","But they could not say that; they could only stubbornly deny it to the death.","\"We are wronged, My Lord! We did not bury any corpse; he is framing us.\"","Zhou Min threw the portrait to the ground. \"Stop quibbling. How could an old man living in the mountains recognize the people from the prince's estate if he hadn't seen them with his own eyes?\"","\"Men, take them to the dungeon and interrogate them under torture. Make sure you get the truth out of them.\"","Everyone present was a trusted aide of Prince Ying. At this point, Sui Zhuangling could only sit on the sidelines, anxious but helpless.","In the afternoon, on a mountain road five miles outside the city, the old man parked his newly bought ox cart by the roadside and slipped into the nearby woods alone.","\"Young General, the matter you arranged has been handled. Those two have been locked up in the Ministry of Justice.\"","In the shade sheltered by leaves, Chu Liuyun, dressed in plain white clothes, slowly turned around and handed him a bundle.","\"Leave the capital immediately and never return. From now on, you can only live incognito.\"","The old man took the bundle and nodded.","\"Rest assured, Young General. At my age, I don't have many years left to live anyway. If the old Marquis hadn't dug me out of a pile of corpses back then, I would have died long ago.\"","\"If I am ever discovered one day, I will absolutely not let myself be taken alive.\"","Watching the gradually fading silhouette of the ox cart, Chu Liuyun turned to gaze in the direction of the capital, remaining silent for a long time.","Inside the County Princess's estate, Song Jinzhao sat in a chair in the study, deep in thought.","The yellow paper on the desk was densely covered with writing, all of it a single person's name—Xiao Chengjing.","Some of the names were also crossed out with black ink, one after another.","\"Sister, Teacher just sent someone with a message. Those two have confessed, and the memorial will be submitted tomorrow.\"","Song Jinzhao folded the yellow paper in half and tossed it aside.","\"So what if it's submitted? It will just be a slightly heavier punishment to gag the court officials. All thunder and no rain; it won't hurt their core.\"","Song Qiming sat down in a chair, feeling a bit dejected.","\"Sister, I have read all the words of the sages from ancient times to the present, and I know the court's laws backward and forward.\"","\"When I first took the imperial examinations, I only wanted to make life better for our family, to let you and Shixue live a life without worrying about food and clothing, with servants to wait on you.\"","Song Jinzhao propped her chin on one hand and asked calmly, \"And now?\"","Song Qiming gritted his teeth and said, \"As an official, one should not fail the heavy trust of the sovereign and the country above, nor fail the hopeful gaze of the common people below.\"","\"If the sovereign I am loyal to and assist is not a wise ruler, and ordinary people are not important in his heart, is he still fit to be a king?\"","\"Whenever I think of this, I can't muster any energy when handling official duties. I feel like everything I do is meaningless.\"","Song Jinzhao couldn't help but smile at his disappointed and disheartened appearance.","His idol's image had shattered.","Once ancient people broke their rose-tinted glasses regarding emperors, the emperor became no different from an ordinary person.","She asked in return, \"Why do you think the civil and military officials are loyal to the Emperor?\"","Song Qiming was silent for a long time before speaking, \"Because the Emperor is the Son of Heaven, and we are subjects of the Dongzhao Kingdom. Being loyal to the sovereign and loving the country is naturally the right thing to do.\"","Song Jinzhao: \"The place we are standing right now used to be the territory of the Chili Kingdom, and going back several generations, our ancestors were also subjects of the Chili Kingdom. You say being loyal to the sovereign and loving the country is the right thing to do, so does that mean our ancestors committed treason?\"","Song Qiming was stunned, momentarily not knowing how to refute.","Song Jinzhao narrowed her eyes and stood up. \"The civil and military officials are loyal to the Emperor because the knowledge they learned from books tells them to be loyal and patriotic. But more importantly, the monarch holds the power of life and death. If they are not loyal to him, they will die. No one is unafraid of death, so they have no choice but to obey.\"","\"Over thousands of years, dynastic changes have occurred countless times. When a country is weak, it falls.\"","\"The sovereign is a boat; the common people are the water. The water can carry the boat, but it can also capsize it.\"","\"A monarch is merely the manager of this country. If he doesn't manage it well, someone else will replace him.\"","Song Jinzhao tapped her finger on the center of Song Qiming's forehead. \"And you are just someone working for the Emperor. If you can't manage to replace this Emperor, then just quietly do your job well and have a clear conscience.\"","That night, Song Qiming stayed awake all night.","He tossed and turned in bed, his mind full of what Song Jinzhao had said, unable to forget it even if he wanted to.","The next day, he went to work at the Hanlin Academy in a daze, only to be jolted awake by an imperial decree.","At Prince Qi's estate, Xiao Rongche knelt on the ground to receive the decree.","\"Prince Qi, Xiao Rongche, has been lax in managing his subordinates and failed in his supervisory duties, allowing scoundrels to usurp authority and assassinate the County Princess. Although he defends himself claiming ignorance, lax management is a dereliction of duty, and an unclean household is the root of disaster. Today, he is stripped of his title as a Prince of the First Rank and demoted to Prince Qi'an of the Second Rank. He is fined one year's salary as compensation to County Princess Linghui, ordered to reflect on his mistakes behind closed doors for a month, and must copy a chapter of the Penal Code daily for self-reflection.\"","Inside Prince Ying's estate, Xiao Rongyan also received an imperial decree demoting him to Prince Yingcheng of the Second Rank.","When Ye Liangyu heard the news, she was so shocked that she knocked over the tea on the table.","Being stripped of a princedom and demoted to a Prince of the Second Rank was already considered a very severe punishment.","He originally thought it would end with at most three or four months of confinement, but he didn't expect it to exceed his expectations.","The civil and military officials in the court discussed this endlessly, especially the officials who had aligned themselves with Prince Qi and Prince Ying. Their hearts immediately began to waver.","It must be known that being demoted to a Prince of the Second Rank basically eliminated one's qualifications to compete for the throne, yet these were the only two princes in the court.","Could it be that the Emperor favored an unborn child in the imperial harem?","In the ancestral hall of the Duke of Zhenguo's estate, the Duke of Zhenguo, who was still observing a period of mourning, placed a lit stick of incense into the censer.","\"Withdraw the people guarding around Prince Ying's estate.\"","The Duke of Qing, Chu Liuyun, held incense and bowed three times to the ancestral tablets. \"Rest assured, Father. Your son already withdrew our people yesterday.\"","The next day, Song Jinzhao looked at the four chests of silver sent over from the Prince of the Second Rank's estate, totaling twenty thousand taels.","Song Shixue opened the chests in confusion. Ingots of silver were neatly arranged on the racks inside.","\"Why didn't they give us banknotes? Transporting so much by carriage is so inconvenient.\"","Song Jinzhao waved her hand, instructing the servants to move the chests to the storehouse.","\"If they sent banknotes, others wouldn't see them. They are eager to let everyone in the capital know that they have compensated me with money.\"","Song Shixue bit her lip and complained in frustration, \"If the Emperor weren't shielding them, we wouldn't even want the money.\"","She flattened her hand like a blade and chopped down heavily, lowering her voice. \"We have to kill them to vent our anger.\"","A month later, Xiao Rongche and Xiao Rongyan were summoned to the palace as soon as their confinement ended.","\"Having been confined for a month, I trust you both know your mistakes.\"","Xiao Rongche and Xiao Rongyan knelt and kowtowed simultaneously.","\"Making Imperial Father worry is our fault. We are immensely remorseful.\"","Xiao Chengjing nodded in satisfaction.","\"It is a great virtue to correct one's mistakes. As princes, you should be role models for the subjects of the realm. Do not repeat this in the future.\"","The two cupped their hands. \"Thank you, Imperial Father.\"","Eunuch Zhao handed two imperial decrees to Xiao Rongche and Xiao Rongyan respectively."]},{"number":298,"title":"Chapter 298: Xiao Chengjing Sends People Away from the Capital, Chunxing Arrives at Song Family Village","paragraphs":["\"The canal has been open for several years now. I have always wanted to travel south for an inspection but have not had the time. Rong Che, you shall go and inspect it on my behalf.\"","\"Although we are not at war right now, the grain reserves across the regions remain of utmost importance. There is still a month until the summer harvest. Rong Yan, you shall inspect the Dongshan and Xiating provinces on my behalf.\"","\"There must be no mistakes this time. Return with achievements, and I will reward you accordingly.\"","\"We thank Imperial Father for your profound grace!\" Two distinctly different voices rang out in unison.","As they bowed their heads, their eyes met. It was like two undercurrents colliding beneath a calm surface of water, neither willing to yield a single inch.","Three days later, two convoys passed through Zhuque Street. After exiting the city gates, they departed the capital in grand processions, one heading south and the other east.","On the second floor of the hotpot restaurant, Song Jinzhao watched the two depart before turning back into the room.","Xiao Chengjing had thus sent his two sons out of the capital. By the time they returned, the child in the palace would already be born.","As the pregnancies of the imperial concubines in the harem gradually stabilized, Song Jinzhao reduced the time she spent in the palace each day. She basically left as soon as she finished taking their pulses and confirmed everything was fine.","She chose to spend more of her time on making money.","In a small, custom-built factory at Shiquan Manor outside the city, a massive, two-meter-tall copper vat was so large it took four people to encircle it.","A gas pipe made of thin copper connected the vat to a condenser pipe submerged in ice water. Beneath the condenser pipe sat a bucket to catch the distilled mixture of water and oil.","Wearing a hat and a face mask, Lan Xi kept a close watch, not taking a single step away to ensure that every procedure was carried out exactly according to Song Jinzhao's requirements.","Thousands of miles away in Songjiacun.","Old Mrs. Song brought the prepared food to the table and said to Old Man Song, who had just returned from the fields, \"The county magistrate said traveling on the official roads is fast, but it's been over ten days now. Why aren't Jinzhao and the others back yet?\"","Old Man Song put down his hoe and used well water to wash the mud off his feet.","In truth, the elderly couple was not short of money now and didn't need to work in the fields, but they simply couldn't sit idle.","Moreover, it was the busy farming season, so they inevitably went to help the first and second branch families.","\"I heard from the village chief that Song Gaoli has to take another exam if he wants to become an official. If they are coming back together, they will definitely wait for Gaoli. I reckon it will be another ten days or so.\"","Old Mrs. Song picked up a piece of meat and placed it in Old Man Song's bowl, chatting about family matters with a face full of smiles.","\"Everyone in the village is waiting for a celebratory banquet, hoping to rub off some of Qiming's scholarly luck. Even Lahuang‘s Wife next door has asked me three times.\"","Old Man Song said as he ate, \"I wonder how Sallow Song's youngest son is doing with his studies at the private school in town?\"","\"Thinking about Yaozu just makes me want to sigh. They all went to Scholar Zheng's private school together. Yongnian managed to pass the prefectural exam, but he couldn't even pass the county exam. The second son was just complaining to me again earlier, saying that Yaozu was kept after class by Scholar Zheng again yesterday. He really has no ambition.\"","Old Mrs. Song's lips moved.","He has no ambition, yet you still paid for his schooling, she thought, but feeling it was pointless to say, she swallowed her words.","Fortunately, they weren't lacking those few taels of silver now. They just considered it spending money to buy some peace and quiet; otherwise, the second branch would definitely come to bother them every day.","In the past, they always dreamed of having three generations living together, believing that a family should all live under one roof.","Now that she and her old man had moved out and lived with the third branch for so long, they didn't have to worry about a whole large family's affairs. Their days were much more comfortable than before.","Now, even when the eldest son invited them back to live in the old house, they didn't want to go back.","Another ten days passed, and Chunxing brought people driving a horse carriage to Songjiacun.","As the carriage drove into the village, the villagers thought Song Jinzhao and the others had returned, and they all ran out to look.","After realizing it wasn't them and asking around, they found out it was just more servants of the Song family's third branch from Anyang Prefecture.","\"Why is it a different one again? The one who came last time was a man. Song Jinzhao really has a lot of servants.\"","Following the route map Fushun had drawn during his last visit, the carriage stopped flawlessly in front of the blue-brick house.","Hearing the noise, Old Man Song and Old Mrs. Song had already walked into the courtyard.","Seeing unfamiliar faces, a bad feeling arose in their hearts.","\"This servant, Chunxing, pays her respects to the Old Master and Old Madam.\"","\"This servant, Hu Sanluo, pays his respects to the Old Master and Old Madam.\"","\"This servant, Zhou Yagu, pays her respects to the Old Master and Old Madam.\"","Compared to when Fushun came last time, Old Man Song and Old Mrs. Song were much calmer this time.","Oldest Song ran over, pointed at Chunxing, and introduced her to Old Man Song, \"Dad, when Yongnian and I went to Anyang Prefecture, Chunxing was the one who hosted us.\"","Old Man Song's voice carried a hint of disappointment.","\"Why didn't Jinzhao and the others come back? Are they going to be a couple of days late?\"","Chunxing glanced at the numerous villagers gathered around and coaxed the two elders into the house before she began to explain.","\"After the Eldest Young Master placed third in the imperial examination, the imperial court only granted him half a month of leave.\"","\"Originally, the County Princess was going to bring the Second Miss and the Young Master back. But then a consort in the palace became pregnant, and knowing the County Princess has excellent medical skills, the Emperor asked her to look after her, so they couldn't come back.\"","Getting his answer, Old Man Song sat down in his chair in disappointment. Even with a room full of things, he felt out of sorts.","Having not seen them for two years, he truly missed them a bit.","\"Then did Jinzhao say when she might be able to come back?\"","Chunxing replied, \"The County Princess had a letter sent back from the capital, telling this servant to ask the Old Master and Old Madam if you would be willing to go and stay in the capital for a period of time?\"","The members of the first and second branches in the room were stunned. Jinzhao wanted to bring their parents to live in the capital?","Behind Oldest Song, Second Song's arm was nearly pinched purple by Second Aunt Song.","If the two elders were going to the capital, they absolutely had to go too.","Second Song managed to pull his arm back with difficulty. \"Let's see what Mom and Dad say first.\"","Second Aunt Song held her breath with full expectation.","The opportunity to turn their lives around and enjoy fortune was right in front of them, and their second branch absolutely had to seize it!","Hearing about going to the capital, Old Man Song's head buzzed.","Sitting beside him, Old Mrs. Song asked uncertainly, \"You just said to go stay in the capital for a period of time. Then when would we come back?\"","Chunxing replied, \"Probably not until early next year. The County Princess said that once the palace consort gives birth, the Emperor might give the Eldest Young Master a few months of leave, and then you can all come back together.\"","Old Man Song and Old Mrs. Song were a bit hesitant about whether to go.","Seeing that the two elders were delaying their answer, the impatient Second Song immediately walked over to Old Man Song's chair and urged him.","\"Dad, since Jinzhao sent someone to pick us up, we definitely have to go. The capital is where the Emperor lives; it must be incredibly bustling and fun.\"","Old Man Song frowned, turned his head to look at Second Song, and said, \"She is picking me and your mother up to go there.\"","\"Yaozu is still studying at the private school, and there is still rice in the fields. What would you all go to the capital for?\"","The corners of Second Song's mouth stiffened.","Second Aunt Song hurriedly interjected with an awkward smile, \"Dad, Yaozu could go study in the capital, and we can just have someone else look after the rice in the fields.\"","\"The capital is so far away, and you and Mom are getting older; you'll need someone to take care of you on the journey. Plus, our three branches could celebrate a reunion for the New Year in the capital.\"","From the corner of her eye, Chunxing glanced at the second branch couple.","It was exactly as Fushun had described.","\"There are servants to take care of them on the journey. The County Princess specifically instructed that since the Old Master and Old Madam are elderly, we should travel slowly and not rush.\"","The County Princess hadn't said anything about bringing the first and second branches to the capital, so she absolutely could not agree to this.","The smile faded from Second Aunt Song's face, and she shot Chunxing an expressionless glare.","What is a mere servant interrupting for? What a cheap mouth.","Old Man Song took in the Second Branch's impatience. The First Branch remained silent, but they surely wanted to go too.","\"It's getting late, so all of you should head back. Your mother and I haven't decided whether to go yet. We'll talk about it tomorrow.\"","The couple from the Second Branch left the room reluctantly, looking back with every three steps they took.","After everyone had left and the courtyard gate was closed, Old Man Song asked Chunxing.","\"Did Jinzhao not mention bringing the First and Second Branches along to the capital?\"","Chunxing nodded. \"The County Princess only mentioned you and the Old Madam.\"","\"The County Princess also said that if you and the Old Madam feel the capital is too far and don't wish to leave Songjiacun, I am to arrange for two servants to stay and attend to you here in your hometown.\"","Old Man Song looked up and down at Hu Sanluo and Zhou Yagu standing behind Chunxing. No wonder she had brought two extra people this time; so that was why.","\"You all stay here for the night. The capital is so far away, the old woman and I need to think it over some more.\"","Chunxing nodded respectfully. \"Understood, Old Master.\"","\"I would also like to ask where the village chief's house is? Young Master Gaoli has entrusted me with a letter and some items to deliver.\"","Old Man Song's eyes widened in surprise. \"Song Gaoli isn't coming back either?\"","Chunxing nodded. \"That's right. Young Master Gaoli has to take up his post at the Ministry of War, so he cannot return either.\"","Old Man Song pushed himself up from his chair, muttering to himself, \"So that's how it is. It seems everyone is very busy.\"","\"Come, I'll take you there.\"","Just as they stepped out the door, a knock sounded at the courtyard gate. Song Mancang and Song Dazhuang were pounding on the door.","When the door was opened, the two men's eyes lit up as they looked around.","\"Old Man Song, is there any news of our Gaoli? When is he coming back?\"","Old Man Song took the letter from Chunxing's hand and slapped it into Song Mancang's.","\"They are all very busy. None of them are coming back.\"","He pointed to the box Hu Sanluo was holding. \"And these, they are all for your family.\"","Song Mancang quickly tore open the letter. After reading it, he looked disappointed at first, but then he smiled.","\"I didn't expect Gaoli to actually be able to stay in the capital.\"","He slapped his thigh happily.","\"Being an official in the imperial city is the most promising path. I knew my grandson was capable.\"","That night in the elderly couple's room, Old Man Song leaned against the wall, his mind troubled.","Seeing that he was hesitating to make a decision and constantly sighing, Old Madam Song couldn't help but speak up.","\"You've been thinking for so long. Are we going to the capital or not?\"","Old Man Song sighed heavily and said, \"If Jinzhao only takes us to the capital and leaves the First and Second Branches behind, the villagers will definitely gossip. Erlang and his wife, especially, will complain endlessly. By then, rumors will spread everywhere, and it will affect Qiming's official career.\"","\"I'm not worried about the First Branch; I'm worried about the Second Branch.\"","\"The village chief said that the biggest taboo for an official is having family members who abuse their power to bully others. If I don't stay in the village, what if my second son relies on having a nephew who is a high official and a niece who is a County Princess to stir up trouble everywhere?\"","\"If he brings a fatal disaster upon himself, heads will roll. I just can't be at ease.\"","Hearing him say this, Old Madam Song also felt a bit uneasy.","With her second son's temperament, if no one kept him in check, he might actually do such a thing.","\"Then let's not go. The capital is so far away, it takes over two months on the road. Our old bones would be shaken to pieces.\"","\"Once we arrive in the capital, we won't know anyone. The children are all very busy, and it would be boring to just stay in the house all the time.\"","Old Man Song hesitated, torn. \"Jinzhao has already sent people to pick us up. Wouldn't it be bad if we don't go?\"","Old Madam Song replied, \"You're overthinking it. Jinzhao does things thoroughly; she has already considered whether we go or not.\"","\"Didn't you see she even arranged servants? Two people to wait on us, they can even pour our foot-washing water.\"","Old Man Song lay down, tossing and turning, unable to sleep.","After a long while, he suddenly spoke.","It was as if he was talking to himself, yet also asking Old Madam Song.","\"Do you think Jinzhao and the others will be able to come back early next year?\"","\"...\" The only response was silence. Old Madam Song had already fallen asleep.","In the early morning, the large rooster in the coop, with its blood-red comb, tilted its head back and crowed loudly. A shocked roar from Song Erlang echoed from the main room.","Zhou Yagu, who was making breakfast, poked her head out of the kitchen. \"What's wrong?\"","Hu Sanluo shook his head. \"It seems the Old Master and Old Madam don't want to go to the capital. We might have to stay here.\"","Zhou Yagu just let out an \"oh\" and nonchalantly returned to the stove to continue cooking.","Before they came, they had already prepared themselves for the possibility of staying forever.","Ever since receiving Song Jinzhao's letter, Chunxing had prepared for two scenarios.","Hu Sanluo and Zhou Yagu were people she had carefully selected.","After all, staying in the village to serve year after year could be said to have no prospects.","Young people with ambition wouldn't be able to stay, and older people couldn't be too old.","They also had to be literate, able to drive a carriage, quick-witted, and willing. It took her two days of picking to finalize the candidates.","\"How can you not go! Jinzhao has already sent people to pick you up. If you don't go, she will definitely be angry.\"","Song Erlang couldn't understand it. How could someone not know how to enjoy good fortune?","Refusing to go to the imperial city—what was so good about staying in the village?","Second Aunt Song was also jumping with anxiety beside him.","\"That's right! It's only proper for grandchildren to be filial to their grandparents. If they are enjoying good fortune in the capital, they should bring us all over together so it's easier to show their filial piety.\"","Old Man Song watched them expressionlessly, feeling more and more that the decision not to go was the right one.","These two from the Second Branch really couldn't be left without someone to keep them in check. He had to stay in the village to keep an eye on them.","Old Man Song said, \"The capital is so far away. At our age, your mother and I cannot endure the hardship of a long journey.\"","\"Every time Jinzhao sends people back, she brings so many things. She is filial enough. Your mother and I won't go to the capital and cause her trouble.\"","Old Madam Song drawled, \"You and your older brother are both in the village. The two of us should give you the chance to show your filial piety as well.\"","The couple was left speechless by Old Man Song and Old Madam Song's words.","The First Branch family was still having breakfast in the old house when Song Erlang rushed in with Second Aunt Song and tried to drag him away.","\"Brother, Father and Mother don't want to go to the capital. Hurry and come with me to persuade them.\"","Oldest Song, who had been dragged to the doorway, grabbed the edge of the door with his hand. \"I have to take Yongnian to the private school right away. We're running out of time.\"","Song Erlang pulled him forcefully and stubbornly.","\"Missing a day won't matter. Going to the capital is the important matter right now.\"","First Aunt Song, who was getting breakfast for her son, said, \"Second Brother, the people Jinzhao sent made it clear they are only taking Father and Mother. You shouldn't waste your energy.\"","\"Why hasn't your Yaozu come yet? We're about to leave.\"","\"Eldest Aunt, I'm here.\" Song Yaozu walked through the door carrying his book box on his back.","Second Aunt Song, finally remembering her son, went up to ask him.","\"Have you eaten breakfast? If not, just make do with a few bites here at your uncle's house.\"","Song Yaozu nodded. \"Eldest Sister made porridge, so I've already eaten.\""]},{"number":299,"title":"Chapter 299: The Disappointed Second Wife, Leaving Behind Hu Sanluo and Zhou Yagu","paragraphs":["Song Yongnian walked out of the room carrying his book box.","Seeing that both children were ready, Oldest Song pulled his hand away from Second Song's grasp. \"Whatever it is, wait until I drop off the kids.\"","Now that Song Yongnian had passed the tong sheng exam, and with Song Qiming's shining example right there, the eldest branch had put all their minds into supporting their son's studies.","Yesterday, when they heard that Song Jinzhao was going to take the two elders to the capital, it wasn't that they hadn't entertained the idea themselves.","But after returning home at night and discussing it, they felt it wouldn't work.","Not to mention that Song Jinzhao hadn't planned to take them in the first place, even if they went, they would have to come back early next year.","The round trip would take four or five months, and without guidance, their son's study time would be wasted.","The capital was so far away, and if they went and upset the third branch, they wouldn't have anywhere to go and would offend people.","Seeing Oldest Song drive the ox cart away with the two children, Second Aunt Song thought about it and walked up to Elder Aunt Song to fan the flames.","\"Sister-in-law, the third branch is enjoying life in the capital now, don't you want to go and see?\"","\"If Mom and Dad go to the capital this time and don't come back, it'll be hard for us to contact the third branch in the future.\"","Elder Aunt Song cleared the bowls and chopsticks from the table.","\"When Sanlang and his wife passed away, we discussed having Shixue marry Shitou to ward off bad luck, and adopting Anhao out to Master Zhao. Jinzhao and Qiming both know about these things, and they hold a grudge.\"","\"Jinzhao might not care about small things, but she's bothered by the big things. She won't take us to the capital, and Dad wouldn't agree either.\"","Second Aunt Song waved her hands excitedly to defend herself.","\"In the end, neither the marriage nor the adoption happened. We had no choice back then, the family was too poor to support them. If Jinzhao had said earlier that she could hunt and make money, we wouldn't have brought it up.\"","Elder Aunt Song took the bowls and chopsticks to the kitchen and came out to continue: \"I say it's good that Mom and Dad aren't going to the capital. With the two elders staying in the village, our connection with the third branch won't be severed. Besides, Sanlang and his wife's graves are still at the foot of the back mountain, they can't stay away forever.\"","\"The third branch is living a wealthy life now. If we really go to the capital and upset them, it'll be hard to ask them for help in the future. I think you should stop thinking about going to the capital.\"","When Yongnian passed the xiucai exam, he would definitely have to go to Anyang Prefecture to study. The third branch had a house in Anyang Prefecture, and they would have to ask to borrow it.","Right now, Elder Aunt Song didn't want to upset Song Jinzhao at all. If she did, she'd end up with nothing, and the loss would outweigh the gain.","Seeing that Elder Aunt Song remained unmoved and even advised her not to go to the capital, Second Aunt Song turned and walked away in anger, muttering curses.","When Oldest Song returned from Xining City after dropping off the children, the couple went to the new house together.","\"Dad, Second Brother said you and Mom aren't planning to go to the capital?\"","Old Man Song nodded, his eyes fixed on Oldest Song's face, observing his attitude.","\"Yes, the capital is too far. Your mother and I are getting old and afraid our bodies won't be able to handle it, so we're not going.\"","Oldest Song shook his head.","\"It's good not to go. It's hot on the way to the capital now, and it'll be cold in the winter when you come back. It's better to stay at home.\"","Hearing him say this, Old Man Song's eyelids relaxed a lot.","The second branch couple sitting on the stools felt tired and helpless seeing that Oldest Song really didn't object.","Mom and Dad weren't going, and the eldest branch wasn't going either. Now there was absolutely no way.","How could people be so stupid, not knowing how to enjoy the blessings delivered to their door? It was maddening.","After everyone left, Chunxing stood in the middle of the main room to introduce the two elders.","\"This is Hu Sanluo. He can read and write some simple characters. In the future, if the Old Master and Old Madam want to write a letter to the County Princess, just hand it to him.\"","\"This is Zhou Yagu. He's a good cook, and you can leave the kitchen matters to him.\"","\"They are both servants who have signed indentured servitude contracts. The County Princess will be responsible for their monthly allowance from now on. You two just need to order them around.\"","Old Man Song nodded. \"They look like honest people. You've gone to a lot of trouble.\"","After explaining everything, Chunxing pulled Hu Sanluo and Zhou Yagu to the small path outside the enclosing wall.","\"In the future, if the Old Master and Old Madam have any issues, write a letter and send it to the capital promptly. Especially keep an eye on the eldest and second branches, don't let anything happen.\"","Zhou Yagu nodded: \"Don't worry, Sister Chun, we'll pay attention.\"","Chunxing: \"The residence in Anyang Prefecture will be handed over to Manager Lu later. If you need anything in the future, write to him promptly, and he'll send someone over.\"","Hu Sanluo, Zhou Yagu: \"We've memorized it.\"","Chunxing left, and the Song family's third branch house gained two servants to wait on people.","The villagers who came to chat saw Old Man Song and Old Lady Song staying at home doing nothing, with people serving them tea and water, and their hearts were filled with envy.","Some also asked Old Man Song why they didn't go to the capital, and they were all dismissed with a single sentence: 'The journey is far, too lazy to travel.'","The villagers discussed this after meals for several days.","Some said Old Man Song and Old Lady Song didn't know how to enjoy their blessings.","Others said it was because of Oldest Song and Second Song that Old Man Song didn't want to go to the capital; after all, grandchildren couldn't compare to sons.","The day Chunxing left Songjia Village, she wrote a letter to Song Jinzhao in Xining City to inform her of the situation, but it would take at least two months to arrive.","After Xiao Rongche and Xiao Rongyan left the capital, the court completely quieted down.","Seeing that there would be a new prince born in the palace, and the Emperor was in good health, the throne might not necessarily fall to the First Prince and Second Prince.","The ministers who had previously taken sides also began to waver, thinking of waiting and watching a bit longer.","In the study of the County Princess's Residence, Lan Xi, who had just returned from Shiquan Estate, handed a bottle of pale yellow rose essential oil to Song Jinzhao.","\"County Princess, this is the sample produced by the factory today. It has been extracted once with high-concentration alcohol as you instructed.\"","Song Jinzhao pulled out the wooden stopper and poured a little into her palm.","Compared to the first batch, the fragrance finally had layers.","It wasn't as strong and heavy as the first time, which lacked the agility of natural floral scents.","Song Jinzhao stood up and walked around the courtyard for a while.","The fragrance faded, and the middle and base notes appeared more natural, not too conspicuous, but very obvious when close, allowing those who wanted to smell it to do so.","\"This standard is acceptable. Follow this from now on, and immediately speed up the progress for the corresponding perfume.\"","Hearing Song Jinzhao say there was no problem, Lan Xi's tense nerves finally dared to relax.","Ever since the County Princess asked him to make perfume and essential oils, his mind hadn't relaxed, afraid he wouldn't be able to finish.","At first, Song Jinzhao taught him theoretical knowledge in the residence, and later they experimented with small distillation tools.","During that time, Lan Xi's brain almost exploded, and he didn't even dare to relax when sleeping at night.","Now it was finally completed.","\"Yes, this servant will arrange for people to start making it as soon as I return.\"","Exiting through the main gate, Song Shixue happened to be getting off the carriage with a medicine chest.","\"This servant greets the Second Miss.\"","Song Shixue stopped in her tracks and looked him up and down in surprise.","\"We haven't seen each other for just a month, how did you lose so much weight, Lan Xi?\"","His cheeks had no flesh, and even his light blue eyes had dimmed a lot, not as pretty as Xuetuan's eyes."]},{"number":300,"title":"Chapter 300: Another Winter Arrives, Xiao Rongyan Returns to the Capital","paragraphs":["Lan Xi pursed his lips and lowered his eyes, his hands resting by his thighs clenching slightly in discomfort.","\"I haven't lost weight, I've just grown a bit taller.\"","Song Shixue reached out to measure his height with her hand; it seemed he had indeed grown a bit taller.","\"The tasks my elder sister assigned to you are important, but you must also take care of your health.\"","\"Don't ruin your health at such a young age. At the house I visited for a medical consultation today, their five-year-old child studies until late every night and has become malnourished.\"","Lan Xi raised his eyes to look at her. \"I understand. Thank you for your care, Second Miss.\"","Gazing at Song Shixue's retreating back, Lan Xi stood rooted to the spot, his heart feeling terribly empty.","It wasn't until she disappeared around the corner that he took a deep breath, let it out slowly, turned around, and rode his horse out of the city.","He was now a servant; there were some things he shouldn't dare to wish for, nor did he deserve them.","In a secluded, humble courtyard in the capital, ten children were practicing martial arts in a room, and the number was increasing every day.","These children, aged ten to fourteen, were all orphans that Qingshuang had bought from various human traffickers according to Song Jinzhao's requests.","Their daily task was to train according to the methods written by Song Jinzhao.","They were to become special forces soldiers equipped with combat prowess, disguise and infiltration skills, and intelligence-gathering abilities in the shortest possible time.","With so much to do every day, time passed by like flowing water.","In the blink of an eye, the pregnant concubines in the palace were already eight months along.","When the first snow of winter fell, Song Anhao, wearing a thick fur coat, hurried out of the side door of the Dongfang family's residence carrying his book box.","\"A'Ying, let's hurry back to the estate. Big Brother has the day off today, and he promised to take me hunting outside the city this afternoon.\"","Twelve-year-old Yao Ying was the guard Song Jinzhao had assigned to her youngest brother; he followed him whenever he left the estate.","Upon returning to the estate, Xuetuan, who was playing in the snow, rushed over and pounced on Song Anhao, knocking him down.","The massive tiger head continuously rubbed against his face.","\"Xuetuan, stop touching me. Your head is covered in snow, it's so cold.\"","Song Anhao pushed the tiger away while scrambling up from the ground. As soon as he entered the house, he smelled the aroma of chicken soup.","Seeing the table full of dishes, he excitedly climbed onto a stool to see if there was anything he liked.","\"Why aren't there any fish balls? I want to eat them.\"","Song Shixue walked over, untied his cloak, and hung it on a rack.","\"Business at the shop was so good that the fish balls sold out. A fresh batch will be delivered shortly.\"","Sitting on the heated brick bed, Song Qiming looked up at him. \"I heard from Yukun that the results of the academy's quiz are coming out today. How did you do?\"","Song Anhao opened his book box, took out two test papers, and ran over to show them to Song Qiming.","\"They are both A grades! I'm also ranked first in arithmetic at the academy. Grandpa Dongfang even praised me.\"","Ever since Dongfang Yuanbin retired from his position as the Director of the Secretariat, he had started a small academy in his home.","Originally, it only taught the children of the Dongfang clan. When Song Qiming found out, he pleaded with Dongfang Yukun and managed to squeeze Song Anhao in.","Therefore, he now went to the Dongfang residence every morning for school.","Song Qiming bent down, picked Song Anhao up, and set him on the heated bed. He took the papers and read them from beginning to end.","Seeing that not a single arithmetic question was wrong, he couldn't resist pinching his younger brother's little cheek.","\"I heard from Yukun that you can solve the problems the academy gives to the ten-year-olds. This cleverness surely takes after me.\"","Song Anhao struggled, turning his head to save his cheek from Song Qiming's grasp.","\"Narcissist! Eldest Sister taught me arithmetic; I didn't take after you at all.\"","Not knowing whether to laugh or cry, Song Qiming forcefully pulled the boy into his arms and rubbed his head.","\"Where did a little kid like you learn such a word? Tell me, what does 'narcissist' mean?\"","Song Anhao lifted his chin. \"Being a narcissist means overly focusing on and admiring oneself.\"","\"Just like Brother Yukun. Not only is he a narcissist, but he's also vain.\"","Song Jinzhao couldn't help but smile, her eyes curving in amusement.","Song Shixue burst out laughing and reached out to pull Song Anhao over to sit in front of her.","\"That's because your Brother Yukun has the capital to be a narcissist. His looks are number one in the capital, and his talent is number one in the capital. It's normal for him to be a little narcissistic.\"","Song Anhao pinched his chin and looked up at a forty-five-degree angle, deep in thought.","\"But I think Brother Cui, who came to our house to see Eldest Sister last time, is better looking than Brother Yukun.\"","Song Qiming shook his head with a helpless smile.","\"Make sure you never say that in front of your Brother Yukun. He'll get angry if he hears it.\"","\"County Princess, the fish balls from the shop have been delivered.\"","A servant walked in carrying a food box. It was so cold that the freshly made fish balls were already almost frozen.","Sitting around the table, Song Anhao spoke while eating, \"Brother, you promised to take me out of the city to hunt this afternoon. You can't go back on your word.\"","\"We will leave as soon as we finish eating. By the time we get there, our food will be mostly digested.\"","Song Qiming said, \"We'll just look for wild hares or roe deer in the nearby woods. It will only take a little over an hour to get there.\"","\"If you can digest your lunch that quickly, we should have your Eldest Sister and Second Sister take a look at you.\"","Song Anhao chewed on his mutton and said, \"I have a big appetite, I can definitely digest it all.\"","And then he ended up overeating. It took a cup of hawthorn tea for him to feel better.","Half an hour later, the four fully armed siblings of the Song family headed out.","Song Jinzhao, Song Qiming, and Song Shixue all rode their own horses, while only Song Anhao sat in the carriage with Xuetuan.","It wasn't until they were out of the city that he let Xuetuan out of the carriage to run on its own, while he shared a horse with Song Qiming.","Half a year ago, Song Anhao used to frequently ride on the white tiger's back.","Later on, as his weight soared, he worried it would be bad for Xuetuan's spine, so he rarely rode it anymore.","The sparse wind and snow hit their faces. While it felt cold, the endless expanse of white fields was a refreshing and uplifting sight.","Considering the time, they didn't go too far. After playing in the nearby woods for about two hours, they prepared to head back home.","They didn't see any other prey besides wild hares, so they simply hunted a few rabbits to roast and eat back home.","Song Anhao looked reluctantly at the four snowmen standing in the snow, which they had just built.","Seeing him stop every two steps, Song Jinzhao simply said, \"If you can't bear to leave them, let's move them back. They won't melt in this weather.\"","Song Anhao shook his head without a second thought. \"It's better to leave them here. The scenery is nice, the space is big, and they can see further.\"","Faced with her youngest brother's childish words, Song Jinzhao merely smiled dotingly.","Just as the four of them were riding toward the main road, a convoy of carriages passed by ahead. Yao Ying drove their carriage to the side of the road to make way.","Looking at the familiar faces before her, Song Jinzhao narrowed her eyes.","These were the guards Xiao Rongyan had taken with him when he left the capital.","As they passed in front of Song Jinzhao, a familiar voice rang out from the carriage.","\"Stop the carriage.\"","As the curtain was slowly pulled aside, Xiao Rongyan's loathsome face appeared before Song Jinzhao.","\"It has been half a year. I trust you have been well, County Princess Linghui.\"","Song Jinzhao led her siblings to dismount and bow to Xiao Rongyan.","\"Greetings to Prince Yingcheng.\""]}]);
